window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":301,"title":"Chapter 301: Chapter 300 - Traversing Space, The Underworld","paragraphs":["In the vastness of space, a single black dot shot forth at extreme speeds.","The starry space was filled with stars, making some regions shimmer with brilliant lights while other regions were completely filled with darkness. Noah, contained in the [Miniature Space] ability of the Amorphous Space Beast, traversed the vastness of space for an entire day and night. There wasn’t a rising or setting sun to show the passage of time, making him feel an unusual feeling as he counted the hours while staring at the worders around him.","He came across vibrant stars that seemed to be filled with life, and also chanced upon planets that held violent elemental storms within as not a single life form could be felt. The most extreme case in this journey was when he came across a star that was shockingly split apart into two pieces.","He had only observed the circular form that seemed to have a line cutting through it when he was far away in the distance, and he changed his direction briefly as he went to observe this phenomenon. The closer he came, the larger the star became as he shockingly saw numerous asteroids floating around this star that was split into two pieces.","His size was extremely minuscule compared to the large shattered star he was looking at, his attention only hanging around this shocking scene briefly as he viewed the broken planet to see what could have caused such a thing. No answers could be ascertained as he looked at this as a sort of reminder for what fate could befall the numerous stars and continued on his journey.","It was an extremely boring and eye-opening trip as he expanded his horizons and crossed multiple Small and Large Worlds, even chancing upon a Prime World that he didn’t even get near of lest he be sensed by some monstrous powers.","He continued forward for another day before he neared the coordinates that the Void Crystal which the Vampyre Prince had given him to foretold. In his expanding sight, the view of a mystically shining planet gradually enlarged and came to view.","The planet in front of him was different from the ones he came across, being even bigger than the World of Cultivation, and having something that Noah had not yet come across with his own eyes. He stared curiously at the enlarging planet that had...a shimmering grey barrier all around it.","The barrier seemed extremely thin, like it could be broken at any moment, but Noah knew this wasn’t the case as just from the single location he was observing from, he could sense life forms not too far from the barrier that were most likely stationed there as guards.","This was the first star that he had come across which held something as unique as a barrier, making him even more interested in understanding just what type of forces were dwelling in it.","The Void Crystal that should have been leading him to the location where the Pureblood Vampyres resided in the Underworld shone a black light as it seemed to have sensed something and sent a signal forth, with Noah only waiting a few minutes as he shockingly noticed a wide octagonal shape opening up in the shimmering barrier, a black interstellar warship shooting out a few seconds later as it neared his position.","The ship held a sleek design, being much smaller than the ones that he previously saw around the doorway that led to the First Realm of Hell. It came close to him as it stopped a few meters away, a grandiose door opening as beside it stood a dashingly handsome Vampyre Prince.","He was looking at the black dot stationed in space as he observed it bloom, the form of a calm dark-haired young man in his 20s appearing magnificently as a sharp light passed through the Prince’s eyes.","\"You seem to always have another face when I see you.\"","Prince Cassius gave a light greeting as Noah seamlessly floated towards the ship with his original human body, a light smile appearing on his face as he expected this prince to at least be surprised at seeing a Saint Realm individual like him float in space with no issues, but it seemed he had left too strong of an impression when he left this Prince the last time.","\"This is my actual form, not the Crixus of the World of Cultivation. The name is Noah, Noah Osmont.\"","Prince Cassius nodded, his imposing sight checking Noah up and down as he entered into the ship that shot back to the octagonal space still open in the barrier. Noah wasn’t bothered with the probing gaze of the Vampyre Prince as he had prepared sufficiently while he was traveling over here, using the Dagger of Time multiple times to check for the different possibilities that could play out for this trip to the Pureblood Vampyre’s abode.","In almost all of the possible scenarios, no harm would befall him, and he only stood to benefit as he learned more about this covert force that was sleeping right under the Celestials’ nose.","He observed the octagonal shape quickly closing behind them the moment the ship passed through, the voice of Prince Cassius ringing out again as they entered the main room of the small ship they were on.","\"Your story has raised quite a few heads, with my Father looking forward to meeting someone that is as bold as I am.\"","The high echelons of the Pureblood Vampyres were wondering who the being that was bold enough to take the life of Celestial Disciples could be, and more so what unknown force this being represented!","Noah smiled at this as he observed the new world unfolding itself in front of him. The Vampyre Prince’s people seemed to have questions about him, and he had even more questions about them as he would come to understand exactly what kind of force they were.","The ship they were on broke through the clouds as the grandiose sight of one of the lands of the Underworld made itself apparent in Noah’s eyes. One couldn’t see the dreary atmosphere that they would come to imagine when the thought of ’Underworld’ entered their minds. What Noah saw was a magnificent sight of a shining metropolis that was filled with grandiose ancient castles that screamed regality.","The largest of these ancient castles were cl.u.s.tered at the center of the wide lands that expanded to the horizon. Noah could not find a location that looked barren as everything around him shone with uniqueness.","The ship they were on neared the centermost region of this wide country, these wide lands that were under the control of the Pureblood Vampyres as Noah made his entrance into the Underworld."]},{"number":302,"title":"Chapter 302: Chapter 301 - The Pureblood Vampyres","paragraphs":["The Underworld was a unique Prime World that stood above many Prime Worlds in terms of power. This was why even though many powers were surprised when they saw the name of a Vampyre Prince shine brightly on the leaderboard for the Infernal Hunt, they understood it as a fact when they connected this Prince to the Pureblood Vampyres of the Underworld.","It was a powerful world that was filled with unique monsters and powerhouses, ranging from the Vampyres, to Werewolves, all the way to the race of Cyclops and other unique creatures.","Out of all the organizations that were distributed across the wide Underworld though, the Vampyres were the most powerful, and the most secretive. They mostly kept to themselves as they continued to expand their lands and power, eventually becoming the known dominant force of the Underworld.","Noah observed the ancient castles all around him that made him feel like he was looking at an upgraded medieval era with monsters and magic as the ship that he and the Vampyre Prince were on landed squarely on a wide area behind one of the biggest castles in the huge metropolis they entered.","The doors opened to a shimmering red carpet that led all the way to wide-open golden doors that led towards the castle, with the right and left sides of the red carpet filled with neatly dressed men and women that all had the look of butlers and maids.","\"Welcome back, O Great Prince.\"","It was an amazing sight to come across as this prince who had most likely just left this castle for a few minutes came back and received a welcome as if he had left for years. The heads of all these beings that Noah felt to all be Vampyres were turned down respectfully as they spoke with reverent voices. Noah turned to the impassive face of Prince Cassius who had already begun walking across the red carpet as he followed along, the prince pointing to the large castle in front of them and speaking out.","\"This castle in front of you is the Royal Castle where many Vampyre Nobles reside.\"","The large castle was filled with a dense aura of blood and regality as Noah ascertained that much, not spreading his aura out too much lest he catch the attention of some powerful character that could put a damper on his plans.","They entered through the wide doors as even more neatly dressed butlers and maids gestured towards a door while bowing, speaking with reverential uniform voices that would make one feel a sense of awe and fear.","\"The food has been prepared, O Great Prince.\"","Prince Cassius nodded as he led Noah further into the castle, bringing him to a wide hall that held a long regal rectangular table. On this table, gorgeously shining meats of rare beasts and animals were abundant, with golden inlaid cups and jugs holding a deep red liquid that glistened in the light. Noah’s attention was grabbed by the resplendent assortment of foods, his nose wrinkling as he smelled the strong metallic scent of blood that permeated the wide room.","The Prince’s face turned grim as he turned to the nearby maids, his voice becoming hard and ringing out in the hall.","\"I told you all to prepare a meal for a guest.\"","The voice was chilling as the maids that were just preparing the food felt their legs buckle, a unique aura erupting from Prince Cassius that forced them to their knees as they apologized with ashen faces.","\"We- we apologize O Great Prince. We didn’t know the guest would be...we shall change it right away!\"","They scrambled towards the long table as they waved their hands, the abundant amount of cups and uniquely golden jugs holding the reddish liquids reducing quickly as the prince waved his hands and set out another command.","\"Leave us quickly. I expect no interruptions.\"","Quick nods were given as butlers and maids ran out as if their lives depended on it, Prince Cassius offering Noah a seat while he himself sat right opposite him as he looked at Noah with peering eyes.","\"Alright, I still can’t figure you out, so you’ll have to be willing to share slightly more things about yourself today.\"","Noah smiled at the peering words, about to reply when the recently closed door was flung open again, causing a vein to appear above the irascible Prince Cassius as he spoke without even turning around.","\"Did I not say there would be no interruptions?\"","\"Now, I would never dare to interrupt your special time O Great Prince, it is just that your father has called for you...and your guest.\"","A calm and jovial voice came out as the one to come in was an aged old man that held a vibrant aura, the large canines coming out of him glistening dangerously as he spoke out.","The Prince’s tone changed as he turned to look at this powerhouse at the peak of the Void Realm as he asked quizzically.","\"Father should still be in the meeting with the Council. I was going to have him meet my guest when he was finished.\"","\"It appears quite a few heads were turned because of your guest, some in the Vampyre Council showing great interest as well.\"","The aged Vampyre replied with a respectful smile, saying words that turned the expression of the Prince sour as he replied his misgivings.","\"That is not the way I wanted this to play out.\"","...","A brief pause came as the bowing Vampyre straightened up and looked at the two figures sitting on the wide dining table filled with an overabundance of food as he now replied coldly, yet still respectfully.","\"It is what your father wanted.\"","Prince Cassius turned passive as he heard this, a confused expression appearing on his face as many thoughts passed through his head, eventually turning towards Noah with an apologetic expression.","\"I apologize for this, it seems I cannot be a good host, and we must meet some old fogeys first.\"","Noah’s eyes shone at the rapid progression of events, nodding as he stood up along with the Vampyre Prince, their gazes landing on the smiling Vampyre that began leading them out of the wide dining hall and deeper into the castle where powerful auras were abundant.","They passed through multiple halls and corners, and even ascended a few floors as the Butlers and Maids that they passed became more and more powerful, with multiple Transcendent Realm Vampyre maids dressed in voluptuous clothing standing outside wide doors that led to an expansive room.","The old Vampyre bowed as his right hand pointed towards the room while speaking out once again, this time his words directed to Noah.","\"Please, enter into the Council Hall.\"","The invitation was crisp as the door opened, Prince Cassius entering with a slightly angered expression while Noah entered the room calmly, the door closing behind them with a clang as the room opened up in front of their eyes.","In this expansive room termed as the Council Hall, numerous auras honed in at Noah’s position as his eyes stared straight to the far corner of the room where an exquisitely large bejeweled throne that screamed regality stood.","On this throne, a being with blood-red eyes and a tight-fitting suit was looking directly at Noah, his expression of great interest as oppressive auras began to permeate the entire room.","In less than an hour after his entrance into the Underworld, Noah was already meeting with the being that stood at the forefront of power for the strongest force established in this world!"]},{"number":303,"title":"Chapter 303: Chapter 302 - The Vampyre Council","paragraphs":["The Vampyre on the throne held a light smile as his gaze focused on the appearing figures of Noah and Prince Cassius. Around this wide and expansive Council Hall, there were multiple figures situated to the elevated platforms on the left and right sides that led towards the throne.","Each of these figures were letting out levels of power no less than the Void Rank, with a few even surpassing it!","\"So this is the conundrum that even the little genius Cassius cannot solve?\"","The Vampyre on the throne spoke in a playful tone as he gazed towards his son. This Vampyre could not be called old, and actually had the figure of a man in the prime of his life, seemingly in his early 40s at most. This appearance would fool many beings as the actual age of this one being ranged in the hundreds of years.","Prince Cassius moved forward, about to reply, when an immense aura suddenly shot forth from one of the elevated platforms and descended on Noah, a unique skill being cast that locked down space entirely!","This change of events was rapid as a booming voice of power erupted from the right side of the elevated platform.","\"This issue can be solved right now. This unknown being observed our prince kill Celestial Disciples, and that is a dangerous knowledge that we cannot leave wandering outside this world. We should simply...kill!\"","OOONG","Vibrations erupted out at the mention of these explosive words, Prince Cassius moving towards Noah as he looked up at the being speaking and replied with a grave tone.","\"Count Shytus, anymore disrespect towards my guest and you will earn my displeasure!\"","The Vampyre Prince’s words were not filled with as much power as the being that targeted Noah, but his body shone with a red glow as it forcefully caused the body of the one called Count Shytus to pull back, seemingly dominated by something else that was not just power!","Noah observed this as many thoughts about the Vampyres passed through his mind, the subject of extremely unique bloodlines that could pressure beings no matter their rank of power coming up.","Count Shytus pulled back his aura as he turned to the Vampyre on the throne and spoke out languidly.","\"O Great King, we know the power of Celestials. Should we really be placing our lives and the lives of our people on a being we don’t even know the origins of, when we can just nip this in the bud right now?\"","The words were filled with strength, gaining the agreement of a few other beings situated on the elevated platforms of the wide hall. Quietness permeated the hall as everyone looked towards the Vampyre on the throne, the playful expression never leaving this being’s face as he spoke towards Noah.","\"So, human with unknown origins. Why don’t you tell us of your origins, and what exactly you wish to accomplish?\"","Complete silence reigned the moment this question was asked, all the powerful auras focusing on the next set of words coming out from this newly appearing being’s mouth as it would decide where they stood on this very unpredictable issue.","The problem at hand for the Vampyres was that their prince had acted and killed the Celestial Disciples, and he was observed by an unknown being while doing this!","The Prince had mentioned the events thereafter when he and this being joined forces and even took down two more Celestial Disciples, which put a few old fogeys in a speculative mood, while others were still convinced and saw this as a grave threat. Because the moment that even the possibility of suspicion was thrown to the Pureblood Vampyres of the Underworld being enemies of the Celestials, it would be the complete eradication of all of them.","So when it came to the option of complete eradication of all of their forces, or simply killing the being holding extremely important information, it wasn’t even a question for a few of the powerful figures in this Vampyre Council!","They honed their gazes towards Noah as they awaited to find out exactly who this being was and what he wanted. All the while Prince Cassius was looking at his father with a questioning and confused expression, as this was not what they had discussed when he first relaid information about the being he met in the First Realm of Hell.","Noah’s heart was at ease as he felt the auras of multiple beings focus on him, knowing his preparations were more than enough for this venture he was about to take. He spoke out cautiously.","\"I am Noah Osmont, and I come from a world that was impacted by the Celestials in the past, and I have been personally moving against them all this time. When I found that another force covertly existed in the dark that was moving against them as well, I had to come.\"","The words were neither overbearing nor servile, but it didn’t seem to have satiated the hungry Vampyres as the being on the throne spoke once more while nodding.","\"What exactly do you hope to accomplish? Going through the information I could find about you- you are acting as a little genius of a sect in the World of Cultivation, with your power at the Saint Realm. A genius, sure, but extremely young. What do you want, and what could our side benefit from someone like you?\"","The smiling expression remained on the face of the Vampyre King as he asked this dangerous question.","Noah turned towards Prince Cassius as he replied.","\"I observed the unique skills displayed by the Prince that were extremely effective in dealing with the Celestial’s probing gazes, and I am in great need of such skills in the coming future.\"","\"HMPH!\"","A snort rang out as Count Shytus spoke out once again.","\"You think a nobody would be given access to the forbidden skills of the Pureblood Vampyres?\"","His tone was domineering and strong as he seemed offended by even the thought of this assertion! Noah moved his eyes towards the Vampyre on the Throne as he did not even look in another direction, knowing this being would be the key for his plans here today.","\"This still does not answer the other half of my question- what can we gain from you?\"","Quietness reigned in the Council Hall once more as a bright smile erupted from Noah.","\"Your people must have seen the appearance of the Celestial Grandmaster near the end of the Infernal Hunt.\"","OONG!","Intense pressure from the seating Council members descended at the mention of the powerful figure, the Vampyre King still comfortably sitting on his throne as he nodded for Noah to continue.","\"That Celestial Grandmaster saw great potential in the being that contributed greatly to the death of the Infernal Aberration, and has invited me...to join the ranks of Celestials.\"","A bright smile covered Noah’s face as he released information that only the Elders of the Profound Astral Sect knew at this moment!","RUMBLE!","The atmosphere in the room suddenly changed as the smile was wiped away from the playful Vampyre King, a destructive aura at the peak of Soul Forging Realm erupting out as a maddening pressure permeated and covered the entire Council Hall, extending to the entire Royal Castle soon after as a bloody world was instantly enacted and covered everything in its entirety!"]},{"number":304,"title":"Chapter 304: Chapter 303 - Domineering","paragraphs":["Immense pressure was unbound in the Vampyre Council Hall as from the right and left of the hall where many Vampyre Counts and powerful figures were situated, many of them had blood red eyes and dangerous batwings erupting from their backs as they were frozen in place. Their hands were outstretched in form of sharp claws as their wide jaws showed long canines ruptured and ready to bite off the being they were all jumping towards, the single human present in the Council Hall!","RUMBLE!","The bodies of all of these powerful Vampyres that were already in motion to descend towards Noah and rip him apart the moment he finished saying the single last explosive sentence were all frozen in place from the domineering aura of none other than the Vampyre King himself that had lost his playful smile and stood up grimly from his throne.","The eruption of his power was not to attack or pressure Noah, but to hold back these voracious Vampyres that had acted the instant his words finished to jump for this human’s life. The body of the Vampyre King pulsed with a red light as a regal aura of the densest Pureblood Bloodline brought tremendous pressure to all surrounding Vampyres and stopped them on their tracks no matter if they were at the Void or Soul Rank.","This was the power that the being holding the purest bloodline of the Vampyres, this was the man known as the Vampyre King!","Prince Cassius was looking at Noah with a shocked expression as even he had not found out this information that he released just now, watching as Noah’s expression remained calm while monstrous auras that were ready to pounce towards him surrounded him from all directions.","The grim expression on the Vampyre King’s face was soon wiped away as numerous thoughts seemed to pass through his experienced eyes. He knew exactly how his forces would react the moment this human let loose the shocking words, and acted instantly to prevent any unfortunate events from occurring. His gaze now remained on Noah as silence reigned in the Council Hall.","The Vampyre King waved his fingers swiftly as the monstrous powerhouse that were already pouncing towards Noah found their bodies unwillingly return to the seats they were in, their fangs and wings retracted as they were given a reminder of the fearsome power of the being that stood on the throne of the Pureblood Vampyres.","\"You all seem to have forgotten, but it is I that makes the rules and is in command of every single creature in these lands. This applies to the rats, the elite vampyres, and even the little pureblood vampyres in this room.\"","Domineering words resounded across the wide Council Hall as powerful Vampyres of the Void and Soul Rank found themselves situated back into their seats like obedient children. They held no control of their bodies as the one holding the purest bloodline activated his authority and turned them as weak as normal unawakened beings!","\"If something like this ever happens again, you all will be the first to lose your heads.\"","\"...\"","Powerful!","Domineering!","Resplendent!","The words of the Vampyre King reverberated as he turned his focus towards Noah and Prince Cassius.","\"You two, let’s talk.\"","He waved his fingers again as Prince Cassius’s body floated towards him, another power wrapping around Noah and bringing him further into the Council Hall where the throne of the Vampyre King stood.","Their bodies arrived right beside the stone steps leading to the throne as another smaller world of blood began to convalesce around them, the voice of the Vampyre King ringing out towards the still trembling Vampyres on both sides of the hall.","\"The rest of you, reflect on your actions for now.\"","OOOM!","The smaller blood world completely covered their three figures as only silence remained in the wide hall. Every single Vampyre in the room continued to be situated with not a single movement, only their eyes being able to show the fear they had forgotten deep in their hearts.","When looking at the Royal Castle where the ruling force of the Pureblood Vampyres resided, many beings could see a shimmering red blood world encircling it endlessly as they wondered exactly what had occurred.","---","More than an hour passed as a bloody world revolved around the Royal Castle, and an even smaller bloody world revolved around three beings in the Vampyre Council Hall. The Vampyres to the left and right of the hall were still seated without a single ounce of movement when they felt a change sometime later, the bloody world in the room dissolving as the three beings came out with different expressions.","The Vampyre King had returned to his usual smile, the Prince seemed to be lost in thought, while the human was calm with slight excitement visible on his face.","The Vampyre King sat back on his throne as he waved his hands, the Vampyres on the sides of the hall finding movement returning to their bodies as they breathed out and remained still, turning to look towards their king with reestablished fear as he spoke out.","\"Our little friend here presents a unique opportunity that our Dark Expanse has never been able to come across in the last hundreds of years.\"","His voice was firm as it resounded in the hall, revealing shocking information about the origin of the Pureblood Vampyres as the King continued.","\"We have always clashed with Celestials, but never have we garnered an opportunity to get inside of their Celestial Stars, or even have someone on our side among them. This little friend right here...\"","The Vampyre King pointed towards Noah as he continued.","\"...will be taking the extremely dangerous task of infiltrating a Celestial Star, and would require our forbidden skills in order to not be found out and captured during his infiltration. Does anyone object to this decision?\"","A question was asked, yet many knew it wasn’t a question, but simply the statement of a fact!","Count Shytus was the first to reply as he bowed his head.","\"No, O Great King. You are wise beyond the years to see ahead to the usefulness this human can bring.\"","\"No, Sire!\"","\"No objections!\"","Numerous voices perked up as their eyes could not even meet the being that controlled their bodies with a simple movement of his fingers, showing their agreement as every single Vampyre in the Council Hall unanimously agreed with the words said by the Vampyre King.","The smiling King nodded as he turned his gaze towards Noah and spoke.","\"Now, I somewhat trust you somewhat after our discussion, and understand your need for information. So...\"","He then pointed with his index finger towards the center of the wide hall as a runic circle appeared in the air, drawing the shocked gazes of the Vampyre Council as they felt the initiation of Ancient Blood Magic.","\"...as a way to prove yourself to me and the pureblood vampyres here, you can enter the Ancient Blood World of our Progenitor.\"","BOOM!","The shocked gazes only continued as many Vampyres abruptly stood up, about to open their mouths when they recalled what just happened an hour prior as they quickly sat back down while affirming the reality of the Ancient Magic they felt being cast.","The runic inscription finished being inlaid as it shone brightly, a bloody red portal appearing in the middle of the hall as a desolate aura released from it.","\"This Ancient Blood World is located near the border of the Light and Dark Expanse, hidden far among the dredged of dead stars. It has the inheritance of our Progenitor, and will have the techniques you seek, as well as allow you to gain more of our trust because...\"","The Vampyre King held a wide smile as he spoke out the conditions he had discussed with Noah during their hour-long discussion.","\"...only a Vampyre can leave this Ancient Blood World alive.\"","...!"]},{"number":305,"title":"Chapter 305: Chapter 304 - An Inheritance of Blood","paragraphs":["An air of ancientness and turbidity was released from the bloody portal floating in the middle of the Council Hall as the Vampyre King finished his words. Some nods of understanding could be seen from a few older Vampyres, seeing the forethought put into the plans of their king as they realized what the results of it would be.","Some still held shocked expressions because they could not believe that a human, not even a vampyre, was being given permission to seek the inheritance of the Progenitor!","One should know that this was an opportunity that very few of even the highest echelons of Pureblood Vampyres received, being something that was given as a prize to the exceedingly genius growing disciples.","Many of them wanted to speak up, but recalling what had just occurred over an hour ago, they sat back in their seats and simply watched the progression of events.","Noah’s eyes were stuck to this glowing red portal as he went over the hour long talk between him and the enigmatic being that seemed to always be smiling, yet it also felt like he was hiding a sharpened blade that could cut down at any second.","The Vampyre King had asked for every single detail of the encounter between him and Prince Cassius in the First Realm of Hell, exactly how they took down the disciples, what they observed, and the final fight between them and the Aberration!","Even more details that he wanted was the conversation that Noah and Elder Spacewarp had with the Celestial Grandmaster word for word when he pulled them from their interstellar ship and offered the invitation of becoming a Celestial Disciple towards Noah.","A cold light passed through the Vampyre King’s eyes when he heard the Celestial refer to the Dark Expanse as lawless place, his eyes scrutinizing every detail thereafter as he observed Noah without blinking an eye until he seemed satisfied with the information.","Before the small blood world wrapping around them was released, the Vampyre King had mentioned that he would give Noah the possibility of gaining the techniques that could escape the mysterious ways of the Celestials, but this came with a few conditions!","The first condition that he mentioned was the obtaining of the skills lying solely in Noah’s hands as he would be given the opportunity to enter the land of their Ancestor, the Ancient Blood World that held the inheritance of many of the techniques he had observed Prince Cassius using, and more.","Only after this was done would they move on to the next stage, the actual discussions of who this force of Pureblood Vampyres really were, and what they were planning against the Celestials.","Noah glanced at the Prince Cassius that seemed to be lost in thought as he gave a light smile and began walking towards the portal letting out desolate energies. He held slight excitement about the techniques of the Vampyres that could evade the eyes of the Celestials, but he more so wanted to experience just exactly what these unique areas and skills he had never come across held in store for him.","The statement about only Vampyres being able to leave this Ancient Blood World did not bother him as his sights went past such things, and he only longed for more strength!","His gaze became firm as he went towards the glowing red portal without looking black, disappearing in a flash as the room returned to quietness. This only lasted briefly as a joyful voice rang out.","\"Haha cheer up. We may have gained an extremely useful ally, but I know not to place everything we have in front of him. This portal will only lead him to the normal inheritance given to Elite Vampyres, not the actual Abode where our Progenitor’s remains rest.\"","The words brought down the sinking feeling that many Vampyres in the Council hall were having as they did not want to raise a word against their king, but felt it extremely blasphemous if the human had really been sent to the Supreme Blood Inheritance that was only meant for Vampyre Royalty.","\"Now, it should take him a few hours or days depending on his talent. We need to discuss how to best use this infiltration into a Celestial Star to our advantage. I’ll also send word back home, as this is truly something huge.\"","The Vampyre Council agreed as their voices slowly began to perk up for discussions, the Pureblood Prince Cassius on the side still lost in thought as he looked at his father. He was thinking heavily about the recent set of events as what his father had done confused him, and he even more so knew that his father was lying!","Noah was not sent to the Inheritance Grounds for Elite Vampyres in the Ancient Blood World, but to the Inheritance Abode of their Progenitor that only he, a Prince of the Vampyre Race, had gone into in the last hundred years!","His thoughts were clouded as he wondered, what exactly was his father up to?","---","It felt like only a blink of an eye as Noah passed through the bloody portal in the Council Hall and came into a brand new area filled to the brim with an aura of ancientness and desolation.","He appeared in the middle of what appeared to be a ridiculously large coliseum shaped structure that could be called ridiculous because it stretched for miles in diameter all around.","He had to use [Observation] just to see the huge walls surrounding this humongous coliseum that was enclosed in a dome shape. All around this miles long Coliseum, numerous lakes were distributed throughout as a metallic smell hung in the air. Near the wall, statues of terrifying creatures were spread throughout, many showing exquisite bat wings and fangs as they held different assortments of expression. They were situated all around the circular coliseum, their gazes intersecting at something at the very center.","At this center most position located a few miles where he stood, Noah could see an ancient shrine that screamed of old age, with an enormous lake of blood around it as the moment he entered, this lake of blood trembled as essence began to converge.","RUMBLE!","Noah focused all of his attention on this movement as he watched with stupefaction at the gradual formation of a being from the viscous lake of blood around this shrine.","The lake was simply too wide, the outline of the being forming rapidly becoming larger and larger as Noah soon found himself staring at something that towered above 30 meters. It held a humanoid shape, but had the grandiosity of a mountain as it floated grandly in the air, its bloody color shining in the desolate and ancient air as two even redder eyes opened and honed themselves on Noah.","OOOM!","The being began speaking, but the opening of its mouth only let out waves of destructive energies as nothing discernable came out, the thing that made Noah the most interested about this being’s appearance was the simple fact that...he could not sense any aura at all from it!","So what exactly was this Inheritance of the Pureblood Vampyres, and what would be the terms to obtain it?"]},{"number":306,"title":"Chapter 306: Chapter 305 - The Guardian of Blood, Challenging the Inheritance!","paragraphs":["Waves of non discernible power rolled off the gigantic bloody being as a wine colored robe went on to dr.a.p.e over its body, a humongously long spear appearing on its right hand, its body coming down and smashing into the ground and causing a quake. It spoke once more, this time being much clearer.","\"Are you prepared to stake your life to fight for the Inheritance of the Blood Progenitor, O...human?\"","A voice of majesty had begun with resoundingly powerful words, but they finished in a questioning tone as the peering gaze focused on Noah. A brief silence came to be before the giant being made of what now looked like shining crystallized blood straightened up and continued.","\"This inheritance is meant for the most powerful beings of the Vampyre Race, are you sure you are willing to stake your life on it, human?\"","Its rumbling voice echoed from all over the miles long coliseum as Noah shouted back without a pause.","\"I am willing!\"","It was a voice full of confidence for whatever this Inheritance would throw at him, this confidence coming from the fact that he was holding on to the Dagger of Time very closely and using [Insight], also ready to take any drastic action if it was required of him to do so.","\"...Good. The test to determine your worthiness will be as such.\"","The giant waved his hands as a red light descended towards Noah, a red runic marking being inlaid on his forehead as a signal came off of his body and was sent towards the bloody giant.","\"The test will be a measure of your intellect, skill, and battle prowess as you face increasingly difficult opponents.\"","At these words, one of many pools of blood in the extremely wide coliseum began trembling as figures began rising from it, Noah observing the shapes of exactly one hundred humanoid bats with razor sharp claws and teeth, with wide wings erupting from their backs.","\"Since you are at the Saint Realm, the first level will start with you battling 100 beings at the same rank.\"","\"...\"","Noah squinted his eyes at the 100 figures letting out power at the peak of the Saint Realm, turning his head towards the bloody giant in a questioning tone as these did not seem to be fair rules in any way for a being at the Saint Realm. The giant let out a slight cough as it continued.","\"Per Master’s wishes, if a being other than a Vampyre was to be let into the Inheritance Grounds, the difficulty would be increased by a factor of 10. Master was fair to all races, but he reserved the tremendous Inheritance in these Grounds to be received by the future progeny of his children. Him even allowing the possibility of other races to fight for the inheritance is a show of his great character.\"","Noah shook his head at the praise of this unknown Ancestor that set up these Inheritance Grounds, his thoughts being affirmed as no normal Saint Realm being would be given the task of fighting 100 beings of the same rank as them, no matter how great their power was. This meant that the first level of this Inheritance normally required a Vampyre to battle only 10 other beings of the same rank!","Noah still had a few questions as he looked towards the bloody giant and asked.","\"How many levels are there, and what are the techniques awarded for passing them?\"","When he discussed with the Vampyre King prior to entering the bloody portal that led to this Ancient Blood World, he was told that the techniques he was seeking would be found in the Inheritance located here, and that it would be up to his strength exactly how many techniques he would be able to get his hands on!","The giant made of blood turned his head to the side at the calm expression of this human about to face a powerful force of 100 beings at the same rank as it replied.","\"There are six levels in total, with very few being able to pass even the third level in the last 1000 years. For a human such as you, the reward of passing the first level is gaining the bloodline of a normal Vampyre, with the techniques that go along with it. Passing the second level grants you the bloodline of an Elite Vampyre. Passing the Third level will give you the refined bloodline of a Pureblood Vampyre, along with the powerful techniques that come with it.\"","Noah’s eyes shone at the mention of these rewards, hearing the talk of Bloodlines and techniques that made him itching to get started, even if the task ahead of him seemed improbable for any other beings to complete.","The major thought that occupied his brain right now was that if the Bloodline of a Pureblood Vampyres was the reward for the third level of this inheritance, just what tremendous rewards were waiting at the fourth, fifth, or even the spectacular 6th level?","These thoughts propelled him forward as he yelled out.","\"Good, let’s start!\"","The huge giant that this Inheritance Ground knew as the Guardian of Blood looked closely at this human as the huge weapon it was holding in one hand raised before smashing towards the ground, acting as the initiation of the battle and letting loose 100 Saint Realm Blood Beasts towards Noah.","RUMBLE!","The force was astonishing to say the least, with the auras of these Blood Beasts actually roaring at the peak of the Saint Realm as they spread out and began surrounding Noah.","He let out a dazzling smile at the rushing of these monsters, multiple defensive skills layering his body as he wanted to test out the skills he held that were extremely powerful, but he didn’t use too frequently as he continued to get more and more ridiculous skills.","Spears, swords, and many other forms of weapons made up of blood began to be thrown in his direction from the encircled force of 100 Blood Beasts as he dodged them with ease.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","They struck the areas behind him as the tremendous speed provided by [Child of Space] and other speed enhancing abilities made the enemies rushing towards him feel like they were in slow motion.","SCREECH!","Uncomfortable screeches were let out by the Blood Beasts as none of their attacks hit, choosing to go in with brute force as they rushed towards Noah with outstretched claws.","Noah stood in place as his smile only became wider, waiting for more of these monsters to get close to him as he weaved in and out of their attacks. The moment he observed that the 100 monsters were all in a circular formation around him, he finally cast a skill as he used [Gluttony Manifestation], a subset ability of the enhanced Sin of Gluttony after the creation of the <<Absolute Sin>>.","<strong>[Gluttony Manifestation]:: The user can apply the effect of [Devouring] anywhere within 5 meters of them, there’s no need to actively eat them.</strong>","VOOM!","Complete darkness erupted from him in a circular formation as it covered more than 20 Blood Beasts, the darkness being recalled a second after as the area it was just in was left eerily empty!","\"..\"","The Guardian of Blood watched with surprised eyes as more than 20 Beasts at the Saint Realm were gone in an instant!","FLASH!","Noah wasn’t done as he teleported in and out of the mass of Blood Beasts around him, covering an area of 5 meters each time to maximize the range of [Gluttony Manifestation] as he repeatedly cast the skill 4 more times.","Quick.","Fast.","Easy.","Noah came to a stop in the air as he saw half cut up bodies, legs or wings that were outside of the range of [Gluttony Manifestation] fall to the ground, not a single Blood Beast remaining around him as he stood victoriously in the bloody skies!","The only thoughts passing through Noah’s mind was the reminder of the extreme usefulness of many of his unused skills as the Guardian of Blood looked forth with a face of stupor."]},{"number":307,"title":"Chapter 307: Chapter 306 - Ridiculous","paragraphs":["The first level of the Inheritance of the Blood Progenitor was passed in less than a minute!","The most shocking thing about this was the fact that this was the difficulty that was raised by a factor of 10. The Guardian of Blood observed the human in the middle of the wide Coliseum as he wondered whether the Inheritance Ground had misjudged their level of power, but confirmed the being was at the Saint Realm as a weak red light shone throughout the Inheritance Grounds, signifying the clearing of the first level.","The resounding voice of the Guardian of Blood resounded soon after.","\"The first level has been cleared, granting you the rewards of the Bloodline of a Normal Vampyre, along with a set of skills that goes with it. Do you wish to claim these rewards and relinquish the remainder of the trial, or do you wish to rest and then continue?\"","Less than a millisecond passed before a calm reply came from the floating Noah.","\"Continue.\"","\"I will remind you that the rewards of the first level will not be made possible to you if you choose to move forward and fail at the second level, as failure will result in death!\"","A warning came from the mouth of the Guardian of Blood as Noah repeated once again with a firm tone.","\"No need for rest, I will continue!\"","RUMBLE!","A red light shined out as essence converged, two more lakes of blood trembling as numerous figures began to rise from them. Noah observed with shining eyes as he counted a number of similarly shaped Blood Beasts rise up, until this number reached 200!","The second level...was twice as difficult as the first one, the number of Blood Beasts simply being duplicated!","Noah smiled at the craziness of this Inheritance that would most likely not be passed by anyone that wasn’t a Vampyre with this crazy upgraded level of difficulty as he looked at the gains from defeating the first 100 Blood Beasts. When he devoured all of them, similar to the Infernals that only gifted Noah with their unique energies in the form of Skill Points, he only obtained the memories of the Blood Beasts as no [Skill Books] or [Cores] were received from their defeat.","The cause either lied from the fact that they were coagulations of blood and weren’t considered to have souls or origins, but they gave absolutely nothing compared to the Infernals that gifted him with the powerful Skill Points as a reward.","He didn’t mind this though, as the reward of a Bloodline and techniques he would receive from taking them down was more than enough!","\"Come!\"","He roared out as a cold light shone in his eyes, his figure flashing towards the 200 Blood Beasts that had grouped together with tight defenses as they began moving the mana in the surroundings to cast long range attacks...or they tried to, but found that they couldn’t activate any abilities!","Confusion permeated in the coagulations of blood as no attacks came out from them, the Guardian of Blood once again being stumped at what was going on as Noah’s laugh resounded. This was simply caused by another ability from the Sins under <<Absolute Sin>>. This time, it was a subset skill from the Sin of Envy, [I’m the Absolute Best]!","<strong>[I’m the Absolute Best] - Opponents are not allowed to use skills known by the user, when fighting the user. Any Unique, Ultimate, or Absolute Skills holding a lower level of power than <<Original Absolute Sin>> are negated and unable to activate.</strong>","The moment that Noah absorbed the first 100 Blood Beasts and perused through the memories, the abilities they could use were all known to him, and thus they could no longer activate those skills when they faced him!","The force of 200 strong Saint Realm beings became disordered at this junction, their bodies instead moving for close combat as they rushed towards Noah, who only greeted them with a resplendence of shining condensed stars as he cast [White Dwarf Throw] with his body glowing from the intense aura of the Sin of Pride.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Resounding explosions erupted as the Blood Beasts had their defenses ruptured by the force of a condensed white dwarf star, the force of 200 strong being taken down in an extremely terrifying manner as the Guardian of Blood looked on with a stupefied expression once again.","It admitted the strength of this human after the first level, but thought that he would at least have exhausted his strength after those deadly attacks and struggle slightly more on the second level...but he was going through enemies at the same level as himself without any issues yet again, and this time, the Blood Beasts weren’t even throwing out attacks!","The Guardian of Blood wondered if the mechanisms of the Inheritance Ground had gotten too old and were interfered with as he confirmed that everything was working normally, watching stupefaction as 200 Blood Beasts were wiped away in the blink of an eye.","\"...The second level has been cleared, granting you the rewards of the Bloodline of an Elite Vampyre, along with a set of skills that goes with it. Do you wish to claim-\"","\"I will continue!\"","A jovial voice that was full of expectations erupted from Noah as he felt like he had found something that very few would come across, and he would be able to take advantage of it in a way that only he would be able to!","His sights were already set on the highest rewards at the 5th or 6th level, even gaining the Bloodline of a Pureblood Vampyre on passing the 3rd level being something small in his eyes!","A brighter red light shone throughout the expansive Coliseum as the third level for the Inheritance of the Blood Progenitor began, this time a force of 400 Blood Beasts at the Saint Realm rising up from the lakes of blood as their reddened eyes focused on Noah.","Normally, a genius Vampyre at the Saint Rank would have faced 20 Blood Beasts of the same realm at the second level, and 40 on the third level to prove their battle prowess and intelligence.","But the difficulty was much higher for Noah... although the number did not matter as he was always faster than them, and they could not even use their full abilities against him!","What occurred next was just plain ridiculousness as the Guardian of Blood watched the unbelievable sight of one man weaving in and out of a crowd of swarming Blood Beasts at the same level as him, stupendous attacks being thrown around until not too long later, only silence reigned.","\"...\"","The Guardian of Blood wondered, was the 10x difficulty set by his master not enough to even make this human sweat? Had humans grown more powerful to raise such geniuses over the past millennia? Worries began to pile up as at this rate, it seemed like this human might actually obtain the inheritance only meant for the noblest of Vampyres!","The giant made of crystallized blood watched on as the forces of the Blood Beasts continued to dwindle until yet again, only a single man remained floating in the bloody skies.","A hardened expression entered the face of the Guardian of Blood as it smashed down the large spear it was holding once again, a bright red light shining out that signified the clearance of the 3rd level, and brought out the monsters for the 4th level.","This time, it was only 10 Blood Beasts that were twice as large as the ones Noah had seen before. It was a small number, but each of these Blood Beasts let out a powerful aura of strength at the Void Realm!","The fourth level of this Inheritance of the Blood Progenitor was to fight 10 beings that were an entire rank higher than the challenger, something that would normally be an impossibility!","The concept of a genius being able to fight a single being of higher rank than them was already a shocking thing to hear about, but going against 10 would only be a joke out of people’s wildest dreams.","Noah looked at the appearance of these 10 Void Rank Blood Beasts as he saw the Guardian of Blood had not even bothered to ask him if he would continue or not, a refreshing smile coming on his face as he asked.","\"What are the rewards of clearing the fourth and fifth level?\"","\"..\"","The Guardian of Blood seemed muted for a second before he replied.","\"Clearing the Fourth level gives you the Bloodline of a Royal Vampyre, and clearing the 5th level gives you the access to the...Absolute Techniques that were used by the Progenitor himself!\"","The Guardian of Blood spoke out about the rewards it never thought this human would even come close to obtaining, its observation landing on the peculiar being that held a confident smile while looking at the 10 Void Rank opponents.","Just what being had entered his Master’s Inheritance Grounds?"]},{"number":308,"title":"Chapter 308: Chapter 307 - Leave while you still have your life!","paragraphs":["The Guardian of Blood looked forth at the stalemate between the human and the coagulations of blood that reached the Void Realm. It wanted to closely observe this human to see just exactly what ability allowed it to throw out such tremendous attacks.","When faced with 10 beings that were a rank higher than him, how would he handle it?","A glorious red light shone as it signified the beginning of the 4th level, the Guardian of Blood watching closely how this fight would unfold so it could learn more about this new being that might be adding a major power to the ranks of Vampyres soon.","The Guardian of Blood was prepared to watch a lengthy fight that would show more of this human’s wit and intelligence when it came to facing multiple enemies at a higher level, as he would not be able to rely on the spectacular firepower of his skills to break through the defenses of being a realm above him.","’So, how exactly will you handle a force of-\"","ZIIING!","A stupendous burst of destructive essence erupted as the Guardian of Blood watched with blank eyes as an aurora of resplendent lights erupted from the human and cut across the cl.u.s.tered Void Realm Blood Beasts, heaving injuring all of them and even directly killing two as their heads burst open from the tremendously destructive energies of...Aether?","Yes! It was Aether! The Guardian of Blood confirmed his thoughts as he was finally somewhat convinced why this human held such battle power. He had actually comprehended the power of one of the abstruse elements, Aether!","The Guardian observed the remaining injured Blood Beasts as he thought to himself.","’Aether is extremely energy-consuming, with that one blast most likely taking the remainder of his energy reserves as he did not even rest while passing through the first three levels. Do you now plan to use your speed to run as your energy recov-\"","ZIING! ZING! ZING!","\"...\"","Ridiculousness unfolded as the Guardian of Blood blinked his eyes to make sure that he had just seen another three extremely destructive Aether Rays erupt from the body of the small human like nothing and shred apart whatever remaining defenses the Void Realm Blood Beasts held.","The Guardian was stupefied, but one must know that when Noah first used the ability of [Sever], it was against an Aberration that was on the verge of ascending to the Second Realm of Hell, with its realm already about to enter the Soul Forging stage, and even it was injured with its breakthrough being brought to a stop as it ultimately faced death at the hands of the War Princess, Athena!","It was an unbelievable sight to look at, but a grand light shined out from the wide Coliseum that signified the passing of the fourth level!","This meant that this human, if he so chose, could receive the Bloodline of a Royal Vampye, something that only the extremely pure ruling beings that stood at the upper echelons of Vampyres had!","But would this human do such a thing? The question in the Guardian of Blood’s mind answered itself as an enthusiastic voice rang out.","\"Continue!\"","The eyes of the Guardian narrowed as the human once again passed a level in a way he never thought was possible, not even taking a second to think about taking the obtained rewards as he directly charged ahead. He had called forth the challenge of the 5th level, which if passed would grant one the techniques of the Blood Progenitor himself!","’Is he actually a human? Could he be a genius of the Ancient Races that has come to play?’","The Guardian of Blood remained silent as many thoughts moved across his mind, acting and moving the long weapon he was holding to smash towards the ground once more, initiating the start of the 5th level as 20 powerful auras of Void Realm Blood Beasts rose from the surrounding Blood Lakes.","He chose not to have any thoughts of underestimation for this human that was somehow filled with an enormous amount of energy and was actually proficient in using Aether, simply watching on passively as he watched for any more surprises.","The Void Rank Blood Beasts spread out the moment they appeared, as if by memory, not wanting to be cl.u.s.tered together as they weaved close to the floating human. A more astute description of what occurred though would be that they tried to spread out, but this action was swiftly stopped at the Guardian of Blood heard a whisper of a voice call out.","[Portals of Terror].","OONG!","In the midst of the moving Blood Beasts, a dark portal letting out a dangerous atmosphere appeared as it released unique energies that spread out in a circular motion, going on to cover each of the Void Realm Blood Beasts that were trying to spread out...and simply yanked them back toward the portal as if tight ropes had bound them!","[Portals of Terror] [Portals of Terror] [Portals of Terror]","The Guardian of Blood thought he was ready for any ridiculous sight, but he still found himself shocked as he heard the whispers three more times, observing as a red, blue, and green portals appeared around the now tightly grouped up and struggling Blood Beasts as they exploded forth with destructive energies unique to the colors they held.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Chilling destructive energies that froze the defenses of the beasts reached them first, destructive poisonous energies that shredded away their remaining defenses hitting them after, as fiery red destructive energies were released from the red portal that completely disintegrated their bodies into nothingness thereafter.","Silence reigned in the Inheritance Grounds of the Blood Progenitor as a brilliant red light shone on the single human left on the wide Coliseum, signifying the successful passing of a level that had not been passed for the last hundreds of years.","\"Wait.\"","The rumbling voice of the Guardian of Blood was released as he watched the lips of the human about to move and call out ’Continue’ once again, but it could not let him do so as a warning had to be released before something drastic occurred.","Noah turned towards the gigantic crystallization of blood that was more than 30 meters as it spoke out once again.","\"I applaud your stupendous battle strength and a once in a thousand years talent in energy and prowess. You would make a great addition to the forces of Vampyres in the future with the rewards you have already obtained.\"","The Guardian of Blood waved his hands a brilliant red light erupted out, revealing a resplendently glowing outline of numerous venous and arterial lines that connected to a blood red beating heart, showing a shining color of red sprinkled with gold.","\"This is the Bloodline of a Royal Vampyre, something that very few beings have in this wide Novus Galaxy.\"","He waved his hands once again as this time, multiple sparkling red jewels appeared beside the humanoid outline of veins and arteries as he continued.","\"And these are the Inheritance Stones that contain the techniques only privy to Royal Vampyres, and even the Absolute Technique of the Progenitor himself.\"","His gaze then focused on Noah as he spoke out the next words carefully.","\"Please, take these rewards and become a strong force for the Vampyres of this age. Do not needlessly continue on to the last level. Because I can assure you, even with the stupendous battle prowess you have shown, you will not be able to pass it.\"","...!","\"I implore you, take the rewards and leave. Leave while you still have your life.\"","A giant made of blood looked forth at the human floating in the air, a single smile that didn’t seem to have an ounce of shame being the only thing meeting his imploring gaze!"]},{"number":309,"title":"Chapter 309: Chapter 308 - See it to the End!","paragraphs":["Noah heard the resounding words of the Guardian of Blood as he looked at the shining outline of numerous coagulating veins and arteries connected to a shimmering red heart that signified the Bloodline of the Royal Vampyres, something that the Vampyre King himself held alone in the Underworld!","The rewards of the 5th level gave one this Bloodline, and numerous techniques that were in these newly appearing Inheritance Stones. These alone were the rewards for clearing this last level! Noah’s heart was now asking for, no- longing for, the rewards of the last level of this Inheritance of the Blood Progenitor!","It was not just greed for more, but simply because he needed strength and unique powers that he had never thought of before just to be able to stand against the force he wanted to go against. He needed strength that could be domineering to his enemies, similar to how he had dominated the numerous Blood Beasts on the past 5 levels just now.","He needed to be even more overpowered than he was right now!","\"I will see this trial to the end!\"","His strong voice reverberated through the expansive Coliseum as the Guardian of Blood looked at him silently, its voice ringing out only a moment later.","\"It is impossible for you to clear the 6th level.\"","There was a firmness in its tone that seemed to be inviolable, it was a tone that was that of someone simply stating the truth!","\"Human, you have continued to surprise me and you now even have the chance to take away the stupendous rewards of the Bloodline of a Vampyre Royalty, along with the Absolute Techniques of the Progenitor. You have earned my respect and wholeheartedly deserve the rewards for your amazing battle power, but I will once more advise you heavily against relinquishing your rewards and trying the last level.\"","The tone was firm, but had actually obtained a small ounce of pleading for this small genius in front of the Guardian of Blood that should not die after coming this far.","\"I have nothing against you, and believe you will become a great character in the future with the abilities you have and the rewards you have gained from here. You joining the ranks of Vampyres makes you one of us, so I implore you once more...do not attempt the 6th level.\"","An impasse was reached as a Guardian did not want to see a genius about to join the forces of Vampyres waste his life away, while the genius believed in himself so much so that nothing would stand in his way to obtain the ultimate prize!","Noah took a calm break in the skies of the expansive Coliseum as he turned his eyes away from the shining and pulsating Bloodline being advertised in front of him, the even more seductive inheritance stones holding unknown techniques fading from his sight as he focused on the Guardian of Blood and stated once more.","\"I will see this trial to the end.\"","It was a voice of calm and conviction, one that knew exactly what it wanted!","OOOOM!","Essence reverberated as the Guardian of Blood adopted an impassive face, standing up straight as its imposing 30 meters came to be even more pronounced. It smashed down the long spear in its hands once more as the numerous lakes of blood around the Inheritance Grounds trembled, the blood contained within the lakes shooting out as they all went towards one direction- towards the tremendously large giant!","WAA!","Majestic waves of power erupted as the numerous lines of blood wrapped around the Guardian of Blood, coming together to exquisitely create a glistening suit of armor inlaid with ancient runes. The spear in its hands trembled as it became even wider, the spear end becoming even sharper as it shone with a bloodthirsty hue.","\"The Inheritance Grounds that Master left behind are not just a place for young Vampyres to upgrade their Bloodline purity and gain more techniques.\"","Waves of power released from the body that was now fully covered with armor all around, a transformation complete as the Guardian of Blood that had no aura all this time...had actually gained one!","\"Ultimately, it was Master’s goal to find a once in a lifetime genius who fit his conditions, obtaining everything he left behind as he would task them with the task of returning the splendor of Vampyres to the center stage once more.\"","SHAA!","The Guardian of Blood waved its tremendously long spear forward as waves that left ruptures in space spread out, its spear pointing directly towards Noah!","\"If you were a Vampyre to begin with, if the rules of this Inheritance Ground allowed me to use loopholes, you might have been that genius who would have taken Master’s mantle. But...the difficulty is multiplied for you, thus for the final stage...you shall face me.\"","WAAA!","Majesty spread out as the Guardian of Blood took a unique stance, the spear in its hand gleaming and calling for blood as it seemed ready to pierce everything in front of it in an instant!","Noah floated in the skies as bloody winds billowed around him, his gaze fully taking in this newly armored Guardian of Blood as the immense aura it was letting out was one at the Soul Forging Realm!","Not Saint, not Void, but at the Soul Rank!","Noah had come across a few Soul Rank beings in the past few days since leaving the First Realm of Hell, but none of them came even close to the feeling of immensity he was feeling as he observed this Guardian in front of him.","Yet, even with this exceedingly dangerous development, even with the knowledge of he was standing against him and stupendous rewards out of his wildest dreams...a wide smile covered his face!","This was because he knew that the things he worked hardest to obtain, would be the ones that have immense value. From the words of the Guardian of Blood, the rewards for clearing this last stage...would be truly immense.","But the question still remained, how would a being at the Saint Rank fare against someone two levels higher, someone that was now furious at not being listened to and was using their full permitted power in the battle?","\"Hooo...\"","Noah breathed out calmly in the face of this terrifying aura at the Soul Forging Realm that did not scare him one bit. The only thing on his mind was a few thoughts that were shocking to imagine.","’I guess this is as good a time as any to test that out.’","A grand expression covered Noah’s face as essence began to erupt all around him, beginning a transformation himself as his gaze focused on the Guardian of Blood that would erupt at any time!"]},{"number":310,"title":"Chapter 310: Chapter 309 - Shocking! Outrageous! Obscene!","paragraphs":["Two gazes locked onto one another on the Inheritance Grounds of the Blood Progenitor. One was emotionless as they waited for the small being in the skies to get ready, the other was filled with calm and unknown confidence!","RUMBLE!","Essence converged and exploded as Noah activated the [Morph] ability of the Lesser Cthulhu, his body rapidly expanding as the humongous form of the terrible entity began to erupt out of nowhere.","Eyes that released stupendous red lights soon came into being as his body’s musculature was rapidly changed, glorious wings palpating with Aether erupting from his back, his body becoming more than 20 meters tall as he gained the terrifying appearance of the Lesser Cthulhu!","The Guardian of Blood looked at this form with a slight surprise, but his gaze remained impassive as he knew that even this would not be enough to stand against him. He shook his head sorrowfully at the thought of killing such a tremendous genius who could even tap into the power of something even he did not understand.","The tentacles and feelers on the lower half of the Lesser Cthulhu’s face palpated with energy as Noah wasn’t done, enacting what he had termed in his mind as the first trump card he could play in unforeseen situations!","OOOM!","Reddish clouds began to gather in the bloody atmosphere as they seemed to have sensed the appearance of something, Noah’s now strong body reverberating as his voice chanted softly, [Arch Demon Lord Transformation].","<strong>[Arch Demon Lord Transformation] :: The user can turn into the Arch Demon Lord; this will quadruple the strength and cost efficiency of all Sin and Demon skills. It will also double the efficiency and strength of all other skills used by the user during the transformation. </strong>","The words were distinct, barely a whisper, but their result was tremendous as something outrageous unfolded because of them.","RUMBLE!","Space quaked at the arrival of something never heard of nor seen before as Noah’s body that had transformed into the Lesser Cthulhu...transformed yet again as two transformation skills were cast at the same time.","Yes! This was the trump card that Noah was testing the efficacy of for the first time! If he were to combine the transformations of the ability of the <<Absolute Sin>> that granted him the epic form of an Arch Demon Lord along with the tremendous form of the Lesser Cthulhu, what would be the product?!","The two skills were from completely different origins, and could not be even combined under skill combination, but he could activate the both of them at the same time!","RUMBLE!","Essence moved chaotically as the body of the Lesser Cthulhu became even larger, tendrils of red energy beginning to mix with the blue-purple Aether as something unstable and unknown was created.","RIIP!","From his back, enormous red wings no lesser than the first two erupted as the grandiose sight of four extremely expansive wings unfolded on his back.","Destructive energies erupted out as just below the stout arms of the Lesser Cthulhu, two red arms filled with devilish runic inscriptions erupted out while the body continued to become ever larger. The size now towered over 30 meters as an engulfing roar erupted out from this new being, destructive energies being released as chaotic elemental storms began raging!","\"OOOOOOOOOOH!\"","A bestial roar of power and defiance rocked the Inheritance Ground of the Blood Progenitor as a newly appearing beast announced itself.","The face was even more terrifying than before, four pairs of eyes actually appearing on it as two pairs shining red and blue were in the front, and another two pairs shining a glorious dark purple were on the side of the face as they moved in a grotesque manner!","Atop this face, two devilish horns had erupted out as they raised to the skies, screaming in defiance as the size of these horns finally made this new form that Noah had taken...actually pass the Guardian of Blood in size, with the both of them just over 30 meters.","The waves of destructive power gradually settled down as the two beings looked at one another, the Guardian of Blood looking closely at his opponent as a barely discernable whisper released from him.","’Maybe...’","A whisper, and that was it as he finally moved, his fearsome body erupting with power as it defied common sense and turned into a streak of red light towards the transformed monstrosity in front of it!","The monstrosity, Noah, actually closed his many eyes as he relished the feeling of tremendous power that only seemed to increase with every passing second.","’This...Ahh!’","A feeling of elation as if he was going in the right direction passed through his mind as even without opening his eyes, he could see the streak of light that was the Guardian of Blood slowly near his position.","This streak of light was coming insanely fast, and yet from his many closed eyes and chaotic energies around him, he was actually watching and following it! He folded his four hands into fists as dense destructive energies permeated through him, moving as he directly aimed to strike at the sharpest point of the coming streak that was the Guardian of Blood.","Baleful energies of Aether rumbled as they followed commands, wrapping around Noah’s arms as they went on to meet the dreadful streak of light.","BOOOOOOOOOM!!!","A spark, an explosion of ultimate proportions was ignited as space shattered and collapsed the moment the two forces met!","Boom! Boom!","Two separate mini-explosions resounded as the Guardian of Blood and Noah smashed into the complete opposite ends of the Inheritance Grounds that were miles wide. The Guardian of Blood felt strong vibrations carry from his spear and into his body as he felt chaotic energies run through him, while Noah’s four hands were shredded as bony and fleshy protrusions that were healing at a speed visible to the n.a.k.e.d eye could be seen.","The locations they landed in exploded out as they moved towards each other once more.","\"Haha!\"","Joyful booming laughter was released from the monstrous form that Noah took as he valiantly rose into the skies and changed positions with a simple flap of his four wings. Energies of baleful Aether continued to gather and disperse around the wings and all over his body as he continued to move. He was only moving speedily, but he felt like he was teleporting as a single flap would fold the space around him and he would instantly appear at the next location!","BOOM!","Another collision occurred in the wide Inheritance Grounds of the Blood Progenitor as a battle of ridiculous proportions unfolded."]},{"number":311,"title":"Chapter 311: Chapter 310 - Breathtaking","paragraphs":["Clashes that shattered space continued to occur as two aurora colored streaks of light clashed against one another!","The Guardian of Blood continued to receive huge shocks as destructive energies spread out to cover his body with every clash, destabilizing the crystallized blood acting as a valiant armor.","Noah’s body always came out mangled and injured as he tested the brute strength and healing capabilities of this monstrous body that was the combination of a Lesser Cthulhu and an Arch Demon Lord. He shook his arms as he watched mangled muscles and bones fall off and new ones take their place, nodding his head as he was finally appeased, this time stretching one of his arms out as he called forth a weapon that would provide even more ridiculous boosts.","[Trident of the Sea] :: A pinnacle treasure in the sea that allows its user to remain unrivaled against all enemies. Attack and Defensive capabilities are quintupled while equipped. Usable abilities include Heart Piercer, Plasma Beam, Command of the Sea, Loved by Water, and Spatial Lock.","The Trident of The Sea appeared between his outstretched hand, being the size of a toothpick compared to the gigantic 30 meters that his monstrous body was. Yet, one had to know that this was a Supreme Treasure!","RUMBLE!","Essence flowed into the Trident of the Sea endlessly as it began to expand and increase in size, growing more and more expansive until it fit in Noah’s large hand. He grasped the trident tightly as the surrounding particles of blood trembled, a smile appearing on his face as he recalled his high school lessons about blood, and how a large percentage of blood plasma was water.","The weapon he now held in his hand ruled anything to do with the water element, and the opponent in front of him...this being made of blood from every nook and cranny...was just asking for a beating!","The Lakes of Blood in the Inheritance Grounds trembled at the appearance of the enormous Trident of the Sea, the Guardian of Blood feeling an oppressive feeling as it felt constrictions begin to appear in the surroundings.","RUMBLE!","A radiant red light that seemed to defy anything that stood against the Guardian of Blood erupted from its body as it broke past the newly set up inscriptions, numerous runic markings freely rotating around its valiant red armor as it streaked across the skies once more.","Noah’s monstrous body angled the Trident of the Sea forward, releasing his grasp on the now large weapon as destructive energies of Aether wrapped around it. The trident slowly began to rotate between his grasp, getting faster and faster as it seemed to call forth all the destructive energies around Noah’s body the more that it spun!","The three pointed end of the terrible Supreme Treasure began to tremble with destructive energies and red and purple mixed in, collecting an obscene amount of essence as Noah moved forth with the Trident of the Sea to clash against the fearsome Guardian of Blood.","ZIING!","Their two figures seemed to pass through one another as Noah’s large body came to halt in mid-air, his entire figure trembling as unstable energies seemed to be running amok all across his body, the unique energies of the Lesser Cthulhu and Arch Demon Lord clashing as numerous injuries began to appear.","The Guardian of Blood halted in midair a moment later, turning around to observe the monstrosity in front of it as its entire left arm beginning from the shoulder was cleanly cut through, falling towards the ground with an eruption of blood!","BOOM!","The wide arm shook the bloody earth as the Guardian of Blood looked at Noah, a small smile replacing its past expression of anger as it spoke slowly while lifting the heavy weapon it held with its remaining hand.","\"You...are truly an outrageous creature.\"","The words were filled with strength as the Guardian of Blood looked at this being, numerous thoughts overtaking it as grand possibilities of the future unfolded.","’Would the master’s legacy actually be rekindled once more?’","Hopes and dreams sputtered forth from the giant made of blood as the runic sigils continued to revolve speedily all over its body, preparing for a last attack as the spear it was holding on to vibrated with power.","Noah looked at the giant building up power as he breathed out slowly, placing even more mana into the two transformation skills he had cast as the instabilities caused by the class dwindled, destructive energies surrounding him once again as he pointed the dangerous trident towards its target. In another hand, a glorious purple light erupted as a sharp dagger was connected to an exquisitely made sheath!","...[Stop].","!!!","The lakes of blood on the ground below him and the droplets of blood thrown into the air from the collisions all came to a halt at this moment, as if speechlessly witnessing something tremendous which they could not disturb! The Guardian of Blood found his body being put in a terrifying mode of stasis where he could not move, his body being frozen in time!","...[Portals of Terror].","In the direction of the Guardian of Blood building up his power, a single portal ready to release horrid energies of destruction appeared. A millisecond later, another one appeared. And Another. And Another! They continued to appear until 18 portals ready to unleash tremendous destructive energies surrounded the impassive Guardian of Blood.","As if this was not enough, yet another whisper could be heard in the wind as Noah cast another skill, another one that directly interfered with the Guardian of Blood.","...[Envy the Mighty].","<strong>[Envy the Mighty] - When fighting someone stronger than themselves, the user can lower the abilities and stats of the enemy by one stage.</strong>","An ability from the Sin of Envy, the counterpart of the [Strength of the Weak] ability that had been giving him constant buffs because he was fighting against someone levels higher than him- was cast at this moment as the Guardian of Blood felt the vibrant essence that he could use reduced by a wide margin!","RUMBLE!","It looked towards this creature that was not just able to interfere with time, it even held abilities to weaken his enemies as he sensed the destructive power surrounding him from the many portals as a smile was actually plastered on its gigantic face.","It only heard one last whisper before everything crumbled down with the brilliant aurora of destructive lights that had been freed from the portals they were held in.","[Sever]!","ZIIING!","A ray of destructive aurora of colors erupted forth as it acted as the trigger, destructive energies exploding out magnificently as the defenses of a Soul Rank being that had been weakened to the utmost limit were shredded to pieces.","BOOOM!!!","A resounding tremor shook the wide Coliseum of the Inheritance Grounds as an explosion of stupendous proportions rocked the surrounding space. A wide void was created as the force had shattered and folden space within itself on impact, shards of crystallized blood being seen shooting out in multiple directions as the giant of tremendous proportion, the Guardian of Blood who towered more than 30 meters...met an unspeakably cruel end!"]},{"number":312,"title":"Chapter 312: Chapter 311 - A Drop of Blood!","paragraphs":["Noah glanced with a pounding heart towards the shattered pieces of the Guardian of Blood as he released the Arch Demon Lord Transformation. His body came down in size as destructive mixtures of energies still coiled around him, gradually fading away as he released the Lesser Cthulhu form as well.","He breathed out slowly as he felt an ache deep within him, feeling a numbing sensation of pain that wasn’t going away even as the destructive energies of the two forms he had taken went away. Noah glanced at his body that felt fine, yet he still felt an uncomfortable feeling inside as he heard the words of his home planet’s core.","[The combination of distinct powers put a strain on your still Saint Rank Origin. It should heal naturally soon, but it seems this power will be easier to use once your attributes reach the higher ranks.]","Noah nodded as he put aside the feeling of an injury he could not even see, turning his attention towards the shattered pieces of the Guardian of Blood that had stopped in the skies and began trembling as lines of blood began to weave from the many lakes covering the Inheritance Grounds.","A gorgeous red light shined as the body was stitched up together seamlessly, although this time much smaller as it stood the same height as Noah. The instant the face of the Guardian of Blood formed, one could see an expression of a being that was about to tear up from too many emotions.","The Guardian turned towards Noah’s direction as he bowed, this bow initiating the start of something wondrous as a brilliant red light went on to cover the expansive Coliseum!","This brilliant light had Noah at the center, his body actually feeling a pull from the ancient shrine looking structure that had remained in peace throughout their battle at the center of the Coliseum, the same structure where the Guardian of Blood had emerged from.","Various mechanisms were initiating as this Ancient Shrine that looked small and dilapidated began to rise from the lake of blood it was in as it became larger and larger. The moment Noah’s body was pulled near it, he could see a golden door in the middle of this risen shrine that snapped open.","The voice of the Guardian of Blood that was still bowing erupted in Noah’s ears at this moment.","\"When Master felt his life running out more than a thousand years ago, he left behind this Inheritance Ground where he placed all the techniques he had passed down over the years, as well as many bloodlines for future generations that might have been born in a lower status but had the strength to achieve great things.\"","The golden door on the red shrine opened wide as Noah let the light that hung onto him pull him in, coming face to face with a crimson interior that was styled simply.","There was a single book shelf in the corner with a few books that seemed like they could turn into dust at any moment, as well as a small table and chair for one to sit on.","The thing that grabbed the eyes of any who entered the room though, were the abundant rings and pouches that populated the table. They shone with a magnificent hue that let one know that only the finest treasures resided in these storage pouches and rings.","\"The last thing that Master did...was end his life early as he enacted a possibility for the future. He knew that with his death, the Vampyres would fall in status and grow weaker over time, and he wanted to pass down something even more treasured to him to a being that was as talented as he was, if not more. This was so that a strong protector could rise into heights even greater than his to oversee and protect the Vampyres.\"","These words brought Noah’s gaze to the only other thing in the crimson shrine, a simple styled coffin that had now been elevated from the ground, and was slowly opening in front of Noah’s eyes.","\"This was the reason he set up these Inheritance Grounds in this Ancient Blood World, and created a harsh test for a future Vampyre genius who was capable enough to take his mantle. Sadly, no such being appeared in the last 1000 years. That is...until your arrival.\"","The coffin in the shrine opened up to reveal a shocking light and an aura of ancientness something brilliant seemed to be contained within. Noah had to blink several times as the outline of the extremely brilliant object appeared in front of him, and it shocked him with the oppressive air and domineering presence it was letting out!","This was because what had floated from the simple styled coffin...was a golden-red drop of blood!","\"The talented Vampyres that clear the first level until the fifth level will receive an assortment of different quality Bloodlines depending on which level they clear, but the one to pass Master’s requirements and be able to pass the last stage...shall receive on their shoulders the full legacy that he left behind.\"","The shimmering golden-red drop of blood began to flow towards Noah as the Guardian of Blood continued to release shocking words!","\"The first of the rewards that comes with this Legacy is the Origin Blood of the Progenitor himself, granting the one that accepts it the reviving Bloodline of the Progenitor himself! Accepting this Origin Blood though...also means you accept the wishes that master left behind, and for you to bear all the responsibilities for the future of the Vampyre Race!\"","Resounding words rang out in Noah’s ears as the shimmering drop of blood flowed in front of him, seemingly waiting for his reply as floated majestically.","Noah’s face hardened as he looked at this unforeseen chance in front of him, nodding his head as he let out words of affirmation!","\"I accept!\"","RUMBLE!","The moment his words were released, the drop of blood flew into him as it pierced through his chest and struck his heart a millisecond later, seemingly impatient to get started.","THUMP!","Noah clutched his chest as the essence within his body suddenly became disordered, his figure dropping as he fell to the floor of the shrine in extreme pain!","THUMP!","\"AAAAHH!\"","This pain was unlike anything he had ever experienced before, his body undergoing enormous changes as his now bulging eyes observed his muscles spasming as his bones creaked, veins and arteries enlarging at a visible rate as the first stage of fusing with this tremendous drop of Origin Blood was...destruction!","SPLAT!","..."]},{"number":313,"title":"Chapter 313: Chapter 312 - Bloodline of the Vampyre Progenitor","paragraphs":["RUMBLE!","Across the vastness of space, four separate planets connected to each other in a unique way trembled as powerful quakes traveled from their cores until they affected their surface!","Even though the Planetary Cores did their best to maintain the powerful tremors, a small force still passed through as various lands across the four Worlds experienced microseisms that disrupted normal activity.","OOONG!","Immense amounts of essence were soon employed by the Planetary Cores as they acted within their defined limits as they focused on one particular blue planet, and this blue planet focused on its connection with a particular being experiencing something much grander than they anticipated.","The reason where a tremor had passed through each of the stars was because the being that they were connected to had come close to the very thing that would cause their death, but this close state of death was required for the metamorphosis about to occur!","Across the vastness of space, in the middle of the Light Expanse and Dark Expanse where the Ancient Blood World was located, deep in the covertly hidden Inheritance Grounds, a being was convulsing painfully on the floor of an aged shrine.","Viscous large amounts of blood, organs, and bones littered the floor in a gory mess as painful screams that could only be brought by if a serrated blade was constantly cutting through someone’s throat continued to be released.","The Guardian of Blood looked at this sight with a hardened gaze as he spoke out, not sure if his words could even be heard or understood by the convulsing mass of flesh that had all of its auditory, visual, and all other systems ruptured and were only now being slowly recreated.","\"The process of fusing with a bloodline is a particularly painful one, and even more so when it comes to something potent as the Origin Blood of the Progenitor. It does not just signify a bloodline, but something much grander. Push through the pain, and something beautiful will await you on the other side.\"","The words were soft and soothing, but were only met with gurgles of screams as Noah continued to experience pain unlike anything he had ever come across before!","If his eyes were still there, he would be weeping helplessly as he begged for this pain to end. The moment the drop of blood had entered and smashed into his heart, this grueling process had began as he found himself in unbearable pain that even halfway through, his broken hands had tried piercing into his chest to pull out the drop of blood that had entered.","The pain was this excruciating, making someone lose their own rationality as they only wanted it to come to an end! His barely reformed mass of muscles on his hands reached for his chest as they trembled, Noah using an unknown force of willpower to stop himself as he continued to tremble and spasm.","The process that was occurring was happening rapidly, and it was occurring on a cellular level as everything had undergone a process of destruction and reformation. The pain was most intense from his heart as it pumped a new quality of blood and life and let forth an outline of resplendent veins and arteries that were still visible even now.","The ruptures bones were just as painful, with Noah feeling the formation of new cells from his bone marrows as he clutched his nonexistent teeth and repeated to himself a single thought in his mind.","Endure!","This was the only thing repeating on his mind as he painfully went through this excruciating process, feeling everything painfully clear as new bones and muscles smoothly connected with the brand new venous and arterial systems of his body.","THUMP!","The heart that was smashed with the drop of blood had become crimson in color as it beat strongly, muscle, fascia, and fair skin all beginning to reappear as a distinct red hue caused his body to begin floating in the air.","THUMP!","A wave of brilliant red was now being released from his body every time his heart contracted and relaxed, the process occurring and leaving a few seconds in between before it occurred once more.","THUMP!","Noah’s head that now held even more brilliant overflowing dark air looked even more handsome, gaining a devilish quality unique to Vampyres as streaks of silver were visible on the mass of darkness overflowing from his head!","RUMBLE!","His eyes opened as they released an oppressive force outwards, his pupils filled with mysterious runic sigils that slowly dwindled as they took the form of a beastial emperor, etchings of a red star slowly receding from his eyes as they focused.","His n.a.k.e.d figure began coming back towards the ground as his fair legs touched the cold floor of the shrine, his attention being pulled to his hands as he brought them up to observe the utter paleness they now showed.","\"I welcome you to the World, my new Master.\"","The Guardian of Blood was kneeling right outside the shrine as he looked down with utter respect towards the n.a.k.e.d being in front of it, wild emotions barely hidden on its powerful face.","THUMP!","Noah closed his eyes briefly as he sensed the tremendous power which seemed to tell him it was not even at its full completion as he noticed a purple aura fairly visible on his body that was letting out a glorious crimson red from the overpowering Bloodline, prompting him to realize that his attributes had crossed from the Saint Rank and into the Void Rank the moment he obtained the transformation and obtained this Bloodline.","This Bloodline...he closed his eyes as he looked at a brief section of his stat panel and observed some new changes.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(4%)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor]","[Vitality: VOID]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: VOID]","He only observed the changed attributes and addition of a section that listed the Bloodline of the Vampyre Progenitor as he looked on impassively, much of his thoughts still recalling the immense pain he just went through as numerous memories that seemed to stem from this bloodline itself began to permeate through his mind.","The memories...were in the form of numerous abilities and skills that only the Vampyre Progenitor had access to!","They abundantly flowed into Noah’s mind as they were quickly isolated and shown on the stat panel, Noah continuing to stare blankly as his n.a.k.e.d figure magnificently stood on the shrine of the Ancient Blood World, still absorbing the tremendously unbelievable rewards that he had just received!"]},{"number":314,"title":"Chapter 314: Chapter 313 - All Mine!","paragraphs":["The first thing that Noah focused on was the memories of the Vampyre Progenitor Bloodline, his mental state still jumbled as many memories flowed into his brain, his stat panel clarifying everything he was seeing in a much simpler fashion.","His gaze focused on the description of the only thing present under Bloodline(s) as he clearly red a set of shocking words.","<strong>[Vampyre Progenitor](Awakening) :: The Bloodline of the Vampyre Progenitor has fused with your origin, slowly continuing to awaken to its full potential as time progresses. Bloodline boosts include: Ancient Being, Vampyre Ruler, Supernatural Beauty, Decelerated Aging,Blood Controller, Bloodline Affinity, Bloodline Bestowal, World Portal, All Element Resistance, Natural Blood Armor, Enhanced Charisma, Unnatural Healing, Unnatural Speed, Unnatural Strength, and Blood Gourmet</strong>","\"...\"","There were truly too many boosts associated with the Vampyre Progenitor as Noah only looked through the descriptions of a few while continuing to stabilize the memories flowing in.","<strong>[Ancient Being] :: From unknown origins, the Vampyre Progenitor is known as an Ancient, this in itself granting them a unique status. An Ancient is able to withstand the dredges of time far longer than most, being able to live for a few thousand years naturally. </strong>","<strong>[Vampyre Ruler] :: Holding the blood of the Progenitor, you can command the forces of Vampyres as if they are your own limbs.</strong>","<strong>[Blood Controller] :: The control of blood will never be as refined as in the hands of the Progenitor. You are able to control blood in a variety of ways, and will only know to what limits as time passes.</strong>","<strong>[Blood Gourmet] :: You become able to sense different qualities of blood and the wondrous unique taste they will bring to your palate, the only choice thereafter is whether you will devour. All abilities will be enhanced by half momentarily as you devour blood. </strong>","Noah picked out three that he was curious about their full effects, his mind shook at the description of [Ancient Being] as more and more memories rolled into his brain. His now starry eyes landed on the bowing Guardian of Blood as he chose to slowly assimilate the memories rushing in while stepping out of the Ancient Shrine.","His thoughts moved as he activated [Blood Controller], the nearby blood and mass of flesh that was sprawled on the floor shooting up and wrapping around him as it formed into a shining red cloak that covered his n.a.k.e.d body. He spoke to the bowing Guardian as his gaze looked across the wide Coliseum they stood in.","\"What exactly is this land we are in?\"","\"Master, this Inheritance Grounds is located deep beneath the Ancient Blood World, a world that the first Progenitor resided in when he was rising in power. It was at one point reaching the level of a Realm, but over the years it has fallen to the level of a Prime World.\"","Noah nodded his head as his figure elevated from the ground, going out of the shrine and shooting into the skies as the Guardian of Blood followed happily beside him. He shot high into the air until he broke through a certain layer, leaving the Inheritance Ground behind as he observed a whole new scene surrounding him.","All around, an air of desolation and ancientness flowed as he observed expansive landscapes filled with a reddish hue. Everywhere he looked, he could see numerous shining crystallites shining a brilliant red covering nearly everything, leaving only a few empty areas of barren landscapes where one could see vigorously powerful Vampyric Beasts scurrying around.","\"Over the millennia, the natural abundant essence of the world has given birth to varying levels of Vampyric Beasts that have populated all lands of this word, the only other thing coming out of it being these Blood Crystals that are filled with dense essence that makes it very easy for Vampyres to break through ranks.","Noah’s eyes shined as he looked at the expansive crystallite stones that covered almost every surface of the wide world he was looking at, his gaze also staying on the numerous Vampyric Beasts scurrying around as he ascended even higher.","His body that already felt weightless when moving because of [Child of Space] had been boosted to extreme levels with the Vampyre Progenitor Bloodline. He felt such abundant strength and speed that his body turned into a streak of red light as it soon crossed the stratosphere and shot even higher, breaking past a glimmering red barrier as he came to the vastness of space that was between the Light Expanse where he had been at all this time, and the Dark Expanse where he had a tremendous amount of questions about.","He looked around the starry space as he observed the remains of numerous shattered stars all around, the entire area seeming like a dead zone of planets as everywhere his gaze landed was just more asteroids and large landmasses stationed in space.","He looked below the Ancient Blood World he had just left as he was actually faced with a sight that only seemed to show more wreckage of dead planets, and not the world he just came from!","He smiled as his eyes shone a dense red color, the Ancient Blood World becoming visible to him again as he marveled at this feature it had of hiding itself from prying eyes.","\"The barrier that master used the last of his strength to erect still stands today, maintained by the world itself as it had been safely hidden from many powers that wish to obtain it.\"","Noah nodded his head as he was finishing the process of receiving the abundant memories, many things becoming extremely clear about the Vampyres as he looked at the Guardian of Blood that was respectfully standing behind him.","This was a being at the Soul Forging Realm, holding tremendous power that Noah had only been able to bring down by combining the use of many skills. A set of memories about this being were flowing through his mind as he spoke.","\"You are...connected to this world.\"","\"Yes, Master. Through the Progenitor’s wondrous genius and the willingness of the Ancient Blood World, I, an Automaton Creation was made to oversee the undertaking of the Inheritance Grounds, as well as the easier use of the World’s power that is heavily restricted by the Universal Laws.\"","...!","Shocking words were confirmed by the Guardian of Blood as Noah’s gaze peered through him deeply, his thoughts actually going to the white-haired girl called Sophia that he knew to be connected to some sort of unique was to his Homeworld’s core.","This was the same girl that the voice of the Planetary System came out of, the one that had opened the portal to the Beast World from a small isolated village, and the one still working behind the scenes now in his Homeworld as she managed things very few could imagine.","This Guardian of Blood in front of him was somewhat similar to Sophia, but much more unique as he was a powerhouse at the Soul Forging Realm. But to Noah, this was not all it signified. This creature was an Automaton Creation that was connected to the Ancient Blood World. This same creature was subservient to Noah, which meant that this entire hidden world that had downgraded to a Prime World from an even higher stage...would now be subservient to him!","A red light erupted from Noah’s eyes as he realized that the rewards for this venture were far more than what he imagined, this Bloodline he had looked at only being a portion of it. Among the other rewards were a number of Skills that the System was slowly connecting and classifying into those fitting into a skill tree or those that were in their own category, as well as the reward of a Prime World just waiting for him to form yet another connection to.","There were too many things to look forward to as he shot back down towards the Ancient Blood World, keen on starting multiple things right away!"]},{"number":315,"title":"Chapter 315: Chapter 314 - Schemes, Aspirations","paragraphs":["Across the vast space, on the 7th Celestial Star, an emergency meeting was underway as powerful figures gathered around a golden hall overflowing with splendor. The figures were shockingly known as Celestial Grandmasters, beings of a ridiculous level of power that even a single one would hold a tremendous sway wherever they appeared.","They were seated on extravagant seats as they surrounded a slowly revolving illusory circle that seemed to portray a great deal of information only to them, their eyes occasionally shining with streaks of gold as they nodded their heads every now and then. After a while, one of the Celestial Grandmasters spoke, addressing everyone in the golden hall.","\"As you all can see, even while moving to the greatest possible extent, the progression of events is still set, with the rise of this new Infernal Lord that will disrupt the balance we have worked hard to create on the horizon.\"","The words were calm and yet somber, many of the Celestial Grandmaster’s turning to observe him as one of them nodded and spoke.","\"Even though you took care of the Aberration in the First Hell, the cowards moving behind the scene could have brought about a new Aberration in any of the other Hells, allowing for things to move in this direction. But...it matters not.\"","Words filled with confidence erupted in the hall as the many figures dressed in a variety of different colored robes nodded. This was because they knew their own power, and how they were able to obtain the position they held now. They had tremendous confidence that even with enemies moving behind the scene...they would not be able to do anything major to them, and they will all be crushed utterly and completely, just like what they had done in the past.","\"But...we have become too entrenched in fate over this last millennium, making it extremely difficult for us to actively steer it lately.\"","A Grandmaster with an exemplary goatee spoke as he turned to look at the Grandmaster that Noah had come across not too long ago.","\"What do you propose, Vredral?\"","The gazes of the powerful figures in the golden hall turned towards the Grandmaster known as Vredral as he opened his mouth while in deep thought.","\"Just as a new Infernal Lord shall rise, we must foster the rise of our own champion that is not yet too affected by fate to make sure our edge over this coming war remains.\"","OOONG!","The Illusory Golden Circle rotating slowly in the golden hall they were in trembled at these words, smiling looks appearing on the faces of the Grandmasters as the one with the exemplary goatee spoke once more.","\"It seems like Fate is not too keen on that idea. So...we shall go through with it! How is the progress with our little War Princess going?\"","A Disciple from the 7th Celestial Star was mentioned as Vredral replied.","\"She is increasingly building up more Fate Lines, being able to withstand against an Aberration that was ready to break through into the peak of rank 4(Soul Forging Realm/Soul Rank) while she still holds Middle Rank 4(Void Realm) strength.\"","The Grandmasters were reminded of the shocking events that had taken place in the Realm of the First Hell recently, where a valiant Athena had stood against a being that was building up power that went past the Void Realm, but she withstood it and with the help of Incarnations and one well timed strike by a being that would soon join them as a disciple, and the Aberration was taken down!","\"Good, but it is not fast enough. We must accelerate her progression and allow her to take in even more Fate Lines rapidly, she will be one of our weapons for the coming war.\"","\"Yes. There are a few other Disciples across the other Celestial Stars who come close to her talent, but she is leading the pack for now.\"","Nods of agreement spread out as Vredral spoke once more.","\"We can prepare to open up the Celestial Realm once more for this generation of disciples. Athena should be able to advance speedily with the treasures contained within.\"","\"Right. It will take some time to get everything ready, but it shouldn’t be a problem. Vredral, we will leave her guidance to you for now. Keep us updated on her progress.\"","The Celestial Grandmaster, Vredral, nodded once more as the golden hall soon erupted into other discussions about a multitude of issues at hand!","Some dealt with intricate problems in the Light Expanse where they held control of, other issues were dealing with the Dark Expanse that they continued to struggle with to this day. It soon became a cacophony of strong auras as the discussions continued, the tide of fate still flowing as the rotating golden circle in the room continued to move steadily.","---","In the First Realm of Hell, the overpopulating Infernals continued to be reduced at an unbelievable rate as numerous powerful figures paved their way across the First Hell. At the forefront was a terrible Lich Emperor who released deathly energies and commanded an Undead Legion with numerous High Tiered Undead that razed any enemies they found to exhaustion.","The numerous powerful undead were protecting an assortment of humans, demons, and beasts as they went on to rapidly increase their power over the last few days.","Noah had left the Spiritual Land floating in the skies of this Infernal Realm, Kazuhiko and company being able to return into this resplendent floating landmass that was overflowing with essence to recuperate from the constant rushing droves of Infernals, while also enjoying colorful Medicinal Herbs and Fruits sprawled out all over the Spiritual Land.","At the central area of this huge paradisiacal landmass, enormous intricately built houses and skyscr.a.p.ers were abundant, taking the styles of Noah’s Homeworld, Beast World, and even the futuristic wonders of the Lost World that brought back some melancholic memories from the Calamities of the Sea.","But it was in this area where an abundant amount of Medicinal Fruits, Herbs, and Cores were contained as it acted as the base for these rapidly rising beings. Some spent too much time in the billowing hot springs and beds that seemed to be entirely made of soft feathers, but they all continued a cycle of training and resting as they continued non stop over the past few days.","Floating above the Spiritual Land at this moment was a particularly arrogant Emperor Penguin that moved its flippers towards the sleek black feathers above its head, its gaze watching the numerous Undead that continued to move day and night in this Infernal Realm.","The penguin was watching his own stat panel that showed how many Skill Points it had left after distributing many of them in a skill tree that heavily boosted his spatial abilities as he wondered just how many Skill Points his master was racking up with these Undead that were killing on his behalf.","He was looking at the efficacy of his Master as he was freely moving around doing dangerous things in a location far away from here, while still continuing to grow his power at an insane pace even faster than all of them.","He wanted to grow and increase his strength even faster! Even though he knew he would never be able to match his Master, he was still the first beast born in the Spiritual Land, still the one leading at the forefront!","RUMBLE!","A milky white aura covered his body as a golden light went on to cover it, the [Pride Embodiment] that went on to allow him to show great strength against the Infernals and push his power even higher being activated yet again as the penguin that had just entered the Saint Rank shot out like a missile from the Spiritual Land and went to join the Legion of Undead to take down even more Infernals.","Feelings of obtaining strength at a rapid speed were not only unique to this arrogant penguin as many of the Harbingers continued to struggle behind the scenes to at least keep up with the ever-expanding strength of a single person they looked up to!"]},{"number":316,"title":"Chapter 316: Chapter 315 - A Connection, <>","paragraphs":["In the Ancient Blood World, Noah was already deep beneath this hidden World’s inner core layer as he came face to face with a Planetary Core much larger than any that he had come across before.","This was the planetary core of a world that had downgraded from the stellar status of a Realm and had become a Prime World!","It rotated strongly in the underground space, an air of ancientness permeating as a voice very similar to the Guardian of Blood rang out.","[I had an agreement with the first Progenitor, and that agreement carries on through the years. What is it that you wish for?]","Noah’s gaze that was wandering all over the mystical aurora of lights surrounding this crimson core focused as he spoke out calmly, moving his hands towards the core as he did it.","\"I only wish for you to accept this connection.\"","His right palm landed on the brilliant core as a unique light released from his body and bathed it serenely, the process of forming yet another line of connection, but this time with a Prime World occurring!","[...]","The Ancient Blood World quietly released its protective barriers, letting the energy freely permeate through its origin as it let this new Progenitor do what he wished!","The Guardian of Blood standing far behind Noah at this time was an extension of this world, an Automaton Creation that moved according to a predetermined set of rules. It was a unique creature that allowed the Ancient Blood World to bypass the many Universal Laws laid down upon the planets, so when the light that Noah released intensified and the core of the ancient world began to realize the meaning of what this new Progenitor wanted to do, the process finished even faster as they connection was established in a much smoother fashion!","RUMBLE!","The overflowing and dense essence of the Prime World that was in no way inferior to the World of Cultivation or the Underworld began to permeate through the established connection between multiple worlds as its overbearing energy rushed down to the 4 worlds that were a level or two lower.","Noah’s Homeworld that had recently undergone a change from a Small World into a Middle World began experiencing changes once again as enormous essence rushed into in the form of feedback loops between the many High Tiered Worlds it was connected to, receiving an enormous amount of essence as its atmosphere began to change yet again!","Upgrades continued to occur left and right as in a short time span, yet another World had been attached to a connection that even those involved did not fully grasp yet.","---","Noah listened to the many thoughts of the Planetary Cores of multiple worlds as he understood the addition of this Prime World was something major. The benefits to the other Worlds would be immense, while his own benefits for coming into this Ancient Blood World’s Inheritance Grounds were far from over.","He had just looked at a few of the boosts given by this new bloodline that always made him feel like he was at the top of the world, but he still had the spectacular skills in the form of memories that the System had classified into categories to look into.","He moved away from the Planetary Core of the Ancient Blood World that had begun communicating with the many entities it was now connected to as he returned to the Inheritance Grounds, his gaze peering in his panel over the first set of skills that came with the Vampyre Progenitor Bloodline, and it was an Absolute Skill to observe first!","<strong><<Blood Progenitor>> Your very core holds a unique relationship to blood, granting you wondrous ways of utilizing it that many can only aspire to. Abilities Include Unique Origin, World Veil, Blood Sea, A Drop of Blood, Telepathy, Vampyrism, and Panacea.</strong>","<strong>[Unique Origin] :: Your extreme proficiency in blood has developed into a higher stage, allowing you to mimic the origin, shape, and aura of any being you have previously come across completely. Unless someone more proficient in blood comes across you, your origin will always be what you portray. </strong>","<strong>[World Veil] :: A great undertaking that is at the level of affecting an entire star. A veil is cast around a world that prevents the detection from any and all beings. Strict requirements must be met before a veil can be cast on any world.</strong>","<strong>[Blood Sea] :: Your body is able to turn into an expansive sea of blood, granting you a unique form that allows you to only ever take half of all physical damage while in this form. </strong>","<strong>[A Drop of Blood] :: From a drop of blood, you can begin anew. A part of your origin can be left behind as a drop of blood, allowing you to never truly die as a part of you can be safely hidden away. If used, the ability will require a period of 81 days before a new blood drop can be created. </strong>","...!","Noah had to come to a stop as he was reading the descriptions of the abilities of the Absolute Skill!","When he looked over [Unique Origin], he was happily surprised as it exactly fit what he wanted to obtain from the trip to the Underworld. His one worry when he would enter into the domain of the Celestials was whether the skills he held would be able to bypass their mysterious means if they took a deep look at him.","He didn’t know exactly what the abilities of the truly powerful Celestial Grandmasters were, but he expected there to be a thorough examination for any of those joining the ranks of Celestials.","This ability made it so that all of his worries were now wiped away, but the stupendous surprises of this trip did not stop there. The [World Veil] and [Blood Sea] were great enough as he continued to read on, but the ability that allowed him to leave a part of his origin behind in a drop of blood was shocking!","The ability brought him a tremendous sense of assurance, but also a reminder that he never wanted to put himself in a position that would force him into having to use the stupendous effects of this ability.","He gazed at the remaining three abilities he had yet to observe as he saw the effects of [Telepathy] allowed him to send and receive thoughts to those he was thinking of over any distance, [Vampyrism] bringing with it the ability to turn others into Vampyres, or even choose a lesser evolution and make them into brute Vampyric Beasts!","Lastly, [Panacea] was an ability that allowed him to release his blood as a supreme medicine, allowing even those on the brink of death to regain their full health and vigor. He could effectively become a machine that pumped out health potions if he wished!","These...were just the Absolute Skills that the System had taken and classified from the many memories Noah received after the Vampyre Progenitor Bloodline had fused with him. He had not even gone through the other abilities that were laid out in the form of a Skill Tree, making them abilities that he could upgrade and strengthen into an unknown stage far into the future!","It felt like he was receiving an overwhelming amount of skills and abilities all at once as his eyes moved on to the Skill Tree that was at Void Rank, with multiple abilities shining below it as it read- [Blood Lord]."]},{"number":317,"title":"Chapter 317: Chapter 316 - [Blood Lord], Harvesting Gains!","paragraphs":["Noah felt like he was being given gifts on top of gifts as he looked at the skills and abilities that came with obtaining the inheritance of the Vampyre Progenitor.","He wanted to finish by looking at the skills that were placed in the form of a skill tree by the System before he began to move out, as there were simply too many things he had to do, as well as wanting to obtain even more information from the Vampyre King back in the Underworld.","His gaze landed on the spectacularly shining set of words on the blue stat panel that began with [Blood Lord]!","<strong>[Blood Lord] (0/30):: A technique that only those with the purest forms of blood can use. It is Ancient Blood Magic that includes the abilities Dawn of the Blood Lord(0/5), Blood World(0/5), Drain Life(0/5), and Nightmarish Descent(0/5).</strong>","<strong>[Dawn of the Blood Lord](Active) :: A descent of a terrible red moon accompanies the Blood Lord, empowering them and their allies as long as they stand under its maddening crimson light. +50% to All Damage, +50% to All Element Resistance, +50% Attack, Casting, and Movement Speed, +50% Increased Area of Effect, +50% to Defense, -50% to All Enemy Elemental Resistance, and the Fear Effect is applied to all enemies.</strong>","<strong>[Blood World](Active) :: An isolated space that prevents peering gazes erupts around you, the actions taking place in this space are between you and the beings remaining in it.</strong>","<strong>[Drain Life](Passive):: Blood is closely connected to a being’s life force. A proficient manipulator of blood is able to layer all of their attacks with an attribute that will drain the life force of their enemies. +5% Lifesteal at all times. </strong>","<strong>[Nightmarish Descent](Active) :: Creatures of unholy origins are summoned at your call, latching onto your enemies as they activate blood magic and encase them in deadly coffins that skewer any poor souls contained inside. </strong>","Yet another set of powerful skills showed themselves to him as he felt like a collector who just continued to eat up way too many abilities. The Blood World was a skill he had already seen before from the hands of Prince Cassius, while the skills [Dawn of the Blood Lord], [Drain Life], and [Nightmarish Descent] were completely new to him with their wondrous abilities.","He would have to make time to test them later, as he was currently impatient to get started with the next set of steps after obtaining the huge boon that was the Ancient Blood World, and also go back to the Underworld for more information. The memories he had obtained from the Vampyre Progenitor Bloodline were about the strengths and techniques it pertained, there was still much mystery surrounding this figure that had passed away and what exactly occurred more than a thousand years ago to cause the death of a being that held a Bloodline such as this, which even held abilities similar to that of having a rebirth.","Noah looked at the subservient Guardian of Blood as he asked just to be sure before he began moving.","\"The memories that the first Progenitor gave you only pertained to the Inheritance Grounds and the Ancient Blood World?\"","\"Much of them yes, Master. Though I was given basic knowledge of the regions of the Universe and the beings that dwell in them.\"","Noah nodded as he waved his now pale hands in front of him, initiating one of his new skills, [World Portal], as he replied to the Guardian of Blood.","\"The enemy that caused his death?\"","\"No knowledge on that either, Master. The only warning that the first Progenitor left behind was...to be wary of the terrifying rising force calling themselves Celestials.\"","The rising force calling themselves Celestials? Noah thought about these words that would have been said more than a thousand years ago as he pondered.","’They’re not just a rising force anymore, are they?’","The skill he was casting completed as he was lost in his thoughts, an extravagantly wide red portal appearing in the Inheritance Grounds of the Ancient Blood World. As for the other location this portal connected to? It was Noah’s homeworld!","Through the ability given from his new Bloodline, [World Portal], he could do what the Planetary Systems had been doing every time a connection was established with other worlds- he could choose to establish a permanent gateway that required immense mana to initiate, and they would continue to be kept active by the essence they absorbed in the atmosphere!","’The boosts and skills are so ridiculous that I’ll have to spend quite some time just to understand how to best use them all.’","Noah continued to ponder as he moved through the wide red portal, the Guardian of Blood following close behind as this Soul Forging Realm individual entered a blue planet.","The constantly improving metropolis of the Blessed Empire appeared in front of their eyes as not too far away, Noah already felt the presence of Steel Mikhail, and the person he had sent a message to the moment the connection with the Ancient Blood World was finished.","The stunning girl with a head full of white hair and blue eyes smiled at Noah as the convoy of humans she brought with her had excited faces.","They only knew of the being in front of them from whispers and stories, never imagining they would meet the Number 1 Hunter from their world that had made so many things possible.","Steel Mikhail nodded at Noah, his gaze looking at him up and down as he wondered whether he was looking at the same person, while the white-haired Sophia smiled cutely and spoke, her gaze landing on the Guardian of Blood behind him as a white light briefly passed through her eyes.","\"It hasn’t even been all that long, Big Brother, and you’re already gifting us with another World.\"","Noah nodded with a smile at this unique being that was connected to the Planetary System in a different way than he was, being extremely similar to the Guardian of Blood as they almost felt like an extension of the World’s wills!","The group that came with Sophia and Steel Mikhail were some of the most powerful Hunters remaining in this world who continued to strengthen their power through dungeon diving.","They had come here today and with such a fast response simply because they were called by the upper echelons of their world, with the word they would be meeting the special being they knew as the highest-ranked Hunter, Noah!","A meeting with this being always proceeded with huge boosts of strength for all those involved as they were excited to find out exactly what stupendous gifts they would be receiving today. The words mentioned by the Guide thereafter only made them more excited as they looked towards this figure who was most definitely more handsome than what they were told.","Noah had gathered these powerful Hunters here, along with many more that were on their way to this location for the singular purpose of harvesting the great gains that were sprawled out all over the Ancient Blood World.","In that wide Prime World, numerous Blood Crystals that literally covered the lands were just waiting to be harvested, as well as the numerous Vampyric Beasts waiting to be taken down. Although, much of these resources could only be fully utilized by Vampyres, so Noah’s gaze turned to these excited humans as he prepared to test a few of his abilities as the Vampyre Progenitor!"]},{"number":318,"title":"Chapter 318: Chapter 317 - New Vampyres, A Messenger from the Dark Expanse","paragraphs":["\"Although it is going to be somewhat painful, I will give you guys a boost in power before you descend into a world with numerous resources just waiting to be harvested.\"","Noah looked at the force of hundreds of humans gathered in front of him as he spoke.","\"Are you all ready?\"","The replies he received were that of excited yells and enthusiasm as the Hunters could not wait to get started. He nodded as he cast [Vampyrism] on these humans who did not fully understand exactly what they had just enthusiastically agreed to!","From Noah’s fair right hand, numerous red lines erupted as they went on to pierce onto the bodies of the Hunters instantly, their faces rapidly changing as they buckled down to the ground and began convulsing.","Noah and Sophia were looking at this sight with interested eyes as Noah wanted to fully observe the effects of a Vampyre Progenitor turning beings into Vampyres, while Sophia was simply another entity entirely and was not even thinking along the same lines. Only the gruff Steel Mikhail was standing by the side with his usual unreadable expression as he watched the evolving situation.","If one were to watch from the side, they would observe Noah’s expression to be impassive as he observed the Hunters wriggling in pain on the ground, only a calculating look overtaking his face as he observed the continuing changes. Unknowingly, another effect of the Vampyre Progenitor Bloodline went to alter his mentality, although the changes were too little for one to notice at this time!","RUMBLE!","A red light permeated throughout the surroundings as the hunters underwent unbearable pain, but nothing like what Noah had gone through as he found their bodies were only going through changes that granted them the bloodline of Elite Vampyres.","This meant that anyone he chose to use [Vampyrism] on would skip the ranks of Normal Vampyres and become an Elite Vampyre right away!","He nodded his head after confirming this test, his aura already locked on the beings from the Beast World and Demon World that had also neared the location where he opened the portal connecting to the Ancient Blood World.","The Hunters in front of Noah began getting up after a few minutes, some still terrified of the pain they went through as they moved their bodies and began to feel the abundant strength overflowing within. Most had directly broken through ranks the moment their change finished, finding a sense of power they never thought to be possible permeating through their body. They looked towards the Strongest Hunter with a feeling of apprehension and familiarity as they felt like he had become someone they could never even think to go against, the aura that Noah released currently putting him at an unreachable position in their eyes!","What followed thereafter was something ridiculous as Noah used an abundant amount of mana and cast [Vampyrism] multiple times on the beings from the Beast and Demon World who had managed to get here in time, before the many newly turned Vampyres were introduced to the Ancient Blood World.","When it came to those in higher positions of power like Steel Mikhail, Noah added another ability on top of it as he also used [Bloodline Bestowal], another ability directly from the Bloodline of the Vampyre Progenitor, to bestow the bloodline of a Pureblood Vampyre.","From the Ancient Shrine where he found numerous storage rings and pouches, an abundant amount of refined Blood Crystals and numerous Bloodlines that the Guardian of Blood had been left with to continue conducting the trials of the Inheritance Grounds were all in his possession.","He was now the Vampyre Progenitor, making there be no need for an Inheritance Ground as he could personally turn beings into Vampyres and bestow Bloodlines as he wished!","The process took slightly more time for anything higher than the Elite Tier, but a brand new Steel Mikhail became the first Harbinger to obtain the Bloodline of a Pureblood Vampyre as his large figure became even more refined and he gained a devilish handsomeness!","Noah continued to play around with the newly found abilities of the Vampyre Progenitor as he initiated the process of using the abundant resources on the Ancient Blood World. In the coming days, more and more forces from the Beast World and Demon World would join in, along with the newly included beings of the Icebound World that had not even fully begun communicating with the other four worlds. The Guardian of Blood would act in Noah’s place for the newcomers as many of the treasures and bloodlines left behind in the Inheritance Grounds would be freely used up in the coming months.","There were many moving parts and numerous figures involved in this process that would take quite some time, but while Noah was supposed to be undergoing a trial to prove himself to the Vampyres of the Underworld, he entered the Inheritance Grounds and took for himself the ultimate inheritance left behind by the Vampyre Progenitor. He then began using the expansive abilities of this fearsome bloodline as he covertly began to create a force of new Vampyres in a distant world, moving with extreme efficiency as he already began the process of using the resources of an entire world that he had gained while he was simply supposed to be undergoing a trial!","It would be out of the wildest dreams for the Vampyres of the Underworld to imagine, as they were about to have their hands full from the return of shocking commands. The Vampyre King had sent word to their forces in the Dark Expanse the moment that Noah entered the portal that led to the Ancient Blood World, letting them know of the recent events and asking for guidance on how to move forward.","What came out as a result was something they did not expect as within the grand Vampyre Council Hall where many powerful figures were still discussing, a dark portal began to form that took the attention of all those in the hall.","The Vampyre King looked on in shock as he quickly enacted a wide Blood World that fully covered the Council Hall, looking towards this expanding dark portal where a stunning figure began to materialize out of with a glimmer of red light.","The eyes of the Vampyre King focused as the usual smile he had was wiped away, letting out a calm voice as if he was talking to someone of the same level, or even possibly higher!","\"You know it is risky for someone who is drenched with the aura of the Dark Expanse to enter into the Light Expanse right away. Are you trying to reveal our position this quickly, my dear Elena?\"","His voice was directed to the woman that had just materialized from a disappearing portal, a woman that held a figure so curvaceous and deadly that it would make many men drool!","Gorgeous silver hair fell down to her shoulders as she looked at the Vampyre King with a light smile that caused the Vampyres in the Council Hall to look down to their feet in respect. They knew the identity of this being that had just appeared, a being they considered to be even more fearsome than the Vampyre King they were serving under all this time!","\"Little brother, you sent such a shocking message that the Alliance couldn’t just send back simple words. If it wasn’t required of me to be here, I would not have come.\"","Shocking words were released as the woman holding a similar status to the Vampyre King that Noah had talked to appeared, and she was a being that had just arrived from the Dark Expanse!","The Vampyre King that was ruling the forces of the Pureblood Vampyres in the Underworld looked at his big sister thoughtfully as he clapped his hands, sending a signal for the many Vampyre Elders to clear the room as he spoke.","\"Are they ready to enact a big move against the Celestials?\"","A wide smile which could be the downfall of entire countries appeared on the Royal Vampyre Elena as she strolled towards the Vampyre King.","\"Oh little brother, you don’t know just how important the news of this human that has a straight path into the 7th Celestial Star is.\"","An interested smile appeared on her face as she looked around the wide Council Hall, only noticing a single red portal, her nephew that was looking towards her with a shocked expression, and the Vampyre King she continued to refer to as little brother.","\"Where is the important being in question, little Adrian?\"","An eerie silence filled the room as the Vampyre King, Adrian, let out a slight cough as he gazed at the red portal, causing the expression of Elena to change as her face turned dark.","\"You sent such an important figure into the Inheritance Grounds?\"","\"...It was to tie him directly to our side as we awaited for word from home. If you had been sharing all the important information with me, maybe I would have known his importance was even greater than what I anticipated. Do enlighten me though, why did those old fogeys send you?\"","Elena turned to her brother with a pitying expression as she spoke.","\"Even I didn’t know this information before I was sent here, it was something that those schemers at the top classified as top secret. You better hope that human comes back in one piece, otherwise the people that are much too tired of this unwinnable war will fry you for losing such an important piece.\"","She walked towards Prince Cassius as her soft hands ruffled his silver hair.","\"My little nephew, you did well with your recent venture. You should come back home soon, all those little princesses you left behind continue waiting for you to return.\"","The Vampyre Prince adopted a docile expression that was nothing like the regal air he had always shown, only being able to nod his head at this bountifully blessed aunt in front of him.","Elena strolled towards the bedazzled throne that the Vampyre King Adrian had been sitting on as she placed her curvaceous body down and crossed her legs, her gaze locking towards the red portal that led to the Inheritance Grounds as she awaited for this being that would play a major part in the ongoing war!"]},{"number":319,"title":"Chapter 319: Chapter 318 - Casting a Veil, The Return","paragraphs":["Noah knew that normally, the trial in the Inheritance Grounds would take Vampyres hours, if not days as they would choose to rest and recover their energies before beginning the next stage.","He had finished his run at the trial in less than an hour, and this was while clearing all 6 levels of the Inheritance, so he knew he had a lot of time before he needed to return to the Council Hall in the Underworld.","He oversaw the gradual introduction of his forces into the Ancient Blood World as the Guardian of Blood acted to protect the newly turned Vampyres if they came into contact with Vampyric Beasts that were too powerful.","Sophia continued her role as a Guide, leaving behind the protected village where she had sent Noah to the Beast World from months ago as she now acted as the representative of the Planetary Core to relay directions to the many forces at their disposal.","There was a wide array of beings from the multiple worlds, and Noah would not be able to look at and interpret all the intricacies of the connections and movements of the worlds he was connected to while also worrying about his own movements against the forces he was putting himself up against.","Sophia acted as the center point as she relayed the intentions of the Planetary System and allowed for a smooth transition of tasks and roles as the many pieces continued to move in order to create a well-oiled machine that would continue to produce powerhouses.","Many projects were initiated to begin in the newly connected Icebound World and Ancient Blood World, while another project that was in Noah’s Homeworld was seeing progress as the Atlanteans finished the construction of the first World Engine!","This was a grand achievement as they had been able to recreate a treasure which the Celestials deemed as something that went against the natural order and balance. The completion of this World Engine would allow for the displacement of a star, a drastic measure that would be used if their enemies ever tracked their coordinates and wished them harm.","The smooth progress of the project to create more World Engines reminded Noah of the supernatural Veil that was covering the Ancient Blood World, allowing it to hide amongst dead stars and escaping the sight of powerful beings for the past 1000 years.","The one who had enacted that Veil onto the Ancient Blood World was the Vampyre Progenitor... and he now held that same power as he recalled the description of one of the abilities he had just obtained.","<strong>[World Veil] :: A great undertaking that is at the level of affecting an entire star. A veil is cast around a world that prevents the detection from any and all beings. Strict requirements must be met before a veil can be cast on any world.</strong>","From the Absolute Skill <<Blood Progenitor>>, the spectacular ability shone with a brilliant hue on the stat panel as now planned to enact it. He teleported to the inner core of his Homeworld for the first time in a while as he observed the slowly rotating hexagonal prism that had become even larger, an enormous amount of essence now circulating through it as the world continued to upgrade to higher levels.","The description of the [World Veil] ability mentioned that strict requirement had to be met before this ability could be cast on an entire world. Those requirements were a being with enough essence to actually enact such a wide-ranging skill, with the second requirement being the willingness of the particular star they wanted to perform this ability on!","Noah met both of these requirements, but this also made him ponder what exactly was the level of power of the Vampyre Progenitor that would allow him to wield such immense mana, unlike him who had access to the reserves of actual planets.","His impassive gaze put these thoughts aside as he communicated with the Planetary System and cast the skill requiring an immense amount of mana, [World Veil].","RUMBLE!","A large amount of essence collected around Noah, before it began exploding outwards as it began to move in a circular direction with him at the center. What was expanding from him was a thin film that would not be noticeable by any of the figures currently on this world, as it rapidly spread across the deeper layers and broke through to the atmosphere, continuing upwards as it spent some time to wrap around the entire world.","If one were to be looking at the blue planet from a vantage point in the vastness of space, they would notice a barely distinct red and black film of light rapidly engulf the entire planet before it quickly faded away, the signs of abundant life it gave off nowhere to be seen as at this moment, one could only observe a collection of dead asteroids floating together around a much larger dead star.","The transformation was seamless and fast as an enormous veil was cast around an entire world, reducing the chances of anyone finding or targeting it through various means!","In the next few hours, Noah continued his extremely efficient movements as he moved across the Beast World, Demon World, and Icebound World while repeating similar things, the mana at his disposal allowing for a ridiculous level of actions.","He would go into the First Realm of Hell where the rest of the Harbingers were still training later, leaving them to continue enjoying the farming of Skill Points before he gave them the option of accepting the strength of the Vampyre Bloodlines!","Seeing that everything had begun moving in the right direction for their incursion into the Ancient Blood World, Noah returned to the Inheritance Grounds where any new Vampyres trying to undertake the trial by the forces of the Pureblood Vampyres in the Underworld would be sent, and neared the still floating red portal that had brought him into this world in the first place.","Beings like the Vampyre King were able to use skill passed down over time to create portals that only lead the Inheritance Grounds, so if such an action happened again in the future, whoever intruded into the Ancient Blood World would only enter into the Inheritance Grounds for their trial. The Guardian of Blood was instructed by Noah to continue this job for now as he did not want to alert the larger forces of Vampyres in the Underworld, and most likely an even bigger force that should be where they came from in the Dark Expanse.","To these Vampyres, nothing had changed with the Inheritance Grounds or Ancient Blood World. But behind the scenes, numerous beings had already begun moving across the wide Prime World as they began to harvest its abundant resources.","Noah stopped briefly as he cast another newly obtained ability, the [Unique Origin] that was under the <<Blood Progenitor>> Absolute Skill. A red light covered him as his aura mimicked a Pureblood Vampyre, the immense aura of the Vampyre Progenitor being hidden away as he wanted to observe the state of the Vampyres currently before deciding on whether to reveal himself.","Seeing that he missed nothing, Noah entered through the portal as brief darkness clouded his gaze, before brightness soon took over as he returned to the wide Vampyre Council Hall.","His observations were met with a new scene as in the wide hall, only three beings were left behind, none of the powerful Vampyre Elders anywhere in sight.","There was Prince Cassius that was standing with his father, the Vampyre King, along with the long legs of a curvaceous woman who looked to be in her prime sitting on the only bedazzled throne in the hall.","They noticed Noah’s return right away as Prince Cassius looked at Noah and noticed the changes in his demeanor, as well as the silver streaks permeated through his dark head of hair and the distinct devilish handsomeness that he only saw in himself. They also felt a strong resonance of blood that indicated Noah had become one of them, and a being that was a Pureblood Vampyre at that! Prince Cassius nodded with an expression that seemed to say ’as expected’, with his father looking at Noah with a deep gaze and then nodding as well, apparently not let down.","To them, it looked like Noah had made huge gains in the Inheritance Grounds, being able to obtain the bloodline of a Pureblood Vampyre as they sensed the abundant aura of blood that could barely be discernable in the eyes of the Vampyres.","Yet, the other person in the room, the Royal Vampyre Elena, had a drastic change in expression as her gaze went from a welcoming smile and into one of absolute shock!","Noah’s sharp gaze observed this minute difference of change on this new being he hadn’t seen before as he quickly processed something, a red light shining in his eyes as they landed on this woman who had somehow seen something that the other two beings in this wide hall did not notice.","He had gloriously returned to the Royal Castle of the Vampyres in the Underworld, an unexpected scene greeting him as he walked out of the red portal leading to the Ancient Blood World!"]},{"number":320,"title":"Chapter 320: Chapter 319 - Welcoming the New Progenitor!","paragraphs":["Unpercebtable to Prince Cassius and Vampyre King Adrian, a red light erupted from Noah’s eyes, and this single red light went on to bring an enormous sense of pressure on the powerful Royal Vampyre currently sitting on the throne!","A telepathic message was sent forward as Elena quickly changed her expression and tried to adopt a normal one, being the first to voice out her normal voice that held a slight trembling within.","\"Little brother, take the young prince and yourself out for a second while I talk with our...important guest.\"","\"Elena, you know that is not proper. You are in my domain now, I will at least be involved in the talks, no matter how important you make them out to-\"","The Vampyre King Adrian was voicing out with slight dissatisfaction when he turned towards his sister and saw an unexpected imploring gaze on her face.","\"Please, Brother. Just for a little while.\"","Brief silence permeated the room as the Vampyre King questioned just what exactly were the contents of the message from the Alliance as he sighed and snapped his fingers, Prince Cassius coming to and following him close behind as they left the Council Hall.","The Vampyre Prince turned towards Noah with an apologetic expression once more, sending a telepathic message towards him as they left.","\"I didn’t think everything would go towards such a direction. I’ll try to be a good host after these talks finish and get you accustomed to the body of a noble Vampyre that you just obtained.\"","Noah smiled and nodded towards the young prince as the doors closed behind him, only a single other person being left behind in this wide Council Hall as the smile was quickly wiped away from his face, his gaze landing on the Soul Forging Realm Royal Vampyre that had gone back to a trembling gaze the moment Noah focused on her!","RUMBLE!","Noah moved his essence as he cast forth a [Blood World], the entire Council Hall instantaneously being surrounded by a protective and secretive layer that nobody on the outside could peer through.","Noah’s gaze became impassive as he looked at the Vampyre that had inadvertently realized something.","\"How did you notice?\"","A cold voice came out from Noah as he addressed this Soul Rank being calmly while moving forward, the body of the curvaceous Vampyre shaking as she couldn’t find the words. There was a huge reason why this powerful being changed her expression the moment she looked closely at Noah, as she had noticed something that Prince Cassius and even her Brother had not been able to notice- and that was the complete and utter domination of blood that the being in front of her let out!","This was a shocking finding as it could only mean one thing, but it was such an outrageous and unbelievable idea that Elena did not fully believe it until a distinct red light passed through the being’s eyes as she felt her entire body locked in place, a message arriving in her mind telling her to send the other two beings away from this room.","This confirmed her shocking finding, as she quickly stood up from the bedazzled throne and kneeled towards the figure of Noah while voicing out with a meek voice.","\"This undeserving child greets Progenitor, and hopes you will forgive her insolence for not realizing and acting right away!\"","Yes! The Royal Vampyre from the Dark Expanse had come to the realization right away that somehow, unbelievably, the being in front of her had the aura of someone that she only knew from her bloodline memories and stories passed down in her clan. This being had the overpowering aura of the Progenitor!","Noah looked at the sight of this gorgeous woman kneeling towards him with an impassive gaze as he continued walking forward, the bloodline of the Progenitor affecting him more than he knew as he was slowly adopting the traits of a being that stood at the absolute peak of a race and had full control over them! The traits of the Ruler of Vampyres that were inlaid in the bloodline he had absorbed were slowly but surely coming out on the surface without him realizing it, a regal air accompanying him as he asked once more.","\"How did you know?\"","\"I- I am the first born of our generation in the Acheron lineage, being blessed with one of the purest Royal Bloodlines currently. The purerer our bloodlines, the closer we are to the Progenitor. This foolish child, Elena Acheron, seeks Progenitor’s forgiveness for almost revealing your identity.\"","A few memories were dredged up from Noah’s mind as he nodded, the words of the powerful Soul Forging Realm being in front of him not holding an ounce of lies as he confirmed she had only been able to see through his disguised state because of something unique about her. This was because he had used the ability [Unique Origin] to take on the aura and look of a Pureblood Vampyre that even the Vampyre King who held a Royal Bloodline did not notice.","The kneeling Elena looked up slowly as she continued.","\"Besides my purerer bloodline, the only other reason is because your awakening happened just recently, and your immense aura has not fully settled, making those slightly more sensitive like me to notice the greatness of the Progenitor. Please...\"","The curvaceous Elena pointed towards the throne in the wide hall while still kneeling, continuing to speak with a respectful tone towards this unbelievable being in front of her!","\"...please take a seat and relax Progenitor, put this undeserving child at ease.\"","Noah reached the position where the silver haired Vampyre with shocking features was kneeling as he used his right hand to lift her face upwards, turning her still shaking eyes towards him as he then released her chin and proceeded to comfortably sit on the huge throne that the Vampyre King had just been sitting on not too long ago.","\"You are someone from the Dark Expanse?\"","Noah asked calmly as he noticed besides the aura of a Royal Vampyre on this being called Elena, she held a distinct aura that he had never seen on anyone else before, and paired with the Vampyres who were connected to a force in the Dark Expanse, he quickly made this connection. It seemed like beings from the different regions held a distinct aura that could be easily discernible!","\"Yes, Progenitor. The Acheron Clan that manages the Vampyres in this Underworld sent me forth with commands for how the one who is about to have access to the 7th Celestial Star should move. Of course, your wishes and plans rise above all others, and I will faithfully follow whatever commands you have for me.\"","Elena replied as her silver hair danced below her shoulders, still kneeling as her gaze brought itself to stare upon the impassive face of her Progenitor.","Noah pondered in silence as he observed this figure in front of him, getting to the most important thing first, and that was information!","\"Rise. For now, let’s start with information. The Vampyres in this world...this Acheron Clan in the Dark Expanse...the Alliance...the Celestials, tell me everything.\"","Elena’s slender legs rose as her heart beat wildly, her immense strength at the Soul Forging Realm meaning nothing in front of this being that was the Progenitor of Vampyres. She calmed her beating heart as she began to reveal secrets very few had access to as fast as she could towards the Ruler that was now seated on a throne!"]},{"number":321,"title":"Chapter 321: Chapter 320 - Unfolding Secrets","paragraphs":["Beginning with the forces surrounding the Vampyres located in the Underworld- they were a force that those in the Dark Expanse had managed to squeeze through the eyes of the Celestials in the period of the last 1000 years as they grew themselves in name and power in the Light Expanse.","The Vampyres held a special relationship with a few powerful figures in the Dark Expanse through the powerful being that held the entire race on her shoulder, the Vampyre Progenitor.","With her death being one of the many results coming out from the war more than one thousand years ago, the Vampyres were more than willing to act as spies in enemy territory, becoming a stable force over the past hundred years as they came to prominence in the Underworld.","The Vampyres also fit this task perfectly as they held abilities that allowed for complete secrecy, the covert qualities of their techniques making them move unhindered for the past hundreds of years.","They had been able to smoothly monitor the grand moves that Celestials continued to make, and even occasionally take down Celestials as was recently done by the rash Prince Cassius!","They continued to be a force that relayed information to the forces of the Dark Expanse for all these years, until the recent developments caused by Prince Cassius grabbed the attention of the higher echelons of the Archeon Clan where the Pureblood Vampyres in the Underworld were from, which also meant they had grabbed the attention of a few figures in the Alliance that oversaw the Dark Expanse.","The Archeon Clan was the top most lineage of Vampyres descending down from one of the first children of the Vampyre Progenitor, with a few other clans taking different names existing, but the Archeon Clan always remained at the top in power and bloodlines.","They held significant power in the Dark Expanse and oversaw a few core operations for the war that continued to occur behind the scenes.","\"So what exactly did the Archeon Clan send you to do?\"","Noah stopped the Vampyre that held a fervent light in her eyes as she continued to speak, the silver-haired Vampyre still not being able to fully contain herself as she realized what the return of this figure in front of her truly meant.","Elena’s immaculate face tried its best to remain calm as she reached into her ample bosom and pulled out a small cylindrical container. It looked like a small ancient bottle with a wooden stopper that contained contents that would draw anyone’s eyes instantly!","In this small bottle, a sparkling black liquid that seemed to be moving by itself was present, a mystical light running through it as Noah observed it closely.","\"The Archeon Clan sent me here to provide the one becoming a Celestial Disciple with this treasure. It is...a unique poison obtained from the Letalis Expanse.\"","Noah observed the mysterious liquid as he couldn’t help but ask.","\"A poison? You all wanted to send me on an assassination mission?\"","\"No such thing, O Progenitor. This is a unique treasure that is aimed at something specifically on the 7th Celestial Star, but it is not for assassination.\"","Elena quickly clarified as she brought the bottle forward, leaving it on Noah’s hands as she continued.","\"Another result from the last full scale war that occurred over a thousand years ago were some very powerful beings imprisoned on the many Celestial Stars. This unique treasure that was sent with me for you to carry into the 7th Celestial Star...is something designed to release the shackles binding a particularly powerful figure imprisoned in that Celestial Star.\"","...!","Noah looked closely at the viscous starry liquid moving within the small bottle that only seemed ancient, but did not let out any other aura. Even his Planetary System did not know anything about it as no information could be found out.","\"A prison break?\"","He spoke to himself as he evaluated his own goals when he eventually stepped into the 7th Celestial Stars, and how exactly the movements of these beings from the Dark Expanse could come into play.","\"The message they told me to pass along was for you to simply pop the stopper on that bottle and release the liquid flowing within into the soil of the Celestial Star, and this treasure would do the rest.\"","Elena spoke respectfully as she observed the thoughtful expression on the Progenitor’s face, feeling her heartbeat increasing as his gaze landed on her again. The fearsome Progenitor in front of her put the small ancient bottle away with a wave of his hands as he continued.","\"Alright, this never ending war you continue to mention. The Alliance in the Dark Expanse and the Celestials in the Light Expanse. What exactly is the history behind this? A Celestial Grandmaster told me the Celestials have reigned over the last thousands of years bringing prosperity and peace over the Light Expanse, while also calling the Alliance overlooking the Dark Expanse to be an unstable collection of stars that sow chaos and disorder. What version of the story will you tell me?\"","Noah asked this Soul Rank being in front of him languidly as he called for more information on the Celestials, and for the exact reason of the apparently ongoing war and conflicts that continued to occur between the Light Expanse and the Dark Expanse.","The only history he had with the Celestials was them almost killing him while they wiped out an entire world because of what they believed in, and he aimed his sword towards them because of this reason. He did not know of their real history or what they really stood for, the memories he obtained from the Celestial Disciple Drax only showing him more of their fearsome power as he continued to go down the path against them.","Elena’s fervent expression actually turned serious at the mention of the Celestials, her gaze becoming somber as she spoke.","\"The Celestials...were an organization that slowly rose up a few thousand years ago. They began expanding their forces across a few worlds at first, preaching a doctrine of Order and Balance as they garnered more forces and support through all means possible.\"","Her shimmering silver hair danced as her voice became stronger.","\"Their rise was paved and built on countless wars and bloodshed under the name of their doctrine, destroying anything and anyone that stood against them as they were labeled heretics and beings that sought to cause chaos and disorder. What made the Celestials even more fearsome was their unbelievable proficiency in the Law of Fate, a Supreme Law that has allowed them to remain unrivaled until now!\"","A grand and shocking story weaved itself out from the red lips of the curvaceous Royal Vampyre as the secrecy covering the Celestials was slowly torn through.","\"The number of beings that have died under the hands of the Celestials over the years, the number of stars that have been destroyed by their deadly weapons...is uncountable.\"","Noah’s entire attention was focused on this silver-haired Vampyre as a picture was slowly being built about the beings that always shone with an ill.u.s.trious golden light, the beings that stood for Order and Balance- the Celestials!"]},{"number":322,"title":"Chapter 322: Chapter 321 - The Celestials, The War of the Righteous!","paragraphs":["The Celestials were beings of immense strength who quickly rose to power by relying on the mysterious Supreme Law of Fate. It was an extremely abstruse law that very few beings could master, and yet the Celestials held numerous techniques that could manipulate the Law of Fate as if it was their own two limbs.","Through the fearsome power given by their domination of the Law of Fate, they rapidly expanded their influence across multiple worlds in the Light Expanse, continuing to dominate many forces over the years until it all led to the culmination of a huge war more than one thousand years ago!","This long war was later known as The War of the Righteous, where two sides with their own strong beliefs clashed in large scale combat that colored the stars red and created thousands of dead planets. It occurred over decades as the death toll rose to the billions just for those involved in the war.","The Celestials that were close to fully expanding their power over the Light Expanse fully clashed against the newly allied forces in the Dark Expanse that called themselves the Alliance.","The Alliance saw the numerous atrocities that the Celestials continued to commit under the banner of Order and Balance as a few powerful figures chose not to stand on the sidelines and finally act, coming together and joining hands against this mysterious force. They banded together as they could already foresee that this force wanted to completely wrap everything in their palm of their hands, and they were destroying anything that stood in their way in order to achieve it!","The Vampyre Progenitor was among these powerful beings that chose to stand against the Celestials and participated in the War of the Righteous, her power matching even the most powerful Celestial Grandmasters as the battle came to a brief impasse with her intrusion.","Alas, it was too late.","The power that the Celestials wielded had grown too much, utterly dominating the battlefield with their unique uses of the Law of Fate as they besieged hidden locations of the Alliance with precision and seemed to always know the movements of their enemies even before they acted.","The Alliance was utterly and completely outclassed as the Celestials went on a crusade of Order and Balance, continuing until their forces completely dominated the entirety of the Light Expanse, pushing many opposing forces into the Dark Expanse as they retreated from their own homes.","The War of the Righteous raged on for tens of years, multiple figures eventually meeting their True Deaths as even the Vampyre Progenitor was among them! Some of her scattered forces of Vampyres surrendered to the Celestials, choosing to occupy a small land in the Underworld as they recuperated from their defeat and losing their Progenitor while living under the rule of the ones that contributed to her death. The other scattered Vampyre Clans ended up running into the Dark Expanse as they rebuilt their homes and licked their wounds. Other powerful beings at the level of the Vampyre Progenitor were taken prisoners or killed as the conquest of the Celestials continued to rage on.","After the Celestials had taken over much of the forces in the Light Expanse, they stabilized their power as they now turned their attention towards the Dark Expanse with hungry eyes!","But this action...would be the one that finally stopped the Celestials on their tracks.","They raised a huge force as they prepared to finish off the forces of the Alliance for good and spread their power across the Dark Expanse as well, but it was at this moment that a horrendous power coming from a region they had not even eyed yet came forward!","From the Letalis Expanse, a terrible being that was only later termed as a Terror, a being at the pinnacle of the Ancient Races that dwelled in the Letalis Expanse came forward and called for an end to the unbelievably destructive war.","The Alliance that was weary with a tremendous number of losses agreed to stand down, but the Celestial Grandmasters that held full belief of their power under the Law of Fate moved forward with their aims, proposing to crush any that would choose to stand on their path.","It was this action...that went on to cause the first colossal losses for the Celestials, and eventually brought an end to the long War of the Righteous.","The moment they chose to continue on this path, aside from the Terror, horrible creatures that would later become known as the Infernals appeared en masse from Realms of Hell that were never before seen as they rained down destruction!","The being from the Letalis Expanse that they ignored the words of- this single being was enraged at the continuation of the unneeded war and acted against the huge army of the Celestials with the terrible creatures known as Infernals, utterly decimating the forces of the Celestials. This Ancient Being held power never before seen as just the size of its body made those that were near look like ants, carrying out attacks that decimated all that stood against it.","Shock!","Awe!","Fear!","This single battle was the reason that this colossal being was given the name of a Terror, as what they brought to the battlefield was nothing but that! This was also the first time many beings came to know the power of the creatures known as the Infernals, especially the cruel Infernal Lords that absorbed the bodies of the defeated to strengthen themselves even more.","The Celestials faced losses they could have never foreseen in this battle as numerous Grandmasters fell along with hundreds of their powerful Interstellar Warsh.i.p.s.","The Infernals faced their own casualties as they receded into the hellish doorways they came from, while the Celestials looked forth as the Terror from the Letalis Expanse left their decimated forces with but a single message.","[Do not overstep your boundaries.]","The message applied to the Celestials that now held control over the Light Expanse, as well as the Allied forces that looked on in shock from the Dark Expanse!","This single being of the Ancient Race from the Letalis Expanse and the forces of the Infernals had brought an end to the War of the Righteous as the forces of Celestials pulled back and recuperated their losses.","Noah raised his head as the curvaceous Elena stopped briefly as she told the story, his mind going to the words of the Celestial Grandmaster who had called the Ancient Races cowards that only slumbered towards their destruction.","He did not understand the reason for that tone then, but he understood now!","A single being had decimated the forces of the Celestial until they could not advance any further!","’Ancient Races and a Terror, huh?’","He wondered about the [Ancient Being] title that he now held as the Vampyre Progenitor as Elena continued on.","\"The Celestials pulled back and consolidated their forces, but they did not stop pushing their aims these last one thousand years. They have continued to grow even stronger as their mastery over the Law of Fate increased. The Ancient Races in the Letalis Expanse have gone silent, while only the Infernals continue to hinder the movements of the Celestials. Constant skirmishes and battles have been held over these last one thousand years in the locations where gates of Hell reside as well as the border between the Light Expanse and Dark Expanse.\"","In the past one thousand years, the power of the Celestials had just continued to grow as wars at a much smaller scale continued to occur, the tide of victory once again beginning to shift to the side of the Celestials as they developed more fearsome strength with the advancements they continued to make with the Supreme Law of Fate.","Many thoughts were passing through Noah’s mind as he heard this story, his thoughts also going to the Infernals that had appeared alongside the Terror from the Letalis Expanse.","There were still clouds of mysteries about the Celestials, Infernals, and these beings from the Ancient Races that he had to slowly figure out as he continued to advance in power...and eventually become able to stand side by side with them in the future.","A smile appeared on Noah’s face that wasn’t the usual calm and enthusiastic smile for the future. The enraptured Elena that was observing the Vampyre Progenitor all this time saw a cold smile that seemed to be hungry for power, a smile of a being filled with confidence even after hearing about the ridiculous levels of strength that his enemies and those around them held!"]},{"number":323,"title":"Chapter 323: Chapter 322 - A Taste of Blood!","paragraphs":["The curvaceous Elena that had just finished relaying numerous secrets about powerful figures became enchanted with the cold smile of the Vampyre Progenitor, the blood within her coursing even faster as they observed the being that stood at the peak of all Vampyres.","This was just one of the huge effects for those that knew about their Progenitor, just the knowledge that the being holding the purest Vampyre Bloodline being in front of them making them feel extreme respect and reverence!","Elena found her red lips unexpectedly moving by themselves as she continued to be lost in thoughts, deviating from her story after she found the state of her Progenitor in thought.","\"This undeserving child wondered if you’ve had the chance to feed yet, O Progenitor. I know you just returned from the Inheritance Grounds now, and I don’t wish to be an even worse servant that hasn’t offered anything to you.\"","\"Oh?\"","Noah returned to the present as he heard the melodious words of the Royal Vampyre whose head shimmered with silver hair. He observed her long hands pull the many strands of her hair to one side as she showed her neck and leaned her head to the right, voicing out with a slightly shaking voice that seemed to hold a tinge of excitement for something that she considered the biggest honor!","\"This undeserving servant offers up her blood for the Progenitor to feed for the first time since Awakening...\"","THUMP!","Noah felt his new heart beat strongly as something that was a trait at the core of its being was presented in front of him. He found his body disappearing into red mist as he instantaneously reappeared in front of the fair woman with her neck turned to the side.","He had just been thinking about the mysteries of Celestials, Infernals, and the beings from the Letalis Expanse when just a few words from this Royal Vampyre had prompted such a strong reaction from the innate nature of the Vampyre Progenitor!","<strong>[Blood Gourmet] </strong>unconsciously activated as found a sweet smell wafting off the docile curvaceous figure in front of him.","<strong>[Blood Gourmet] :: You become able to sense different qualities of blood and the wondrous unique taste they will bring to your palate, the only choice thereafter is whether you will devour. All abilities will be enhanced by half momentarily as you devour blood. </strong>","The smell told his senses that the blood he could obtain from the figure in front of his eyes was of extreme quality, something that would be his first taste as a Vampyre that he would not be able to forget!","Noah felt his mouth open as shining fangs glimmered in the area fully covered by a [Blood World], his right hand holding on to the neck where he could now see numerous veins and arteries pumping, his left hand bringing the plump body of this Royal Vampyre closer as he felt his teeth sinking into her soft neck, the taste of something he would have never before imagined bursting in his mouth in a cacophony of wondrous taste!","\"Ahh...!\"","It was the scene of a devilishly handsome Vampyre sinking his teeth into a damsel, a scene that many would be shocked to see as it would forever remain a secret for the only two beings in the revolving Blood World!","’Blood...tastes this good?’","A terrifying thought was coursing through Noah’s mind as he bit further down, causing the powerful figure at the Soul Forging Realm to tremble as she felt like she was floating on cloud nine.","---","The Vampyre King Adrian and his Son were sitting in another location as they talked, their auras still locked in on the Council Hall not too far away from them where they couldn’t observe a single thing.","\"Father, from my experiences with Noah, he stands firmly against the Celestials and will be a great ally to have on our side. If you can...please make sure aunt doesn’t do anything bad to him.\"","Adrian looked at his son thoughtfully as he nodded. He knew the strength of his sister was even greater than his own, standing stably at the peak of Soul Forging Realm. If she wished to do anything to the newly advanced Pureblood Vampyre that was Noah, he would be helpless to fight back.","\"No need to worry. Her being here means the Archeon Clan treats this matter with great importance. They would not want to get on his bad side. You did well bringing such a character to us this time around.\"","The Vampyre King gave his son a proud gaze as he nodded, their talk continuing for another hour before they felt a portion of the Blood World opening, meaning they were being invited into the Council Room once more!","They passed through the small entrance made as it quickly closed behind them, their gazes landing on a calm Noah that was standing by the side, and the amorous Elena looking towards them in a commanding expression while not being able to hide her ecstatic smile.","\"Alright, the details of the mission have been discussed, with our important guest agreeing to go through with it. We’ll have to be good hosts in the next few days as we welcome him to our family and culture. Little Cassius, you can handle this job?\"","Elena turned towards the Prince who was already standing next to Noah and checking if he had been bullied or charmed in any way, nodding his head as he gestured for Noah to follow him.","The Vampyre King Adrian looked at his sister thoughtfully as he noticed her much bubblier expression, speaking towards her in a questioning tone.","\"Elena, you need to fill me in on the exact details of what is happening. I cannot lead an organization if I am kept in the dark about the important things occurring at this time.\"","His serious gaze was interrupted by the curvaceous Elena waving her hands dismissively as her gaze remained on the figures of Noah and Prince Cassius who were leaving the slowly dissolving Blood World.","She snapped her fingers as a thin layer of bloody mist surrounded her, covering up the distinct aura of a being from the Dark Expanse as her brother watched her figure become blurry as it went out towards the same direction as Noah and his son.","\"I’ll fill you in telepathically. I have to...observe our guest some more and make sure the mission is carried out with no issues.\"","The silver-haired beauty disappeared from the Council Hall, leaving behind only a befuddled Vampyre King who had noticed something else was occurring besides the surface layer that his sister was letting on.","A lone Vampyre King was left in the wide hall as a Prince led Noah outside of the castle, a Soul Forging Realm expert that knew the tremendous identity of this being following close behind in the shadows as her slender arms stroked her healed neck where powerful fangs that made electricity course through her body had just pierced."]},{"number":324,"title":"Chapter 324: Chapter 323 - Preparing to enter enemy territory","paragraphs":["The rest of the day in the territory of the Pureblood Vampyres in the Underworld was spent with the young Prince Cassius who introduced the culture of Vampyres and the delicacies that they enjoyed.","At a certain point, they returned to the wide dining hall where numerous sparklings foods were laid out, this time the chalices and adorned cups holding viscous red liquids being returned as Cassius offered Noah a drink.","\"This will be your first taste of something that you would only understand the wonders of as a Vampyre, go on.\"","The Prince was observing closely as he thought he was undertaking the job of feeding an important new addition to the clan for the first time, not knowing a gorgeous silver-haired beauty had already offered up blood of even greater quality not too long ago.","Noah sipped the blood rolling in the chalice as he compared the taste, observing the much lower quality as he unconsciously wanted the first one he had again.","\"Hmm good! Let’s continue.\"","Prince Cassius continued to act as a good host as the day went on, numerous things occurring behind the scenes as the Vampyre King Adrian made preparations while a being at the peak of Soul Rank was hidden in the shadows closely looking over her Progenitor that only she knew the identity of at this instant.","When Noah had finished feeding for the first time, Elena had collected herself as she lookedd to the shimmering red eyes that told her at the current time, it was to remain a secret that the blood of the Progenitor had awakened once more.","If a being such as this had faced destruction in the past, Noah wanted to continue playing in the shadows without knowledge of it spreading out too widely. Elena could only give a nod of affirmation as she collected herself and then passed the commands to the entering Vampyre King and Prince Cassius thereafter.","Time passed like this as Noah spent a few days in the Underworld, familiarizing himself with the many abilities that came with the Vampyre Progenitor as he learned more about the workings of the Celestials and the Alliance during the day, and conducted some more tests when night time came.","The first night, he received a telepathic message from the Royal Vampyre Elena that went along the lines of- ’Can this undeserving servant be of any use to the Progenitor?’","Noah did not pass up the opportunity to become more familiar with the body of the Blood Progenitor, surprising the Royal Vampyre who had expected other things to occur when he began asking her to conduct secret field battle tests which allowed Noah to come to some spectacular conclusions after the numerous tests throughout the next few days.","The first conclusions were regarding the boosts of Unnatural Strength, Speed, and Healing that came innately with the bloodline itself. Noah surprisingly found his strength and speed almost entering the realm of the Soul Rank while his body still held Void Rank attributes, the boosts from the bloodline as well as the passive trees from the Lesser Cthulhu and other abilities continuing to boost his power in ridiculous ways.","The other conclusions were regarding his healing, where he commanded Elena to let out a strong enough attack that was able to pierce his body that now held a [Natural Blood Armor] that provided enormous defenses, observing emotionlessly as his right hand fell to the floor, and then numerous lines of blood shot out from his shoulder as they reconnected the lost limb without a scratch in a matter of seconds!","There were too many wonders that came with his new body as he had only gotten more monstrous.","He gradually wrapped up his preparations on the third day as he made it known that he would soon be moving out, going through another round of discussions with the Vampyre King and a few knowledgeable Elders about the 7th Celestial Star he would soon enter, and go through even more thorough discussions with the completely subservient Elena at other times regarding the secretive information that very few could obtain in the Dark or Light Expanse.","He gradually expanded his horizons until the time came to leave with his tremendous gains on this trip to the Underworld, finding himself in the wide Council Hall once more as Elena gave numerous commands to the surrounding Vampyres.","\"Be more active with the spy networks and collect even the most unimportant information that deals with the Celestials. We need to know any possible moves they might be making in these next few weeks as our new brethren risks their life to enter one of their homes.\"","Confirmations rang throughout as the Vampyre King stood to the side shaking his head as his authority was ever so slightly pulled away by his sister. Elena turned to Prince Cassius as she spoke once more.","\"Little Nephew, you will be heading back to the Dark Expanse to lie low after killing those Celestial Disciples. You need to upgrade your strength and purify your blood even further, and there are also too many awaiting your return back home.\"","Prince Cassius nodded with a devilishly cold expression as he only cared about increasing his strength, and watching as Noah was about to jump into the jaws of enemy territory only made him seek faster growth of his own power.","\"Be careful not to be swept in by the Celestial’s doctrines, we don’t want you changing sides just a few months in.\"","The young prince let out some ominous words towards Noah as he left to prepare.","Noah only smiled at these words as he spoke out to the Vampyre King and Elena.","\"I’ll be taking my role as Crixus and begin to head towards the 7th Celestial Star. I’ll be sure to make contact if anything drastic occurs.\"","The two Royal Vampyres nodded with heavy expressions as they watched Noah disappear into particles of light, knowing that the Alliance had given him a dangerous mission that would result in the release of a powerful being held prisoner on the 7th Celestial Star!","The Vampyre King only wished success for the new brethren that had joined their ranks, while the Royal Vampyre Elena held a fervent light in her eyes as she watched the being only she knew as the Progenitor take on the most dangerous task. She turned to her little brother as she sent a telepathic message, knowing they would also be getting busy for the days to come.","Many thoughts and ideals were spreading across multiple beings as Noah’s intrusion in the Underworld came to an end, leaving while taking with him enormous rewards that very few even knew about!"]},{"number":325,"title":"Chapter 325: Chapter 324 - Gifting Bloodlines, Transformations","paragraphs":["When Noah disappeared from the territory of the Pureblood Vampyres in the Underworld, he rematerialized in the fiery skies of the First Hell just above the mystical Frozen Plateau Spiritual Land.","He spread his senses out as he observed a few people resting and recovering in the Spiritual Land, while others were in the heat of a fearsome battle far in the surroundings where the Spiritual Land was located.","The Undead legion had formed a circular defense line that blocked enemies from all sides, the tireless undead holding the fort against the constant rush of Infernals as every single death caused by them went on to give Noah more Skill Points.","He could observe the Emperor Penguin in the front lines flashing in and out as a silver light appeared and reappeared to reap the lives of numerous Infernals. Noah thought back to the history he had just found out about the Infernals, where he did not fully know of their origins, just that they had fully come into the spotlight over a thousand years ago during the War of the Righteous.","There were numerous mysteries to unravel with their appearance and the special existences in the Letalis Expanse known as Terrors, but he put this in the back of his mind as he focused on the next set of things he had to do.","His devilish figure sent a telepathic message to all the Harbingers of Sin, calling them back to the Spiritual Land briefly as he wanted to share the gains of the Ancient Blood World with them as well.","The Abhorred Lich Emperor controlling numerous High Tiered Bone Dragons, Blue Phoenixes, and Specters ascertained its Master’s overpowering presence as it roared out, becoming even more fervent with its command of the battle as the Saint and Transcendent Rank Harbingers pulled back briefly.","Everyone was collected in a small clearing on the Spiritual Land that held swaying white grass covered in snow, numerous farmlands holding resplendently glowing Medicinal Plants all around them as they observed Noah in shock once again.","Barbatos floated in the snowy skies as she used her hands to turn Noah’s face in multiple directions, playing with the silver streaks of hair on his head as she voiced out while shaking her head.","\"How are you going to beat me in looks as well, little fish?\"","Many of the beings in the Spiritual Land were shocked to find the man that looked to have undergone a makeover, his skin getting a slightly pale complexion as his eyes shone with a l.u.s.trously dense red light, the silver streaks of hair on his head extenuating the [Supernatural Beauty] even more as people could stare wide-eyed for hours.","\"Bloodlines?\"","Kazuhiko looked forward with shining eyes as he placed his hand on the right side of his face, gazing upwards as he laughed with excitement, turning towards Noah thereafter as an imploring gaze replaced it.","Noah laughed as he waved his hands, multiple l.u.s.trous beating hearts connected to numerous veins and arteries appearing in front of him. These were some of the many bloodlines still left behind in the storage rings and pouches located on the Ancient Shrine of the Inheritance Grounds of the Ancient Blood World, with Noah freely helping himself to them as numerous Pureblood Vampyre Bloodlines were displayed in front of him!","He could choose to use [Vampyrism] and simply turn any beings into Elite Vampyres, or simply use [Bloodline Bestowal] to grant them the level of bloodline he wished. His own Origin Blood would be used up in the future if he chose to synthesize more bloodlines, but there were currently more than enough left behind by the old Progenitor that he would not have to do this anytime soon.","The Harbingers of Sin looked at the shimmering treasures in front of them as they wondered exactly how much their power would be boosted, while Noah was looking forward to the new forms they would take after they withstood the tremendous pain that came with the bloodline fusion.","When he used [Vampyrism] on humans, they simply gained the strengths and qualities of the Vampyres, but when the same process was applied to Beasts and Demons, some adopted fearsome transformations as they gained abilities unique to them.","An example was how the first Pureblood Vampyre in Noah’s forces, Steel Mikhail, had simply become a more gorgeous and stronger version of himself as he now held the bloodline of a Pureblood Vampyre, but the beasts from the Beast World underwent transformations that made them even more fearsome. Noah looked forward to the transformations of the Calamities of the Sea and the beasts of the Spiritual Land as he flicked his fingers and sent forth the many bloodlines floating in front of him towards them.","\"Endure the pain and enjoy the rewards thereafter.\"","RUMBLE!","A large among of essence began to converge as he reminded them to endure the immense pain they were about to face, beginning to observe the minute changes occurring on every single one of them himself.","The demonic figure of Barbatos floated into the skies as a misty red light surrounded her body, her already curvaceous and deadly proportions being extenuated even more as bloody wings erupted from her back!","The miniaturized figure of the Kraken trembled as numerous red tattoos went on to cover its body, the runic sigils forming fearsome shapes as its long arms and tentacles gained fanged edges.","The Imperial Phoenix had transformed into a glorious bird of red and blues flames that were mixing smoothly to create an interesting contrast of energies that would burn anything to cinders.","\"RAA! RAA! RAA!\"","Battle cries were already resounding from the Emperor Penguin as numerous sigils spread across its body as well, its figure becoming slimmer. Its flat flippers shone with a cold light as they became knife-edge, the sleek black and white color over the body of the penguin becoming even more vibrant as numerous sigils went on to cover portions of his body.","Many of the beasts and demons had their own unique transformations depending on their initial compositions, with the Humans like Kazuhiko only gaining similar strands of silver hair like Noah, their bodies gaining tremendous strength while keeping much of their physiology the same.","Among the Harbingers, a Bloodthirsty Kraken had arisen! A fearsome Vampyric Phoenix floated in the skies with blue and red flames painting both sides of her body, as an Emperor Penguin became even more arrogant as it felt the numerous tattoos all over its body. Barbatos’s demonic figure gained unreal proportions as beautiful shining red wings held her in the air like a demonic queen!","An air of regality and nobleness spread out as Kazuhiko and the rest of them rose, shimmering eyes filled with power looking at Noah as they sensed an even deeper connection with him, their strengths heavily boosted once more as their bodies were honed even more for battle!"]},{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: Chapter 325 - A Mission, Crixus Returns!","paragraphs":["Noah affirmed the spectacular changes of the many beings around the snowy landscape of the Spiritual Land, every single one of them having gained something unique to them as their bodies pulsed with power.","Similar to how his bloodline came with memories about the innate skills of Vampyres, they would also receive memories about their innate abilities, albeit they would be of much lesser quality than the Absolute and Void Ranked Skills that Noah received from the Vampyre Progenitor Bloodline.","\"I’ll be stepping into the den of the Celestials soon, where things can go a multitude of ways depending on what fate has in store.\"","He spoke to the upgraded Harbingers in a serious tone as they gradually adapted to their new bodies. They looked towards him with complicated looks as they each carried the same set of emotions. To them, it felt like Noah would always pierce into the front lines and brave the most dangerous fights while they just enjoyed themselves and received rewards that he had worked hard to obtain later.","They felt stifled, and hated feeling like things just continued to be handed to them without them doing anything for it! They also wanted to do their part! They also wanted to go on dangerous missions where they could bring back unexpected and glorious loot to share with others!","The Emperor Penguin could not hold it in any longer as he voiced out.","\"Master, what can we do? What other worlds can we conquer?!\"","They knew they were weak, and that training in an area like this First Realm of Hell was something that would greatly boost their strength over time, but they also wanted to contribute!","Noah held a wide smile as he looked at the imploring gazes that wanted to do more than train day and night. A few thoughts crossed his mind as he thought of a certain peak Prime World he just left. A world filled with supernatural monsters all the way up to the Soul Forging Realm. A world with Pureblood Vampyres, Werewolves, Cyclops, and numerous more ridiculous creatures.","\"There is a world filled with monstrous creatures that scale up to the Soul Rank. Many of you are still at the Transcendent Rank with only a few at the Saint Rank, so this world would be dangerous but filled with opportunities for you all to advance.\"","Numerous red lights shone as they heard dangers of beings up to the Soul Rank, though smarter ones like Barbatos were looking at Noah with an apprehensive expression that seemed to say- ’Won’t we just die if we jump into that world?!’","Noah laughed as he squashed any fears down with his next set of words that also smacked them into shock once again.","\"You guys should be fine, there is a Soul Rank Royal Vampyre under my command who will take the lead and look after you all.\"","The Harbingers looked at him as they shook their heads depreciating, Noah himself using [Telepathy] as he sent a message to Elena that held shocking contents.","Besides the current mission of covertly observing and doc.u.menting all the movements of the Celestials in the areas where the Pureblood Vampyres had their eyes into, yet another task had been laid on her lap. That task...was the expansion of the forces of the Pureblood Vampyres in the Underworld!","The Royal Vampyre who had begun looking at stacks of paper and using her essence to read over an abundant amount of information in shining floating crystals accompanied by the Vampyre King received this message as her body shook, a radiant light coursing through her eyes as a smile appeared on her lips.","Her Progenitor had tasked her with a mission, and she would be receiving beings he held close to him for her to take care of and raise their strength while this mission was underway. Her long legs stood up straight as her shimmering silver hair danced wildly, boldly speaking out towards the Vampyre King looking up at her like she had a few nuts loose.","\"A mission has just been passed down. Our forces are to start the process of expanding our power over the Underworld soon. Send me the divisions that aren’t spread out across worlds as we prepare legions for battle here!\"","Elena’s strong voice filled with enthusiasm that wanted to please a being it respected greatly rang out, her little brother looking at her and shaking his head as he simply did not even know what was going on anymore.","\"Won’t this draw attention to us?\"","\"Every Prime World knows how the Pureblood Vampyres keep to themselves even though their power is greater than many of the forces in the Underworld. This will simply be seen as the rise of our force that had been lying in wait all this time, even going forward to remove any suspicions about us. Move little brother, we mustn’t delay.\"","\"...\"","Tides of change had begun once more, this time on a Prime World populated with beings at the Void and Soul Rank as Noah made plans to let newly upgraded Harbingers loose on the Underworld!","Even though he sent a message to Elena and told the Harbingers to still adhere to a set of principles not to hurt the innocent during this expansion, Noah inadvertently did not notice that his past mentality would have gone through many round about ways to justify his actions or find a specific group that could be considered evil for his forces to target. He could have simply put the Underworld’s forces under the banner of the Celestials in the Light Expanse and used that as a justification!","But his significantly changed body and mind that was being constantly affected by the awakening Blood Progenitor Bloodline did not even go through this roundabout way of thinking! He simply knew he and his forces needed to quickly increase their strength, and the conditions of the Underworld were perfect for it. Even though his forces would target those they considered to be evil or causing harm, Noah had still inadvertently begun a battle for conquest on a Prime World that was relatively balanced with only a few clashes over the years.","Thus...chaos was slowly beginning to propagate in some of the higher powers in the Light Expanse ever so slowly.","This chaos would only continue as Noah’s body that was now completely changed to the form of Crixus reappeared in the Cultivation Abode of the Profound Astral Sect he had left days ago.","His form this time was changed through the use of [Unique Origin], where his physical aspects and his own origin all portrayed that he was Crixus, the core disciple of the Profound Astral Sect, and that was all he was!","Nobody would be able to look past this ability stemming from the Absolute Skill of the Vampyre Progenitor as his aura had now fully settled with everything being contained.","The eyes of ’Crixus’ opened as he came out of what was supposed to be his last cultivation session to stabilize his Saint Realm before he set off, sending a message to his father as he relayed a singular sentence- I am ready!"]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: Chapter 326 - Towards the 7th Celestial Star","paragraphs":["A bustle of activities was underway at the Profound Astral Sect as the Elders and Sect Master prepared to send off one of their Core Disciples to join the forces of Celestials!","The powerful figures of the Profound Astral Sect knew their sway over the World of Cultivation would only increase the more connected they were to the Celestials, making this a grand occasion to look forward to.","The Shining Son of the Sect, William, found out about this news from an Elder a few days back as he felt a myriad of emotions when looking at the Crixus he knew and the one that had gradually changed as he made a breakthrough to the Saint Realm. A sense of defeat almost overcame him, but he reminded himself of his own genius as his heart grew firmer, promising himself to continue his cultivation journey no matter what was happening around him!","Crixus’s father, Elder Baldwin, was accompanied by Elder Spacewarp and the Sect Master as they used their aura to observe the exquisitely made interstellar ship that would be powered by numerous Void Realm Spirit Stones until their disciple made his way to the 7th Celestial Star.","\"The Spirit Stones will be enough to last the entire journey?\"","Elder Baldwin asked with a bit of concern as Elder Spacewarp laughed and replied.","\"Relax old man, Crixus will be fine. We almost emptied our vaults just getting this many Spirit Stones for the entire trip.\"","The surrounding Elders that were slowly gathering along with the Sect Master smiled as they looked far into the future, their gazes turning in one direction as they saw a determined face finally leave the cultivation abode and near the interstellar ship.","\"Sect Leader, Father, Elder Spacewarp.\"","Noah nodded to the frontmost figures as he showed off an expression of a man ready to take anything that would be thrown at him, spending the next few minutes receiving the goodwill of the surrounding Elders and more advice from his Father and Sect Master as the doors of the small Interstellar Ship opened for him.","\"Show off your genius in the Celestial Star and make the name of the Profound Astral Sect even more renowned!\"","The Sect Master palpating with power said a few last words as Noah nodded, the door of the ship closing behind him as the mechanisms in place initiated. He pulled out the Void Crystal that the Celestial Grandmaster left him with as the coordinates of the 7th Celestial Star were placed into the ship, numerous Spirit Stones beginning to burn as it lifted off the ground and began shooting off into the skies.","Hopeful gazes were left on the ground as a single disciple from the Profound Astral Sect went off, the effects of his journey towards the Celestial Star still unknown at this moment!","---","A small interstellar ship cruised across the vastness of space as the figure inside it sat down serenely in a meditative pose. Void Realm energy was constantly released from his body as he powered up the ship, taking a majority of the Void Rank Spirit Stones that the Profound Astral Sect had prepared as fuel as they knew their disciple to still be in the Saint Realm.","He had begun absorbing the Void Rank Spirit Stones that were just refined [Core]s with enormous amounts of essence, powering up his own realm as more than 2 days had passed since he had begun traversing through space towards the Celestial Star.","The purple Dagger of Time was slowly rotating in front of him as he used [Insight] to try and peer through any possibilities in this upcoming journey, but it felt like he was trying to see in an extremely dark tunnel that only occasionally had spurts of light. When it came to anything surrounding the Celestials, he couldn’t freely observe them!","This was especially so as the place he was entering this time was a planet that was filled with monstrous beings that were extremely proficient in the Supreme Law of Fate. One of the biggest things he wanted to obtain out of this venture was to gain more understanding of this abstruse law that seemed to evade everyone but the Celestials.","As for what else would occur after his entrance into the Celestial Star? All of this was left in the air as only a few possible paths were visible in his mind.","His joining of the Celestials had to be significant, where he wouldn’t just be any other Celestial Disciple like Drax who had most likely died in the Infernal Realm. In this venture he was undertaking right now...he had to rise through the ranks of these Celestials as he gained more and more access to their secrets! He saw this as one of the few ways he could continue to stand against them, with the smallest of possibilities to dismantle them from the inside!","A sharp red light pierced through his eyes as he continued to pass numerous stars, finding more and more vibrant stars with powerful lifeforms filling up in the direction he was going in.","This single Celestial Star seemed to be a center point of activity as the closer he got towards it, the more planets filled with abundant life he could see as the ship he was on continued forward speedily.","He confirmed that [Unique Origin] was working perfectly, stopping the usage of his own energy as he let the ship use the Void Rank Spirit Stones for fuel once again, observing the aura surrounding his body to be nothing more than a cultivator at the Saint Realm as he neared the 7th Celestial Star.","The first thing that he observed was a brilliant light!","This brilliant light expanded to cover his surroundings as he gradually became used to it, being able to see and sense an immensely large planet that was bigger than any he had previously come across continue to expand in front of him.","One could observe a layer of golden light wrapping around the entirety of the planet, a few vessels floating around this layer of light as some lights could be seen leaving and coming in. One could distinctly observe these lights to be vessels, while others were the figures of experts that shot out with speeds just as fast.","It looked like a resplendent hubbub of activity that also seemed quiet at the same time, a level of calmness spreading out from this star that seemed to portray absolute strength and confidence!","The Void Crystal he received began to shine with a golden light as it sensed the coordinates of the intended location, a brilliant planet full of splendor opening itself in front of Noah as he arrived at the 7th Celestial Star!"]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Chapter 327 - White Robed Celestial Disciple","paragraphs":["As Noah observed the behemoth of a planet in front of him, he unexpectedly did not find his heartbeat increasing nor did he feel any sense of nervousness. He looked at his fingers to see if he could find even a semblance of trembling, but he was extremely stable!","This was confidence! Utter and complete confidence in the abilities he had prepared in advance, and utter confidence in himself to be able to make the best out of this huge opportunity!","He rose as he came to full attention, nearing the 7th Celestial Star as the Void Crystal he held blinked even more rapidly, a reaction occurring from the shimmering star in front of him a ray of golden light shot out and struck the vessel he was on.","RUMBLE!","The numerous vessels surrounding the Celestial Star only stared at this newly appearing ship briefly before they returned to their own posts, only observing as the golden light that attached itself to this small ship pulled it towards the planet slowly until it smoothly passed the golden barrier that covered its entirety.","Noah continued to expand his senses as he observed everything around him, not being able to explain this golden light that attached itself to his small ship and was pulling him towards an unknown location on this star!","He pierced through the stratosphere and accelerated down even faster, soon piercing through the veil of clouds as a resplendent scene opened itself up in front of his eyes. Beyond the layer of clouds, he could see expansive and mystical landscapes that screamed power and serenity as he observed numerous mountains and valleys palpating with dense essence.","The overabundance of essence was not the only thing that one could feel, as the more time he spent in this Celestial Star, the more he could feel a convergence of another force he had come in contact with a few times before- fate!","It gave one an oppressive feeling that seemed to say whatever power you held, fate would always be above it!","Noah continued to let his aura explore the new world around him as on the mystical landscapes that held their own unique environments, he could see numerous unique structures that could be considered shrines and monasteries, along with expansive dome-shaped buildings that were spread out all around.","The golden light was pulling him ever so closer to an expansive rectangular building that held an expansive clearance where the ship he was on soon came to a stop, the golden light that was pulling him forward disappearing.","The clearance he had landed in was filled with happily swaying grass as a scene of peace and serenity showed itself, Noah expanding what should be his Saint Realm aura to observe the massive energy signatures of multiple beings in the paradisical clearing, as well the huge rectangular monastery that was at the center of this expansive clearing between tall mountains.","There was a wide rushing river not too far away from the position he was at, the waters extremely clear to observe as colorful fish could be seen floating within.","The door of his ship opened as Noah stepped out, letting his eyes land on this paradisiacal scene of majesty as he waved his hands and stored the ship into a separate space.","His wandering gaze met the auras he had sensed on this wide clearing, finding himself facing numerous figures dressed in white robes that were accompanied by a few powerful figures dressed in black robes. Many of the beings clad in white robes held auras that showed their strength at the Transcendent Realm, with a few standing stably at the Saint Realm!","The few dressed in black robes were all at the Void Realm, and Noah observed the figures of 2 beings encased in red robes that held a vibrant aura at the Soul Forging Realm!","Above all of these beings was a single old man that he had met once before, the same Celestial Grandmaster that had invited him to join the ranks of the Celestials not too long ago!","This Celestial Grandmaster was adorned in a golden robe as he was surrounded by the numerous white robed disciples, a few black robed disciples, and 2 that wore shining red robes all paying close attention to him. His gaze turned to the appearing Noah as he gave a light smile and spoke.","\"As foretold by fate, the last one to join us has arrived. Not too early, not too late. Just in time, and we can begin with the introductions.\"","His voice was clear as it resounded across the wide clearing they were in, many new faces turning to look at Noah as he came closer and bowed.","\"Grandmaster!\"","He called out as he judged the situation around him, seeing the faces of the numerous white robed disciples that were most likely in the same position as him look towards him with complacent gazes.","SNAP!","He saw the fingers of the old man snap as a white robe appeared in front of his eyes, along with a shining storage ring that held numerous things as he used his essence to bind the ring and wrap the robe around his body. The Celestial Grandmaster nodded as this action was complete, continuing.","\"The others have gotten here some time earlier and have thus become slightly more familiarized, but the core teachings will start now as you join us.\"","Noah nodded as he came forward, glancing at the other white robbed disciples that ranged from various races, with many of them mostly humans. He ignored the looks he was receiving for now as he moved closer and joined their ranks, the Celestial Grandmaster speaking once more.","\"For the basic introductions, all of the newly appearing Celestial Disciples will be distinguished by the white robes they wear, with those who distinguished themselves and rose in power being able to receive the black robes, and once you become full fledged Celestials, obtain the red robes.\"","\"As you have all noticed, the robes do not hold any sort of special defenses or power, and are simply there for distinction as you pave your way towards higher levels of power.\"","The Grandmaster spoke to the faces around him, many of them already knowing this information, with Noah being the only one receiving it now. The Grandmaster looked at the white robed disciples as he continued.","\"Many of you have been recruited across the vast stars because of the unique talents and skills you have shown, with some of you even personally chosen by me.\"","A few happy faces could be seen as this was mentioned, the speaker paying no heed as more information was divulged.","\"What I can tell you now is that we are honest and straightforward here, rewarding those that excel, while those that lag behind will gradually being forgotten in the dredges of time. We create champions that are able to stand for Order and Balance, but all of these champions begin at the same place you are all in, so have faith!\"","Many of the white robed disciples remained with their strong expressions as they heard these words, believing utmost in their genius that had managed to catch the eyes of the Celestials and have them invited to be here in the first place.","\"In this Celestial Star, you will learn a source of power that reigns the strongest, and you will learn how to properly utilize this power as even the genius feats you made before will all be left in the dust.\"","Vibrant gold light shone from the Grandmaster as he finished these words, waving his hands as the entire scenery around them changed, a brand new atmosphere appearing around them as they saw numerous golden rivers moving past them, with sparkling stars occupying their sights as it felt like they weren’t just standing on a mountainous clearance just now!","It was a magnificent scene of a fantastical environment where one could observe numerous rivers of gold passing around them with numerous stars hanging all around to complete the picture.","The Celestial Grandmaster clenched his fist as they observed a small golden river pulled towards him, his eyes sparkling with a grand light as his voice resounded once more.","\"We must start you off with a strong base and knowledge, so we shall start with something that is extremely simple, yet also the most complex. We will start by talking about Fate.\"","...!","A shimmering scene of wonder began playing itself out in front of Noah as he intruded on the 7th Celestial Star, receiving lessons the moment he arrived as it seemed they were just waiting for him!"]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: Chapter 328 - Fate 101","paragraphs":["Many would find themselves pondering, what exactly was fate?","Some call it destiny- a predetermined set of events that were bound to happen, but was that all it was?","\"This golden river in my hands, or the free-flowing river you were all observing before I changed the surroundings, they all have a predetermined reality that they have to follow.\"","The mythical river that the Celestial Grandmaster had plucked was struggling in his hands as it wanted to quickly find a way out.","\"But...what if it was possible to manipulate that reality? What if it was possible to manipulate fate?\"","Thin lines of light released from his body as they covered the struggling river, gradually causing it to come down as it became as docile as possible. No more struggles occurred as the river became a circular lake, standing still as the Grandmaster raised his hands up.","\"When one becomes proficient enough, manipulating and influencing these predetermined sets of realities becomes possible.\"","As he was speaking, his hands plucked out multiple golden flowing rivers around him as he turned them into docile lakes that serenely floated around him. It was at this moment though, that one could see the first river he had turned into a lake begin to tremble as it reformed back into a river.","\"But this brings us to the next point that all of you have to ingrain into your origins. Things will always go back to the natural state they were in, a natural state that is filled with randomness and disorder. From a calm lake into a surging river, the thing to be understood is that at the core of all of it- randomness, or disorder, will always increase.\"","The lake had reformed into a raging golden river that flowed around the Celestial, disrupting the nearby lakes as they soon began to tremble. The point that the Grandmaster seemed to be making was that once things returned to this state of disorder, they would go even further as they made the surrounding entities also fall into a similar state!","\"That is where the Celestials come in. We are students of Fate, and our goal is to make sure that the things which have been influenced and manipulated remain in that state of balance, that they remain ordered. This can be very hard to achieve for those who are not proficient in the Law of Fate.\"","He waved his hands again as numerous golden lines fell onto the trembling lakes that were about to return into rivers, their forms being stabilized once more as they remained still. But the single raging river fought against the thin golden lines as it remained wild, the raging waves around it actually increasing!","\"Though sometimes you will have a force that will simply not adhere to this influence of fate, and continues to fall into more and more randomness, bringing about even greater disorder. When you reach this stage...\"","The golden lines releasing from him turned a shade of red as they wrapped around the golden surging river, tightly binding it as destructive lights were released, the Celestial Disciples watching on in shock as the river was slowly strangled until it exploded into a steam of nothingness!","\"...you will learn to simply snuff this force out, and observe as everything around it more easily and permanently maintains Order.\"","Noah watched on with wide eyes at this principle as the numerous rivers which had been turned into lakes floated serenely around the Celestial Grandmaster, not a single one of them even showing a sign of changing back as even the slightest trembling could not be seen!","\"This world we are in, this galaxy, this universe- they are all in a constant state of randomness and disorder that only increases as time passes. Whatever is born will eventually die, no matter if it is a human, a fairie, demon, or even a star.\"","The voice of the Celestial Grandmaster was gradually becoming elevated as it seemed he was releasing a profound lecture that they would never come across again in their entire lifetimes.","\"We, the Celestials, have chosen to be the pioneers of fate that work every second to bring Order and Balance in this environment of constant and ever so increasing disorder!\"","His voice boomed out as it shook the origins of every listening disciple, even the ones that had already heard this speech before!","\"With our continued understanding and proficiency in the Supreme Law of Fate, we have been able to bring an order never before seen in this Light Expanse, a level of Order that has prevented the deaths of trillions of beings and millions of stars.\"","\"I know many of you come from different worlds where you may have heard different rumors and ideas about us on what we really stand for. Some of you may have a picture of us as simple tyrants who force our wills onto others. Some of you may look at our actions and call them vile or detestable, while some of you may think of us as merciful saints who have saved neighboring worlds and beings you know!\"","The gaze of the Celestial Grandmaster was moving across every single white robbed disciple as his voice reached a pitch that seemed to resonate with the mystical flowing atmosphere he had transferred all of them in.","\"Some of you may have lived in worlds where our name brought fear and silence, while some of you may have lived in stars where you looked up and were proud just to hear the name of Celestials be mentioned. You may think a great deal of things about Celestials, but you will only truly understand who we are and what we do after you have truly stepped onto the path to becoming a Celestial yourself!\"","His gaze landed on Noah as he felt a sense of gravity unlike anything he had come across before, the gaze of the Celestial Grandmaster shifting to a being next to him as he became able to breathe easy once more.","\"Once you become a true student of fate and you start asking yourself- what does fate have in store for me, and how can I influence it to bring about the most order in the lands around me- only then will you be able to understand just how paramount the task we Celestials have out in front of ourselves is.\"","A shimmering look occupied the aged face of the Grandmaster as he continued.","\"We are going against the natural flow of events, bringing and maintaining order in worlds that seek to constantly be more random! It is a task that you will only realize the immensity of in time...\"","\"So, our new recruits, pay attention as you begin to explore the workings of fate, and pay even closer attention to your own actions and the result they bring. To start you off on your journey, we shall start with the simple techniques that will allow you to condense the abstruse Law of Fate into your own bodies.\"","The Grandmaster waved his hands as numerous shining crystals appeared in front of every single White Robed Disciple.","\"This is the primary technique that will allow you condense Lines of Fate into your body, these Lines being your most supreme foundation as you will realize that ranks and levels become meaningless in your eyes, that if you have the talent in the Law of Fate and hold an insurmountable number of Fate Lines- not a single thing will be able to stand against you!\"","A shocking impact was left on the hearts of many of the new disciples as they reached out towards the sparkling Inheritance Stones, Noah reaching out for the one in front of him as numerous information entered his mind and a new skill became available to him.","Under the tab of unique skills, a golden shining skill by the name of {Fate’s Disciple} was showing itself in a spectacular fashion as he received the first lesson from the Celestials!"]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: Chapter 329 - Fate 101 (II)","paragraphs":["\"The first technique that we shall start with is the basis of all Celestials. It is the technique that allows us to condense lines of fate into our origins, and we can then use these Fate Lines to provide us abundant strength.\"","The Grandmaster continued to speak as numerous bouts of information was received by the White Robed Disciples from the floating Inheritance Stones. Noah already had this information simplified in front of him as he observed the details of the unique skill!","<strong>{Fate’s Disciple} :: A technique geared towards cultivating the Supreme Law of Fate. Grants the user the ability to inscribe the unique energy of fate into their origin in the form of Fate Lines. </strong>","The description was fairly simple, but Noah did not even think of activating it as he looked forward to the Celestial Grandmaster.","\"Many of you were chosen because of your own unique genius, and you will have a chance to prove yourselves in the next few days as you get to learn whether you are a true genius, or simply a star that shone slightly brighter than others.\"","\"I will remind you now that we reward those who exceed, while those who do not show talent almost always get left behind!\"","The gaze of the Celestial Grandmaster was impassive as he said this, waving his hands as multiple outlines of humanoid bodies appeared in front of them.","\"What do I mean when I say talent? Talent for the law of fate varies across beings, but the first prerequisite for a high talent in being able to comprehend this law is the utter and absolute mindset of high aspirations for yourself and the things you are connected to. You will come to find that most geniuses of fate are the ones that have numerous connections, their livelihood influencing the fates of many beings that they are connected to.\"","The three outlines of humanoid bodies in front of them glowed different shades of color. One was dark, another had a slight golden light, and the third was shining bright gold!","\"Take this first being for an example.\"","The Grandmaster pointed to the dark humanoid outline as he continued.","\"There is no talent in fate, while the next one has slight talent, and the third one has tremendous talent. But...!\"","RUMBLE!","Essence erupted as the outlines rapidly changed, showing a gradual passage of time as the outline that was dark became brighter and brighter, the second outline that held a slight gold light remained the same, while the third outline that shone brightly before became dimmer and dimmer.","\"...you will realize as time passes that those who are talented can become nothing, others simply remain the same, while those with no talent can rise to unimaginable heights. All of this will depend on a being’s aspiration, and what they do to actually act on their aspirations and influence the fates of numerous beings around them.\"","\"We, the Celestials, have grand aspirations! Aspirations that cover numerous planets, and we have actively acted on our aspirations over the years, granting us unbelievable power under the Law of Fate as we influence things at a scale never before imagined.\"","The Grandmaster waved his hands as the images of the humanoid outlines disappeared, his gaze landing on the many White Robed Disciples enraptured with his presentation.","\"Over the next few days, you will find out whether you already hold tremendous talent with numerous lines of fate converging towards you the moment you begin cultivating {Fate’s Disciple}, or if you will be a late bloomer who will struggle before exploding...or if you will simply be left behind.\"","POP!","They heard the sound of a bubble popping as the illusory world that the Grandmaster had summoned them to disappeared, finding themselves back on the paradisiacal clearing with numerous vegetations all around, the large building in the distance standing strong.","\"If you find yourselves stumbling, ask the Black Robed and Red Robed Celestials for help. I will be observing your progress closely.\"","The Celestial Grandmaster finished his words as he began disappearing into particles of light, the two Red Robed Celestials that let out an oppressive aura at the peak of Soul Forging Realm nodding their heads to the disciples and standing up as a cacophony of discussion erupted from all around.","Noah was rereading the description of the unique skill, {Fate’s Disciple}, as the many White Robed Disciples around him had split off into groups or had begun talking with the higher-ranked Black Robed Disciples.","One of the Red Robed Celestials observe Noah standing blankly by himself as he waved his hands, a golden plaque appearing in front of his eyes that described everything there was to know about the being called Crixus, his eyebrows lifting as he read about the ability this genius had to use Aether!","He nodded in satisfaction as he approached Noah and asked.","\"Young disciple, what can I clarify for you?\"","Noah glanced at this being that was smiling in a helpful manner as he replied.","\"These Fate Lines you mentioned, how exactly does one use them after they are condensed into their bodies?\"","Noah asked a random question as he wondered how he should play his cards for this very important beginning of this new journey, a brilliant reply coming as the body of the red-robed Celestial began to shine with numerous lines.","\"I’ve made my own Fate Lines visible as an example. Using {Fate’s Disciple} uses up your own essence in exchange for assimilating a line or a few lines of fate depending on your talent and reserves of energy. You sometimes find people who have a grand fate laid out for them to be able to assimilate numerous Fate Lines very quickly, only to be hindered by the small amount of energy they have as they advance slowly thereafter.\"","\"You also find those with high realms and abundant energy not being able to condense any Fate Lines as they have no talent for it. All you have to do is move your essence according to {Fate’s Disciple} and observe what talent you truly have. You do not need to actively use your Fate Lines for now, as they augment your strength passively!\"","The Red Robed Disciple spoke with a fervent expression as his body gave off an oppressive feeling, the numerous golden lines on his body bringing a horrible feeling of oppression to anyone that was near.","\"You will realize the uses of Fate Lines more as you receive more techniques in the future, but I can tell you a huge secret now about Fate Lines.\"","Noah listened closely as the light gradually died down on the being in front of him.","\"If you are proficient in condensing fate lines and acc.u.mulate a tremendous amount of them, you will find yourself easily matching those in higher realms simply because of the force that Fate Lines provide your strength. A Saint Realm being defeating a Void or Soul Forging Realm expert is within the realm of possibility!\"","Grand words came out of this Red Robed Celestial’s mouth as it sparked the spirits of the numerous listening White Robed Disciples as they began to cultivate {Fate Disciple}. Noah nodded to the being in front of him as he took a meditative position himself, being very careful but very much looking forward to seeing how this would all turn out!"]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331: Chapter 330 - Talent?","paragraphs":["Noah’s ears were picking up a few discussions from his expanded senses as he gradually came to realize the reason why he had received some looks when he first came here.","Beside him, many of the selected Celestial Disciples that wore the white robes currently were tremendous geniuses from powerful Prime Worlds, or were beings that already lived in this Celestial Star and were just now beginning their journey on the Law of Fate as official Celestial Disciples.","Some of them already had Fate Lines condensed in their bodies, as they now sat serenely while their bodies glowed a tinge of red, small golden colors appearing above them that went to enter their bodies.","It was these beings who were surrounded by other disciples as they were asked more about their experiences, while Noah found himself alone as the single Red Robed Celestial came to check on him as the first day as a Celestial Disciple progressed.","To put it simply, these powerful geniuses and natives of the Celestial Star that held huge beliefs in themselves didn’t look at Noah as anything much, only the Red Robed Celestial that held their information placing some slight interest on him!","Noah smiled at this atmosphere as he watched one of the White Robed Disciples begin the process of condensing lines of fate, using the {Fate’s Disciple} technique for the first time.","OOONG!","A wave of golden light released from his body, calling the attention of numerous practicing disciples and the Celestials as they closely watched this disciple who seemed to have some talent in the law of fate.","One..two..four...eight...numerous golden lines rapidly formed above his head as they went to descend to his body, a vibrant feeling of strength releasing from him as words of acknowledgment rang out from the Red Robed Celestial.","\"Being able to condense 10 Fate Lines the moment you step onto the Law of Fate is good, and it means you have good possibilities for the future!\"","The young genius nodded with a passionate face as he closed his eyes and returned to meditation, much of his energy spent to condense these 10 Fate Lines as he slowly retrieved before he began the process of slowly collecting more Fate Lines.","\"I can tell you all the number of Fate Lines now for you to have a goal in mind. 1-100 Fate Lines make you eligible to be a full-fledged White Robed Celestial Disciple, going past 100 and nearing 10,000 Fate Lines puts you at the peak of Black Robed Celestial Disciples, going past 10,000 and nearing the limit of 100,000 Fate Lines relinquishes your role as a Disciple and makes you a Celestial, putting you above even me, who only holds 37,145 Fate Lines currently!\"","The Red Robed Celestial resonantly spoke as Noah learned more about the terms of the Celestials, committing them to memory as he observed a few other scenes occurring throughout the next few minutes.","A white robed disciple activated {Fate’s Disciple} next as he shockingly was able to condense 25 Fate Lines instantly!","Another disciple began the process as they condensed 15. Another condensed 5 right away, with a fourth one causing a resonance of essence as they condensed more than 40 Fate Lines in but an instant!","\"Good, it seems like we have many good seeds this time around.\"","The Red Robed Celestial nodded with a proud expression as the training continued, only a few disciples like Noah remaining who had not begun the process of condensing their first Fate Lines.","The gazes of the other geniuses who were recuperating their energies turned towards those who had not yet begun condensing their lines of fate as the remaining disciples were put on the spotlight.","A disciple from the Stone Race rattled as he received the gazes of numerous disciples and the two Celestials, closing his eyes as he initiated {Fate’s Disciple}, a golden light shining down that slowly began fizzling before it reached him.","The proud light on the Red Robed Celestial’s face was wiped away as he sighed and pityingly spoke.","\"No talent as of now. Work hard in the future.\"","The words were impassive as their gazes moved on to the next disciple, this time a being of the human race whose face was holding a determined expression after seeing the failure of the last disciple.","They initiated {Fate’s Disciple} as they watched to their dismay...only 2 Fate Lines descending down!","\"Subpar talent.\"","The impassive words of the Red Robed Celestial rang out as the gazes of disciples and Celestials alike continued to move on to more beings, a competitive atmosphere occupying the surroundings as some shone in the spot light while others sputtered out in shame.","15 Fate Lines.","\"Good!\"","5 Fate Lines.","\"Subpar.\"","20 Fate Lines.","\"A Talent!\"","Noah observed this process continuing with a smile, the numbers of disciples who had not yet condensed their Fate Lines reducing until only he was left among the joining White Robed Disciples who had yet to use {Fate’s Disciple} for the first time.","The gazes of the proud disciples that were called talents or geniuses landed on him, the probing gazes of the two Red Robed Celestials arriving soon after as they watched to see what this being who had arrived last among the party of disciples had to offer.","His heart was calm as he took in the gaze of the many beings without any sense of nervousness, his mind replaying the words of the Grandmaster who talked about fate.","’Fate favors those with high aspirations who also happen to act on their aspirations and influence the beings around them huh?’","The words of the Grandmaster rang in his ears as he thought about himself. He thought of his own aspirations, the things he had already done, the things he planned to do, and the influence he already had on the numerous planets and beings connected to him.","If all of this was put into the picture...","A confident smile appeared on his face as he thought about this, realizing where some of the strength of the Celestials came from as he thought of all the stars in the Light Expanse that they held sway over.","No wonder that those in the Dark Expanse lost to them!","No wonder their strength seemed to completely overpower everything else!","Just from the first hour of his entrance into their Celestial Star, he had learned one of the core things behind their source of strength- which was the more entities one influenced the fates of, the stronger the power of the Law of Fate they could display.","As for himself? When it came to aspirations, there were many, and they were huge! When it came to connections, he had literal connections of worlds attached to him! When it came to the most crucial aspect of embarking on the path of the Supreme Law of Fate, actually taking the steps towards one’s own grand aspirations...he had always continued to do this, and at an extremely rapid rate at that!","So when it came to his talent to amass these so-called lines of fate?","A dangerous smile appeared on Noah’s face as he prepared to do something huge. He had arrived in the 7th Celestial Star and was already impressed just in the first hour. He had learned a small bit of their ideology as numerous thoughts passed through his mind, comparing them to his own experiences and the things he heard from Elena. He wanted to peer more into the secrets of the Celestials, and understand even more the core of their power!","To do this...he would make a shocking first impression on his first day here as he gave them a show they would never be able to forget!","OOOONG!","Essence began to tremble around him as the gazes of the many unconvinced disciples and probing Red Robed Celestials watched on, the color of the sky changing as Noah initiated {Fate’s Disciple} for the first time."]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332: Chapter 331 - This is Talent!","paragraphs":["RUMBLE!","A tremor spread out as the Celestial Grandmaster who had just left the training disciples and teleported into his small monastery surrounded by extravagant medicinal plants opened his eyes and looked towards the location he just left. The Grandmaster, Vredral, found his aged eyes opening wide as his body flashed towards the training grounds once more, his eyes landing on a single being at the training grounds who was shining a brilliant golden light!","Numerous Fate Lines were converging in the skies, turning the entire area golden as an unforeseen event occurred in the midst of the training grounds. The face of the Grandmaster underwent a change of expressions as he observed the stupendous sight playing out in front of him.","From all directions in the skies, numerous lines of fate that turned the entire sky a shade of gold had appeared, and they were all heading towards a single being meditating stably on the clear paradisiacal grassland. His dark hair whipped wildly around him as one could distinctly observe a smile of utter confidence and control!","---","OOONG!","Noah felt like he could hear the melodic sounds of something that felt foreign yet at the same time was always with him. The moment he initiated the {Fate’s Disciple} skill, he became rooted in the spot he was in as he felt a tremendous force appear in the skies.","He could feel just a portion of this massive force, and he observed the usage of {Fate’s Disciple} as it gave him the ability to directly pull a minuscule amount of this tremendous source of strength towards his body!","WAAA!","A cacophony of sounds rang out as it felt like a wave of golden light washed over him, his body feeling the descent of numerous brilliant lines that went on to tightly wrap around his Origin. He felt as if he was being elevated to a position he never before knew existed as a profound sense of strength overcame him.","RUMBLE!","Line after line descended from the skies as they clutched onto his body as speedily as they could! It was a ridiculous sight for those observing as the Red Robed Celestial had bulging eyes, the cause being that he counted more than 100 Fate Lines descending down in the last few seconds, and it didn’t seem like they were stopping!","The unconvinced White Robed Disciples held disheveled looks as they were blown black by the domineering air being let out by the constantly converging mass of golden lines as they looked forward in shock.","Those who were proud of the words of praise for being able to condense 20 or 30 Fate Lines at once felt a sense of shame as the words of the Celestial Grandmaster repeated in their minds. They thought they were geniuses, they thought they were talented! But when it came to this being in front of them, what was talent?","This was talent!","The Celestial Grandmaster watching from the skies held an indiscernible expression as his vigorous essence in his body moved, summoning a few skills unknowingly as the colors of his eyes became liquid gold.","Time seemed to have slowed down for him as he gazed in the skies where the numerous Fate Lines were slowly converging, following them as they descended onto the body of one disciple as he tried to discern a few things.","He was trying to figure out where all these lines of fate were coming from, trying to peer through and understand just what type of fate this disciple in front of him had invited!","To his surprise, he couldn’t follow the origin of the lines as they seemed to condense and rush down to the ground indiscriminately, their source unknown. A pondering look came unto Grandmaster Vredral as he continued to observe, sensing the auras of new arrivals as similarly dressed celestials like him appeared in the skies he floated upon.","A Celestial that held the unique feature of an exemplary goatee squinted his eyes from the brilliance as he voiced out.","\"What do we have here, Vredral?\"","Their gazes were all locked onto the singular being that continued to absorb Fate Lines rapidly, the number having long surpassed a thousand as it didn’t seem like it would stop any time soon!","\"Another disciple with a Noble Fate, and this one seeming much more monstrous than we have seen before.\"","A profound reply was released from Vredral as they continued to watch the unfolding events, the celestial with the goatee nodding as he spoke once more, a knowing smile appearing on his face.","\"This is a great boon, but could also be a source for danger.\"","\"No worries, all that needs to be done is to make sure we properly mold him, and when have we ever failed at that?\"","Grandmaster Vredral quickly replied as the intense golden light in the skies gradually calmed down, the brilliance of colors fading away as a few hundred more fate lines wrapped onto the body of a now floating figure.","It was a majestic sight to see as numerous Fate Lines were swirling visibly around Noah’s body, one of the Red Robed Celestials deploying a technique as a white last passed through his eyes, releasing a sound of shock thereafter as he was able to count exactly how many lines of fate had descended down and locked on to this disciple’s body!","\"9,999 Fate Lines all at once!\"","...!!!","Alarm spread throughout the paradisiacal clearing as this number was mentioned, the pondering looks on the three floating Celestial Grandmasters in the air becoming even deeper.","The Grandmaster with the goatee spoke to the aged Vredral once more as they observed the stupendous process finishing.","\"That is two beings that hold a Noble Fate on your hands. You are sure you can handle this?\"","An imperceptible smile floated from Grandmaster Vredral’s face as he replied with confidence.","\"With extreme confidence. It is even better since both of them can receive tutelage in a similar environment. There is nothing to worry about, Grandmaster Ramiel.\"","The Celestial with a pronounced goatee, Grandmaster Ramiel, nodded as his body and the bodies of the other Grandmasters that had come to observe faded away, leaving behind only Grandmaster Vredral as his body slowly floated towards the ground!","Noah felt his own body that was elevated in the air palpate with a tremendous sense of strength, the numerous glowing lines slowly receding to the deepest portions of his origin. His eyes opened as a glimmer of shimmering light faded, feigning an expression of exhaustion with his gaze landing on his stat panel that showed a new addition.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(5%)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 9,999]","[Vitality: VOID]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: VOID]","Beneath the portion that showed his bloodline, the number of Fate Lines was displayed as a curious light passed through his eyes, this curiosity being cut short as he felt the aura of a Celestial Grandmaster that had left not too long ago.","Noah’s body instinctively lit up with numerous Fate Lines as the probing gaze of the Grandmaster landed on his body, a shocking thought actually passing through his mind as he realized something stupendous.","The domineering strength that could make one feel overwhelmed that this Celestial Grandmaster always released...it felt more bearable at this moment as Noah felt like a few shackles became unbound!","\"Genius!\"","Resounding words shattered the atmosphere of stupor as the newly arriving talented disciples were able to see exactly what a true genius was!"]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333: Chapter 332 - Ones with a Noble Fate","paragraphs":["Noah’s gaze stayed on the Celestial Grandmaster as he reveled in the feeling of abundance of strength, his thoughts communicating with the Planetary System as he tried to get a better understanding of just what these Fate Lines were.","[It is a source of power that is hard to quantify. Besides knowing how many Fate Lines you currently have and that they augment your strength, we cannot quantify exactly in what way.]","Numerous thoughts passed through Noah’s mind as he heard this, being pulled out of his thoughts as the Grandmaster came near him with an acknowledging expression.","\"I chose you because of your talent in Aether, but not once did I expect for you to have the talent to be a being blessed with a Noble Fate.\"","A foreign set of words were released as Noah quickly caught on and asked quizzically.","\"Noble Fate?\"","\"Yes, Noble Fate. It is an indication that a being is meant to have a huge hand to play in the future, affecting the fates of many of those around them. Of course, this is only an indication and is not set in stone. There have been a few beings with Noble Fates in the past who never got to fulfill them, dying early or wasting their lives away. But...those that have managed to use their Noble Fate to the fullest have left behind unforgotten marks in history.\"","Noah’s eyes shone as these words reached his ears, realizing instinctively that the explosive entrance he wanted to create in this 7th Celestial Star was more than enough!","The Grandmaster neared his position as his aged eyes stared at him up and down, shimmering lights passing through them as he nodded and turned to the other talented disciples.","\"This is the type of talent you should all aspire to have. Do not let this young genius’s talent shadow your own, and continue working hard.\"","The Grandmaster nodded at the Red Robed Celestials that were still looking at Noah as if he was a monster, realization hitting them that if Noah had condensed just a few more Fate Lines, he would have directly skipped the White and Black Robes distinctions and entered the same distinction as them!","They watched on as the Grandmaster placed his hands on Noah and disappeared, turning to the disciples who still held blank eyes as they spoke.","\"Ahem. Let’s continue. After the condensation of fate lines...\"","A discussion continued for the White Robed Disciples in the now peaceful grassland as Noah found himself disappearing and reappearing in a small monastery in an atmosphere that held an even denser concentration of Medicinal Plants than his own Spiritual Land. The monastery was located at the peak of a mountain, a few clouds being visible in the distance as a scene of peace and serenity showed itself.","\"A talent like yours needs strict direction, so I will directly be acting as your teacher from now on.\"","The Grandmaster was walking ahead in front of him as he spoke out, an expression of remembrance on his face as he thought of another disciple that fate had pointed to as someone unique, but they had faced their death not too long ago in the First Realm of Hell. Fate was unpredictable in this manner.","But, this new disciple he was directly taking in was one that held a Noble Fate, something that only one other being had shown an indication of in this 7th Celestial Star!","His aged figure walked forward as Noah followed close behind, his eyes continuing to gaze over the Medicinal Plants that held an abundant amount of essence as the Grandmaster continued, his perception noticing Noah’s looks.","\"Whatever resources you need will be provided to you as you embark on your path on the Supreme Law of Fate. You have just now condensed Fate Lines for the first time, and have not been taught the most proficient way of using them.\"","Noah followed the Grandmaster into the Monastery as he passed through the small doors, finding his vision expanding as he actually came to see the inside was somehow much more expansive than what the outside of the monastery showed.","In this large room of the monastery, the Celestial Grandmaster turned towards Noah as he spoke with a serious voice.","\"I am the 9th Ranked Grandmaster of the 7th Celestial Star, Vredral. Do you take me as your master?\"","Noah looked at this aged figure whose power in no way went together with the old age he showed, his gaze becoming firm as he bowed and spoke out.","\"I do!\"","His affirmation received the smile of Vredral as he spoke out once more, bringing his right hand to his chest as he did so.","\"Rise. In the lands of the Celestials, the greeting and signs of affirmation are done by placing your right palm to your chest, just beside your beating heart as a sign of commitment and truthfulness.\"","Noah’s eyes shone as he saw this, nodding as he placed his palm on his left chest while looking forward. The Grandmaster nodded as he waved his hands, about to bring to light numerous Inheritance Crystals that held a multitude of skills!","\"You have just learned how to condense Fate Lines, and have actually condensed more than enough to proficiently use the techniques that we have honed over the years to begin your journey on the law of fate. These techni- Oh?\"","The continuing Grandmaster stopped abruptly as Noah was just about to receive numerous new skills freely, a presence nearing the monastery as a smile appeared on his face.","\"It seems we must stop briefly as you get the chance to meet the only other being on this Celestial Star that holds a Noble Fate similar to you, and you’ve actually met them before on your journey that ultimately brought you here. It’s mysterious how fate works, isn’t it?\"","The presence of a domineering figure could be felt as a valiant aura burst forth, a being with exemplary beauty and valor appearing in the monastery that Noah and Grandmaster Vredral were in as she placed her right hand on her full chest and paid respects, her gaze landing on Noah thereafter as a surprised expression appeared on her face.","RUMBLE!","The Grandmaster looked up and pierced through the veils of the ceiling of the monastery as his gaze landed on the skies, noticing the convergence of numerous lines of fate as he smiled, many thoughts passing through his head as two beings that had met once before with completely different statuses met once again, this time holding a similar title!"]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334: Chapter 333 - [Fates Guardian], A Spar","paragraphs":["Noah’s gaze landed on the figure of the valiant Athena as he processed the words of the Grandmaster. She was also someone given the title of a being with a Noble Fate, a concept he was just introduced to and did not fully know exactly what it entailed.","\"Grandmaster, is this the same Crixus of the Profound Astral Sect? He holds a Noble Fate?\"","Athena walked in as her gaze landed on Noah, asking respectfully as a jolly laugh wiggled the facial muscles of Vredral.","\"Yes. This is why fate is always something we must continue deciphering and learning, as even I didn’t think the being we met briefly could have a talent like yours.\"","The Grandmaster replied as Athena adopted a look of responsibility, going towards Noah as she spoke towards him in a friendly manner.","\"Nice to see you again, and under much greater circ.u.mstances at that.\"","Noah smiled as numerous thoughts crossed his mind, still evaluating everything about the Celestials and comparing it with the information he was given by the beings from the Dark Expanse as he spoke towards this valiant figure.","\"Likewise. I look forward to learning alongside you.\"","Athena nodded as she turned towards the Grandmaster.","\"Has he had any combat training yet? I will gladly fulfill my role as the Senior Disciple to make sure he learns the techniques of fate well.\"","Grandmaster Vredral smiled as he continued his motion of waving his hands, bringing to light numerous Inheritance Crystals that floated towards Noah serenely.","\"He just finished condensing his first few thousand Fate Lines, so it will be a perfect opportunity for him to learn our techniques and test them in combat right after.\"","Athena nodded towards the Grandmaster as a valiant light bounced off her body, her gaze firm and full of righteousness as she replied.","\"Leave it to me, Grandmaster!\"","Noah’s eyes were already locked onto the multiple Inheritance Crystals floating in front of his eyes as he grabbed them without reservations, a tremendous amount of information on how to fully utilize the mysterious lines of fate that were fully bound to his origin entering his mind!","This mass of information was taken in strides by the System as it carefully took everything and categorized it, Noah observing in real-time as he watched the formation of a brilliant skill tree which unlike the previous ones, shone with a l.u.s.ter of gold!","His eyes shone with light as he gazed upon yet another Void Ranked Skill, and this one was called [Fate’s Guardian]!","<strong>[Fate’s Guardian](0/30) :: As a beginner just learning the workings of fate, the role of a guardian that protects the weak and eviscerates evil is given to you. Abilities include Empyrean Guards(0/5), Empyrean Armament(0/5), Smite of Liberation(0/5), and Judgment(0/5).</strong>","<strong>[Empyrean Guards](0/5) :: A guardian is called forth to defend you and stand against your enemies. The Empyrean Guards are capable of healing and offensive magic, their strength only increasing depending on how many Fate Lines the user has. Current Summon Limit: 1</strong>","<strong>[Empyrean Armament](0/5) :: The user is covered with the brilliance of the summoned Empyrean Guards as every point in their body gains extreme boosts. +5% Soul Damage, Physical Damage, Speed, and Defense for every Empyrean Guard absorbed.</strong>","<strong>[Smite of Liberation](0/5) :: Cleanse the souls of those that stand against you as you smite them with a Blade of Liberation. The blade is corporeal and yet physical at the same time, granting +50% Physical and +50% Soul Damage. </strong>","<strong>[Judgement](0/5) :: A declaration of death for all those that stand against you is called forth. Those that cannot defend themselves will have their bodies destroyed and their souls shattered as they become lost in the river of fate.</strong>","His eyes quickly ran through the numerous shining descriptions as the skills he received were extremely familiar to the abilities that he had seen Athena use in the battle against the Aberration in the First Realm of hell! Much of his thoughts were on just exactly how strong he could make them once he added the Skill Points he continued to passively collect from the Legion of Undead that was still razing Infernals to the ground even as he stood on this Celestial Star.","\"The abilities that are coursing through your mind right now are fairly high leveled, where they are normally utilized best by those in the Void Realm. But this...is where the first use of Fate Lines comes in.\"","RUMBLE!","The body of Grandmaster Vredral pulsed with power as an uncountable number of golden lines appeared on his body. They were all extremely thin and condensed, being so imperceptible that it looked like a sea of gold instead of extremely thin lines!","\"Fate Lines will directly reduce the energy required when casting abilities that influence fate, and this is just in addition to their offensive feature where they can boost your power to unimaginable levels. This is where you will have an incident like the one you observed in the First Realm of Hell, where Athena was able to take down a being stepping into the Soul Forging Realm with her realm still being of the Void.\"","The resonant voice of the Grandmaster rang out as the brilliance he portrayed died down, Athena moving further into the monastery as Noah continued to marvel at the expanding space inside this building that seemed extremely small from the outside.","\"The best way to learn how to utilize Fate Lines well is to test them in direct combat. Junior Brother, come. Let me show you how wondrous the abilities of [Fate’s Guardian] really are.\"","A wide smile appeared on Noah’s face as he showed a grin of determination, his body lighting up as numerous lines of fate could be seen as he spoke out.","\"Yes, Senior Sister!\"","RUMBLE!","Essence converged from the surroundings as space was manipulated, the space in the monastery they were in gradually continuing to get larger and larger as it completely defied the reality of the size of the monastery when looking from the outside.","\"Since you have condensed...close to 10,000 Fate Lines currently, I will only be utilizing that amount when sparring with you. We will start gradually as we get you used to the techniques, and then ramp up the difficulty thereafter.\"","A valiant look accentuated itself even more from Athena as her dark hair automatically tied itself into a ponytail, her voice tinged with surprise as she confirmed Noah had really condensed 9,999 lines of fate in this short time period. Her energy moved as essence erupted from her body, a single Empyrean Guard appearing beside her with a resonation of power!","Noah looked on with a gaze full of interest, numerous unknown thoughts coursing through his mind as he tuned everything out. At this instant, he just simply wanted to see just what benefits he could wring out from this coming spar, and exactly how many more skills he could continue to receive from the Celestials as he continued. He did not forget his mission. He did not come here to mingle nor make friends. He came for the singular purpose of power and position among the beings in this incredible organization, and he would not stop until he achieved it at the highest levels!","[Empyrean Guards].","A whisper left his mouth as the lines of fate in his body pulsed, a being clad in golden armor carrying a long hammer appearing in front of him, its eyes blazing forth with a golden light as it looked at the opposing summoned Empyrean Guard that looked exactly like it in the distance.","\"Good. [Empyrean Armament]!\"","Before the Empyrean Guard standing next to Athena could even move, it became a streak of liquid light as it latched onto her body, her valiant figure gaining a golden chest armor along with a dangerously shining gold hammer that she swiftly waved it in her hands towards Noah.","[Empyrean Armament].","Noah whispered the name of the same skill as he observed the wondrous feeling of the powerful summon in front of him turning into a gold liquid light that went on to cover him, feeling his capabilities boosted as a chest armor and a golden hammer appeared on his hands as well.","OONG!","Two distinctly different pressures released from the golden lines on each of their bodies clashed in the air between them as the Grandmaster moved at a far away distance and observed with a smile, Athena making the first move as she initiated the beginning of the spar!","\"Yaa!\"","Her body left behind a mirage of light as it quickly appeared above Noah’s position, the heavy hammer in her hands swinging down dangerously as Noah smiled and clasped tightly onto his own hammer, swinging it up as a burst of gold light erupted out.","CLANG!","Noah felt the ground beneath him breaking as a tremendous sense of pressure rushed down, his body feeling light soon after as brilliance erupted from the numerous lines of fate around his body as he laughed, his eyes landing on the War Princess as he charged forward!","A simple spar had begun in a small monastery in the 7th Celestial Star, the winner of which was still unknown at this moment in time!"]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335: Chapter 334 - Athena teaches her Junior!","paragraphs":["Athena’s POV","---","I let out a deep breath after the brief first impact between me and this mysterious being that I had met once before in the First Realm of Hell. This being, Crixus, was an anomaly through and through, but the only thing that mattered to me was that we had gained yet another combatant to help bring about more order in this chaotic landscape.","I took the words of the Grandmaster in stride as this Crixus apparently held the same Noble Fate like me, this development being one of the things that sparked my interest as for too long I had been asking myself- what exactly did fate want from me? What Noble Fate was waiting for me at the end of all of this?","This being in front of me having a similar fate...I wanted to know more about him, and exactly what the influence he would have for the future!","\"Yaa!\"","My body moved across fluidly as I found myself closing my eyes, using my senses to more clearly observe the flow of mana, and the numerous lines of fate pulsating in my own body, and the body of this being in front of me.","CLANG!","Brilliance exploded out as the two hammers clashed again, making me realize this Crixus could freely match the pace of the battle as he seemed to be adapting to the first and second stages of the abilities of Fate’s Guardian fairly easily.","This means...we can increase the difficulty!","Empyrean Guard! Empyrean Armament!","RUMBLE!","I cast the skills multiple times as two more celestial guardians wielding hammers full of strength appeared, only to turn into streams of light soon after as they attached onto my body, completing the lower half of my armor as the usual cooling helmet covered my head.","I made sure that the strength was still only being taken from 9,999 Fate Lines as I observed the reaction of this junior disciple. Would he be able to keep up?","My expanded senses observed a smile of confidence as Crixus waved his hands, two Empyrean Guards appearing as they quickly became streams of light that attached to his body, granting him a similar set of armor as mine.","You can still keep up? Good!","I felt a small smile appearing on my own lips as my love for battle was slowly bubbling forth, trying my best to contain it so that I wouldn’t accidentally destroy this junior disciple in front of me.","He moved first this time as he seemed to be enjoying the feeling of strength that Empyrean Armament provided, my body evading to the side as the oppressive hammer smashed onto the area I was just standing on.","Good! Good!","My body moved automatically as clashes of light began to resound throughout the expanded room we were in, Crixus surprisingly keeping up with my movements as time passed.","CLANG! CLANG! BOOM!","A few craters were left behind as I could only see dark eyes locking onto my figure from the slits of the golden helmet that covered his head, his body moving towards me yet again as his movements gained a similar fluidity I had worked so hard to achieve over the years with ease.","His use of the innate strength of Fate Lines was seamless as with every clash, I could feel the strength he let off increase more and more!","I could feel essence palpating on my body as his attacks increased in speed, my eyes watching in slow motion as I bent back and watched the merciless swing of golden hammer barely pass through the tip of my helmet.","’Ahh Junior Brother, you shouldn’t have done that!’","My closed eyes opened as a burst of golden light released from me and pushed back the being that was sticking around me tightly while throwing out attacks, a slight trembling running through my body as I realized I could no longer withhold the need for battle that had been brought forth by his stupendous attacks.","’Forgive me, Junior Brother, but I’ll have to enjoy myself for a bit!’","RUMBLE!","Essence converged as yet another Empyrean Guard was summoned and quickly turned into a stream of liquid light that attached onto my body, the feeling of having gloriously fluttering wings appearing once more as my speed was increased yet again.","My eyes that were filled with a thirst for battle locked on to the figure that still seemed to be in top shape, a small smile appearing on my lips as I observed with stupefaction as yet another Empyrean Guard appeared next to him, turning into a stream of light as this Crixus gained a resonantly shining set of wings similar to mine!","’Junior Brother...aren’t you adapting to these techniques too fast?’","The thought did not match my actions as my body was already moving by itself, turning into a streak of light towards the being that seemed to have no problem pulling out the power of abilities he was just introduced to with precision and grandeur I had not come across before.","BOOM!","The golden hammers clashed yet again as the impact smashed the figure of Crixus back, his armored body hitting the wall on the opposite side as I stopped briefly, wondering if I had gone overboard. My expectations were defied yet again as the only thing I observed was a streak of light shooting towards me, a peal of childish laughter ringing out.","’Haha, good!’","RUMBLE!","All reservations were let loose as it seemed this Crixus was capable enough to withstand my attacks, even if they were limited to only 9,999 Fate Lines.","My body began to feel the joy of battle as my figure shot through the skies to meet this mysterious being that could match my pace of battle with ease. Was he truly like me? Is this really a being with a Noble Fate waiting for him in the future?","BOOM!","The last clash actually pushed the both of us back as my questions weren’t answered, but I knew I had found an interesting being to play with as essence coursed through my body and was released in a splendor of colors once more.","\"Come, Junior Brother!\"","A cry left my mouth as the thrilling battle continued, my focus tightly wrapped onto this rapidly adapting Crixus as I wanted to peer through his defenses and everything that surrounded him!"]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336: Chapter 335 - Never Before Seen!","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes moved rapidly as he easily kept up with the streak of light letting out valiant cries in front of him. The streak of light seemed to be fluid at times and extremely rapid a second later, causing the state of a battle that was filled with unpredictability.","When the battle began, the thought it would be a simple spar that would allow a junior disciple to learn the ropes of the abilities, but he found the pace becoming faster and faster as this Athena seemed to be enjoying herself after a while!","His own body was rapidly adapting to the feeling of strength that the close to 10,000 Fate Lines provided, going with the flow as he gradually added Skill Points into [Empyrean Guard] and [Empyrean Armament] to match the pace of the battle.","After placing three Skill Points into [Empyrean Guards], the summon limit was increased to 4 as he then cast [Empyrean Armament] to take on the form of resplendent being covered head to toe with a golden armor and wings of golden light that he had only seen on Athena!","He could feel his body buzzing with power as he sensed a unique form of strength being released from the numerous Fate Lines now surrounding his body, confirming that the energy required to cast the skills under the [Fate’s Guardian] skill tree were extremely minimal, with their power being higher than any skills at the same level!","He finally understood why the Celestial Disciple Drax at the Transcendent Rank could match those in the Saint Realm, and how Athena so effortlessly matched an Infernal Aberration that was stepping into the Soul Forging Realm.","Their techniques that utilized fate were simply that powerful, with much less energy being required for use while their damage was great, only increasing the more Fate Lines one held.","BOOM!","A clash occurred yet again as Noah found himself slowly on the losing ground, this woman in front of him long forgetting this was supposed to be a spar as he could see her figure expertly predicting his next moves with ease, dodging fluidly as she then counterattacked aggressively!","’Alright then.’","An imperceptible smile appeared on Noah’s lips as he looked at the many Skill Points he had with, adding full points into [Empyrean Guards] and [Empyrean Armament] as the two skills were maxed!","<strong>[Empyrean Guards](5/5) :: A guardian is called forth to defend you and stand against your enemies. The Empyrean Guards are capable of healing and offensive magic, their strength only increasing depending on how many Fate Lines the user has. Current Summon Limit: 6</strong>","<strong>[Empyrean Armament](5/5) :: The user is covered with the brilliance of the summoned Empyrean Guards as every point in their body gains extreme boosts. +30% Soul Damage, Physical Damage, Speed, and Defense for every Empyrean Guard absorbed.</strong>","His body dodged the oppressive attacks of Athena as he looked at the expanded boosts of the two skills after their Skill Points were maxed, feeling his body trembling with power as he already had +120% Soul Damage, Physical Damage, Speed, and Defense for the four Empyrean Guards he had already absorbed through [Empyrean Armament].","Now, he could summon two more, something that he hadn’t even seen Athena do while battling with the Aberration. His smile only became wider as he knew he was about to do something that would most likely surprise the watching Grandmaster and the valiant Athena.","But since he had planned to show off a talent unlike any other in the eyes of the Celestials, he would go all the way and show exactly what genius was!","RUMBLE!","His essence moved as he summoned two more Empyrean Guards in the skies, his senses observing the Grandmaster standing up with his calm gaze changing as Athena’s eyes bulged out from the thin slits of her golden helmet.","They observed the summoning of 2 more Empyrean Guards, something that they knew to not be possible as even the most proficient users of [Fate’s Guardian] could only summon 4 Empyrean Guards, no matter their level!","They watched as these extra two Empyrean Guards turned into streaks of light and attach onto Crixus’s body, a transform they had not come across before occurring as it went past the simple full body armor and golden wings.","From Crixus’s back, the wings of golden light became more physical as they began to observe with stupor the appearance of brilliant white-feathered wings that expanded magnificently!","The metal looking battle armor covering his body dissolved as what replaced it was a regal golden robe that dr.a.p.ed over him comfortably, a shining golden sword with a sharpened edge and a brilliant golden shield filled with numerous runic inscriptions appearing on his two hands as he floated grandiosely in the skies.","His image shone with l.u.s.ter as when one looked at him, they would find themselves saying- ’This was what a true Fate’s Guardian looked like!","Noah had pulled the abilities of [Fate’s Guardian] to the extremities with the use of Skill Points, bringing about a transformation that those who handed him this technique did not even think to be possible.","Grandmaster Vredral’s face gradually returned to calmness as a peering gaze stayed on Noah, his aged heart that was always calm feeling ripples as this new recruit he took in simply had too many surprises.","Athena looked on with shining eyes towards Noah’s transformation as her gaze was one of brilliance, wanting to try this new technique with her own body as she fearlessly rushed forward with her hammer in hand!","Noah felt the abundant strength flowing through him as the shield to his left hand made him feel like he would never be harmed, the sword on his right hand making him feel like he could bring judgment and cut down all those he wished.","His languid gaze landed on the rushing Athena as he swung the sharp sword from right where he was floating in the skies, not even moving an inch. But the result was stupendous as the rushing Athena foresaw an attack smashing into her a millisecond later, an attack that even though she knew was coming, she could not evade it!","BOOM!","PAH!","An explosion resounded first, with the sound of a body smashing to the ground hitting later as Noah stood stably in the skies, the figure of Athena smashing into the ground and causing a crater to form.","\"...\"","Silence reigned briefly as the scene cleared, Noah’s gaze piercing through the dust and seeing the figure of Athena standing stably at the center of the crater.","RUMBLE!","Her helmet was split apart as it broke in two and began to dissolve into particles of light, her hair that was tied up in a ponytail swinging wildly as tens of thousands of Fate Lines became visible on her body. A domineering aura erupted forth as a smile that could shatter the hearts of men appeared on her now bronze figure, the color of the sky gaining a hue of gold!","\"Stop.\"","A resonant voice of a happy Grandmaster resonated out as a man with a grand celestial appearance of a guardian of fate looked down from the skies, the War Princess looking from below as her gaze longed for another battle!"]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337: Chapter 336 - What do you want?","paragraphs":["Athena reigned in her wild aura as Noah’s brilliantly shining white wings began to disappear into particles of light, his body gradually descending down.","\"It’s my loss, Junior Brother. You seem to be more capable than we have imagined.\"","Athena’s face regained calmness as the War Princess with a thirst for battle disappeared, her eyes only shining with a strong competitive light as she looked towards Noah.","\"How exactly were you able to summon more Empyrean Guards and obtain that transformation though?\"","A curious question was thrown out as it wasn’t Noah, but the Grandmaster was the one that replied as he laughed joyfully.","\"Those that are really loved by fate can sometimes find new ways to use techniques or go past what we normally believed was the limit. Crixus has just shown us that [Fate’s Guardian] has many areas to improve on. It is the skill of someone who is naturally talented in the Law of Fate!\"","The interest in Athena’s eyes only increased as she heard this, watching as the Grandmaster came close to Noah and glanced at his body up and down.","\"Marvelous. The Fate Lines you recently condensed have all but fully assimilated in your origin. Do you know why you were only able to condense 9,999 the first time you tried?\"","Noah shook his head as a profound look appeared on the Grandmaster, replied as his eyes continued to gaze deeply towards him.","\"Passing the 10,000 Fate Lines is a mark that makes you a Red Robed Celestial, but it is also a point of distinction for a being that is only stumbling in the light of fate, to a being that can actually influence it and use techniques to even probe it. No matter how high your talent is in the law of fate, your body still has to take some time assimilating this new source of power, and you will come to find that even condensing tens of Fate Lines in a day becomes harder as time passes.\"","Noah listened carefully as the Grandmaster continued on.","\"Over the next few weeks as you assimilate more Fate Lines and get used to the abilities of Fate’s Guardian, I will provide you with even more skills that will be hard to comprehend, where even with your monstrous talent it would take you quite some time.\"","Noah nodded as the gaze of the Grandmaster finally moved off of him, going towards the valiant Athena on the side.","\"Athena, show Crixus to his living quarters for now. Let him absorb the experiences of the spar today and all of the new abilities. I’ll be inquiring your help to conduct more sparring sessions with your junior brother in the future.\"","The War Princess’s eyes shone as she heard this, nodding respectfully as she beckoned towards Noah, their figures leaving the expansive area of the monastery that was filled with broken walls and craters.","Noah followed along as numerous thoughts passed through his mind, his body lifting to the skies as the figure of Athena flew off the mountain into a lower elevation where an expansive clearing with three dome-shaped buildings stood. He was about to speak when Athena broke the silence first, and it was with a question he didn’t expect as their figures landed on the clearing next to the large dome shaped buildings.","\"What do you want?\"","Noah turned his head to the side as he replied in a confused manner.","\"Pardon me?\"","Athena turned towards him with her eyes clear, her gaze impassive as the figure of a being relishing battle was all but gone, only piercing eyes gazing towards Noah.","\"What is it that you seek? What is your goal?\"","The question was very straightforward, taking the calculating Noah by surprise as he adopted a pondering face on what exactly to reply. Athena continued on as she looked around at the expansive clearing.","\"My goal is to pierce through the mysteries of fate and understand exactly why a Celestial saved me from a dying world and brought me to where I am today. It is to understand this apparent Noble Fate that I hold, and what exactly it wants from me in the future.\"","Noah’s outward gaze continued to be one of pondering as his mind was impassive. There were many thoughts running through at this moment, but in his mind, this War Princess in front of him was marked for death long ago!","He was just beginning to delve into the ideologies and secrets of the Celestials, understanding very briefly about their motivations and how they tied in to the Law of Fate, but that still did not change the actions that this woman in front of him had carried out.","One could say it was a mission given by the Celestials. One could say she was indoctrinated to believe that what she did was correct, that she wholly believed in what fate foretold, that taking the lives of billions of beings of the Lost World in the name of reducing a tremendous amount of chaos in the future because of what they foresaw from the use of the Celestials’ mysterious skills. It was these same skills that Noah was patiently waiting to get his hands on, skills pertaining to fate that would allow him to see exactly why the celestials would give missions to destroy entire stars.","\"I want to understand why a clueless girl was saved and elevated to the position she is in today, all the while doing my best to reduce the chaos constantly spreading across many worlds. So, what exactly do you want?\"","Her gaze landed on him again as her calm eyes locked with his, each one thinking their own thoughts as Noah replied with a smile.","\"I want...certainty, plain and simple. Over the years, I have seen that strength and power are the only things that guarantee a level of certainty in life. They are the only things that grant me the ability to keep my life, and the lives of those around me, without something unexpected coming and taking everything away.\"","Noah’s eyes became firm and more determined as he gazed upon this being he still held the same mindset about.","\"I want strength that allows me to live free of worries, for me to enjoy my life and do whatever I want without worrying about an exceedingly powerful force that could disrupt everything I have out of nowhere. Fate...is just something that I will grasp along the way towards that level of strength.\"","Athena’s eyes shook as she heard this, her ability confirming that not a single lie could be found in those words!","This being that held a tremendous talent in the law of fate...wanted to simply use it to amass even more strength to himself!","A light smile appeared on Athena’s lips as she heard this, nodding her head as she felt like she understood the being in front of her some more. She had always been asking herself what fate wanted from her. As she looked at this being who apparently held a Noble Fate similar to her she now wondered- what exactly did fate have in store for him?"]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338: Chapter 337 - Chaos Across Worlds!","paragraphs":["Athena’s intense gaze stayed on Noah for a few seconds before she turned around and waved to one of the spectacularly designed dome-shaped buildings in the area they landed.","\"This will be your dwelling for the near future. It is located on this Inquiring Mountain that is under the watch of Grandmaster Vredral. It will contain a dwelling as well as an expansive training field, medicinal garden, and a dining area where servants will bring food whenever you wish.\"","Noah followed her gaze as he looked at the unique architecture that held reminded him of ancient cathedrals with a hint of something new. He nodded towards Athena as she began to move towards the adjacent building next to it, saying a few last words before she disappeared from Noah’s senses.","\"The Grandmaster will continue to train you based on your talent, so expect an even harder training regiment and...much longer sparring battles as you increase your understanding of fate and the spectacular abilities you can use with it.\"","The War Princess disappeared with these words, leaving a calm Noah looking at the expansive building in front of him that would be his new abode for who knew how long. He went inside to familiarize himself and think over the many things that had happened today, his heart still hungry for even more information, and the abilities of Celestials that continued to show wondrous uses.","Over the next few days, Noah’s life would take on an interesting schedule as he spent a majority of the time in his dome-shaped dwelling as he amassed more Fate Lines, the rest of his time being divided into lessons from Grandmaster Vredral who would go on to talk about Fate, or the occasional sparring session with a woman that seemed to live for battle. He kept contact with his forces that were moving between the First Realm of Hell to farm Skill Points and the Underworld to hone their skills as he made sure things were going in the right direction, but much of his attention was now focused on Fate Lines and the law of fate!","His findings with {Fate’s Disciple} were especially noteworthy, as he was able to break through from 9,999 Fate Lines on the second day as he went on to understand the rate at which he could normally condense this mysterious force of fate.","Passing the 10,000 point was the distinction of one becoming a Red Robed Celestial, something that was completely out of reach for the other White Robed Disciples that were still hanging at the level of less than 100 Fate Lines after one day.","Noah’s monstrous rate of collection of 9,999 in a single day completely went against the norms and caused a huge blow to some of the geniuses watching on that day. But he found that the rate of progression after that...was extremely slow!","This was because the words of the Grandmaster actually came to be true, where in a day, he could at most condense 100 Fate Lines. This was still completely out of the Grandmaster’s expectations as he looked at Noah with even more attention, as he had predicted even condensing a few tens of Fate Lines a day would be the limit. To others, this would be an unbelievable rate of growth, but it was extremely slow for him who had pulled in a few thousand in a single day.","This fast rate of condensing Fate Lines that he did not make a secret caused numerous ripples on the 7th Celestial Star that he still was not aware of. But this level of genius caused the favors of the Celestials to descend down like pouring rain on a stormy night.","This caused Noah to begin receiving the high-level techniques of Celestials every week, the techniques that could be considered mysterious as they worked to directly influence fate, or pierce the veils of secrecy surrounding it!","By the end of a single month of his stay in the 7th Celestial Star, he had amassed enough skills for the System to classify them in form of an Absolute Skill, and this one was from the hands of the Celestials themselves!","---","As Noah spent his days in the 7th Celestial Star continuing to learn about the Supreme Law of Fate and the abundant secrets of the Celestials, time continued to pass as numerous figures in a wide array of worlds moved with their own goals.","A month was neither a long nor a short time, but it was enough for huge movements to occur behind the scenes.","In the Prime World that was the Underworld, sparks had begun to fly between the border of the Pureblood Vampyres and the Lineage of the Royal Silverbourne Werewolves, the surrounding forces preparing for war as they noticed this change early.","Many people had begun discussing in knowledgeable tones as they held a similar view across the board- The Pureblood Vampyres had finished consolidating their power as made a power grab for the entirety of the Underworld!","Small scale battles had already begun here and there as rumors of monstrous combatants that looked even more fearsome than those in the Lineage of the Silverbourne Werewolves appeared on the side of the Pureblood Vampyres. Rumors of a new ruler had also spread out as those watching in the dark began to frequently see the curvaceous figure of a gorgeous silver-haired beauty that could topple kingdoms give commands to the forces of Vampyres. On the hands of this gorgeous figure, one could always see the outline of a miniaturized penguin being carried around like a fluffy plushy toy, many people not trusting their senses as they were feeling an extreme aura of arrogance coming off of this small penguin.","War was on the horizon, but not just for the Underworld as across the vastness of space, a shocking truth had come to light that directly put two Prime Worlds against each other! The forces of the Time Immemorial Sect, a sect in the lands controlled by the Profound Astral Sect of the World of Cultivation- had uncovered a heinous scheme by the forces from the Magus World after their encounter some time ago!","Grand Elder Amos has begun investigating the reports that Elder Dan returned from the Devilish Abode with, following the trail of exactly why the Magi from the Magus World were targeting the people of his sect. After Elder Dan was saved by the mysterious entity that held numerous draconic heads and tentacles, he moved rapidly to report this and chase down any leads as to why the Magi were targeting them in the Devilish Abode.","Grand Elder Amos had thought it was a grudge that he didn’t know about or an old offense that was just uncovered, but as he followed the trail, he came to realize that many forces all over the World of Cultivation were being targeted by Magi from the Magus World!","He quickly brought this information to the attention of the Profound Astral Sect as a thorough investigation was carried out. This investigation revealed a shocking horror as the powerhouses of the Profound Astral Sect were able to catch and imprison a magi in the act, and the things this Magi revealed made a chill run down the spines of all those listening!","A shocking truth was revealed on that day, with the grand designs of the major organization of the Magus World specifically targeting the beings in the World of Cultivation to obtain their bodies for experimentation and the creation of abominations that moved without souls!","This shocking truth enraged the entirety of the World of Cultivation as all travel was closed off, the portals connecting it to the Magus World being the first to be destroyed as everything single remaining Magi on the World of Cultivation was purged that day.","Blood and mayhem ran through the mountains and clouds, this single action heavily offending the forces of the Magus World as they denied any wrongdoings and called the actions of the World of Cultivation baseless murder, sparking a chain of conflicts as the two Prime Worlds now stood at the cusp of a War!","It was not just these two powerful Prime Worlds that were on the precipice of war and conflict as ever so slowly, chaos spread across the worlds as many other powers faced their own rising issues and conflicts, many thinking they were isolated incidents, but only those commanding higher levels of power being able to look at and realize that restlessness and chaos was spreading across the stars."]},{"number":339,"title":"Chapter 339: Chapter 338 - Discerning Fate","paragraphs":["In the Inquiring Mountain that was under the control of Grandmaster Vredral, Noah was sitting on the lush greenery outside of his expansive dome-shaped dwelling that felt too much like a cathedral.","His eyes were closed as he had {Fate’s Disciple} activated, his body gaining a l.u.s.ter of gold as wisps of light converged above him and ever so slowly descended onto his body in an orderly fashion. He felt like he was some wizened being pondering on life as numerous Fate Lines descended within the next few hours, his face that of calmness and peace as the environment around him was really too conducive for this sort of mental state.","He was actively condensing Fate Lines while expanding his senses to cover the well-ordered plants that held an array of colors surrounding the location where he and Athena stayed on this Inquiring Mountain, many of these plants creating snaking paths that went up or down the mountain as simple roads were visible.","The mountain was thick with essence everywhere you turned, causing one’s body to bubble in excitement just by being there. He remained in this state as he thought back to the events of the past few days, being interrupted when he heard the familiar voice of a particular War Princess.","Noah’s sharp eyes opened as he received a message from his ’Senior Sister’ Athena who was staying alongside him in a similar expansive dwelling on the same mountain.","\"Master is calling for us.\"","The message was curt and simple, Noah cutting off the mana he was supplying to {Fate’s Disciple} as he got up with a calm expression and began heading out.","It had been over a month since his intrusion into this 7th Celestial Star, the gains being nothing short of stupendous as he was able to get his hands on a myriad of skills and abilities.","This was especially so in the last month as after he passed the point of 10,000 Fate Lines, he began receiving techniques of even higher tier every few days as he advanced forward and collected more Fate Lines.","The one thing he didn’t like was the fact that no matter how many times he tried, condensing a maximum of around 100 Fate Lines was always the limit everyday, no matter how much longer he chose to active {Fate’s Disciple} with his expansive energy. This had only allowed him to amass a bit over 3000 Fate Lines this past month. While this seemed like a small number to him, it was actually a monstrous rate to anyone who heard it as it had exceeded any metric set before!","In the 7th Celestial Star, a rumor had begun to spread about a genius under the tutelage of Grandmaster Vredral that shone even brighter than the War Princess.","Noah thought about this War Princess that he had regularly sparred with this past month, one of the few things he came to learn about her being her love for battle. She never went past the relationship of a Senior Disciple teaching her Junior, and always kept their talks short as all that seemed to be on her mind was learning about fate and battle!","Even this was something unique as while Grandmaster Vredral watched their interactions, he mentioned to Noah how Athena had never given this level of treatment to any past disciples before. There was a level of interest and importance she placed on Noah as the both of them carried the title of those with a Noble Fate!","None of this mattered to Noah though, keeping his mind on the prize as he kept being spoiled with techniques and Spirit Stones freely.","Under the guise of his monstrous talent and the numerous treasures they handed him, he had publicly shown Grandmaster Vredral that he had a breakthrough into the Void Realm a few days ago!","The Grandmaster nodded deprecatingly at this level of genius as he advised Noah to take a slower pace and consolidate his foundation, having no need to rush through the ranks in this manner.","At this point in time though, Noah could be considered a full-fledged Red Robed Celestial, his Fate Lines being a bit over 13,000 at this moment!","His thoughts gradually came to a close as he neared the monastery at the peak of this Inquiring Mountain that was under the control of Grandmaster Vredral, coming face to face with the aged figure and a Red Robed Athena standing respectfully by the side.","The Grandmaster donned his usual golden robe that dr.a.p.ed over his body, hiding an aged figure that palpated with power. One could see the numerous wrinkles that covered his face, along with the abundant white hair and a long beard that shone with l.u.s.ter and vitality, making one think of both age and power.","\"You have surpassed all my expectations so far, and now have the chance to join in on an extraordinary mission that would have fallen solely onto the shoulders of Athena. Yet, this is also a mission that involves something special to you, thus granting you possible participation.\"","Grandmaster Vredral’s aged face shone with splendor as he spoke, Noah putting his right hand on his chest to respectfully greet him as he continued to listen. The Grandmaster waved his hands as a projection of two worlds appeared in front of them, Noah observing closely as he recognized a few features from one of the worlds!","\"We will test your proficiency in the Absolute Techniques of Fate that you have been studying to see whether you will qualify for this mission. In front of us lies your home, the World of Cultivation, and the Magus World. We have noticed a particularly significant level of disorder between these two worlds that could propel into something even more chaotic. Use [Fate Discernment] and tell us of your findings.\"","Noah’s eyes latched on to the projection of two Prime Worlds as they slowly rotated in front of him, his mind thinking to the skill that the Grandmaster mentioned, as well as the Absolute Technique it was connected to!","[Fate Discernment] was a singular ability from the biggest boon he had received from the Celestials so far, an Absolute Skill that actually allowed him to get even closer to the truth of this abstruse Supreme Law of Fate, containing abilities that finally opened his eyes to understand why Celestials held their monstrous level of power.","<strong><<Herald of Fate>> :: A technique of unknown origins that holds tremendous power. The mysteries of the Law of Fate can slowly be understood while this technique is in use, allowing for the user to gain knowledge of possibilities and the constant movements of the River of Fate. Abilities include Fate Discernment, Fate Traverser, Fate Concealment, and Fate Harvester.</strong>","<strong>[Fate Discernment] :: The clouded and abstruse fates of different entities or beings became easier to see. Strict conditions must be met for any usable information to be discerned.</strong>","<strong>[Fate Traverser] :: As one that is proficient in the workings of fate, you have more of a leeway over your own fate. This ability allows you to traverse to the most favorable outcome of your fate.</strong>","<strong>[Fate Concealment] :: The user’s own fate or the fates of their targets can be made hard to decipher, where others will not be able to find exactly where fate will take them.</strong>","<strong>[Fate Harverstor] :: An ill-advised ability given to the Herald of Fate that allows them to pluck away the good fate of others while steering away from a bad fate. It is an ability that requires enormous forethought, as it can lead the Herald of Fate into areas they should not peer into.</strong>","Over the past 30 days, he received four abilities in total that made the Absolute Skill, <<Herald of Fate>>!","This was the first Absolute Ability that Noah obtained which held the low amount of 4 abilities, but each one was shocking in itself as he received a first-hand look at how the Celestials operated and used their power.","The Grandmaster in front of him had asked him to use [Fate Discernment] on two planets, a tremendous task that would require an enormous source of essence and extreme use of Fate Lines to be able to perform well! Yet, this was his first barrier for this mission that was already on Athena’s shoulders.","He thought of the possibilities of what could have occurred between the World of Cultivation and the Magus World as a few ideas came to mind, but he focused on the task at hand as he prepared to use [Fate Discernment] on these two worlds.","Athena and Grandmaster Vredral were watching closely as they personally knew how hard it was to manipulate the Law of Fate and be able to discern the fates of entire planets.","Yet to Noah, this was the simplest thing as he did not even know how to manipulate mana, much less being able to manipulate the law of fate!","He did what was always made available to him- the act of simply casting the skills he held in his stat panel as the System he held did the rest, his thoughts simply watching as [Fate Discernment] moved the lines of fate in his body in unique ways as it began searching for something.","The ability mentioned that strict requirements had to be met for fate to be discerned, and the biggest requirement was that the caster had to know exactly what being or entity they were casting the skill for, as well as what they wanted to know from it!","Noah’s thoughts focused on the illusory images of the World of Cultivation and the Magus world as his eyes closed, a layer of golden light wrapping around him as he soon began to receive images and wisps of information that he never knew existed.","Grandmaster Vredral watched from the side while shaking his head in amazement, Athena looking forward as a sharp light passed through her eyes. Even to these monstrous beings, they had to admit that this disciple in front of them was too monstrous!","Being able to so seamlessly cast [Fate Discernement] and even be able to get it right on his first try, just exactly how much of a monster was he?!"]},{"number":340,"title":"Chapter 340: Chapter 339 - A Mission of Destruction!","paragraphs":["Bountiful information entered Noah’s mind as he focused on the images of the World of Cultivation and the Magus World. Golden light continued to converge and disperse from his body as [Fate Discernement] worked to show Noah something he never knew before.","This process continued for a whole 30 minutes before Noah finally came to the end of it, the end which caused him to feel a chill run down his back as eyes snapped open!","RUMBLE!","The Fate Lines within his body trembled from the unexpected impact as the Grandmaster reached out and clasped onto Noah’s body to stabilize his energies. His gaze was one of wonder as he looked at Noah like he was some prized possession.","\"What did you see?\"","Noah breathed heavily as he was not even acting, the things he had seen while using [Fate Discernment] being that shocking. His eyes calmed down as he replied.","\"I saw...the utter and complete annihilation of the World of Cultivation and the Magus World.\"","Yes!","Noah’s first use of this stupendous ability allowed him to see that in the near future, both of these two worlds would actually face destruction!","This thought drove him to cold sweats as these were two Prime Worlds, what exactly could bring worlds at this level to be destroyed? What exactly was coming in the future?","[Fate Discernement] had only shown him that at this moment in time, the flow of fate was going towards both of these worlds being destroyed. It did not tell him when, nor did he know how- he just held the simple knowledge that both of them would be destroyed. He looked over to the Grandmaster who had begun speaking in a serious tone.","\"In the past months, the major force of the Magus World has been harvesting the bodies of the cultivators from the World of Cultivation for their own uses.\"","The Grandmaster began, but Noah’s mind received a bolt as he recalled the Magi he had come across the moment he finished taking down the Devilish Time Unveiler in the World of Cultivation.","He had chanced upon the one called Black Serpent who was hunting the cultivators from the Time Immemorial Sect, choosing to save them as he devoured the Magi and actually obtained memories of their plans in the World of Cultivation!","Their memories told him that the Magi were holding grand designs to build up a force similar to the Punishers that the Celestials held. From the Celestial’s side, the Punishers were beings from the Elven Race that had lost their will, giving rise to a force that dutifully followed the orders of the Celestials with strong bodies to aid them.","The main powers of the Magus World sought to create a similar fighting force, and they found their experiments to be working the best while using the bodies of the cultivators from the World of Cultivation. Thus they had begun targeting them as they conducted a project to build creations that fully followed their orders while holding tremendous power!","Noah found out and knew about this plot more than two months ago, but he had simply put it out of his mind as he simply did not want to add another thing on his plate, focusing on infiltrating the Profound Astral Sect as he put this information about the Magus World in the back of his mind.","Yet now...he was receiving this same information again, and this time it was linked to the cause of the possible destruction of two Prime Worlds!","\"They hunted down and massacred countless cultivators before their doings were found out, creating a situation where both stars are now on the brink of war. We saw this increasing chaos and discerned fate just like you did just now but at an even higher level, coming to know that the result of this conflict between these two worlds would result in the destruction of both of them.\"","Noah was listening with rapt attention as numerous thoughts swirled in his head, still shocked at the fact that he knew [Fate Discernement] did not lie to him, and that these two worlds really were facing destruction.","\"But the chaos does not just end there. Both of these worlds have their own allies and enemies, where their conflict will embroil numerous Large World and Prime Worlds, contributing to a rapid increase in disorder that will only exacerbate across the surrounding stars.\"","The Grandmaster waved his hand as a golden plaque appeared on it, his aged eyes reading it as he revealed the contents of the mission that would shock many!","\"Thus, we have to act in accordance with our beliefs and bring about Order and Balance, preventing this chain of chaos that will begin with these two worlds at the center. This brought about the mission that would have fallen on Athena’s shoulders, and now it had fallen upon yours as well so that you can gain more experience on the workings of fate as you observe the changes to occur with the completion of this mission.\"","\"To prevent the chain of chaos and disorder, we have discerned fate and looked at numerous possibilities, the verdict coming down to a singular path that would allow for the most Order and Balance. The mission you two will carry out is to oversee the destruction of the Magus World before this conflict can continue any further.\"","...!","Noah couldn’t help but look towards this Grandmaster in shock as he continued with an impassive face.","\"The Magi have played with forces beyond their control while in a quest for power, their actions culminating to the eve of a war between two Prime Worlds that would go on to cause tens of billions of deaths over the next few weeks as many surrounding powers get pulled in. To prevent this fate and bring about Order and Balance, you two will use a Prime Warship to act out the Verdict of Celestials and bring an end to the instigators of this war.\"","THUMP!","Noah could feel his heart beat increasing as he continued to listen to the words of the Grandmaster, a shocking mission landing on his lap, and this mission required for the destruction of an entire planet!"]},{"number":341,"title":"Chapter 341: Chapter 340 - Chaos Reduction, Fear!","paragraphs":["Silence reigned in the area of the monastery that Noah, Athena, and the Grandmaster were in as the two were looking closely at Noah. The words of the Grandmaster repeated in his mind as even more came.","\"I realize the concept of a destruction of a world is very foreign to you, even more so when you have to act to personally cause it, but the fact that doing this would save the world that you came from should act as a buffer and cause you to come out of this with even more experience.\"","The Grandmaster held a passive look as he casually mentioned the destruction of an entire star along the lines of training. Noah’s mind went back to the Lost World that had received a similar verdict of destruction months ago, where Athena had been the one to initiate the destruction under the watch of a Celestial.","He was trying to think what exactly the Celestials had observed while using [Fate Discernment] that made them pass a verdict of a destruction of a world similar to what they were doing to the Magus World now.","Noah took a deep breath as he looked at the Grandmaster while wrapping up his thoughts, speaking in a thankful but difficult tone thereafter.","\"I’ll have to thank you first Grandmaster, for keeping in mind the World of Cultivation amidst this chaos. I will gladly do anything to prevent the destruction of the world I was born in, but...\"","He looked at the impassive Athena by the side who was watching him with a piercing expression and the impassive Grandmaster as he continued.","\"The destruction of the entirety of the Magus World...is it really the only way to stop this possible chaos that would come from this conflict?\"","\"..\"","Silence reigned in the room as for the first time since his entrance into the 7th Celestial Star, a look of disappointment appeared on the face of the Grandmaster as he observed Noah. This look only came briefly before it changed to one of pondering, looking towards Noah is an understanding tone as if the powerful figure had realized something.","\"Your talent has been so bright that I had forgotten you have only been here for a month, and haven’t been given the supplementary teachings on the best ways to reduce chaos.\"","The Grandmaster pointed to the illusory figures of the rotating World of Cultivation and the Magus World as he continued.","\"Over the thousands of years that we have been influencing fate and honing our techniques, we have come to create the best course of actions that we follow strictly. Such actions range from the destruction of worlds to the saving of numerous more. IT is these actions have guaranteed a high level of success in reducing chaos and instituting order.\"","\"When it comes to a case like these two planets whose conflict will only expand to the surrounding stars, the routine course of action is the destruction of the star and the beings responsible for instigating such chaos.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes gazed upon this Grandmaster as he controlled his thoughts and put on a quizzical expression while asking.","\"Grandmaster, what about those that had nothing to do with the course of events that the major force of the Magus World undertook against the World of Cultivation? What about the families of poor unknown beings that had no hand to play in this war? Why should they also face death along with those responsible?\"","The Grandmaster looked at him with an impassive face as he replied.","\"You are not the first disciple to have questioned the destruction of an entire star as the most suitable method to reign in the caused chaos and reinstitute order. I will tell you now that besides the complete destruction of all those responsible, there is another factor that weighs in heavily to correct the chaos and establish order. That factor is...the fear that creeps into the hearts of all the neighboring stars and any that would hold similar designs like those who were just utterly destroyed.\"","...!","That’s right!","This was the way the Celestials had found to be the most useful in reducing the chaos instigated by a particular planet while also bringing about an era of peace and order that was achieved through the fear of those that would know of the results of actions that caused death and chaos!","The destruction of those involved in their entirety would stop any future possibilities of them rising up again and continuing a cycle of chaos, while their actions acted as a message to all those withholding similar grand designs for power and made them never even put such ideas to light.","\"We work to bring order, and look at our actions to make sure that we save the most lives in any given situation. This current situation where the erupting war between these two planets will cause deaths in the tens of billions across multiple stars...the verdict took the course of action that would save tens of billions of lives by taking away a few billion from the origin of this instigated chaos.\"","\"If we do not act, tens of billions will die. With our action to destroy the Magus World that is responsible, only a few billion beings die while an era of peace and order can be established on the surrounding stars as those who consider themselves powerful are reminded yet again of the result of causing chaos. With all of this in the picture, why would we not act? Why would we not move to save tens of billions of beings?\"","The impassive gaze of the Celestial Grandmaster and the piercing Athena closed in on Noah as they observed him closely. His hand was placed on his chin as he seemed to be pondering, no words coming out from him as a reply!","He was thinking about the reasoning of the Celestials and the results achieved from their actions, even if they seemed vile and horrendous. Just what exactly was the right course of action?"]},{"number":342,"title":"Chapter 342: Chapter 341 - Other means to achieve the same goal?","paragraphs":["With the intervening of the Celestials, tens of billions of lives would be saved. All that it cost was the death of those involved, along with the destruction of their star as they also served to send a message that would discontinue any more thoughts of chaos and disorder!","So why should they not move to save so many beings? Should they let tens of billions die?","Noah actually did not find an answer to the Grandmaster’s question, his mind going towards the Lost World yet again as he wondered- what exactly did the Celestials foresee with this world and its World Engines that they passed the verdict for its destruction?","It was only a Large World that was not that well known, so it didn’t serve to send a message to anyone important. He was also moving in this world, which made him wonder if the fate they discerned had something to do with him as well!","Because of the actions of the mysterious Karmic Sect Master Inuit, Noah had survived from the planet that was Spatially Locked as Athena pushed the switch to blast it to pieces- which meant that their purpose of destroying everything had failed, and whatever they were trying to prevent from what they had foreseen would still come to pass.","The thought of this mystery made Noah question many things as his ideals were still the same. As of this moment, he had not turned into some mad man who would agree with the destruction of an entire star and all those in it, even if they had nothing to do with the chaos being caused. This was the same reason he stood against the Celestials-because of their rampant destruction of the Lost World without a care for who was in it and whether they deserved that verdict!","He had obtained [Fate Discernment] himself now and understood more of the reasoning of the Celestials for their actions, where he would pierce through the veils of mystery to find out exactly what they feared from the Lost World that made them call for its destruction. But at this moment, for the Magus World that was at hand, numerous ideas floated in Noah’s mind as he finally lifted his head and met the impassive gaze of the Grandmaster.","\"This disciple is slightly eccentric, and I have only gotten where I am today by looking at things from multiple different angles. I have absolutely no issue carrying out the mission of the destruction of the world responsible for the future chaos that would allow for the destruction of the world I was born in and tens of billions of beings. But what if...there was another way to achieve this same level of reduction of chaos, the saving of lives, and the instillment of fear to prevent future disorder?\"","\"...\"","The Grandmaster and Athena looked closely at him as they remained the same, indicating for Noah to continue as his gaze moved between them.","\"You mentioned the destruction of the star achieves all the goals- wiping out those responsible while also sending a message. What if...we can send that message at the same level, if not more, and cause an even bigger reduction of chaos?\"","Athena’s eyes opened widely at these bold claims as the Grandmaster looked on while a sharp light passed through his eyes. He looked at Noah as he spoke.","\"Let me guess, you want us to simply send our interstellar warsh.i.p.s and Celestial Grandmasters to reap the lives of the powerful leading organization of the Magus World and let that stand as a message? It will not be effective, nor as efficient as simply using a Prime Warship to simply destroy the Star.\"","The words were laced with a reprimanding tone of an Elder teaching a Junior, Noah shaking his head as he replied with a determined expression.","\"No. Do not send in any battlesh.i.p.s or Grandmasters. To achieve the goal of punishing those responsible for this chaos while sending a message that will bring about order across the stars...send me- a single Celestial Disciple at the Void Realm to take the heads of those responsible.\"","...!","The Grandmaster’s eyes narrowed as he looked closely at Noah, a wide smile appearing on his face as he spoke out.","\"You realize that the most powerful beings in the Magus World are at the peak of Soul Forging Realm? I would not even be surprised if they had a being half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm for them to be so bold as to think they could get away with such actions under our eyes.\"","The power of the Celestial Grandmaster came out in waves as he said this, his words revealing the next rank above Soul Forging, which was Domain Expansion!","This was the same realm that this single Grandmaster Vredral, who was just a single Grandmaster among the many on the 7th Celestial Star, held! From Noah’s and Athena’s Void Rank, this being surpassed Soul and stood at the peak of the Domain Rank!","With his abilities as a Celestial, one would dread when they realized the power that allowed them to even fight those above their levels as his presence became all the more terrifying!","Noah stopped thinking about the realm of this being for a moment before he continued.","\"That is precisely why, Grandmaster. Send in a single Void FRealm Celestial Disciple to utterly destroy the forces of those responsible. We will achieve the goal of destroying this force and stopping the war, while sending an even stronger message about the power of Celestials who could raise a single Disciple to have the power to wipe out the major force of a Prime World.\"","\"...\"","Noah looked at the gaze of the Grandmaster that was still unconvinced as he squeezed his mind for more ideas and continued.","\"Let them know that Celestials do not just rely on their powerful Warsh.i.p.s to destroy those causing chaos. Let them know that even a single disciple at a lowly Void Realm will be enough to rectify chaos caused at the planetary level. This message can be instilled even more clearly by broadcasting this entire event to the surrounding powers that are involved in this issue!\"","The eyes of the Grandmaster shone at Noah’s last set of words, his gaze being more profound as he seemed to be pondering. He looked at Noah briefly later as he said a set of words that held the tone of not being able to be denied.","\"You are a tremendously unique genius, so I will give you this chance as a lesson to show you that the things we have established and done for centuries are the most efficient. I will use [Fate Discernment] when your actions are done to see whether they were effective in reducing chaos as it would have been if we simply destroyed the Magus World, and you can even check this yourself as soon as you finish.\"","Noah’s figure stood up as he placed his right hand on his chest as a sign of respect for being allowed this chance, the Grandmaster continuing with a smile as he watched this.","\"Since we can’t have a genius like you accidentally dying, Athena will still accompany you on this mission. There would be many beings above your levels in this world after all, and this could serve as a great method of training.\"","Noah’s eyes shone as he heard this and looked at this still impassive Athena who simply just nodded while looking at his with an unreadable expression.","\"Broadcast your actions to the surrounding powers huh?\"","The Grandmaster muttered under his breath as he found himself thinking this idea of his disciple was at least interesting, even if it might not work!","But for the sake of a lesson for this incredible genius, they would put it to the test. Would his proposed idea be enough to achieve the same level of reduction of chaos and the instillment of fear into the surrounding powers while saving the same amount of lives, or would something entirely different occur?","A wide smile appeared on the face of the being at the peak of Domain Expansion Realm as he looked at the bowing disciple and the valiant Athena by the side, his mind already working and sending multiple messages for a change of plans and new preparation to be put underway for a particular mission!"]},{"number":343,"title":"Chapter 343: Chapter 342 - An Inevitable Conflict","paragraphs":["Across the dark and shining vastness of space, the Magus World floated serenely, its position surrounded by numerous stars, with some being tens of thousands of miles away and others being more than a couple hundred thousand miles away. It was a Prime World that was known for its power and unique use of Rune Magic and Bloodlines by the many Magi populating it.","At this moment in time though, a heavy atmosphere surrounded the Magus World as in the central location of the Order of the Black Serpent, the organization that stood at the peak of power in the Magus World- a meeting was taking place as a few being were running back and forth busily.","In an enormous castle several levels high, a dark-haired Magus with shining red eyes sat at the centermost seat as surrounding her were an assortment of different colored Magi, each palpating with their own levels of strength. She was listening to the hectic discussion of her people as her gaze was cold, a trace of anger being visible on her face.","\"Quiet.\"","Her single word sent the busy and bustling room into silence as they all looked towards her. She glanced at each of their faces that she could observe a trace of fear from, and this fear was not caused by her.","\"This is an issue between us and another world, the Celestials would not intervene for something like this. As for the World of Cultivation, just my power alone can stand against all the three Sect Masters that are still fighting for control of that world, so this war will undoubtedly end in our favor.\"","Her words were crisp and clear, clearing up some of the gazes of the Magi in the room while some remained unconvinced.","\"...there have been some rumors that a disciple of the Profound Astral Sect joined the ranks of the Celestials. What if this causes their intrusion?\"","The dark-haired woman with sharp red eyes who was the leader of the Order of the Black Serpent that ruled the Magus World, the Snake Queen Caara- looked at the powerful Magus at the Soul Forging Realm who had spoked up. This was one of the few beings standing at a similar level as her and would still have the guts to speak up their minds. She replied as her body wiggled amorously in the central seat.","\"You all fear the Celestials too much. They care for their reputation too much to make a move on a Prime World right now, and the Dark Expanse is keeping them plenty busy as I can already smell the signs of a coming war. We have no need for worrying. What we are doing is not too far off from what the Celestials did with the Elven Race to create Punishers. The surrounding powers will only realize their hypocrisy if they move against us with that reasoning.\"","\"We will continue building up our forces with the bodies of Cultivators we have obtained so far, and we will obtain even more bodies in the war that should fully begin in the next few days.\"","An invisible red aura permeated from her as it went on to ease the fear of the beings in the surrounding, her gaze that of extreme hunger for power as she repeated to the room full of Magi.","\"Our world and power has been stuck at the level of a Prime World for too long, this war is exactly what we needed to advance to the next stage, so we will use this chance to the fullest!\"","OOOOOH!","A resonation of essence erupted as the amorous Magus Leader shook the fear from those in her organization, her curvaceous body standing up as her red eyes adopted dangerous vertical slits that one would only find in the most vile of snakes.","\"Prepare our own Punishers. When the war begins, we shall have the cultivators taste death from people of their own world as we amass even more bodies. We shall let the name of the Order of the Black Serpent resound across the Prime World, we shall let them know of our Ancestor’s Bloodline and our fearsome Magic!\"","OOOOH!","A rallying speech continued for another few minutes in the major force controlling the Magus World as they prepared for War, their leaders not fully knowing exactly what fate their actions lead down to.","In the opposing world that they were facing off against, the leaders of the three most powerful sects in the World of Cultivation were meeting as they discussed with heavy tones on what to do for the coming future.","Two of them were half a step into the Soul Forging Realm, with only a single one actively stepping into the Soul Realm as their power paled in comparison to the enemies that stood against them.","\"Sect Master Rudolf, why do seem even calmer than all of us even though your power is only second amongst us?\"","The Sect Master of the Sword Sky Sect held sharp eyes that were filled with worry for the future as he questioned the Sect Master of the Profound Astral Sect who smiled mysteriously.","\"I know you have all heard some rumors since our Elders have been somewhat irresponsible, but the word of one of our Core Disciples joining the Celestials are not false.\"","...!","\"What?!\"","\"Truly?!\"","The figures of the two Sect Masters stood up and let out exhaustive exclamations as their faces changed to that of happiness as if it was their own sect disciples that had joined the Celestials.","But they knew what this signified!","If...just if they had this sort of connection to the powerful force that was overseeing the Light Expanse, maybe this unwinnable war against a world that held multiple powerhouses stronger than them would actually not be so hopeless.","\"Have you sent word to your disciple?\"","The Sect Master of the Sword Sky Sect asked hurriedly, Sect Master Rudolf returning a smile as he spoke mysteriously.","\"I have, and gentlemen...the path in front of us is bright and filled with the light of the Celestials.\"","...!","The forces of one world felt relief and ecstatic as they looked upon the force overseeing the Light Expanse as a force filled with righteousness and mercy as they hoped for those murdering their people to be brought to justice, while one world held slight worry for this same force as they called them hypocrites who would not dare move with everyone watching.","What they didn’t know was that for the coming conflict...every single being would be made to watch something that would be etched onto the recesses of their memories for as long as they lived!"]},{"number":344,"title":"Chapter 344: Chapter 343 - Setting Off!","paragraphs":["In the expansive Inquiring Mountain that was under the control of Grandmaster Vredral, a golden ship that was much different than normally seen warsh.i.p.s was lifting off into the skies.","One could observe an array of dangerous cannons made out of unknown materials, the runic markings inlaid all around them contributing to an ancient feel that only showed a glimpse of their power.","The entire vessel was larger than 2 kilometers, its contrasting colors of red and gold plastered on its smooth rectangular appearance making it eye-catching as it passed through the protective layer of the 7th Celestial Star and shot off into the vastness of space.","On this specialized Interstellar Ship that was called a Prime Warship, Noah was standing beside a girl with a brilliant aura that was only enhanced by her bronze skin that did not seem to hold a single blemish. She held smooth dark hair that was tied up in a simple ponytail, adding to this simple look even more as she only adorned a red robe.","Behind them in the room that held the central command of the Prime Warship, Grandmaster Vredral could be seen using wisps of his expansive energy to propel the ship forward as it became a streak of light in the vastness of space.","His pondering gaze was on the back of the stupendous Genius that had turned the heads of many on the 7th Celestial Star, his potential quickly making those in the upper ranks compare him to Athena and the plans they had for her.","Similar to the War Princes, they had discerned that Crixus was a being that held a Noble Fate, a position that very few would hold in the centuries that pass. Those with a Noble Fate held very distinct positions as it was extremely hard to discern their future, making it critical to raise them well in the eyes of the Celestial.","Vredral had only given this young Celestial the chance to try his new method of reducing chaos in the upcoming conflict for this reason, as he knew of the unpredictability that those with a Noble Fate could bring. It would serve as a lesson should he fail, and on the off chance that his method reduced the level of chaos and deaths as much as what they originally planned with the complete destruction of the Magus World?","A smile appeared on the Grandmaster’s face at this thought as he observed Crixus turning and talking towards Athena.","---","Noah’s now calm aura of a Celestial bounced off his body as the abundant Fate Lines brought forth a unique air, his face turning towards Athena as he fished for more information.","\"Have you done a mission similar to what this one was originally supposed to be? Have you overseen the destruction of an entire world?\"","An indiscernible light crossed Athena’s eyes as she heard this, staring towards the constantly changing vastness of space as she replied calmly.","\"Once before. On a Large World that went under the name of the Lost World.\"","\"Oh? What did their forces do?\"","An interested look appeared on Noah’s face as he listened closely to finally get the history for the reason of the destruction of the Lost World.","\"The world was first brought to our attention because of the beings of a few other Worlds that they held skirmishes with, coming to our knowledge that they were creating Cursed Items which directly went against the Universal Laws. Usually, this alone isn’t enough to warrant the verdict of destruction, but when a Grandmaster used [Fate Discernement] on this world, they came to find a terrible fate that would arise from this world.\"","\"They foresaw that a being would rise to usher in a new rule above this Lost World, going on to use the Cursed Items created from this world to usher in an era of chaos across the Light Expanse.\"","...!","Noah’s mind shook briefly as he heard these words, many thoughts coursing through his mind as he continued to listen.","\"The Verdict for the world’s destruction was made soon after, the mission of overseeing it falling on my shoulders. We were successful in reducing chaos with its destruction, with no more information being able to be ascertained after its destruction.\"","Noah outwardly nodded outside while an array of thoughts rapidly came and went in his mind. Athena’s words possibly held a shocking meaning as they repeated in his mind, a big question appearing as even though he didn’t want to think too highly of himself, he was most likely the being that the Celestials foresaw to take the reigns of the Lost World after he defeated Baal, using their World Engines as he was already planning to right at this moment!","This thought felt ludicrous, but it was also the most straightforward one! Through [Fate Discernment], the Celestials had foreseen him coming to power, and they had almost succeeded in killing him in the Lost World...were it not for one particular Sect Master Inuit.","\"...\"","Noah adopted a thoughtful look as he stared out into the changing vastness of space as the Prime Warship they were on got ever closer to the Magus World, a variety of feelings coursing through his mind as he realized even though it was not his fault, the reason that the Celestials destroyed an entire World with billions of beings was because of him!","This thought lingered in his mind as he tried to get past it and look forward to the future. He could not change what occurred then, but he was trying to look at the possibilities of changing things now. There was another world in the near future that was marked for death, and this one also had a singular force that was the target for the Celestials.","For the sake of tying off all loose ends, permanently cutting off the cycle of chaos, and sending a message of fear to the surrounding powers to reduce any further disorder- the Celestials would accept the loss of a few billion lives. They justified this because were they not to act at all, the chaos that would unravel would cause tens of billions of lives.","Noah knew they weren’t wrong, as he himself had confirmed this with [Fate Discernment]! But...he just didn’t want those that were completely innocent finding their world placed under a spatial lock as they watched destruction close in. He did not want a repeat of the Lost World where he saved the Ocean Master and tens of thousands of others in Atlantis, but left behind billions more.","In this brief moment in time, his humanity pushed back the ever so expanding bloodline of the Vampyre Progenitor that gradually made him colder and more calculating as he was now focused on achieving the same goal as the Celestials, but through different means that did not require the destruction of an entire star and all those in it.","But this possible path...would be much bloodier, and much more cruel for the instigators who would have just faced quick deaths.","A gaze of determination overcame his face as he looked forward, the reality of the past and future much clearer in his mind."]},{"number":345,"title":"Chapter 345: Chapter 344 - A Show for All to See","paragraphs":["The Prime Warship was much faster than the vessels Noah had been in before, where in just a few hours they were nearing the location of the Magus World.","The outline of this Prime World was slightly bigger than the World of Cultivation, a thin barrier enveloping it that looked ready to break at any time. It was less for protection and more of a message that they held the power and strength to erect any kind of barrier over their world.","The Prime Warship that was capable of laying waste to entire stars appeared near the Magus World silently, its enormous size of more than 2 kilometers paling in comparison to the grandness of an entire planet, but the weapons it held still as terrifying!","The instant it appeared, Grandmaster Vredral calmly tapped a few things on a red crystal connected to the Prime Warship, its many weapons locked and loaded as a few specialized ones released a film of golden light to rapidly begin wrapping around the entirety of the Magus World.","---","The Snake Queen Caara who was overseeing the continuing operations in the Magus world was the first the feel the changes as her awareness was much more sensitive than others, realizing a second late that a spatial lock was rapidly spreading throughout the Magus World!","Her face turned ashen as her gaze shot to the skies, piercing through the layers as the snake eyes located an enormous ship with runic markings and weapons that would cause fear to creep into any knowledgeable being’s soul.","The vessel that towered over the Magus World paled in comparison to the world’s size, but its significance caused the Snake Queen to see an image as if this single ship was bigger than the entire Planet!","This was because this Prime Warship was known and feared among the knowledgeable powers of the Light Expanse. It was the only piece of technology that was unique to the Celestials, its power being unmatched as when piloted by the powerful Grandmasters that made up the ranks of Celestials, this vessel could lay waste to entire worlds!","This Prime Warship could only be piloted by a being in the Domain Expansion realm, the level of energy required being immense for anyone lower. Along with this requirement of energy, the unique essence of Celestials was required before one could ever get close to this spectacular weapon of mass destruction.","Its appearance above the Magus World only meant one thing, and the Snake Queen who stood at the top of the Order of the Black Serpent understood this as her ashen face became enraged.","\"Hypocrites!\"","She screamed out towards nothingness as the other powerhouses on the Magus World quickly noticed the situation, their gazes turning to those of despair as they understood what was about to happen.","\"No!\"","\"They can’t!\"","Fearful feelings of terror began to creep into the hearts of many powerful beings all over the Magus World as they expected a horrendous scene to occur in the next moment, but minutes passed as nothing else but the solid spatial lock that covered the entire planet appeared thereafter.","Some breathed easier as they tried to send communications out to their allies to see if any would be capable of stopping the hands of the Celestials that had appeared above the Magus World, but no communications were coming in or out of this locked world as they watched on helplessly.","The horrendous activation of weapons they had come to fear over the years did not activate as the beating heart of the Snake Queen still held a furious expression as she looked towards the skies. Her expression remained one of rage as it didn’t seem like she feared death one bit if it came for her!","Many of the powerhouses of the Magus World looked on to see what their fate would be among the despairing atmosphere as they observed an enormous illusory screen begin to materialize right above the Magus World.","This screen was humongous in size, even passing the size of the Prime Warship as any beings at the Void Rank or above would be able to observe things with clarity as long as they focused on the skies. The image in the huge illusory screen became clearer within a few seconds as they observed it to be the point of view of two red-robed figures.","One was a dark haired man who held a calm expression, the other was a dark-skinned woman that had a tight ponytail waving valiantly behind her as her eyes shimmer with light as they looked forward to what the screen was showing- which was simply the view of these two beings as they stared at the Magus World from the ship they were on!","This mystical illusory screen did not just appear in front of the eyes of the powerful forces of the Magus World, another one just like it appeared above the World of Cultivation. Another one appeared on the Underworld, another one appeared on the Automaton World...the illusory screen showing the point of view of two Red Robed Celestials was being portrayed across many of the surrounding Prime Worlds that held connections in any way to the Magus World and the World of Cultivation, even adding along other Prime Worlds that simply held many powerhouses.","The Lone Moon, The Infantile Globe, The Storm Territories, The Burning Archipelago, The Flameborn World...numerous Prime Worlds were introduced to this humongous illusory screen that showed two beings looking at the expansive Magus World.","The knowledgeable powerhouses of these worlds felt an eerie atmosphere as they recognized what the red robes signified, their assumption confirmed the moment this ridiculous capability of allowing an illusory screen like this that portray an entirely different environment hundreds of miles away above their worlds confirming all of their thoughts as they wondered just who had earned the wrath of the Celestials!","What they didn’t know was that to make this a possibility, Grandmaster Vredral had instructed numerous Celestials to direct Interstellar Warsh.i.p.s besides the Prime Warship he was in with Crixus and Athena to move out to the numerous Prime Worlds in the surrounding quadrant that the Magus World was in.","This amounted to tens of Interstellar Warsh.i.p.s being spread out to cover the distances of over a hundred Prime Worlds that either had connections to or knew of the Magus World and the World of Cultivation, as well as the war that was brewing with these two powers at the center.","These numerous sh.i.p.s held the technology similar to what Noah had observed them do outside the doors of the First Realm of Hell, the technology to portray an illusory screen for many to see. This same technology was being used now as numerous sh.i.p.s traversed near numerous Prime World to portray an illusory screen that showed a video with extreme clarity.","The Grandmaster held slight interest when Noah further explained how he wanted to enact his different path that wasn’t the destruction of the entire planet, and that was to put on a show.","To prevent the destruction of an entire world while only taking down those responsible, and at the same time achieving the Celestial’s goal of using fear to reduce the compounding chaos...Noah would put on a show for all to see!"]},{"number":346,"title":"Chapter 346: Chapter 345 - Merciful Saints, Cruel Tyrants","paragraphs":["Many of the beings seeing the screen above the skies of their worlds recognized the image of the War Princess that was already widely known, the one that became even more renowned recently as she took the number one spot in the recent Infernal Hunt.","A few recognized the image of Crixus, being mostly those in the World of Cultivation as they looked on with shining eyes as this disciple appeared grandly on the screen.","In the Underworld, the curvaceous Elena was surrounded by forces of Pureblood Vampyres as they looked on with faces of solemnity, her infatuated gaze landing on the dark haired male as intense lights shone from her eyes. There was a small miniaturized penguin sitting on her shoulders as its beak rose high, its beady eyes trying to focus on the screen above as its Saint Realm essence could not see the image as clearly.","The monstrous figures of the other Harbingers that held different transformations after absorbing the bloodlines of Vampyres were also observing the screen above them, with a few missing it as they were in the Infernal Realm along with the Abhorred Lich Emperor continuing to farm Skill Points!","Their eyes gazed at this stupendous illusory screen as something finally changed.","\"The Magus World has sown an enormous amount of chaos and had received the Verdict of destruction long ago. But...\"","A resounding voice began to echo from the illusory screen, spreading through the targeted worlds that Grandmaster Vredral wanted to spread the message across as he continued to speak.","\"...my new disciple wanted to try things a different way, and bring justice using a brand new path. That is what you are about to watch- justice for those responsible for sowing chaos, and the return of Order and Balance from it.\"","His words finished as the faces of many powerful beings turned somber, their gazes fully locking onto the events that had begun on the screen as a sense of unease spread throughout.","\"The disciples to enact this Verdict will be Athena and Crixus, disciples at the Void Realm who will descend into the Magus World to bring to justice the forces responsible for this chaos.\"","...","The influential and powerful figures turned quizzical for the first time as they thought they had misheard something. They knew that the force that controlled the Magus World was the Order of the Black Serpent, a powerful organization that held numerous Void Realm powerhouses, and even a few beings at the Soul Forging Realm standing at the top.","To carry out this verdict of the Celestials, only two Void Realm disciples were being sent out to combat all of these forces?","Skeptical looks began to appear among the faces of many beings across the stars as they wondered exactly what type of message the Celestials were trying to send with this action.","In the humongous Prime Warship that Noah and Athena stood on, a small door opened in front of them as their bodies became enveloped in the aura of the Void Realm, their figures floating out serenely as they began flying towards the Magus World. This image caused the eyes of many to skip a beat as they realized the Celestials were truly serious about sending in two talented disciples at the Void Realm to stand against powerhouses that reached the Soul Forging Realm!","They watched on with rapt attention as the illusory screen closely followed the viewpoint of Noah and Athena, the features of the Magus World becoming more and more clear as their figures descended down and passed through the golden film of light that was now covering the entirety of the world.","This barrier of golden light did not just prevent spatial movements, any being that tried to break past it without the permission of the Domain Expansion expert that was piloting the Prime Warship would find their actions being all for naught as the barrier locked everything in completely.","The instant the figures of Noah pierced through the stratosphere of the Magus World, they began descending down in a particular direction as both Noah and Athena were using [Fate Discernement] to see where they aura of chaos originated from the most. Their findings were leading them directly to the central lands of the Magus World where the Order of the Black Serpent was located!","RUMBLE!","Their bodies trembled with essence as they shot force speedily, soon arriving at the skies above grand buildings of a now tense capital. At the forefront of these forces, the Snake Queen looked towards Noah and Athena with a looked of furious unwillingness as her overflowing aura began to rise from her body in a maddening fashion.","\"This is how you hypocrites wish to humiliate us?! Sending weak disciples to send the message of your strength?\"","Her voice was laced with poison as she was not even speaking directly towards Noah and Athena, simply speaking in their direction as her words were aimed at the Celestials and all those that she knew would most likely be watching a similar illusory screen like the one they were seeing.","\"Don’t you all see? These hypocritical celestials have no moral compass! They will kill whoever they wish under the name of justice and order. In this Light Expanse, they are simply tyrants! It may be my world targeted today, but what’s to stop them from doing the same thing to your worlds next? What’s to stop them from proclaiming a verdict of destruction on the Flameborn World or the Underworld in a few days?!\"","Her unwillingness was portrayed in her voice as her figure became flanked by two beings of similar rank to her. One was a middle-aged man with furrowed brows that held a tall stature, the other was a scantily dressed woman in her prime that held a similar venomous look on her face.","The many worlds being shown the events occurring in the Magus World reflected as they heard the words of the leader of the Order of the Black Serpent, the one to reply being Athena as around her, numerous Empyrean Guards had begun to appear en masse.","\"We, the Celestials, care not whether you see us as saints or abominable tyrants.\"","RUMBLE!","A golden hue covered the skies above them as tens of thousands of Fate Lines could barely be discernible by those proficient in fate, others simply seeing the aura that Athena carried increase boundlessly as the numerous golden figures she summoned turned into streaks of light that fused into her body.","\"What we care about is the Order and Balance of this Light Expanse, the balance of this increasingly chaotic universe.\"","A brilliant golden light shone out as the golden lights finished fusing into her, the appearance of a resplendent figure covered head to toe with a golden armor, expansive shining light wings, and a pulsating golden hammer making its appearance at it aimed itself towards the three figures that fate pointed the most chaos towards, these same figures that were quickly being surrounded by numerous beings at the Void and Saint Realm to protect them on all sides from the attackers in the skies.","\"You all...have sown discord and chaos in the surrounding stars, and your verdict is...death!\"","RUMBLE!","A brilliant light shone out as she finished these words, Noah glancing at the thousands of beings he could sense above this single central building where the Snake Queen stood at the forefront of, tens of thousands more moving around this central base of the Magi who all held an aura of chaos on their bodies.","Accompanying their ranks were the lifeless bodies of numerous cultivators that wore robes hiding their features, many of them mixing into the ranks of the Magi as they followed their given commands lifelessly!","Noah observed all of this as he sighed and began summoning numerous Empyrean Guards himself, committing to fully saving this Magus World from complete destruction. But for him to be able to do that, he had to dye its central lands red from the blood of all those responsible for initiating this chaos to begin with!"]},{"number":347,"title":"Chapter 347: Chapter 346 - Devouring Winged Serpent","paragraphs":["The Snake Queen Caara that stood at the top of the Magus World stared at the golden figures shimmering with light as the ideology of the Celestials reached her heart with extreme precision.","They cared not how they were perceived, as long as beings feared and obeyed them, as long as they knew of their terrible power- this was all that mattered! Her furious expression softened as it soon became devoid of emotions, her senses catching the many Magi that were grouped all over the central base cl.u.s.ter around her as they prepared to fight against the two invading Celestials. Looking at this scene, something seemed to have clicked in the mind of the Snake Queen as words devoid of emotions left her red lips as her body began to bubble forth with power.","\"So be it. [Devouring Winged Serpent].\"","RUMBLE!","A red light shot to the skies as a skill was cast, an immense aura overflowing with power at the Soul Forging Realm was released maddeningly!","This aura held a significance that could be felt by every being around, as those standing at the Soul Forging Realm had stably begun strengthening their souls, the aura of power they released causing a coagulating pressure to descend down upon those that stood against them.","This was the power of the soul, an abstruse force that very few could grasp!","But the beings that the snake queen was up against held even more fearsome techniques that allowed them to use the Supreme Law of Fate, the numerous Fate Lines that they condensed on their bodies giving them the capability to inflict Soul Damage, as well as granting them a level of protection that nobody else had!","The aura of the Snake Queen continued to overflow as Noah observed her body begin to expand rapidly, numerous dark red scales that were meters thick enlarging at an alarming speed as this being began the transformation into a monstrous creature.","On either side of her expanding figure, two Magi floated in the skies as they looked at the Snake Queen’s transformation, their expressions those of unwillingness as they turned towards the shimmering figures of Noah and Athena, and even further above to the horrible Warship that could disintegrate them and their entire planet.","They did not fear the two Void Realm beings in the skies as they were confident in their own power at the Soul Forging Realm, but what they feared was the actions these celestials would ultimately take once they killed the two disciples in the air!","They felt like an aura of death was approaching them as their gazes focused on the humongous ship that was barely discernible in space, but their gazes were in the wrong direction as this would most definitely not be the cause of their deaths.","The two Magi activated their own Bloodline abilities as their bodies also expanded and began to change, numerous scales spreading as one held a fully black aura, with another shining with a red light as their sizes quickly exploded to tens of meters.","The numerous powerful beings watching across worlds wore grim faces at this show of power, the illusory screens above their stars showing the majestic form that the leader of the Magus World had transformed into- and it was the terrible form of an expansive Nine-Headed Winged Serpent!","ROAAAR!","The air trembled at the resounding roars of its numerous heads as the [Devouring Winged Serpent] floated magnificently in the air, its nine heads waving menacingly as each one shone with its own color that symbolized expert control of multiple elements.","Many watched this overwhelming power at the Soul Forging Realm as they affirmed that the opponents the Celestials sent were extremely mismatched. They knew the power of the being called the Snake Queen from rumors and the spies, but they never witnessed it close hand as her grandeur was clearly portrayed in the illusory screens above the numerous stars. This was affirmed even more as her resounding voice that was laced with fearsome power rang out as if she was standing right in front of them.","\"If that hypocritical grandmaster above doesn’t come down to face me himself, then he can simply come to collect the bodies of his disciples along with mine!\"","Yes! The Devouring Winged Serpent floating in the skies knew that with the intrusion of the Celestials, she, along with all of her forces, would be facing their death today!","But still, amidst this terrifying feeling of unfairness and despair at a greater power coming out of nowhere spouting what seemed like bullshit in their ears, they could not do anything to stop it and had to simply accept it. So they would accept it...but they would also take down others as well, especially the disciples of the ones responsible.","The numerous eyes of the Devouring Winged Serpent focused on the shimmering golden figures of two beings standing less than a mile away from her, her tremendous body nearing 40 meters in size trembling with power as it was joined side by side by two slightly less fearsome Winged Serpents.","The two Soul Forging Realm Magi that were standing beside her had transformed into a Dark Winged Serpent and a Flame Winged Serpent as they each adopted their own spectacular forms that were just a few meters smaller in size than her own.","The Dark Winged Serpent had tendrils of darkness rolling through its scales as its body pulsed with menacing power, while the Flame Winged Serpent had molten flames spurting out all around its body, rapidly increasing the temperature of the surroundings.","An overwhelming feeling of strength released from them as slowly, the gaps in the skies began to be filled with numerous different forms and colors of snakes and basilisks that held fearsome expressions!","The forces of the Order of the Black Serpent had fully withdrawn their fear as they used the power of their bloodlines to transform into a frightening army of an assortment of fearsome serpents.","The skies soon became blotted with dots of beings from the central base of power of the Magus World, their numbers nearing tens of thousands as they ranged from Legendary and all the way to Void Realm. Among their ranks, the dead cultivators devoid of souls that were turned into beings similar to the Celestial’s punishers were filling the gaps of these ferocious Magi.","These were only the members of the Order of the Black Serpent that held power above Legendary Rank, with millions more that held lower power levels spread out across the central lands of the Magus World as they watched the unfolding events with uncertainty and fear.","Leading the gathered forces in the sky, at the forefront was a Devouring Winged Serpent at the peak of the Soul Forging Realm, her power seemingly being able to overflow into the next realm at any moment. Flanking her two sides was a Dark Winged Serpent and a Flame Winged Serpent that trembled with elemental energies of their respective bloodlines!","The most powerful beings of the Prime World that was known as the Magus World, the Bloodline Magi of the Order of the Black Serpent that all knew in their hearts death was coming for them in the hands of the Celestials- they had all fully prepared and transformed as their angered and despairing gazes turned towards the two beings calmly floating opposite to them.","In front of this ever so expanding army, the brilliantly shining golden figures of Athena and Noah raised their weapons forward, their eyes shining with confidence as they didn’t seem to think this tremendous force was anything much!"]},{"number":348,"title":"Chapter 348: Chapter 347 - Shining Blades Pierce the Skies","paragraphs":["The numerous forces of multiple Prime Worlds watching this scene portrayed in the point of view of Noah and Athena found it breathtaking to watch as they could so clearly observe the converging of essence from the army of the many serpents standing opposite to these two beings.","In their hearts, they knew they never wanted to be in this situation in their lifetimes!","Yet the two beings facing this terrible army held calm eyes as one was shining a resplendent gold, her body covered in full golden armor and shining golden wings where only her unshaking eyes could be seen. The other held an even more unique look as a golden robe dr.a.p.ed over him regally, from his back the appearance of grandiose white-gold feathered wings erupting out in a glorious array of colors as his face was that of calmness!","The two Celestials were completely unfazed by this tremendous scene of an entire army in front of them.","In the Prime Warship floating above the space of the Magus World, the Grand Master was looking at this scene closely, his power ready to jump in at any instant if something went wrong.","Even though it seemed like his actions of allowing Athena and Crixus to go into the Magus world were easy to arrange, he had to send messages to various Grandmasters before he got his way. He affirmed that this experiment would only be for the training purposes of these two exemplary disciples, and that no harm would come to them under his watch. Thus he was watching with even more interested eyes than the numerous forces that were watching the illusory screens above their planets.","\"Death it is!\"","The furious Devouring Winged Serpent voiced out loud as her words acted as the trigger for the start of the battle.","OOOOH!","Immense waves of energy erupted out as Noah observed with calm eyes the rushing of numerous serpents towards them.","It was a scene of terror as those watching from a distance of multiple planets far away felt their hairs rise at the scene of this humongous force rushing towards the two beings floating in the skies.","As a response to this rushing force, Noah turned towards Athena and asked this valiant looking figure.","\"Shall I make the first move or will you?\"","His mind continued to be that of slight interest towards this impassive and noncommunicating senior disciple that he had sparred with multiple times over the span of the last month.","Every time they fought he always held an edge over the battle as she limited herself to the same number of fate lines that he held. But his skills that were fully enhanced with skill points and the numerous passive boosts that he received from multiple other abilities made it so that she could never get a winning edge over him. Yet after the end of each battle, he only felt that the fight was becoming harder and harder for him.","This monstrous Athena was adapting extremely fast at his power, even while limiting herself to a specific number of fate lines. At the last few sparring matches, even with his enhanced abilities, the matches were actually coming out as a draw! This was the shocking talent of this being that was apparently also holding a Noble Fate!","He could already see the shining light within her eyes, the fact that she loved battle being the only thing that he understood about her.","Athena’s eyes were locked onto the singularly most powerful Devouring Winged Serpent that was rushing towards them at a fast speed as she replied.","\"Junior Brother, since this is a mission that you proposed, why don’t you start us off and show me the skills that you could not show me before?\"","Feeling the enormous source of strength from the golden robe that dr.a.p.ed over his body as well as the glorious wings from his back that came from [Empyrean Armament], Noah couldn’t help but shake his head at the insane boosts of the skills he obtained from the Celestials.","After putting the maximum skill points in the two abilities, [Empyrean Guards] allowed him to summon 6 beings made of immense light as [Empyrean Armament] granted him a boost of 30% to Soul Damage, Physical Damage, Speed, and Defense for every Empyrean Guard that he absorbed!","This granted him a shocking boost of 180% to all the aforementioned features in the form of the golden robe that dr.a.p.ed over him, granting him tremendous defense and making his body feel even lighter than he thought possible as he put into account the [Lesser Cthulhu]’s Child of Space ability.","The golden sword and shield he held on either of his hands also made him feel like he could defend and attack against anything that came towards him, this confidence only being shot higher as he felt his Fate Lines resonating within his body.","He still did not fully understand and could not quantify the boosts of these spectacular Fate Lines that allowed Celestials to fight beings of higher levels than them, but he would gradually come to know, with this battle today granting him a chance to learn many things.","As for the words of Athena, during their sparring matches he had only ever used [Empyrean Guards] and [Empyrean Armament] as both Athena and he knew very well the next two skills were ones that could deal Soul Damage when cast, that they were not skills to be used in a spar and thus Noah or Athena had never cast these skills before.","Noah’s thoughts moved fast as he looked at the first one he wanted to try, confirming the changes of the skill when he placed the maximum number of allowed skill points onto it.","<strong>[Smite of Liberation](5/5) :: Cleanse the souls of those that stand against you as you smite them with a Blade of Liberation. The blade is incorporeal and yet physical at the same time, granting +300% Physical and +300% Soul Damage. Limit of 5 Blades of Liberation per cast.</strong>","Noah gazed at the spectacular numbers of the skill and the added description of the number of blades as the numerous figures of deadly serpents that were rushing towards him, the three at the forefront being the most dangerous. An impassive look appeared on his face as he breathed out and steeled himself, ready to test whether he could defeat those of the next level with ease while using the abilities of the Celestials, his mind fully prepared and ready to carry out a bloodbath.","It would be the bloodbath that would go on to save this planet, only taking down those responsible for sowing the abundant chaos that was going to spread across the stars. He knew he was walking on an extremely tight rope here as he had joined the ranks of Celestials and was even carrying out missions similar to them, yet he did not want himself to completely be against them as he did not agree with the way they did things!","It was a very thin line to walk on, and this test, this bloodbath on the Magus World, would be the first step to seeing whether he could do things differently than them.","His gaze met the ferocious charging army of serpents as light words escaped his lips.","[Smite of liberation].","RUMBLE!","A golden hue spread across the skies as a droning sound could be heard by all those in the surroundings. The color of gold was slowly replaced as sharp points of blades began to appear from the skies, the blades being enormous in size as one could very clearly make out their physical features being tens of meters wide.","They observed the sharp ends of multiple blades as they pierced through the layer of clouds and began descending down at a ferocious speed!","VOOM","The blades pierced through the layer of clouds as they became more and more pronounced, those watching being able to see sharp white blades that were attached to golden hilts. These five blades carried with them a golden aura of righteousness that seemed to be smashing straight into the army of the Order of the Black Serpent.","Noah’s own body was trembling as his fate lines had become barely discernible, their presence going on to augment the strength of [Smite of Liberation] even more as besides the increased Physical and Soul damage, the blades rushed down to their targets even faster.","The Devouring Winged Serpent turned her eyes upwards in shock as she felt this stupendous attack that in no way should have come from someone in the void realm.","This took her by complete surprise as her numerous heads faced the skies and opened their wide terrifying mouths, letting out enormous colorful blasts of elemental energies that rushed to oppose the descending blades.","BOOM!","Just the simple size of the Blades of Liberation made it so that the terrifying attacks from a being that was at the Soul Forging Realm to only strike the tip of the blade points as they seemed to be cut apart, the blades themselves continuing to descend down as a sheen of gold light covered them, the Supreme Law of Fate backing them not being able to be withstood by the attacks of the Devouring Winged Serpent as they went on to smash into the ranks of the numerous serpents coiling in the skies.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!!!","The color of gold erupted out and it was soon followed by a bloody red hue as many watched with rapt and unbelievable faces at the bloodbath that had begun in the Magus World!"]},{"number":349,"title":"Chapter 349: Chapter 348 - Unmatched Judgment!","paragraphs":["Everywhere that these tremendously large Blades of Liberation passed, numerous beings no matter their power levels were sliced through, the blades sliding down as if they were cutting through butter.","Only the tremendously powerful bodies of the Soul Forging Realms experts felt their scales being ripped apart as they suffered heavy injuries, just the sizes of these blades going on to inflict a horrendous amount of damage that they never thought would have been possible at the beginning of this battle!","As the numerous forces that were watching from the multiple Prime Worlds watched on, their jaws were slacked wide open, nearly reaching the floor as they observed the being with golden-white wings and the shimmering golden sword and shield cast a single skill that went on to disrupt an entire army.","In the underworld, the arrogant Emperor Penguin stood on the shoulders of Elena as its flippers rose victoriously in the air, its eyes full of pride as it nodded vigorously. Elena’s eyes showed even more infatuation as she watched her Vampyre Progenitor go on to cast skills she never thought to be possible for someone like him to cast so seamlessly.","This simple casting of Smite of Liberation was just the beginning of a very, very bloody battle as Athena’s eyes shone at the destructive extent of the damage caused by this simple casting of the skill which allowed five Blades of Liberation to descend down compared to the one blade she could summon with a single cast.","Even more questions erupted in her head as she wanted to drill into the secrets of the exemplary being next to her, but her thirst for battle won her over as she looked at that disordered army of terrible serpents and instead rushed forth towards them!","\"YAA!\"","Her resounding scream acted as a reminder as the shocked Devouring Winged Serpent lit up with numerous abilities, it’s expert use of the many elements granted to it by its numerous heads coming forth as enormous balls of fire appeared in the skies. They were followed up by a sharp formation of ice spears that threatened to pierce any that stood to oppose them.","The leader of the Order of the Black Serpent continued to cast numerous innate skills as she felt an unbelievable feeling while looking towards the shimmering figure with white wings. She affirmed his power was at the Void Realm, but the ability he cast was enough to even injure someone in the Soul Forging Realm. This unbelievable reality caused a sliver of fear to appear in her cold heart as this simply did not make sense!","She continued casting abilities as enormous boulders of earth also began rushing down, while destructive bombs of darkness and blades of wind and numerous more elemental attacks appeared in the skies with ease","The Devouring Winged Serpent was enraged and no longer underestimated the two beings in front of her, seeing the horrible color of red spreading out all around her as hundreds of beings faced death from just that one attack.","OOOOH!","A battle roar rang out as the numerous elemental attacks cast by her flew towards the figures of Noah and Athena. The two of them were fearlessly rushing in as the shield in Noah’s left hand shone as a shimmering golden barrier appeared to wrap around his body.","Athena’s own body was fully protected by a golden metal armor as she weaved in and out of the dangerous molten balls of fire, boulders of earth, and ice spears, the hammer she wielded in her hands smashing into any attacks that neared her as spectacularly, her body pulsed with tens of thousands of fate lines!","It was an image that struck itself into the minds of all those watching as they observed two winged figures weaving into a destructive storm of elemental attacks cast by a Soul Forging Realm Bloodline Magus, their bodies effortlessly weaving in and out in a beautiful fashion.","The Grandmaster watching from above had his expression shining with pride as he observed the thrumming of tens of thousands of Fate Lines on Athena’s body, his aged heart looking forward into the future as he waited for a similar number of fate lines to appear on the monstrous genius fighting alongside Athena who had shown them yet again how different their own techniques could be used.","When it came to Athena, she only held the power of the Void Realm, and at the peak of it at that, but her power was augmented into insane levels because of the tens of thousands of Fate Lines that she held in her body.","Even Noah himself currently only held a bit over thirteen thousand Fate Lines, but even he felt an enormous sense of power from them, not to mention the strength Athena could draw out given how many lines she had already condensed in her origin.","The Grandmaster continued to ponder how this genius was bringing out even more exemplary effects from the techniques of [Fate’s Guardian] as he watched the resplendent Blades of Liberation disappear in the bloodied army of serpents, wondering exactly how monstrous the perception of Crixus was!","The War Princess weaved in and out of the numerous attacks thrown by the Devouring Winged Serpent as she placed more energy onto the golden hammer that she carried in her hands to strike down towards one of the heads of the huge serpent as she targeted the strongest beings in the opposing army!","BOOM!","The descent of her fierce hammer was actually also a prelude as from the skies, a bright Blade of Liberation with features different from the ones Noah had cast descending downwards rapidly, its target the many necks of the weaving Devouring Winged Serpent.","The battle continued explosively as the two Soul Forging Dark Winged Serpent and the Flame Winged Serpents turned their red eyes towards Noah, their bodies already moving as numerous destructive skills were cast towards him. This was accompanied by the attacks of tens of thousands of other Bloodline Magi as runic inscriptions beautifully colored the skies, the product of these runes being deadly elemental spells that rushed towards his position.","Noah’s gaze was impassive as he pointed his blade forward and cast the second skill that he had yet to cast after placing the maximum number of allowed Skill Points into it.","<strong>[Judgement](5/5) :: A declaration of death for all those that stand against you is called forth. Those that cannot defend themselves will have their bodies destroyed and their souls shattered as they become lost in the river of fate. The ability has been enhanced further, becoming an area of attack ability that affects targeted beings in an area of 100 meters.</strong>","The description of the skill was nothing to scoff at, with the possibilities of who could be affected when the skill was cast nearly endless as the last added description was ridiculous to even think about.","The skill stated that it was a declaration of death for all those that stood against him, so Noah wielded the golden blade of light in his right hand as he pointed forward at the numerous magi snaking towards him and simply cast the skill, his gaze landing on the centermost location where the two Soul Forging Magi were moving along with all the beings surrounding them.","[Judgment].","RUMBLE!","He felt an enormous amount of mana leak from his body, an amount that was greater than any of the other Celestial abilities he had ever used before as he instinctively realized he would be going overboard and moved to stop supplying mana to the skill a second later, but his enormous reserves had already given a significant amount of mana as a ridiculous area of attack ability that used to be for a single target, an extremely high damage dealing skill that even brought death to an aberration in the Infernal Realm- came to life in the most stupendous way possible!","’Ah, whoops.’","A single thought coursed through his mind as the very skies screeched and trembled at the appearance of this attack!","The numerous powerful forces watching from the illusory screens above the prime worlds, the ones who believed they couldn’t be shocked anymore found themselves questioning their eyesight as an ability of ridiculous proportions presented itself in front of their eyes, numerous golden spears appearing en masse in the skies as they descended down to skewer everything in sight with a righteous light of judgment!"]},{"number":350,"title":"Chapter 350: Chapter 349 - Golden Robes Stained with Blood","paragraphs":["From the illusory screens that stood above the many Prime Worlds that were connected to the Magus World, an unbelievable site was playing itself out in front of the eyes of many observing forces.","RUMBLE!","They watched in a trance as the winged celestial pointed his sword forward, bringing about unbelievable judgment onto those that stood against him as in the next instant, numerous golden spears began to appear as if they were needles in the vast skies of the Magus World!","Their numbers were too many to count as they appeared in an area of 100 meters, their extremely sharp tips pointing themselves forward as they went on to skewer everything in the area of 100 meters!","SPULCH!","A bloody mist spread out a moment later as silence reigned over the battlefield.","\"...\"","A moment of silence came as not a single being could speak while observing the incredible level of power. Many were asking themselves in their minds- Were their eyes playing tricks on them or was this really the power of a Void Realm being?!","The powers spread out over the many Prime Worlds weren’t the only ones shocked at the development. The Grandmaster that was watching the fight with the rapt attention in the Prime Warship that was floating above the Magus World was watching with wide eyes as he observed yet another skill that he had been using for hundreds of years be used in the hands of this new genius disciple.","This same skill was portrayed vastly differently to the extent that he had to ask himself- Was this the same skill? Was this the same technique that he knew all this time?","The air of the battlefield had changed with this single attack as even while Athena weaved in and out of the destructive elemental skills that were raging all around, her attention went to the skewered beings in an area of 100 meters that had turned bloody!","The only remaining beings were the Dark Winged Serpent and the Flame Winged Serpent who had sustained heavy injuries on their bodies, most of them from the soul damage aspect coming from Noah’s attack that they did not have too many defenses of.","Athena’s eyes shone with a grand light as she wanted to take a close look at her junior brother who had managed to surprise her even more than she thought was possible. But her attention focused on the immensely powerful peak Soul Forging Realm expert that was the Devouring Winged Serpent.","Her unique ability foretold of every single possible attack that her enemy might make before they made it. This allowed her to escape and move through the battle with ease as she began conducting a symphony of blood. Her attacks reigned down on the Devouring Winged Serpent as she evaded everything thrown towards her!","The air of the battlefield had changed to that of oppression and powerlessness as the forces of the Magus world actually found themselves on the losing end when fighting two Void Realm Disciples, each of them coming out with spectacular attacks and reaping many of their comrade’s lives while not a single speck of damage could be seen on their golden figures!","The beings watching across the stars were struck frozen as a somber atmosphere overcame them, not completely understanding how these two Void Disciples were decimating forces with such a vast difference in power.","In the area of 100 meters where the color of the sky was changed to a bloody red, the area of death was eerily silent except for the two Soul Forging Realm beings that had happened to survive. Their gazes were that of fear as they gazed towards Noah. This fear came from the fact that besides the physical damage they felt when numerous sharp spears produced by [Judgement] pierced their bodies, the even worse damage came directly to their souls as a type of damage that they had no way to prevent struck their origins!","They glanced towards the Devouring Winged Serpent who seemed to be falling into the pace of a beautifully moving Athena as they looked for possibilities and exactly what to do. They would not be given the time though as Noah’s eyes scanned the entire battlefield, steeling his heart as he wanted to wrap up and end this bloodbath. He had to control his emotions even more as he saw the overflowing blood rushing out from the bodies of his enemies, his [Blood Gourmet] ability telling him the quality of blood for these Soul Forging Realm experts would be of great quality.","He breathed out as he calmed his mind and instead continued casting [Fate Discernment] to see all the beings that needed to have their lives taken today before the chaos that threatened to take over multiple planets was completely reduced. To reduce the same amount of chaos that destroying the entire world would have caused, they had to erase this Order of the Black Serpent out of existence!","The shimmering golden sword in his hand vibrated as his body turned into a streak of light, choosing to put the close combat skills he had learned over the past month while sparring with the War Princess to the test and going down towards the two Soul Forging beings who could not decide what they wanted to do. This would also be training to make sure he would control himself in the battlefield filled with blood, as he was only playing the role of a Celestial Disciple right now.","OOOH!","Unwilling roars released from them as they went on to clash with Noah’s winged figure, not being able to do anything as they saw from his speed that they could not even run!","BOOM!","A shower of blood erupted out as Noah swung the golden sword down, the immense physical and soul damage boosts that he carried with him being deadly with every strike. A single sword slash landed on the chest of the Dark Winged Serpent as it felt horrendous damage course through its origin. Its body lit up with essence as spears of darkness exploded out at Noah’s position, the explosions only making apparent the shimmering golden barrier covering his body from the shield he carried in his left hand.","His Fate Lines looked to be pulsing in his body as he effortlessly withstood the attacks of the Dark Winged Serpent, using the shining sword in his right hand to land even more deadly attacks!","At the same time, the Flame Winged Serpent had blazing fires raging around Its body, using this chance where Noah was preoccupied to try and bite down on his golden shimmering figure. Its many heads let out molten breaths of fire as the extreme heat pushed away any nearing beings.","Noah did not even turn his gaze as he continued to focus the attacks of his deadly sword onto the Dark Winged Serpent, his left hand that held the shield turning towards the attacking Flame Winged Serpent as he called out slowly.","[Sever].","ZING!","The baleful and destructive energies of Aether could be felt for a single second as a ray of destructive light erupted from Noah’s hands and diagonally cut through the space where the Flame Winged Serpent was attacking him!","RUMBLE!","A shocking sight where numerous heads of the Flame Winged Serpent were cut off with a ray of Aether going on to bisect the entire left side of the unsuspecting enemy displayed itself, with Noah revealing his true target and letting out this extremely quick surprise attack that actually brought death to a Soul Forging being, its body bisected in two as spurts of blood erupted out!","Shock!","Incredulity!","Fear!","\"...\"","Silence reigned as the Dark Winged Serpent fending off Noah’s attacks trembled with fear, Its body turning the other direction as it quickly wanted to run from this terrible enemy! Seeing how its long time friend at the same realm as it had not even managed to hold off the destructive ray that this celestial shot out, she did not want to stay behind any longer as she could feel the cloud of death pull towards her ever so closely!","Noah was relentless, not letting up as he turned into a streak of light and followed behind closely as a destructive Aether ray was called out once again.","[Sever].","ZING!","Numerous heads flew out once more as the running Soul Rank expert felt his body split apart, terrifying darkness clouding his vision as the hands of death wrapped around him. The abundant essence in its body, as well as the strong soul that had received horrendous damage from the Blades of Liberation and countless spears that came from [Judgement], could not hold on any longer as its origin became even more destabilized with the destructive ray of Aether.","In the span of a few seconds, Noah’s introduction of the ability of the [Lesser Cthulhu] skill tree that the Celestials had seen him use before in the First Realm of Hell was pulled out as he used it in conjunction with the enhanced abilities of [Fate’s Guardian] to quickly reap the lives of two early Soul Rank experts!","His gaze remained impassive as he continued to use [Fate Discernement], locating tens of thousands of Magi running away or the millions hiding tens of miles in numerous locations of the central lands of the Magus World as the golden blade in his hands vibrated. He would save this world from destruction, but many of those responsible would have to die in order for this to occur. This included all of the beings in this Order of the Black Serpent!","He remained impassive after defeating two Soul Rank beings, his figure turning his attention on the running Magi as he turned into a streak of light and flew towards them. The number of beings he would have to personally kill would be many today, but even more would have been killed were this entire planet to be destroyed completely by the hands of the Celestials.","As these thoughts crossed his mind, he continued to remind himself to be very clear on the thin line he was walking on, as it seemed he was thinking more and more along similar thought processes as those he did not agree with!","He put these thoughts in the back of his mind as pandemonium ensued everywhere his figure went, the numerous powers watching from the Prime Worlds felt a feeling of oppression while observing the easy deaths of two Soul Forging beings. Their hearts felt tight as on the illusory screens they were watching, they could see the shimmering golden robe of this celestial gain a red hue as he chased down and reaped the lives of many Magi, the blood of those he struck down coiling around him tightly!","It was a dark contrast as even the white-feathered wings erupting behind him were now stained with blood, the air of holy brilliance increasing the feeling of somberness and oppression from all those watching.","As they watched the ensuing bloodbath in the Magus World, they were shown the faces of tens of thousands of beings that would be considered powerhouses. They would be considered respected and holding high achievements because of the realm they achieved, but under the hands of this single Void Realm Celestials, they were cut down as if they were nothing.","It was a horrible scene of carnage that many would not come across in their lifetimes, but the beings in the numerous Prime Worlds were made to watch with rapt attention as they were reminded once again of the organization that stood at the top of the Light Expanse.","In the Prime Warship above the Magus World, the Grandmaster was discerning fate while he watched this exemplary disciple emotionlessly chase down all those responsible, his aged heart actually trembling as his discernment told him...the aspect of fear that the Celestials wanted to show to the surrounding powers was being etched into the minds of all those watching, and in a much more memorable way at that!","It seemed like this pathway that this genius disciple was trying...might actually be able to achieve the goals of the Celestials without taking billions of lives from an entire planet!"]},{"number":351,"title":"Chapter 351: Chapter 350 - Fear","paragraphs":["Yet another eerie silence took over the battlefield as many beings could be seen deserting it, while a single shimmering figure smoothly crossed the lands and skies while swinging down a golden blade of light.","Flames of furious anger erupted from the Devouring Winged Serpent who was being cornered by Athena, its aura bubbling forth as it found its forces were decimated and those that were remaining were running away in fear.","It’s gaze looked at the figure of Noah who’s golden robe now held a bloody sheen, the rivers of blood erupting from the bodies of the numerous serpents that he had just cut up wrapping around him and diminishing the shine of his regal robe.","It was a terrible contrast to see- Gold tinged with red while the gaze of this terrible being continued to chase down the disordered and broken forces of the Order of the Black Serpent while also striking down the bodies of Cultivators devoid of souls that they had obtained over their months-long project in the World of Cultivation.","The reality that he had just simply killed two Soul Rank beings not even seem to register in the mind of the winged Crixus as he wielded his blade and continued the bloodbath. One could occasionally see the appearance of resplendent Blades of Liberation pierce through the skies as they went on to smash onto the ranks of the Order of the Black Serpent and cause even more destruction!","The devouring black serpent looked at all of this with unbelievable hopelessness as her numerous heads roared forth in anger while her voice resounded out yet again","\"Hypocrisy! Unfairness!\"","BOOM!","Its roars were only met with one of its heads falling, Being severed from one of Athena’s attacks as a blade of liberation had descended down and cleanly cut through one of the heads!","An exciting look was on Athena’s face as she continued to attack this being an entire realm above her. The trembling tens of thousands of fate lines in her body continuing to thrum strongly as they reduced the energy she required to cast all her skills while at the same time providing horrendous boosts to her speed and damage.","In the corner for eyes. She simply observed the figure of Crixus continuing to move across a battlefield as a river of blood began forming in the ground from the numerous serpents that continued to have their lives diminished. It had now turned into a simple scene of a massacre as even those watching from the numerous Prime Worlds looked on with fearful and somber eyes!","The image of this winged being dr.a.p.ed in a golden robe that shone with the brilliant terrifying color of blood was etching itself into the recesses of their memories.","\"Hypocrisy!!!\"","The shouts of the Devouring Winged Serpent rang out again, but nobody paid any attention to them. The only things running through their minds as they watched this unbelievable scene of beings at a much lower realm decimate tens of thousands of beings and even those that stood above them playing out clearly were- So what? What if it was hypocrisy? What if it was unfair?","In the face of beings like this, in the face of a single Void Realm Celestial being able to decimate two Soul Forging experts while continuing to rain down destruction endlessly, what could they do?","The many beings watching from the numerous Prime Worlds were reminded once again about those they knew to be looking over the Light Expanse. They were reminded once again of the terrible power of beings that studied the Supreme Law of Fate!","As they watched Noah’s figure weave in and out of tens of thousands of magi in the Magus World, they were reminded once again of the power of Celestials!","Those hiding in the dark and those who considered themselves powerful or had simply forgotten the sway of the Celestials etched this lesson into their hearts as it looked like the massacre in the Magus World was ending, the peak Soul Forging Devouring Winged Serpent bellowing forth as her aura began shooting up unstably.","Noah was chasing down running Magi a few miles away when he felt this change, his impassive gaze looking towards Athena’s direction as he disappeared and quickly reappeared near their location.","\"Yaa!\"","The valiant War Princess did not even spare a glance to him as her figure continued to land horrendous attacks to the rapidly changing and convulsing body of the Devouring Winged Serpent, its bellowing screams not landing in here ears one bit as she dodged attacks with a hair’s breadth and continued to damage the origin of this being an entire realm above her with attacks that dealt heavy Soul Damage.","\"Since my death is coming anyways, I’ll be sure to bring you all down with me! Oh, Great World Devouring Serpent Ancestor! Descend! Wreak havoc! Eradicate these hypocrites in front of m-\"","RUMBLE!","Noah watched as this Devouring Winged Serpent was trying to undergo yet another transformation and call down a very powerful force by the meaning of the words she spoke, so he didn’t bother letting her finish her words nor her transformation as he cast the singular skill capable of immense damage while also disrupting the essence of a being to the point of destruction.","[Sever].","ZIING!","\"GAH!\"","A ray of destructive Aether pierced through the chest of the Devouring Winged Serpent as its aura was about to bubble forth half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm, whatever technique it was calling forth failing from Noah’s intrusion as Athena moved forward Valiantly.","[Smite of Liberation]! [Judgment]!","A combination of skills was called forth by her as the unstable converging essence around the body of the Devouring Winged Serpent was bathed with gold, numerous spears coming into existence as they dug into her body, a Blade of Liberation descending down as it even further dealt horrid injuries.","SPULCH!","Noah’s mind rapidly moved as he joined in the last moment when he saw the Devouring Winged Serpent was still hanging on with signs of life, joining Athena in her last attacks as he wanted to kill steal this powerful being and gain a few more Soul Rank [Skill Book]s.","BOOM!","Resplendent skills smashed onto the convulsing body of this powerful being as she was ganged up on, not given any respite as her calls for unfairness and hypocrisy were only met with a single verdict- Death!","Her body exploded in a shower of blood as Athena’s figure breathed heavily, having withstood the power of the peak Soul Forging Devouring Winged Serpent the longest as she didn’t hold even a single scratch of damage, her golden armor and wings bathed with blood.","It was a terrifying and yet an enticing scene to watch this resplendent figure, Noah turning his gaze as he used [Fate Discernment] yet again after the death of the head of the Order of the Black Serpent.","He found that his goal was actually nearing completion, with the war against the World of Cultivation completely evaded and an enormous amount of chaos reduced, but it still was not enough!","It did not achieve the same level of effect as the destruction of the entire Magus World would have yet, so his body turned into a streak of light once more as he moved to track and kill all those remaining in the central lands of the Magus World that held the auras of chaos.","The heads of the leaders were cut off, and now he had to take down all those that followed in their actions as he continued to achieve the factor of Fear to all those watching. They all had ingrained in their minds that what they were observing now could happen to any of them, and that the only way to prevent this was to not do actions similar to this Magus World!","What Noah didn’t know was that fear had already completely crept into the hearts of those watching the ridiculous strength of two Void Realm disciples decimate an entire army of a Prime World.","[Fate Discernment] didn’t show this yet as time simply had to be given in order for this fear to spread and reduce chaos even more as many forces would turn careful with their future actions!"]},{"number":352,"title":"Chapter 352: Chapter 351 - Crixus the Destroyer!","paragraphs":["The numerous somber beings across the Prime Worlds who were already reminded and had etched the experience into their hearts were made to continue watching the conclusion of this bloodbath as Noah’s figure continued to track down all those involved as he swung the shimmering bloody golden blade down.","The gazes of those watching hardened as they saw the illusory screens above their planets portraying a scene of destruction and chaos, a title of this bloody Celestial forming in their minds that would later go on to spread across the Light Expanse.","Among the many things coming out from this event, the name of a particular Celestial would spread like wildfire to the many quadrants of the Light Expanse as the rampage was concluding in the Magus World.","---","The gaze of Grandmaster Vredral was bright as he looked at the scene of carnage continuing from the viewpoint of Crixus and Athena.","After the defeat of the powerful Soul Forging experts of the Order of the Black Serpent, many had deserted the battlefield and spread across the lands of the Magus World in fear, with the two Celestials going on to track them down through [Fate Discernement].","Any that held an air of chaos from the results of the actions of killing and abducting the cultivators from the World of Cultivation were all cut down where they stood as the process continued for another hour!","In the illusory screens, the forces of the many Prime Worlds watching could see the impassive and emotionless expressions of Crixus and Athena as one used his shining sword to split apart the bodies of their enemies, while another used a hammer shining with a glorious light to shatter their bodies apart. They felt their bodies turn cold at the continuing carnage as they watched on, the illusory screens continuing to broadcast everything is spectacular detail.","Every now and then, tremendously large Blades of Liberation could be seen descending down and destroying entire bases where the forces of the Order of the Black Serpent were hiding in, the barriers erected not being able to stop the advancements of the blades even briefly.","All of this carnage and destruction was attributed to the two Celestials still moving in the Magus World, but many already knew of the War Princess Athena who had recently won the first rank of the Infernal Hunt.","Many more were unfamiliar with the name Crixus, so while watching the carnage and destruction occurring in the Magus World, the name that would gradually spread among the mouths of many was Crixus.","This was the title that carried with it fear and brilliance. It was a title that many would say when they discussed the power of the Celestials and their forces. Many would remember the War Princess Athena, as well as the newly introduced Crixus, the Destroyer!","Crixus the Destroyer!","A bold title given to the Celestial that rained down righteous Blades of Liberations and called for Judgement that skewered and destroyed all those that stood against him!","In the central lands of the Magus World, an eerie silence reigned as shockingly, not a single being remained alive across the vast expanse of a normally bustling center of a Prime World!","Noah’s shimmering figure floated in the air as a golden aura roasted around him, confirming with [Fate Discernment] for the last time that his goal had indeed been achieved.","The aura of another being neared his side as he turned to his right to look at a valiant Athena who had her golden armor fading away one particle of light at a time. The War Princess had a brilliant smile as her eyes locked onto Noah’s figure, her expression that of interest as it did not match the atmosphere of someone that had just participated in the bloodbath of millions of beings.","\"You are an anomaly, Junior Brother.\"","The tight ponytail waved behind her as she turned her head to the side and looked over Noah, seemingly trying to figure out what secrets he held in his body. Noah glanced back to the bloodied central lands of the Magus World as he voiced out.","\"You’ve observed the changes with [Fate Discernment]?\"","\"Mmm, yes. This time through reaping the lives of millions while broadcasting it, we have saved tens of billions. Don’t you feel a sense of satisfaction after reducing this much chaos and steering fate to a direction you want?\"","Athena seemed much more talkative and jovial after the blood pumping battle, her expression not the usual impassive one as Noah could observe an eerie level of happiness as she did not think much of their actions just now. He pondered her question as he nodded and replied while their figures began to shoot towards the Prime Warship in the distance, leaving behind an empty and bloodied capital that used to house the strongest powers of the Magus World.","\"It feels good knowing there are other ways to reduce chaos that don’t directly jump to the destruction of planets.\"","He said these words nonchalantly as Athena’s eyes squinted towards him, a brilliant smile erupting from her as Noah heard her laugh for the first time.","\"Haha. You might have been right this time Junior Brother, but don’t get too c.o.c.ky. Now that I know your talent is even more spectacular than we imagined, I won’t be matching the same number of fate lines while sparring anymore. We won’t even need to worry about the abilities with Soul Damage when sparring if your skills are this advanced.\"","Dangerous words were released from her as the thrill of the battle had fully gotten into her system, recalling Crixus’s exemplary [Smite of Liberation] that allowed for multiple Blades of Liberation to descend down. She was interested in this dangerous attack that could damage one’s soul, wondering exactly how this Junior Brother of hers had managed to enhance it so much!","Noah only nodded at the changed pace of Athena as they neared the humongous Prime Warship and went inside, going through multiple doors before they returned to one of the huge central command rooms where Grandmaster Vredral stood.","The gaze of the Grandmaster was that of joyful vigor as his eyes locked on Noah’s and Athena’s figures, waving his hands in front of them as he did not even wait for them to report.","With the wave of his hands, numerous illusory screens appeared in front of them. These illusory screens reflected the many Prime Worlds that had been watching the bloodbath they carried out in the Magus World as their somber reactions were portrayed. Many shocked and fearful reactions could be seen, with many more that of pondering as numerous powerful forces were put in deep thought as they were visually reminded of the power of Celestials.","Noah gazed upon many of these screens as numerous voices compounded upon one another, but he could clearly make out the most repeated words out of the numerous illusory screens in front of him","\"...The War Princess..\"","\"Athena...\"","\"...Celestials...\"","\"...the Destroyer..\"","\"...Supreme Law...\"","\"Crixus...the Destroyer!\"","RUMBLE!","Numerous things seemed to be mentioned throughout the numerous Prime Worlds he was watching, but the one he came across most was the name of the being he was taking the shape of, his body actually feeling a change as he received another lesson on the law of fate while watching the effects of his actions!","The room of the ship they were in turned a shade of gold as numerous Fate Lines rushed down into Noah’s body, although he wasn’t alone as Athena’s face shone with brilliance as hundreds more Fate Lines were added to the already terrifying amount that she held.","Because of his influence of fate that had averted tens of billions of lives, Noah had realized that the condensing of Fate Lines had become even easier and faster, counting a few hundred descending in a matter of seconds as he gained more knowledge on fate, and just exactly what he needed to do in order to move even further along this Supreme Law of Fate!"]},{"number":353,"title":"Chapter 353: Chapter 352 - A Grandmaster Has an Epiphany","paragraphs":["THRUM!","The bodies of the two Celestials thrummed with power as the golden light gradually died down, Noah adding another five thousand Fate Lines onto his body and bringing up his total to slightly above 18,000, while Athena added around two thousand fate lines to her already abundant amount that Noah could not completely discern.","The air gradually settled as the commotion brought because of the descent of thousands of fate died down, the wizened expression of a Grandmaster stroking his beard making itself apparent in the eyes of the two disciples.","\"The more you influence fate, the more you will naturally increase in the power and understanding of the law of fate.\"","The Grandmaster beamed out loud as he looked at them like some prized possessions.","Athena stared at the added lines of fate in her body as she nodded naturally, this instance not being something completely foreign to her. Her eyes languidly gazed upon her Junior Brother though, who had somehow managed to have more than twice the Fate Lines descend onto his body even though they participated in the same event.","Noah looked at the abundant Fate Lines running through his body as he gained knowledge of the way to rapidly increase them- which was to simply continue influencing the fates of many beings! This would cause for the abrupt increase in the number of Fate Lines he held, and most likely the increase on how many he could then condense each day as time passed.","The Grandmaster’s gaze focused on Noah as he nodded towards him happily and spoke once more.","\"Your plan succeeded very well, with the amount of chaos reduced even slightly exceeding the result of simply destroying the entirety of the Magus World. You are a genius unlike anything I have ever seen!\"","Noah only smiled as he placed his hand on his chest and asked respectfully.","\"Thank you for giving me the chance, Grandmaster. I am curious though- since we have completely destroyed the power structure of this world and taken its most powerful leaders out, how will it move from here when looking at the effects of our actions?\"","The Grandmaster waved his hands dismissively at this question, replying while rubbing his exemplary white beard.","\"You don’t need to worry yourself about that. The World of Cultivation that was hurt the most by the Magus World will soon be informed to descend down and take the reigns, as well as numerous missions being created that will be given to our disciples to descend to the Magus World and influence the fates of the beings there for training.\"","\"Not everyone jumps through ranks like you, going on to directly influence the fates of numerous Worlds. Other disciples have to start on a much smaller scale, and influencing the fates of beings in a special position like those in this Magus World fits our criteria. But...that is not what I want to discuss the most right now!\"","Grandmaster Vredral’s face became bright as he began walking towards them, his presence began to erupt with golden vigor.","\"You have reminded me of something that I should have never forgotten during this venture. It is the reminder that even worse than me, the beings in this Light Expanse are naturally forgetful.\"","He walked towards them as with every increasing step, his face seemed to glow more and more as if he had an epiphany!","\"After the end of the war 1000 years ago, many have forgotten our power, only hearing about it occasionally when we move to punish those that need to be punished and during the Infernal Hunts. This momentous event you just called forth, Young Crixus, is a reminder that the beings in this Light Expanse need to be shown exactly why Celestials have the power that they have.\"","\"Just like they observed your genius battle prowess, they need to be shown the brilliance of the Celestials yet again in order to reduce this ever-increasing chaos! Not just this small quadrant that we showed off your battle to, but all the quadrants of the Light Expanse!\"","The voice of the Grandmaster was trembling with aged excitement near the end as Noah’s heart tightened, not knowing exactly what would come forth from this unexpected development!","---","In the Magus World that Noah and Athena had just left, the illusory screen faded as the fearfully hiding inhabitants of the world came out en masse, the powerful Magi that were not in the Order of the Black Serpent feeling the spatial restrictions lifting off as a large Prime Warship began moving away from their worlds.","Their hearts were full of grief and pain as they replayed the events which had just occurred, especially the demonic figure of a brilliantly shining winged Celestial that rained down horrendous blades from the skies and struck down many of the powerful beings they knew.","When they looked at the figures of Noah and Athena, they only held memories of fear and hate as they recalled their fearsome power that had caused the downfall of the ruling force of their world, but they also felt a sliver of thankfulness!","This was a very interesting sight to come across, as the inhabitants of the Magus World heard the words of the Celestial Grandmaster before the bloodbath began. His voice had resounded across the world as it told them that the verdict for their world had been destruction! The only reason this verdict had changed was because of the thoughts of a single disciple- the same being that had come down to carry out the massacre.","So they were thankful to this disciple, and at the same time they were increasingly fearful of him and the force he represented!","In this Magus World that was soon about to be divided up by the forces that the Celestials would send down to stabilize and rule the world, a new era of fearful submission would begin for its inhabitants as only a single motivation would come to rule this world...and it was fear!"]},{"number":354,"title":"Chapter 354: Chapter 353 - Celestial Realm?","paragraphs":["A grand Prime Warship was coursing through the vastness of space as numerous communications were being sent all around because of the recent actions.","The scenes of the illusory screens that appeared on many Prime Worlds had long since been recorded by others through their own means, with their events being disseminated to many as the days passed.","This would go on to achieve the goal of fear that the Celestials had as many watched the battle prowess of two Void Realm disciples go on to decimate powerful beings at the Soul Forging Realm.","If this was the power of the Celestials at the Void Realm, just how terrifying were they when they were at a higher level?!","This was the question that would spread among the hearts of many that would come across the bloodbath of the Magus World, a question that would go on to influence the actions of numerous forces as they would always think back to this event when they planned their actions for the future.","In the Prime Warship, numerous thoughts passed through Noah’s mind as he thought back to the words of the Grandmaster.","The old man’s white beard was brilliantly shining as his face became brighter while he talked about the reminder that Noah had given him about the forgetful nature of beings, and how they could move from now on while putting into account this nature!","When Noah had asked exactly what the Grandmaster was intending to do, he had only received a single answer.","\"The Celestial Realm!\"","Athena’s eyes had shone intense lights at these words, with the Grandmaster’s face turning to that of pondering excitement as he rambled out a few more words.","\"...Well, this would require the permission and compliance of numerous Grandmasters and Celestial Stars...but I am sure an agreement can be reached after they see and evaluate the influencing of fate today.\"","Grandmaster Vredral’s domineering aura erupted out as he finished his words, his white beard waving majestically as his eyes shone with light!","\"I see a way to rapidly expand our influence as we prepare for the coming war...Haha, yes!\"","It seemed like the ramblings of an old man, but there was an enormous power behind it as his figure disappeared from Noah’s and Athena’s eyes, their auras sensing him reappearing in the central command area of the ship as he sat down in a meditative pose and closed his eyes, most likely working to send numerous telepathic messages out!","Noah replayed this scene in his mind as he thought about his own actions and the effects they had, as well as achieving his goal of successfully stopping the destruction of an entire world.","With the Magus World, he realized that the destructive ways of the Celestials could definitely be avoided if only they did things differently than looking at the numbers of lives in such a nonchalant manner.","To them, if they could save the lives of tens of billions and the cost was a few billion, it was worth it and they would have no qualms about it. But if there was a possibility to reduce the number of deaths even more, why not do it?","He actually found himself agreeing with the Celestial’s use of the law of fate to discern coming chaos, but completely disagreed with them when it came to how they carried it out! These recent experiences did not change his viewpoint of them too much, only making him more vigilant about their true aims as this powerful organization gave such little regard to the lives of those they reigned over.","He now wanted to move forward while continuing to learn more about the workings of the Celestials, especially this Celestial Realm that Grandmaster Vredral had mentioned. His mind moved fast as he used [Fate Traverser], the absolute ability that came with the <<Herald of Fate>>!","<strong>[Fate Traverser] :: As one that is proficient in the workings of fate, you have more of a leeway over your own fate. This ability allows you to traverse to the most favorable outcome of your fate.</strong>","In the expansive room of the Prime Warship that he was in alone, a golden sheen appeared to cover his body as he peered into the most favorable possibilities for his own future.","The skill was extremely mysterious to grasp, not exactly showing him the course of events to follow, but simply bringing to his mind a few images and thoughts that if he were to follow, he would be able to achieve the most favorable outcome for his future!","His eyes shone with l.u.s.ter as in his mind, the words ’Celestial Realm’ coursed through multiple times, while a drop of blood shone brighter as a unique energy went into it. The Last thing he saw while under the influence of [Fate Traverser] was the brief image of a shimmering floating landmass.","His eyes snapped wide open as he breathed out, collecting his thoughts as he garnered more information on how he should move in the near future. They would deal with the Celestial Realm, his Spiritual Land, and something to do with the Vampyre Progenitor!","He deciphered the things he saw while under the influence of [Fate Traverser] as he focused on the one thing he could effectively change right now, and this was the scene where a unique energy was going into a drop of blood. He applied this to himself and the abilities he had as this made him believe that for his next course of actions, they would play out most favorably for him if he focused on using the unique energy that was the Skill Points to further along the skill tree he gained in the Ancient Blood World.","Not the stupendous Celestial Skill Tree that was the [Fate’s Guardian], not the terrifying skill tree of the [Lesser Cthulhu], nor the [Abhorred Lich Emperor] that continued to amass Skill Points in the Infernal World for him even now!","[Fate Traverser] was showing him to first put his focus on [Blood Lord], the skill tree under the Vampyre Progenitor, as the thing that would help him the most in the near future. His eyes shone as he looked at the number of Skill Points he had amassed now, and began pondering exactly how he should go about upgrading this skill tree from the Void and into the Soul Rank. The major thought in his mind as he did this was- What exactly came in the next rank of this skill tree that would cause his journey to go in an even smoother direction?"]},{"number":355,"title":"Chapter 355: Chapter 354 - Steering Towards the Optimal Fate","paragraphs":["The Prime Warship continued to smoothly traverse through the vastness of space as it was returning to the 7th Celestial Star at a much more relaxed pace than when it departed.","Noah was meditating in a wide room on top of a uniquely designed bed as he pondered on his next moves.","There were numerous things occurring at this moment as a result of his actions in the Magus World, but he had already wiped his hands as he looked forward into the future, watching the results of his actions continue to come as time passed.","The thing he was placing his focus on currently was the upgrade of a particular Skill Tree that [Fate Traverser] hinted to be one of the things that would lead him towards his optimum fate.","His gaze turned towards the Skill Points that the Abhorred Lich Emperor had continued to farm on his behalf, the unique energy smoothly being passed from his summon and unto him as the number rose drastically over the last month. The current number of skill points caused Noah’s eyes to shine a brilliant light!","[Infernal Skill Point(s)] :: 601","Currently, he held more than 601 Skill Points as the Lich Emperor worked hard to take down Infernals as well as keep watch over the training Harbingers!","This large number allowed for many possibilities, but also directly affected another thing he was very much looking forward to.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(20%)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor]","[Fate Line(s): 18100]","[Vitality: VOID]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: VOID]","With the increase of Skill Points, it also meant he was collecting the unique energy of the Infernals at a rapid rate, increasing the unique energy he required before he could fully gain and embody the title of an Infernal Lord!","This was also a momentous event by itself that he had to be very careful about as an Infernal Lord directly stood against the Celestials, and even though he had learned a few of their abilities and had become able to actively conceal his fate, there were still many things he had to be careful of.","He placed the title of an Infernal Lord aside for now as he looked at the Void Realm [Blood Lord.]","He had not been able to raise the proficiency of the skill at a rapid rate as usual because he was contained in the 7th Celestial Star, much of his time spent condensing Fate Lines, learning from the Grandmaster, and sparring with Athena. Under the watch of the powerful beings that were the celestials, he did not even bring the Spiritual Land with him as he left it in the First Realm of Hell for the Harbingers to use as a base as they moved.","Thus, he also could not lock himself in the Time Space to quickly raise the proficiency of skills!","This meant that in order for him to successfully upgrade this skill tree currently, he had to reduce his progress in collecting Skill Points and actually use a few of them to raise the proficiency level of [Blood Lord]. For a Void Rank Skill, 5 skill points had to be permanently used up in order to max the proficiency of the skill, and this would then allow him to produce a (+) level skill through combinations, allowing him to then open up the next stage of this skill tree.","Usage of the Skill Points in this manner was not something that he wanted to do, but he currently had no way of leaving the Celestial Star, and the use of [Fate Traverser] and his own intuition told him that he would most likely find an answer to this problem in the abilities of the Blood Progenitor!","He sighed as he steeled his heart and commanded 5 skill points to go into maxing the proficiency of [Blood Lord], his eyes then turning to the numerous skills he had gained from the many Magi that he had just defeated.","Every time he struck down the Bloodline Magi in the Magus World, their origin energy would smoothly be absorbed by the System as it was turned into the usual Skill Books and cores that would have normally gone directly into his storage pouch or rings, but since he did not have need of them since the advent of the ability contained in the absolute skill <<Astral Connector>>, all the [Core]s and [Skill Book]s went directly into the [Expansive Space] of this absolute skill.","In this wide space that acted like an inventory that only he had access to, numerous [Core]s and [Skill Book]s that came from beings ranging from Legendary all the way to Soul Forging were laid out majestically!","This was one of the few good things to come out of the bloody venture, actually allowing Noah to be able to farm new skills and cores from these powerful beings, the most important thing being the fact that he got his hands on Soul Rank cores and skills that would boost his power even more.","Of those worthy to note, from the deaths of the Dark Winged Serpent and the Flame Winged Serpent, a total of four Soul Rank skills landed on his lap! From the kill steal of the most powerful Magus of the Order of the Black Serpent, the Devouring Winged Serpent, Noah actually gained a Soul+ Rank skill that would allow him to take on the form of the Devouring Winged Serpent itself.","But his focus currently wasn’t on these Soul Rank skills that he could not freely use in his current environment, but on the Void and Void+ Rank skills he had gained from the Void Realm beings that he had taken down along with the leaders of the Order of the Black Serpent!","It was these skills that he needed to use in order to upgrade his Skill Trees to the next level. There were a large amount of Void Realm Magi in the bloody battle that just occurred, giving him tens of Void Rank [Skill Book]s and a total of 9 Void+ skills that came from the most powerful combatants on the battle field.","The collection of all of these skills made it possible for him to use another 5 Skill Points on one of the newly obtained Void Rank skills, maxing its proficiency as he went on to sacrifice this skill in order to take [Blood Lord] into the Void+ level!","He watched the stat panel with rapt attention as the classification of [Blood Lord] went from Void to Void+ without even a name change, the only thing changing being the number of skill points required for him to open up the next pathway of the skill tree after he met the requirements.","<strong>VOID+ [Blood Lord] (30/45)::</strong> A technique that only those with the purest forms of blood can use. Two Skill Trees for evolution are possible once sufficient points and a base requirement of two equivalent level sacrificial skills are reached: <strong>>>Elder Vampyre</strong>- Leads the Blood Lord towards the path of a Ruler, gaining abilities geared towards leading the race of Vampyres. <strong>>>Kin of the Ancients</strong>- Leads the Blood Lord towards the path of Ancients, awakening the qualities only found in the strongest of the Ancient Races.","Noah’s eyes shone in the quietly moving Prime Warship as he observed the details of the next pathways of the [Blood Lord] skill tree. Elder Vampyre or Kin of the Ancients, what would it be?","He smiled as he already knew his choice right away while he read the description, his thoughts already moving as he sent the command to add in the needed Skill Points and ready 2 of the newly obtained Void+ skills to be sacrificed, his eyes looking forward to what the grand future would bring!"]},{"number":356,"title":"Chapter 356: Chapter 355 - As if one wasnt enough!","paragraphs":["Of course, the choice was simple when considering Noah had the bloodline of the Vampyre Progenitor himself, the need for abilities that would help with leading the race of Vampyres not being useful to him at all as he had ultimate power over them just with his bloodline.","What he went for...was the pathway that talked about the Ancient Races!","His eyes shone as he made sure to activate [Fate Concealment] and continue using [Unique Origin] to ensure that nothing suspicious was found out by the Celestials in the Prime Warship. He watched with anticipation as two of the newly obtained Void+ skills from the numerous Void Rank Magi he had taken down disappeared, while a brand new extension appeared on the spectacularly designed skill tree that was the [Blood Lord].","<strong>SOUL [Blood Lord] (45/45):: A technique that only those with the purest forms of blood can use. It is Ancient Blood Magic that includes the abilities Dawn of the Blood Lord(5/5), Blood World(5/5), Drain Life(5/5), and Nightmarish Descent(5/5). >> [Kin of the Ancients] (0/60) :: Ancient Blood Scion(0/5), Ancient Blood Clone(0/5), Summon the Ancients(0/5), Blood Rage(0/5)</strong>","<strong>[Ancient Blood Scion] :: Take on the form of the scion of blood and rain down destruction on those that oppose you. This form allows you to heal 5% of all damage dealt and received, increase Physical and Elemental Damage by 30%, as well as enhance all the abilities of [Blood Lord] by 5%.</strong>","<strong>[Ancient Blood Clone] :: The user can create a clone through using Origin Blood. This clone will be connected to the user as if it is an extension of their own limbs. The clone can only exhibit 10% of the original’s abilities. </strong>","<strong>[Summon the Ancients] :: Your call travels through space and time as you call forth the Ancients that are bound by blood. Limit: 1 Ancient</strong>","<strong>[Blood Rage] :: A destructive storm of blood begins to rotate with you at the center, raging with the capabilities of disintegrating all enemies caught within. Affected Area- 50 meters. </strong>","Noah glanced at the stupendous additions to the Blood Lord skill tree which further enhanced the previous abilities and also added new skills that he was looking at with joy!","Putting the transformation ability that was the [Ancient Blood Scion] aside, he had gained yet another summoning ability- and this one allowed him to summon the beings called Ancients!","The current limit of this was 1, but this number would undoubtedly rise when he began to pump skill points into it.","The other skill worthy of note was [Blood Rage] as it seemed to be an extremely powerful area of attack skill, and he couldn’t wait to watch the skill at work with his own eyes whenever he got the chance to try it.","But the ability that made him the happiest was the [Ancient Blood Clone] ability!","The use of a skill like a clone might seem mediocre to others, especially when this clone would only be able to exhibit a percentage of the original’s abilities. But for Noah, this was the most important ability to come out of this upgrade, one that he could already see huge implications of!","His gaze became one of pondering as his thoughts rapidly moved, many possibilities on how to utilize these newly gained skills and how they went in line with the hints he received from [Fate Traverser].","In a few seconds, numerous plans laid out in his mind as he then went on to focus on the shining words of [Ancient Blood Clone] on the stat panel. He moved his thoughts as 5 Skill Points were quickly added into the ability, the number on the description changing drastically as a result.","<strong>[Ancient Blood Clone] :: The user can create a clone through using Origin Blood. This clone will be connected to the user as if it is an extension of their own limbs. The clone can only portray 60% of the original’s abilities. </strong>","He glanced at the ability as currently, it could create an Ancient Blood Close that would be able to exhibit over half of his power! When he thought about this limitation while putting his so-called skills into account though...Noah could not help but smile as he knew for him, it wouldn’t be anything to worry about!","His gaze hardened in the next moment as he prepared to do something bold, his attention placed on the [Fate Concealment] ability as well as the [Unique Origin] of the Vampyre Progenitor, making sure both of their auras of concealment covered his surroundings as he cast [Ancient Blood Clone].","The movement of mana that only he could feel erupted out as he felt a minuscule piece of himself detaching from him, shooting out of his body speedily as it came out as an extremely dark red drop of blood!","The dense drop of blood shone with a unique l.u.s.ter as it came from his own origin, his gaze only being able to observe it briefly before it began expanding and ballooning up rapidly.","He watched with care and fascination as this single drop of blood gradually transformed into a n.a.k.e.d red figure that gradually seemed to gained bones, muscles, and skin as soon enough, an extremely dashing image of himself was seated in front of him.","It was a weird and eerie feeling as he felt his consciousness within both bodies, feeling both of his eyes stare back at himself as he performed some simple movements. The mind enhancing skills like [Parallel Thought] soon came into play to smoothly allow him to think with clarity while he controlled his now two bodies.","The clone had the image of his original body as Noah, not the image of Crixus as he was currently portrayed. He looked over it briefly as he nodded his head at this devilishly handsome being in front of his eyes as he couldn’t help but let out a laugh.","Accomplishment was apparent on his two faces as the clone’s waved his hands, a red robe draping its body as in the next second, it disappeared into particles of light!","He reduced the mana he was continuously placing into [Fate Concealment] and [Unique Origin] as in the room he was in, the same calmness continued. While in a far away region across the vastness of space, the figure of Noah had appeared above a grand Spiritual Land that was stably floating in the skies of a fiery hell.","One being was on a Prime Warship heading back into the lands of the Celestials, another being had just teleported into the First Realm of Hell. As if one of him wasn’t already ridiculously overpowered enough, Noah would now have two of him moving across the Novus Galaxy as he planned to move with monstrous efficiency!","If his enemies had found out about this advancement, they would weep as they cried unfairness, as the future was bound to be even more tumultuous!"]},{"number":357,"title":"Chapter 357: Chapter 356 - Progress, Shocking Plans","paragraphs":["As his consciousness continued to familiarize itself with the feeling of controlling two bodies, his original one continued its way on the Prime Warship towards the 7th Celestial Star, while the Ancient Blood Clone teleported into the First Realm of Hell.","His original body would still have to be the main one he was moving with when associating with the Celestials because as the [Ancient Blood Clone] ability described, the clone was was an extension of himself akin to a limb! He could observe his stat panel and all of his skills through the clone’s eyes, as well as do anything else that his original body could do.","It only held a portion of his origin that was able to use his strength, though he would have to test exactly to what extent he could utilize this clone as there were a few things to make sure of.","He had to first confirm the abilities of the clone when it came to its strength and capabilities, as well as usefulness in helping him increase the proficiency of his skills. He was thinking all of these things as his clone began by spreading his awareness towards the Spiritual Land and the eerily calm blazing earth that was normally surrounded by Infernals but was currently filled with numerous undead that orderly kept watch.","His intrusion above the skies of the Spiritual Land was first noticed by Barbatos, only to be later followed by the Abhorred Lich Emperor that was tens of miles away, its senses only picking up the distinct aura of its master as it left behind a high tiered Bone Dragon and Undead Phoenix to patrol the skies that the Spiritual Land was floating on.","Barbatos held the highest strength amongst those that followed him, her senses picking him up around the same time as Noah found her to be relaxing on a snowy planting field that was packed with numerous Medicinal Fruits and Herbs along with the Imperial Phoenix.","The two of them were both in their humanoid forms, simple thin dresses draping over them as they walked around the plot of resplendently glowing plants that held bright fruits, reaching out and plucking them to enjoy as they wished.","When paired with the abundant essence in the Spiritual Land, it was a paradisiacal scene of enjoyment that very few would have the chance to come across. Barbatos senses his aura first as she looked up and shot into the air, the Imperial Phoenix following close behind as these were some of the few Harbingers to remain in the First Realm of Hell while others were in the Underworld. Barbatos looked up at him with a mischievous smile as she called out.","\"Little fish, I thought you’d be stuck with the Celestials for months. They already gave you a break?\"","Noah smiled as he saw the Imperial Phoenix also near and nod towards him, descending down into the Spiritual Land with them as he told them the shocking truth that the body they were currently seeing was just a clone!","Barbatos only shook her head while saying deprecatingly,","\"Haaa of course it is, as if you weren’t already crazy enough.\"","While the Imperial Phoenix only looked towards Noah with shining eyes. He enjoyed the company of the people that weren’t Celestials as he descended into the Spiritual Land and got up to speed with everyone’s progress, which was shocking to say the least!","For those that stayed on the Spiritual Land and used the ridiculously amazing Time Space, they were able to practice their skills and raise their proficiencies rapidly in this span of 30 days that was actually more than a few months depending on how much time they were in the Time Space.","They didn’t have Noah’s nearly unlimited mana, so of course they weren’t training day and night. But they worked arduously as they spent months in the Time Space raising their skills’ proficiencies, fully utilizing the ratio of 1:20 as they made huge gains even when considering their abilities.","Noah was the only outlier that could abuse the Time Space to the fullest, but his Harbingers were able to utilize it along with the use of Skill Points to smoothly have many of their ranks and skill trees at the peak of SAINT!","To normal beings, this was a rapid rate of progress, although it might seem like a turtle’s pace when putting Noah’s speed into account, and how rapidly he would have grown if he had been spending an entire month in the Time Space that now had the ratio of 1:20. For now, the harbingers only required a few more combinations before they could stably push their skills from Saint and into the Void Rank.","But...this was where Noah would come in to cause an explosive boost in their strength as after a recent bout with hundreds of thousands of Magi, he had obtained for himself numerous [Core]s that would be able to bring many of them from their Transcendent or Saint Ranks and allow them to stably step into the Void Realm.","This held an even bigger significance to Noah when it came to the beasts of the Spiritual Land, as their jump from Saint and into the Void would have a stupendous meaning by itself.","When he left to head into the 7th Celestial Star a month ago, the Emperor Penguin was the only beast to have stepped into the Saint Rank, where many other beasts needed to reach the same rank before the qualifications of upgrading the Spiritual Land to the next tier was met.","In the span of the last month, many more of these beasts had stepped into the Saint Realm, fulfilling the requirement to upgrade to the next tier! But Noah would not just stop there, as the many [Core]s and gifts he had obtained from the Magus World would be focused towards these beasts as he planned to directly pump the tier of the Spiritual Land by 2 all at once!","He would push these beasts into the Void Rank forcefully as he wanted to see why [Fate Traverser] held the Spiritual Land as one of the three things he could currently use to push him towards his most optimum fate.","The [Blood Lord] skill tree had made it possible for him to create a clone, which would have its own stupendous uses as time passed. Now, he wanted to pierce through the veil of the continued usefulness of the Spiritual Land as he planned to domineeringly push its rank by two tiers all at once.","It was defying common sense, and it wasn’t something that anyone else could do. But he wanted to and he had the capability to do it, so he would!"]},{"number":358,"title":"Chapter 358: Chapter 357 - Power Leveling!","paragraphs":["Noah sent a telepathic message towards the Emperor Penguin and the other Harbingers that were still in the underworld. They were confused at this message but followed it nonetheless as they left behind the things they were doing and soon began appearing in the underground layer of the Spiritual Land where a red portal stably stood.","The figure of the Emperor Penguin became ecstatic as it sensed the familiar energy signature of the master of the Spiritual Land, his figure teleporting to the location where Noah stood with Barbatos and the Imperial Phoenix as his beak snapped open in stupefaction.","\"Master!\"","The arrogant penguin was shocked because he had just been observing his master rain down destruction in a Prime World not long ago, and knew he should be surrounded by the powerful forces of Celestials at all times!","Noah nodded towards the penguin with a smile as the others gradually came in, those that were training in the Time Space of the Spiritual Land and those that were taking down Infernals in the far distance all returning as he repeated his circ.u.mstances yet again.","\"Successfully infiltrated a crazy powerful force while picking up skills that even allow you to make a clone. We have to celebrate!\"","The boisterous Kazuhiko returned as he gave Noah a bear hug and called for a celebration before anything else, Noah pondering for a bit before agreeing as he would relax his mind a bit before carrying out the stupendous upgrades.","\"Little fish, can you prepare something for us? It’s been a while since I tasted something remotely as good as the food you whip up.\"","Barbatos looked at him with shining eyes as she called out, causing a smile to form on Noah’s face as he looked back to the Rank A [Cook] he had not put to use in a while. He acquiesced to their requests as his figure teleported into the seas of his homeworld to quickly grab some delicacies in the form of deep-sea fish. He quickly popped into the Beast World as well, grabbing the Frozen Queen and the Shadow Guard that was always with her thereafter!","The process didn’t take him longer than 5 minutes as he returned to the Spiritual Land, numerous deep sea fish in his [Expansive Space], and the fl.u.s.tered face of Queen Adelaide accompanying him.","A fire was soon set ablaze as Noah looked at the [Cook] skill, putting 5 Skill Points into the Rank A ability just for fun before he began, a blazing fire erupting thereafter as the aroma of food that would make Rulers jealous spread throughout the Spiritual Land.","In under half an hour, numerous well roasted meats were ready for devouring, even the Calamities of the Sea feeling no guilt as they smelled the fragrant aroma seeping out of the glistening deep sea fish rotating above the simmering fire.","\"Dig in!\"","Noah called out as he used [Architecture] to create a simple styled outdoor dining area where he laid out the numerous delectable dishes, the many beings around him digging in thereafter as the next few hours were spent in bliss enjoying dishes cooked by a Rank A skill that was enhanced with Skill Points.","It was a surreal experience for Noah as his original body was nearing the 7th Celestial Star, returning to the abode of the Celestials as another piece of him was somewhere else doing something he did not expect to be doing a few hours ago!","He smiled at the crazy possibilities that the skill trees could bring to life as he enjoyed himself for the next few hours, the taste buds of the clone being no less than the original as he relished on his own creations.","He wrapped up this brief relaxation period in a few hours as his gaze shone while looking at the numerous beasts lined up in front of him.","The Emperor Penguin was at the peak of the Saint Rank, his brothers and sisters already entering the same rank in the past month as more than enough beasts had already met the requirement of upgrading to the 7th Tier Spiritual Land.","But...he wouldn’t stop there!","He waved his hands towards the beasts as numerous Saint and Void Rank [Core]s appeared before their eyes, one of the few positive things coming out of the Magus World showing itself into the eyes of everyone around him as they looked on in shock.","Others were simply shaking their heads deprecatingly as what they knew to be the norm continued to be destroyed by this single being in front of them.","The beasts wasted no time as they followed the commands of the Spiritual Land Master, beginning to consume the cores right away as the dense essence of the Spiritual Land continued to converge around them.","RUMBLE!","Noah watched on from the sides with careful eyes as he observed every minuscule change. In under an hour, the Emperor Penguin was the first to finish consuming numerous Void Cores as his rank was finally pushed from Saint and into the Void!","The process continued on for another half a day as one by one, the beasts gradually rose to the peak of the Saint Realm and then consumed more and more of the provided cores until they broke through into the Void Rank.","This number continued until it passed 10, where Noah was confident it would be more than enough for the requirements of the upgrade as he nodded his head with an accomplished gaze. The requirements to upgrade the Spiritual Land into the 7th Tier was to have more than 5 beasts step into the Saint Realm, and he was sure the upgrade into the 8th Tier would be similar, if not the number being slightly higher.","Looking at the unstable realms of the beasts that just broke through, and the many more still continuing the process of absorbing Cores and pushing their ranks up unceasingly, Noah’s face hardened as he breathed out, feeling the connection with the main body and the immense mana it was connected to, his close simply acting as another limb as it called forth this bubbling mana while he initiated the upgrade of the Spiritual Land into the next tier.","This time, he would not just stop at one upgrade, but would also continue with the next one soon after!","His gaze looked ahead into the far future as he pondered the results of these upgrades. He knew the 7th Tier would unlock the [Law Space], something he had yet to wrap his mind around on exactly how crazy it would be. But, what would be the prize for upgrading all the way to the 8th Tier?"]},{"number":359,"title":"Chapter 359: Chapter 358 - Upgrade of Multiple Tiers","paragraphs":["On the 7th Celestial Star, the party that had set off towards the Magus World had returned with refreshed faces as they successfully achieved the mission. Athena held a light smile as they returned to the Inquiring Mountain that Grandmaster Vredral had the control of, the Grandmaster himself letting them know that he would be meeting with the other Grandmasters that were overseeing their own disciples and jobs on the 7th Celestial Star.","His face was that of profound enthusiasm as it seemed the task he was going to be talking about with the other Grandmasters was one of great importance! This sense of atmosphere only made Noah more inquisitive about the Celestial Realm that the Grandmaster mentioned, waiting patiently to find out from this Grandmaster what this location would entail.","When it came to others like Vredral, each of the Grandmasters on the 7th Celestial Star had their own divisions that they handled, paving way for a very well oiled organization that Noah was only beginning to get a grasp of. He had only been staying in the Inquiring Mountain for the past month, and his thoughts were leading him towards exploring this star some more in the coming days as he got more of a grasp on the domain of the Celestials.","Noah was taken out of his thoughts as the still vibrant Athena spoke towards him melodiously, her gaze that of shining brilliance.","\"Junior Brother, why don’t we reflect on our recent battle with a spar while we wait for the Grandmaster? I would love to experience the power of those wondrous Blades of Liberation myself if you don’t mind.\"","The War Princess that lived for battle called out with shining eyes as Noah turned towards her, hiding his thoughts as he replied with a smile.","\"Of course, let’s go!\"","He followed her lead towards a peaceful area on the wide Inquiring Mountain as he humored her thirst for battle, knowing his own skills would be increased as he continued to fight with someone holding such a grand title as the War Princess.","While his main body had begun a spar on the 7th Celestial Star, his clone was using even more mana across the stars on the First Realm of Hell as he oversaw a stupendous upgrade!","In the fiery skies of the First Hell, an aurora of colors was spreading out as the expansive Spiritual Land was exploding with numerous mystical lights. The essence converging within this floating island was becoming so thick that one almost felt like they could grasp it.","On the side, the [Abhorred Lich] emperor had pulled back many of the forces of the Undead Legion as they patrolled the blazing lands and the fiery skies of the First Hell, stopping any rushing Infernals on the outer perimeters as they didn’t want any disturbances to come to their master.","Numerous Bone Dragons, Undead Phoenixes, and Specters were floating across the skies around the Spiritual Land as an aurora of colors continued, until they reached a crescendo that exploded outwards!","RUMBLE!","The skies trembled as Noah confirmed the Spiritual Land had successfully been upgraded to the 7th Tier, checking the requirements of the upgrade for the next tier as he saw it was having 10 Beasts born in the Spiritual Land to have reached the rank of Void.","He smiled as his preparations were correct, the essence he could access with the clone body rumbling once more as he used {Spiritual Land Management} to initiate another upgrade of tiers seconds after one just finished.","WAA!","The essence of the First Realm of Hell that was gradually calming became wild once more as ridiculously, even more converged towards the Spiritual Land, a denser convergence occurring this time around something stupendous repeated once more.","The Harbingers watching this process on the side actually did not find themselves overly shocked anymore, the things they watched Noah do so frequently becoming less and less of the crazy actions they seemed as they now became the norm.","The process of convergence of essence into the Spiritual Land repeated once more as both the mana in the surroundings and Noah’s own mana continued to be sucked into the floating landmass, the result this time even more significant as when it finished, a blue circular ring of light shot forth from the Spiritual Land as it announced the arrival of something grand!","The owner of this magnificent Spiritual Land was the one looking forward to seeing the results of this upgrade the most as he quickly pulled up the stat panel and looked under {Spiritual Land Management}.","<strong>{Spiritual Land Management}</strong>","<strong>[Frozen Plateau-8]</strong>","<strong>Beasts: F-XXX, E-XXX, D-XXX, C-XXX, B-XXX, A-XXX, S-XXX, EPIC-15,285, LEGENDARY-3,286, MYTHICAL-1432, PHANTASMAL-345, TRANSCENDENT-99, Saint- 14, Void- 13</strong>","<strong>Plants- Whitefall Trees, Snow Vine, Sacred Rye, Pigmy Melon, Ice-fire Persimmon, Ice Phoenix Fruits, Spirit of the Arctic, Frozen Angelica, Regal Flora, Qilin’s Cold Stone, Resonant Okra. Available for planting(Arctic Flora, King’s Collard, Athramire, Phantom Mulberry) </strong>","<strong>Features- Size Regulation(Unlocked), Movement(Unlocked), Anchor(Unlocked), Boost Surroundings(Unlocked), Architecture(Unlocked), Frozen Barrier(Unlocked), Offensive Maneuvers(Unlocked), Time Dilation(Unlocked), Treasure Hunter (Unlocked), Interstellar Travel(Unlocked), Law Space(Unlocked), Blacksmith’s Forge(Unlocked), Division(Locked)[email protected]#%#$%(Locked)</strong>","<strong>Upgrade Conditions: 10+ Spiritual Land Beasts at the Soul Rank, A Small World Core</strong>","The new additions gained from the upgrade of the Spiritual Land to the 8th Tier were clearly laid out in front of his eyes, with the features labeled as Law Space and the new feature called the Blacksmith’s Forge that was obtained from the 8th Tier Upgrade making his eyes burst with excitement!","Something even more ridiculous that he saw at the end of {Spiritual Land Management} was the upgrade condition for the 9th Tier of the Spiritual Land...it stated that aside from the usual condition of beasts achieving the next rank, a Core of a Small World was required!","The implications of this requirement were so grand that even Noah’s wildest imagination could not fantasize about what exactly would come out of an upgrade that required a Core of a world. The significance of the actions he would have to do if he wanted to carry out this future upgrade only dawned on him a second later.","But...he put these thoughts aside for now as he looked back at the new features that were respectively labeled Law Space, and the even more domineering one called the Blacksmith’s Forge!"]},{"number":360,"title":"Chapter 360: Chapter 359 - Law Space, Blacksmiths Forge!","paragraphs":["The first thing Noah observed was the details of the Law Space under the tab of {Spiritual Land Management}.","<strong>[Law Space] :: Fields containing a higher concentration of particular laws can be created, granting increased comprehension speed to all that cultivate within. Currently unlocked spaces: Water, Fire, Earth, Air. Locked spaces: Time, Space, Light, Dark, Fate, Chaos...</strong>","His eyes shone as he read the simplistic details of the features called Law Space, seeing its stupendous uses in the future, but his heart aching for the fact that it did not yet have the space that dealt with Supreme Laws like the Law of Fate unlocked!","He looked forward into the future as he would do whatever it took to raise the tiers of the Spiritual Land until the most unbelievable boosts were unlocked. He placed his attention next to the feature called [Blacksmith’s Forge] as he became even more surprised.","<strong>[Blacksmith’s Forge] :: A unique forge created for the purpose of smelting the most refined Items. The level of the Item created will be reflected on what materials were provided. A singular Item or an Item Set can be created. An immense output of energy is required to use the forge. Currently craftable Item Ranks: ...Saint, Void, Supreme Treasure. Locked: !#[email protected][email protected]$ Treasure...</strong>","A tremor passed through Noah’s heart as he read over the descriptions of the newly added features of the Spiritual Land, the Blacksmith’s Forge being the most unique one that he could not wait to try out!","He currently wasn’t cultivating any of the laws that would be boosted by the available Law Spaces, and he would utilize this feature to the fullest extent when the higher ranked Law Spaces were finally unlocked. He had some percentages in the Law of Water and the Law of Space, but many of his skills weren’t geared towards them currently, and he didn’t have something as profound as [Fate’s Disciple] that allowed him to draw in the unique Fate Lines.","When it came to Items, besides the Supreme Treasures like the Trident of the Sea that he rarely used on big fights, their use had gradually diminished for him as his body would almost always have more than enough defenses that an armor would be rendered null. In some cases, even his own skills like the abilities in [Fate’s Guardian] provide their own weapons and armor that are capable of dealing tremendous damage while protecting him from harm.","Thus, he knew that items of the Saint or Void Rank would be fairly useless for him, but this didn’t mean they wouldn’t be extremely useful to his forces. Not everyone had the capabilities to passively keep defensive skills active at all times with their unlimited mana, so Items would still show extreme usefulness to them. As for Noah himself, only something like a Supreme Treasure could boost his abilities further, as they almost always held sub-abilities that heavily enhanced his battle power.","He breathed out as he realized he had many things to do, his senses sweeping over the wide Spiritual Land to observe the numerous changes as the essence coming off of the floating landmass was palpable.","It seemed like a haven for increasing one’s power as he was sure any normal being would awaken instantly the moment they stepped on this Spiritual Land. He put his thoughts aside as he outlined what he had to do as his main body continued moving in the 7th Celestial Star.","He had to check out the newly available plants and begin spreading them out over numerous fields, he had to observe the workings of the Law Space, the Blacksmith’s Forge, and then finally begin the task of training the proficiencies of his skill trees in the Time Space of the Spiritual Land. There were numerous things to take care of, but he felt full of energy as he descended down towards the Spiritual Land, the Harbingers following his lead as they explored this paradisiacal floating landmass anew once more!","---","\"Haaa.\"","In the 7th Celestial Star, a heavily breathing Noah and Athena were taking a break beside the bank of a destroyed stream, numerous pits and fissures spread out around them for miles in the small section of the Inquiring Mountain they were on.","The pits and fissures spread out all around were caused from the horrendous attacks coming from Blades of Liberation, the rest of the destruction simply caused by the impact of their spar over the last few hours.","The valiant Athena let out small breaths as she shook her head in a ludicrous manner while looking at Noah, not believing the talent of this being as he had managed to withstand her power even after she used 30,000 Fate Lines!","The Junior Disciple in front of her currently had a bit over 18,000 lines of fate, and yet all she managed to do was finally make him sweat as he called for a break while citing the lack of energy as the excuse.","Even though they had been exchanging attacks evenly this whole time, Athena took it as her win as she had managed to drain this Junior Brother of all his energy until he couldn’t continue any longer!","Noah took in Athena’s gaze as he utilized his acting skills to slowly reduce the rapid breaths he was taking, pausing the ongoing spar where he learned many things as he played the role of a younger disciple that couldn’t go on any longer.","\"Thank you for the spar, Senior Sister.\"","Athena nodded towards him as a smile appeared on her face, expressing much more emotion as her guard dropped more and more around this Junior Brother. She looked thoughtfully at him as she said slowly thereafter.","\"Call me Athena. We’ll drop the ranks of Junior and Senior for now as you seem to be keeping up even if I go above the power you can effectively utilize. The moment you stop keeping up you’ll have to call me Senior Sister again.\"","The expression of a younger disciple nodding proudly appeared on Noah’s face as he was about to reply, his words cut short as both he and Athena heard the words of a certain Grandmaster ring out in their minds.","\"Come to the Monastery, I have good news!\"","Without a second delay, the two of them rose from the destroyed area of the mountain they were in as they began to fly towards the peak of the Inquiring Mountain. The immense damage they had caused had already begun the process of healing as the immense essence covering the mountain had already spurted the growth of plants and vegetation in the destroyed areas that would soon return to the original beauty!","Their figures went into the Monastery where Grandmaster Vredral sat serenely while stroking his white beard, his gaze looking towards them with a nod as they respectfully sat in front of him.","\"Athena, how much do you know about the Celestial Realm?\"","\"Grandmaster, all I have overheard over the years is how it is a land of immense opportunity, and the reason why we hold the sway that we have over the Light Expanse today is because of this Celestial Realm.\"","Athena replied quickly as her eyes shone, the Grandmaster laughing in affirmation as he began weaving a grand story about something at the center of the Celestials’ strength, he began talking about the Celestial Realm!"]},{"number":361,"title":"Chapter 361: Chapter 360 - A Vast Realm Unlike Any Other","paragraphs":["\"This is something that only the Grandmasters have knowledge of so far, but you two will be playing at the centermost position in the coming months that it is knowledge which you are cleared to have!\"","The voice of the Grandmaster had a hint of solemnity as he began, both Noah and Athena sitting down respectfully in front of him as their eyes looked forward, hungry for information.","\"Much of what I am about to tell you pertains to the Celestial Realm, a realm that is unique in our Novus Galaxy, and the place that allowed for our domination these past thousands of years. It is not our destructive Warsh.i.p.s that can destroy entire stars, nor is it our proficiency in understanding the Supreme Law of Fate- it is this place called the Celestial Realm that is the reason why we stand where we are today!\"","Noah’s heart shook as he heard these words, numerous thoughts crossing his mind as the solemn Grandmaster Vredral continued to speak in front of him.","\"This is because everything we have...our weapons, our techniques that allow us to influence fate...all of this came from the Celestial Realm.\"","RUMBLE!","A tremor ran through Noah’s body as he listened with rapt attention while a Grandmaster that stood at the core of one of the Celestial Stars began revealing secrets out of his wildest dreams.","The Celestial Realm was something that a few powerful beings had found thousands of years ago, and it was these powerful figures that began to explore this realm and everything it held within it.","Their intrusion into this realm allowed for them to experience never before seen wonders, granting them unbelievable techniques and power out of their wildest imagination.","At the same time, they came to understand that it was extremely dangerous!","Among the few powerful figures that went into the Celestial Realm, only three managed to keep their lives after they delved too far within, their progress blocked by the very things that granted them techniques and immense ways to utilize mana that they never thought to be possible.","The things that made it possible for them to gain phenomenal strength while also causing the downfall of a few of them was what later came to be termed...Celestial Beasts!","At this juncture, the Grandmaster became silent as he looked at the two of them closely, seemingly arranging his thoughts before he continued.","\"It is these Celestial Beasts that are among the many things you will be looking for when the time comes for the gates of the Celestial Realm to be opened. When the Founders encountered this first bottleneck that stopped their advances, they pulled back to the perimeters of the Celestial Realm to recuperate and absorb the treasures they had obtained, growing their power exponentially before they returned to carefully exploring the Celestial Realm for the next hundred years.\"","The beings that Grandmaster Vredral called Founders were the powerhouses that stood at the top of the power known as the Celestials!","They spent more than one hundred years after breaking into the Celestial Realm as they explored the wonders within it, as well as the numerous dangers it held. In the 99th year of their exploration, they came across a particular area where they almost lost their lives, but with the danger passed, they were rewarded with a set of techniques that made them who they are today.","It was in this 99th year since they began exploring the Celestial Realm that the founders came across the techniques dealing with the Law of Fate that would go on to allow them to rapidly increase in power, going on to dominate an entire region of the vast Novus Galaxy they were from as their exploration of the Celestial Realm only continued at a rapid speed.","With their obtainment of these powerful techniques, they understood that to utilize them to their fullest, the users had to have a tremendous amount of influence on many beings. The more numerous and the more powerful the better!","\"Our founders looked upon the boon they received as they put it to use for the betterment of the Novus Galaxy they were in, going on to study the law of fate and use it to establish a reign seeking Order and Balance.\"","Grandmaster Vredral finished these words with a profoundly respectful tone as his eyes were lost in thought. Noah was absorbing all of this new information as he filtered out the enormous levels of bias and possible lies from the Grandmaster, realizing that the thing that prompted the Celestial’s quest for power and domination was simply these techniques and treasures that they obtained from this Celestial Realm.","It wasn’t some inborn need to reduce the natural order of chaos that everything was going towards, it was because the techniques they trained in required for them to have an overwhelming amount of influence on numerous beings that they chose to expand their power under the name of Order and Balance!","The power they continued to gain over the years...all of it actually went back to this Celestial Realm as they continued to explore it all this time. The Grandmaster returned to the present as his eyes focused on Noah and Athena, continuing to release huge secrets that very few were privy to.","\"In the thousands of years that followed, the Founders created the power that came to be known as Celestials, expanding their influence and recruiting more qualified forces as the years passed.\"","\"In the 1523rd year of exploration of the Celestial Realm, a few newly recruited Celestials came across treasures that you all are familiar with currently- the technology known as the Prime Warsh.i.p.s and even more phenomenal weapons that you all have yet to see. But what I want you two to realize is that all of this was made possible solely because of the Celestial Realm. What is the most shocking thing though, is that in the years that followed until this very day, the percentage of this Realm that we have been able to explore and map out...has not passed 10%!\"","...!"]},{"number":362,"title":"Chapter 362: Chapter 361 - Fantastical!","paragraphs":["The last words of the Grandmaster smashed into Noah powerfully as his thoughts rapidly moved, the meaning and possibilities behind these words being so immense that he could not even imagine!","In the last thousands of years as the Celestials expanded their power while exploring this Celestial Realm, they had only explored a measly 10% of the entire Realm!","In this area they had explored though, they were able to come across ridiculously powerful treasures that could destroy stars, as well as obtain techniques that gave them the prodigious positions that they held in the Light Expanse today.","Noah’s heart was shaking as his eyes looked forward into the unlimited possibilities of the future.","If...just if he was given access to this realm that even the Celestials had not fully explored...just what would he be able to pull out when the Celestials already received so much from just covering 10% of it?","\"There are still numerous secrets to uncover when it comes to the Celestial Realm, but the one thing we have confirmed is that the rewards are abundant. This was also the reason why knowledge of it has been kept very scarce, the privilege of exploring it given only to powerful Celestials or disciples that show overwhelming potential over the years.\"","The solemn gaze of the Grandmaster fell on the figures of Noah and Athena at this moment.","\"This is where you two come in! In the near future, you will be exploring this vast realm as you learn to grow your power even faster. With your status as those who hold a Noble Fate, who knows what you might discover, and if it would come close to the level of things that we have discovered over the years, or something out of our wildest dreams!\"","The eyes of the Grandmaster were shining as he looked at them, Noah reading between the lines as he realized that the Celestials did not just permit them entrance into the Celestial Realm for the purpose of rapidly increasing their strength, but also to use their titles as those with Noble Fate to see if they can chance upon anything at the level of the treasures they have come across over the last thousands of years.","The deep thoughts behind the actions of the Celestials made Noah more careful as the Grandmaster continued to speak.","\"Although this time it is going to be different. As I oversaw the mission in the Magus World and observed the changes in the workings of fate in real time, an idea struck me that I have passed on. We are now just awaiting confirmation but for the near future, for the first time in history- we should be opening the doors of the Celestial Realm to select individuals that do not hold the identities of Celestials!\"","His words carried an unknown meaning as he did not fully delve into what idea he had proposed and passed on, but Noah knew something huge would be occurring in the Light Expanse in the very near future.","At the center of all of it were the Celestials, and now, he had stably instituted himself in their ranks as he would be given access to a fantastical Realm he never knew existed, to the realm where the immense power of the Celestials came from!","He hid his deep smile as he continued to listen closely to the solemn Grandmaster, his eyes set on the future that seemed to be calling out to him brightly.","---","As Noah received profoundly secretive information of the 7th Celestial Star, his clone was sitting in the underground layer of the Spiritual Land that was not too far away from the expansive Time Space.","This area in front of him held a uniquely shaped black building that looked to be sculpted from metal, the sleek black color giving it an ancient aesthetic as a single metal door opened itself as Noah neared.","He entered inside to find a simmering Hearth that seemed to be calling out for it to be used as blue flames sn.a.k.e.d within, drawing a mystical contrast as he observed everything else in the Blacksmith’s Forge.","The outlines of numerous weapons, armors, and all sorts of other items he wasn’t familiar with were all laid out over the walls of the smithy, a simple styled workman’s bench placed at the very center.","Noah had a light smile as he brought himself to sit on this workman’s bench, a blue panel appearing before his eyes in a simple manner as it laid out beautiful words.","<strong>[Blacksmith’s Forge]- Unlocked Features: [Forge] [Refine] [Repair]. Locked Features: [Evolve] [Recipe Design]...</strong>","The words shone in a blue l.u.s.ter as he focused on them, gaining even more understanding as he read their descriptions.","<strong>[Forge] :: Depending on the materials placed into the forge, an exemplary item that stands at the peak of its stage will be created. If a material has a potential of synergy, the Forge will create an Item Set once sufficient materials are placed. </strong>","<strong>[Refine] :: An already completed item can be enhanced to bring out more of its potential. Requires [Core]s of sufficient level for refinement. Supreme Treasures require Unique Materials for refinement.</strong>","<strong>[Repair] :: A broken item can be repaired to its prime. Requires [Core]s of sufficient level for repair. Supreme Treasures require Unique Materials for repair.</strong>","Noah’s eyes shone as he read over all the descriptions of the things he could currently do with the Blacksmith’s Forge, many more questions appearing on his mind as he wondered first and foremost what materials would be considered unique!","From the information he read, if he used a material that was classified as a Void Rank Material, the item produced would simply be a Void Rank Item. If he got his hands on the materials that were termed Unique, creating Supreme Treasures was not an impossibility!","His mind was already going towards the Trident of the Sea when he looked over the feature of [Refine], as well as the Dagger of Time that was listed as Incomplete at this moment. In the future, it seemed like it was possible to enhance these Supreme Treasures even more, while there were numerous features to be unlocked in the future that made Noah itch with anticipation.","At this moment in time though, he would try an initial use of the Blacksmith’s Forge as he gained a better understanding of it. His clone was expressing the marvelous emotions that his real body was feeling but could not express in the 7th Celestial Star as he continued to listen to the secrets of the Celestials, numerous plans about this Celestial Realm he would delve into sometime in the future circling his mind as the clone worked steadily in the Spiritual Land!"]},{"number":363,"title":"Chapter 363: Chapter 362 - What do you know about fate?!","paragraphs":["In the innermost region of the 7th Celestial Star below the fantastical mountains filled with dense essence and medicinal herbs, there lay a horrendous golden cage that had numerous spears piercing through a single being.","This cage was located in the area in the deeper layers of the Celestial Star in a position that very few disciples had access to. It was placed at the center of this wide underground cavern that had foliage shimmering with blue and purple lights, the foliage being the type of plants that never saw the light of day. It was normally a silent area as years would pass before any being would intrude upon it, but there was a shimmering golden robed figure walking towards the cage that held a disfigured being pierced on all sides.","This individual held an exemplary goatee on his face, being the Celestial Grandmaster that oversaw many of the operations on this Celestial Star- it was Grandmaster Ramiel!","His expression seemed to be one that was lost in thought as he strolled towards the restrictive cage holding a single being, only looking up as he was inches away from it, the figure of the prisoner within being extremely clear. The one chained to the floor of the cage with numerous golden rods piercing through his body turned his head unnaturally as one of his eyes landed on Grandmaster Ramiel.","The Grandmaster that was lost in thought actually pulled back from the cage as he bowed respectfully, reigning in his bubbling aura that stood at a rank above the Domain Expansion Realm and bringing forth a shocking scene that could not be understood by any of those watching!","\"This unworthy disciple greets Master. I haven’t been down here for quite some time, and I’ll have to bother you with some of my ramblings again.\"","Grandmaster Ramiel began a monologue as he let out shocking words, slightly revealing the identity of the being that was mutilated by numerous spears within the cage!","\"The tides of fate continue to ebb and flow forth, where we are now reaching an impasse with the Infernal Lords joining hands with those in the Dark Expanse. The period of war is fast approaching once more, with all forces raising their own champions to steer this coming battle into their favor.\"","Grandmaster Ramiel began walking around the cage as he talked, seemingly lost in his own musings as the being he had called Master continued to silently listen!","\"The position of the Infernal Lord we had killed long ago is about to be filled again as a new Infernal Lord rises. The Warlocks and Witches controlling the Dark Expanse continue to refine their spells as they congregate with the Infernal Lords, while our forces have located a few beings with Noble Fates that we continue to raise.\"","Grandmaster Ramiel walked around the cage thoughtfully as he continued to ramble on, his expression that of extreme focus as he laid out numerous secrets calmly!","\"We have continued to monitor those insane entities in the Dark Expanse, but it seems they won’t be moving for this coming war, all indicators pointing to some sort of restriction binding them from acting once more.\"","He came to a stop once more as his eyes focused on the imprisoned being.","\"Our newest action would actually deal with the wondrous place you helped locate long ago, where we are thinking of influencing the fates of those in the Light Expanse even more by letting them explore that Realm, and then using this force in the coming war as well.\"","RUMBLE!","The air around them trembled as a plot that would shake the minds of many who heard was laid out simply!","\"Their lives would at least serve some meaning as they stand in the front lines, contributing to the establishment of Order and not the chaos that they continue to cause.\"","Blood continued to leak out of the imprisoned being as his barely freed facial muscles rose up in a smile, numerous thoughts coursing through his mind as the one that called him Master continued to ponder next to his cage!","\"Our rule has tightened over the years in the Light Expanse, but this will be the first time that we include its inhabitants on something this grand as we continue to steer fate in the direction that we want. What do you think about this move, Master?\"","Grandmaster Ramiel shook his head as no reply came from the being in front of it, his gaze turning towards the golden rods that locked him in place as he shook his head in wonder.","\"The treasures of the Celestial Realm amaze me to this very day. I never would have once believed that a being like you could be locked down for this long, your strength continuously drained, your millions of Fate Lines shattered as your power continues to drain every second. Yet...your power still seems as boundless as ever, Master!\"","His words were those of reverence and respect as he looked upon the being skewered in the cage, shaking his head wistfully as he turned around and began walking away. Grandmaster Ramiel had the habit of coming down here frequently every tens of years as he reminisced about the past and thought of the grand history of this being caged beneath this star. To him, this was just a repeat of what he usually did as he came down and began leaving soon after, his thoughts already going towards the many things he had to take care of as a few last words left his mouth.","\"Why, Master? Why did you do that? Ay...\"","His melancholic words faded as his figure went higher and higher, gradually disappearing as he left behind the skewered body that continued to leak blood. The imprisoned being in question looked at the leaving being as a disfigured smile appeared in its skewered face, a small whisper that no one would be able to hear leaving his lips.","\"Steering fate huh? What would you children know about fate, or how fickle it can be!\"","THRUM!","The numerous golden rods holding him in place trembled at the immense aura of this being, things gradually calming down as the imprisoned figure raised his head above the cage, his eyes piercing through the layers of earth as they came to rest upon a particular mountain on the 7th Celestial Star.","At the place his eyes were gazing at, the figures of Noah and Athena were respectfully listening to a particular Grandmaster. The imprisoned being looked at this scene as a wide smile covered his disfigured face, a look of anticipation covering his face.","\"Soon!\"","..."]},{"number":364,"title":"Chapter 364: Chapter 363 - Infernal Set!","paragraphs":["In the underground layer of Frozen Plateau Spiritual Land, immense heat was coming off a particular Blacksmith’s Forge as Noah looked at the results of trying out this new feature for the first time.","He had first checked the possibilities of the feature called [Refine], pulling out the Supreme Treasure that was the Trident of Sea as it was quickly swallowed up by the Hearth at the center of Blacksmith’s Forge!","The numerous blue flames wrapped all around the shining trident before a prompt appeared on Noah’s eyes.","[Supreme Treasure Trident of the Sea- requires Unique Materials that would enhance the efficacy of the item by an unknown amount.]","The first test was a dud as he still did not come across something that could be considered a Unique Material, his mind leaning towards the Celestial Realm he was learning more and more about as the place he might be able to get his hands on something like this.","This idea also brought into account another feature of the Spiritual Land that Noah had not had a chance to use too often, and that was [Treasure Hunter]!","The abilities of the Spiritual Land continued to affect his rise in strength more and more, going on to unimaginable degrees at this moment as it seemed to always hold newer and more fantastical surprises. He put the thoughts about how he could possibly move in the Celestial Realm as he gathered more information on it first, checking to see if it would be even possible for him to take the Spiritual Land along on that journey.","When it came to the Locked abilities of the Blacksmith’s Forge, there was [Recipe Design] and [Evolve]. The latter was vague and he didn’t know how different it would be from the [Refine] feature, but the [Recipe Design] was something that made his heart shake in excitement as he wondered exactly what were the limits to what the Spiritual Land would allow him to personally design in the future.","When his thoughts came to this stage, he almost wanted to look into the problem of obtaining a Small World Core right away while trying to upgrade the strengths of the Beasts of the Spiritual Land into a rank that even he had not stepped into yet.","He shook his head at the numerous thoughts as his attention reverted back to the [Forge] feature of the Blacksmith’s Forge as he took back the Trident of the Sea from the dancing blue flames in the Hearth.","When he first initiated the use of [Forge], he didn’t have anything that could be considered a material on him, so he tried the only thing holding a possibility of being counted as a material while also being abundant near his location. Being in the First Realm of Hell, he quickly procured the bodies of a few Void Ranked Infernals as he teleported back to the Blacksmith’s Forge and threw a few of them into the Hearth!","The function of [Forge] was selected as an exuberant amount of mana began leaving his body, the numerous dredges of Void Rank Infernals beginning to melt in front of his eyes as blue flaming snakes went on to cover all over them, wrapping them up entirely as more than half an hour passed while Noah watched the burning flames.","RUMBLE!","An explosion of light that seemed to portray the arrival of something grand spread out from the Hearth that Noah was closely watching, the shining light disappearing as an exquisitely designed b.r.e.a.s.tplate and a glimmering red serrated sword floated in front of him, their identities being revealed as their descriptions floated in front of his eyes beautifully!","<strong>VOID [Infernal’s Serrated Sword] :: A sword forged from the very origins of Infernals themselves, carrying their vengeful emotions with every strike. +50% Physical Damage. +20% Increased Attack Speed. (Part of the Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set)</strong>","<strong>VOID [Infernal’s Spiked B.r.e.a.s.tplate] :: An armor meant to withstand all the wrathful attacks thrown towards it. +50% Defense. +20% Increased Elemental Resistance. +50% Increased Fire Element Resistance. (Part of the Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set)</strong>","<strong>{Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set} :: The complete set that only those capable of taking down numerous infernals are rewarded. Set Bonus: 2 Pieces- Apply the Fear Effect to all those at lower ranks. 4 Pieces- Gain a unique enhancing energy in the form of a Frenzy Charge after every kill. The Frenzy Charges gradually disappears after 30 seconds. Each Frenzy Charge grants +5% Increased Damage. 6 Pieces- Enter the state of Infernal Rage whenever you are low on life, granting you 100% more Damage and Regeneration, as well as the gained Frenzy Charges not expiring.</strong>","\"...Well damn.\"","Noah’s mouth was wide open as he looked at the details of the two items laid out in front of him, not imagining in his wildest dreams that the first items created in this Blacksmith’s Forge were this marvelous in their capabilities!","He had made the assumption that only Supreme Treasures would be able to enhance his abilities, but it seemed the items created from the Blacksmith’s Forge were something entirely different. This was especially so because of the bonuses one could obtain if they wore the entire Item Set created from the bodies of the dead Void Ranked Infernals.","The items provided increased speed, damage, and armor, which Noah could disregard if he wanted, but his curiosity was raised when he looked at the unique features that could be obtained if the remaining 4 items were created and worn all at once, gaining the boost given for the complete Item Set!","This also made him very much look forward to the possibilities of the types of Supreme Treasures that could be created from the Blacksmith’s Forge if something at the Void Rank came out as spectacularly as this. Even though the items in this {Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set} would not grant him crazy boosts to his already insane abilities, he knew it would be an immense help to those around him, allowing them to raise their power much quicker as well as gaining another layer of protection.","He waved his hands in anticipation as he took out more than 10 other Void Rank bodies of the Infernals, throwing them all into the Hearth that pulsed with a blue flame as he created items unique only to him, something that his people would wear and become known for in the future that he had yet to perceive!","In the coming war that would affect the dynamic of trillions of lives, a monstrous force that wore designs of similar Items that Noah had begun creating would become known across the reaches of the Novus Galaxy..."]},{"number":365,"title":"Chapter 365: Chapter 364 - A Move of Consolidation","paragraphs":["Word was soon passed from the 7th Celestial Star and into the numerous other Celestial Stars spread out over the Light Expanse, going on to reach the ears of the upper echelons that made the true decisions.","The Grandmasters in the 7th Celestial Star were confident after they had used their own techniques to discern the possible effects and results of letting inhabitants of the Light Expanse explore the Celestial Realm for the first time under strict conditions, and they saw the effects to be marvelous and heavily favoring their aims!","So word was passed forward to the higher-ups, but they knew the ultimate decision would be the confirmation of this never before done event as they were approaching the precipice of another war, and the use of the beings in the Light Expanse in the front lines of this war would only leave them in a better position.","Grandmaster Ramiel had left the underground area where a being lay imprisoned, these numerous thoughts coursing through his mind as he shone a resplendent gold light, numerous skills activated as he overlooked the activities of the 7th Celestial Star.","When it came to raising forces, one could forcefully throw them into their deaths, but what if you could raise beings to fight on their behalf willingly with their own wills?","The Celestials had been doing this for ages with the act of recruiting disciples, going on to create the force of hundreds of thousands of those qualified in learning about fate over the years as these beings were spread out all over the stars of the Light Expanse.","But the epiphany that Grandmaster Vredral had as he watched the constantly changing influence of fate of numerous Prime Worlds that had their emotions and beliefs pressed down and changed in a matter of hours as they watched the power of Celestials had brought forth this new possibility.","The Celestials had been steadily influencing the fates of the numerous stars in the Light Expanse, but not to the extent that they were about to do in the near future.","They were involved in the affairs of the numerous stars, even going as far as providing them with minor treasures after their participation in the Infernal Hunts. But this coming future would have the inhabitants of Light Expanse work closely and tirelessly with the Celestials as they would go on to fight for them in the front lines after their strengths were boosted in the Celestial Realm!","They would not be forced or conscripted to fight and throw away their lives, but they would be influenced ever so slowly with the power of Celestials they continued to observe as they tasted the treasures that they had already been eating for years. Then, they would willingly lay down their lives to the enemies that the Celestials pointed their fingers towards.","Grandmaster Ramiel smiled as he thought this, numerous message transmissions leaving his mind towards numerous beings as he moved forward with the plans to influence the beings of the Light Expanse even more the moment he received the permission he expected to receive as the information returned from the many Celestial Stars.","This time, it wasn’t just through fear as the beings of the Light Expanse observed the majestic power of Celestials similar to the bloodbath in the Magus World, but also through awe as they would come to observe and appreciate the Celestial Realm they would soon be given a chance to dive into under strict conditions!","It was a plan of using fear and propaganda to further enhance their already stable influence of fate, and now it would also produce more powerhouses to fight in the coming war as more and more beings explored and chanced upon the wondrous treasures of the Celestial Realm.","---","Only a few days passed before thousands of Prime Worlds began receiving astounding pieces of information directly from the Celestials!","Only worlds at the level of Prime received this piece of information, very few of the tens of thousands of Large Worlds or the hundreds of thousands of small and middle worlds filled with weak life forms were receiving this message as it was focused on those that were powerful and capable in the Prime Worlds.","The message’s contents told them all that a chance had arrived!","A never before given chance that would allow the powers of the Light Expanse to progress in strength as they worked together with the Celestials to explore something phenomenal.","Many of the worlds already knew of the Celestial’s power, and worlds like the World of Cultivation had already been receiving resources from the Celestials over the years. So when they saw the contents of this message, they knew it would be something unbelievable!","The numerous powerful worlds in the Light Expanse began to bustle with activities at the advent of this message, many of them looking forward into the future as they prepared.","Only a few knowledgeable figures and the beings watching from the Dark Expanse looked at these large movements as they realized something momentous was occurring with the Celestials. Those watching closely from the Dark Expanse came to realize that the Celestials were consolidating their power as they prepared for their future war once more, and this consolidation of power was so expansive that they were now involving the entire Light Expanse!","In the Underworld, the Royal Vampyre Elena received a similar message as she closed her eyes and mumbled with an amorous smile.","\"The Celestial Realm, huh?\"","Her red eyes were languidly looking forward to the bustling Pureblood Vampyres that continued to expand their forces in the Underworld. She looked towards her brother who was overseeing the campaign with a frowning face as she spoke of with a smile.","\"Little Brother, we’ll have to call back little Cassius from the Dark Expanse so he can enjoy a piece of the pie opening itself up soon.\"","A thoughtful expression was on the Vampyre King’s face as he replied.","\"This Celestial Realm that these mongrels are choosing to open up to the public now...there should be numerous hidden meanings behind it. Not to mention the dangers.\"","The Vampyre King was careful as he thought of the possibilities and meanings behind the actions of the Celestials, but Elena only smiled as her bountiful body bounced up.","\"Oh little brother, danger brings with it an opportunity, and this opportunity to get our hands into the treasure bowl of the Celestials...I’m sure the Alliance is going to do everything in their power to take full hold of it!\"","Across the worlds, bustling movements had begun as many beings plotted and schemed with their own plans. At the same time, a being was designing terrifying weapons and armors in a fiery hell, and was at the same time training at the core of the Celestials themselves as he garnered more status and power. Among the schemes and plans, who knew which power would come out on top?"]},{"number":366,"title":"Chapter 366: Chapter 365 - A Penguin Clad in Armor, Towards the Celestial Realm!","paragraphs":["As many beings prepared for the profound opportunity opening itself up, Noah’s clone was in the underground layer of this spiritual land where an amazing sight was taking place as a Penguin of immense arrogance raised its beak even higher into the skies because of the majestic Item Set it was currently adorned in.","Noah was standing in front of the Emperor Penguin as he observed the tight fitting of the <strong>{Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set}</strong> with shining eyes.","The strongest beast of the Spiritual Land was the first to be tested as the moment it equipped the items they went on to tightly wrap around his body and fit as if they were meant for him. The <strong>{Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set}</strong> contained the sword and the b.r.e.a.s.tplate that he created first, and then later on he was able to craft the leggings, shoes, armguards, and a helmet! The entire set shone with a red l.u.s.ter as it fully covered the penguin, the multiple pieces going on to smoothly attach to his body.","Going back a few minutes prior, the Hearth of the Blacksmith’s Forge had produced the last 4 four pieces of the set as they floated grandly in front of Noah’s eyes, the descriptions of their boosts being around the same as the last two items.","<strong>VOID [Infernal’s Spiked Leggings] :: Leggings that are meant to provide smooth movements while granting increased protection. +50% Defense. +20% Increased Elemental Resistance. +50% Increased Fire Element Resistance. (Part of the Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set)</strong>","<strong>VOID [Infernal’s Spiked Helmet] :: A crown created to exemplify the qualities of one that is stained with the blood of Infernals. +10% Attack and Cast Speed, +25% To All Element Resistance.(Part of the Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set)</strong>","<strong>VOID [Infernal’s Spiked Armguards] :: Armguards that are meant to provide versatility while also reinforcing the strength of the user. +10% Attack and Cast Speed. (Part of the Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set)</strong>","<strong>VOID [Infernal’s Spiked Boots] :: Swift and strong, this Infernal footwear provides the speed and agility required to move across tough terrains. +20% Movement Speed, Unaffected by the extreme burning grounds you stand on. (Part of the Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set)</strong>","Once the set fully came together, it created a menacing armored figure that was adorned with a fierce helmet that had two horns protruding on either side. It made for a demonic picture, and this contrast was especially interesting on the emperor penguin.","Its flippers were fully covered as numerous spikes protruded from the armed guards, it’s beak holding a red sheen as a thin red film of light came to protect it. Its beady eyes were able to be seen from the thin slit that was visible from the small opening of the helmet of the infernal set.","This was the completed and finished creation of the first set that Noah had crafted from the use of the Blacksmith’s Forge. It was a fully void rank {Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set}! One of the things that Noah found to be marvelous about this Item Set was the unique abilities they provided after one wore all 6 items.","<strong>{Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set} :: The complete set that only those capable of taking down numerous infernals are rewarded. Set Bonus: 2 Pieces- Apply the Fear Effect to all those at lower ranks. 4 Pieces- Gain a unique enhancing energy in the form of a Frenzy Charge after every kill. The Frenzy Charges gradually disappears after 30 seconds. Each Frenzy Charge grants +5% Increased Damage. 6 Pieces- Enter the state of Infernal Rage whenever you are low on life, granting you 100% more Damage and Regeneration, as well as the gained Frenzy Charges not expiring.</strong>","The concept of Frenzy Charges that increased your damage output every time you took down an enemy reminded Noah of Berserkers that would continue fighting in a bloody battlefield as they only became stronger with time. This was complemented even more when looked over the last boost given for equipping all 6 pieces that allowed one to enter an actual berserker state. He knew that this type of Item Set would definitely go on to be extremely useful for his forces in the future.","He had used up almost all the bodies of the void rank infernal that he held to create enough set items to completion, but the product was worth it!","\"How do you feel?\"","He asked the flexing emperor penguin as he wanted to get feedback on the boosted strength from someone that didn’t have the crazy boosts that he personally held.","\"Powerful master, it feels as if I have an exhaustible amount of energy!\"","Noah nodded as he replied while moving out","\"Good. Let’s test it out in combat and check out the boosts provided by the set bonuses themselves.\"","The plan that Noah’s clone was currently carrying out was collecting as many bodies of dead Infernal as possible and using them as materials to mass produce these spectacular item sets that enhanced the strengths of his people by a large margin.","There were still many tests to conduct as time passed, his attention also divided into the increased ratio of the Time Space where in the last two tier upgrades, it did not double as it had been doing in the past. From the 6th to the 7th Tier, the upgrade went from 1:20 to a ratio of 1:25, and the 8th Tier granted a ratio of 1:30!","It felt like a nerf had been placed as the ratio would have become simply monstrous if it continued to double, but it didn’t mean much to Noah as the ratio of 1:30 was already insane by itself. This was because a single passing day outside would mean 30 days in the Time Space of the Spiritual Land. It was already a crazy concept that would allow him to swiftly raise the proficiency of his skills that continued to become harder to raise the more they advanced in rank.","This was just another thing that he had on his to do list, with his tasks expanding to create numerous Item Sets using the Blacksmith’s Forge, spending some time in the Time Space to increase the proficiencies of his [Lesser Cthulhu], [Fate’s Guardian], and the [Abhorred Lich Emperor] that was actually leading in proficiency as it had been active this entire time, as well as explore the features of Law Space. As the clone steadily moved to accomplish these goals, in the 7th Celestial Star, a few days passed since the Grandmaster broke the news of the Celestial Realm to Noah and Athena.","Today, Noah had once again received a telepathic message as he was condensing Fate Lines in his Abode.","\"Come! We have gained the go ahead for you and Athena to delve into the Celestial Realm first!\"","Noah’s eyes shone as he received this message, a light smile appearing on face as his figure disappeared from his Abode and reappeared near the Monastery.","Athena wasn’t too far behind as the girl had her hair already tied in a ponytail, the red robe she wore hiding her bountiful figure beneath as the both of them came to see the Grandmaster.","\"Haha, this is a great opportunity. You two will get firsthand knowledge on how to move in the Celestial Realm, and you...\"","The wizened Grandmaster Vredral turned towards Noah as he finished his words.","\"...will get to meet even more astounding geniuses besides Athena. Some may not be on your level, but they should still be able to give you a fight!\"","The Grandmaster neared their positions as a brilliant light erupted to cover the three of them, their figures fading away as the light died down, their bodies reappearing inside a familiar Prime Warship they had used just a few days ago.","\"We are setting off towards the land of opportunity and magnificence, the Realm filled with peril and danger, but also filled with treasures out of your wildest imagination!\"","The voice of Grandmaster Vredral rang out as Athena and Noah looked towards each other, a thrilling light passing through their eyes as each of them held their own thoughts. Athena longed to find her purpose and what fate laid in store for her, while Noah was hungry for this phenomenal realm that was largely unexplored even after thousands of years, and for what possible treasures were waiting within!"]},{"number":367,"title":"Chapter 367: Chapter 366 - A Breathtaking Golden Door","paragraphs":["A grand Prime Warship streaked across the vastness of space, having been a few days since it first left the 7th Celestial Star.","Noah and Athena were on a uniquely designed rectangular dining table that had a white cloth draping over it, numerous dishes that glistened in the light filling this table as the two ate while talking.","\"It’s disheartening to find out that even your cooking skills are out of this word.\"","The Senior Sister that was gradually opening up to Noah said these words as her clear eyes looked at Noah inquisitively as she threw out a question. Noah replied as he grabbed the fat golden thigh of a large bird as he took large bites.","\"My time in the Profound Astral Sect wasn’t just spent cultivating, I made sure to at least get the skill of cooking down when everyone was still looking down on me.\"","Athena nodded as she carried on with light conversation. They had been on the ship passing through numerous stars over the past few days that after training in their separate rooms, they routinely got together to eat. Noah used the time to show off his cooking skills as he slowly gained more and more trust from the valiant War Princess, as well as the old Grandmaster that simply shook his head after realizing the disciple he considered a genius had another thing he excelled in.","\"Oh? It seems like we are finally nearing the location.\"","The War Princess that was licking the oil on her ring finger called out, her senses reaching a region tens of miles from where they were. Noah spread his own senses out as he came to observe the appearance of numerous Prime Warsh.i.p.s much larger than the one they were on.","These Prime Warsh.i.p.s only increased in number as they neared, Noah noticing the protective formation that the numerous sh.i.p.s took as if they were protecting the most treasured thing possible.","Each of these sh.i.p.s was at the same level or higher from the Prime Warship they were on, meaning there were numerous sh.i.p.s capable of destroying entire stars spread out all over the location that held the entrance to the Celestial Realm!","The Prime Warship they were on continued to get closer as it smoothly passed the circles of protection, its identity being known long in advance as the profound weapons of numerous other sh.i.p.s did not even turn towards it.","The further in they went past the initial perimeter, the more powerful sh.i.p.s that contained horrendous auras they could feel as they realized how heavily protected this location was by the Celestials!","Noah could already feel numerous auras at the Soul and Domain Expansion Realm overlooking these many sh.i.p.s, but his gaze stayed up front as he began to sense the appearance of a shining light.","This shining light only became brighter and brighter as their ship went closer, continuing to grow in size as it soon came to overshadow the large vessel they were on.","His figure flashed away from the dining area and into the front of the ship that held a clear glass screen, his eyes landing on this brightening light as it gradually became more and more clear, his eyes finally registering the appearance of a humongous Golden Door!","It was a breathtaking scene to observe as this door stood serenely in space, gold particles of light ever so slowly coiling around it as it portrayed a sense of majesty Noah had not come across before. The only thing that slightly took away from this majesty was the numerous Interstellar Sh.i.p.s surrounding it on all sides, the eyes of the Celestials protecting this door as if it was their lifeline.","\"The Celestial Door, a breathtaking sight to come across for the first time as it is nothing compared to the gates leading to the Infernal Realms you have come across before.\"","Grandmaster Vredral appeared next to Noah as Athena joined their position, his wizened gaze deepening as he stroked his beard and continued.","\"One can look at the names of the two and say they are similar, but the Celestial Realm and the known Infernal Realms are not even capable of being at the same stage of comparison. The entire size of the First Infernal Realm cannot even compare to one-hundredth of the minuscule amount of lands that we have managed to explore in the Celestial Realm.\"","The words of the Grandmaster revealed the immensity of the Celestial Realm more and more as their ship came to a stop not too far away from the Golden Door. The more than 2000 meters in size Warship seemed tiny compared to this grand door floating in front of them.","\"Now, let’s go in and have you two take a first look!\"","The Grandmaster voiced out with a happy expression as a wide door opened up on the side of their Prime Warship, their figures stepping into the void of space as they began to head towards the Golden Door.","None of the numerous Interstellar Sh.i.p.s even batted an eye towards them as they all knew their identities to be important figures from the 7th Celestial Star!","Many of the beings that were stationed in the numerous vessels to protect the perimeters of the entrance to the Celestial Realm were beings that were average in talent, using many of the years on missions of securing the perimeter as they cultivated for tens of years in these vessels before they were assigned to other missions.","Some of them had not even been given the chance to enter the Celestial Realm yet until they completed their missions!","Noah’s party smoothly bypassed all of this as they neared the door with the Grandmaster at the lead, and under the eyes of everyone, they came to float just a few meters from the Golden Door. The simple l.u.s.ter and brightness of the gate caused them to squint their eyes as the Grandmaster spoke once more.","\"The moment anyone touches this Golden Door, they will be transferred to a specific region that we have long ago colonized and made our own, and it will be this region that you all will spend quite some time to get acquainted in before you begin to fully explore the dangers and opportunities of the Celestial Realm.\"","Noah and Athena nodded as their figures came ever so closer to the Golden Door.","\"It will be my honor to welcome the newest geniuses of the Celestials into the first region of the Celestial Realm, the Sanctum!\"","The voice of the Grandmaster reached a crescendo as they fully came in contact with the Golden Door, their figures disappearing in a flash of light as Noah Osmont, a nobody from a Small World had finally stepped into a Realm that would allow for unpredictable changes for the entire Light Expanse!"]},{"number":368,"title":"Chapter 368: Chapter 367 - The Sanctum!","paragraphs":["How would one describe something they found so beautiful and grand that no words came to their minds?","How would you describe something that looked exactly like what you imagined a paradise would be like?","How would one bring themselves to describe the first place that everybody was teleported to when they entered the Celestial Realm, the place known as the Sanctum!","Noah and Athena’s figures appeared on a magnificently white marble clearing as their eyes landed on the wondrous buildings all around them that rose to the skies.","They seemed to be a blend of ancient architecture that Noah would have seen in olden times, but also the futuristic designs that made one feel they were in an entirely new land!","Many of the structures around them had pointed peaks that rose to the skies, the crystalline structures tinged with the colors of white and gold as they glistened in the light. Those that didn’t have pointed peaks had artistic dome-shaped outlines that released an air of regality.","All around these enormous buildings, the ethereal outlines of huge ancient trees that rose to heights no less than the buildings themselves were present. The trees seem to shimmer with abundant life essence as they provided an aesthetic of nature that could not be violated. It felt like they were in a land filled with nature, and at the same time, this land had undergone the process of change that kept the natural aesthetic while simply adding the unique architecture all around it.","They could feel the oppressive feeling of immense essence all around them, the quality so powerful that every time they breathed, they felt as if their noses were getting unclogged after days of having a cold, finally being able to smell the vibrant smell of spring!","Noah felt his own body almost feeling gleeful as it settled in this environment that held a profound quality of essence.","They could sense numerous powerhouses spread out all around, the least of which held power at the Void Realm, with the auras of multiple Domain Expansion experts being present!","Their surroundings were bustling with activity as numerous different robe colored Celestials could be seen walking around, only the white marble circular area they stood on being secluded and empty.","The Grandmaster looked at the paradisiacal scene around him as he voiced out with a tinge of wonder.","\"Welcome to the first area that all who step in through the Golden Door of the Celestial Realm are introduced to, welcome to The Sanctum that is our home base in this expansive Celestial Realm.\"","Noah continued to glance at the phenomenal array of golden and white colors around him as he sensed a brand new atmosphere in this Celestial Realm he had stepped into. He realized the first subtle differences by the many bustling figures that were moving around the Sanctum, but he couldn’t find anyone in the skies.","He noticed this difference as he felt a type of restriction landing on his body, and he wanted to test it as his body slowly jumped to the skies, but he was thrown back down by his weight the moment he reached just a few meters high, finding that he could not use his energy to hold himself up!","\"Haha, you have caught on to the differences of the Celestial Realm fast. Yes, one of the things you will come to realize here is that numerous restrictions exist, and one of them is that you cannot fly! Unless you are on a ship or flying on a winged beast, you will find your energy is useless in keeping you afloat...that is until you reach a certain realm.\"","The body of the Grandmaster began to float stably as he said this, his figure remaining in the skies jovial before he came down in a few seconds.","\"Of course, the other differences are more astute, but you can easily discover them in time. Come, the newcomers need to gain their preliminary knowledge of the nearby geography and exactly where to go or not go if you want to keep your life.\"","The Grandmaster pulled them away from the white marble area they entered in as they went towards one of the ancient buildings that had its golden peak pointing to the skies, the shape of two huge white wings spreading out from the sides of this unique structure as it let out an air of magnificence.","Their party passed through the glass doors as two guards clad in a unique white armor bowed with their hands clasping their chest.","\"Grandmaster.\"","\"Grandmaster.\"","Grandmaster Vredral gave a simple nod as he took Noah and Athena forward, the two disciples curiously watching everything around them as they observed numerous Celestials moving in and out of the building they were in. They climbed a set of circular stairs as they came to reach a higher floor that held huge wide open doors leading to a hall where a few figures were cl.u.s.tered around an oval table.","There was a powerful aura at the forefront that turned towards Grandmaster Vredral and called out raucously.","\"Vredral! You’ve finally returned, and with new disciples I see.\"","The smooth reacquaintance of two old friends occurred as the wizened Grandmaster gave a huge bear hug to this being.","\"Commanding Officer Raizel now is it? Haha, we’ll catch up later. I bring with me seeds of the future that need to be looked after extremely well. They need to be brought to speed on the safe and dangerous regions around the Sanctum, as well as the areas they can begin to explore in this wide Celestial Realm of ours!\"","A nod of understanding came on the face of the one called Raizel as he smiled and looked towards Noah and Athena, his powerful aura at the Domain Expansion realm focusing on them as he nodded.","\"You have been gone too long my friend, the regions you knew to be dangerous have turned safe after years of exploration, and some of the safe regions have turned dangerous after the Celestial Beasts reclaimed them. Haha, no worries though, let’s enjoy ourselves a bit with delicacies only found here before we delve into the crux of everything.\"","The being called Commanding Officer Raizel waved his hands toward the table as numerous doc.u.ments and papers were moved away, a collection of rainbow-colored fruits that pulsed with immense essence appearing on the table as the eyes of a few guards standing by the side shone with light.","\"Do you remember these? The Aurora Fruits from a dangerous region we had not yet captured towards the west. We have been able to get our hands on them now, and they are delicacies you definitely have to enjoy!\"","Raizel invited them to partake as Noah’s hands grabbed an Aurora Fruit himself, feeling enormous amounts of energy the moment the rainbow-colored fruit landed on his hands as surprisingly, his Planetary System showed a few blue colored words interpreting the features of the fruit’s unique energy signature right away.","<strong>[Aurora Fruit] :: A unique medicinal fruit only capable of growing in unique environments. Has the effects of fully recovering one’s energy and vitality to the maximum, and granting them +100% energy regeneration for the next hour.</strong>","His jaws nearly dropped at the description of a simple fruit that he had come across as he first stepped into the Celestial Realm, his gaze turning towards the jovial Celestials in front of him as the hunger he felt for the unknown things in this Celestial Realm only grew.","He had just arrived at the base of the Celestials in this Realm that was called the Sanctum. He wanted to learn more about exactly what awaited outside this Sanctum, and what dangers he had to brave if he wanted to get his hands on ridiculously amazing items such as the ones he had just come across a few minutes of entering into this Celestial Realm!","He was also extremely impatient as his thoughts went to a feature of his Spiritual Land that would be something phenomenal to have in this land filled with opportunities. He was thinking of the feature of [Treasure Hunter] that he wanted to use in this Celestial Realm right away, his gaze looking far into the future on the unlimited possibilities.","He had just stepped into the Celestial Realm, and already his heart felt a strong pull as he was swept off his feet instantly!"]},{"number":369,"title":"Chapter 369: Chapter 368 - Celestial Beasts","paragraphs":["As Noah and Athena sat down with the one called Commanding Officer Raziel and Grandmaster Vredral, the picture of the Celestial Realm gradually became clearer in their eyes.","The location known as the Sanctum was the first area that the Celestial colonized, going on to build a central base here as they gradually expanded over the years.","This expansion was a tug of war between them and the inhabitants that could be found in this Celestial Realm- the Celestial Beasts!","They were termed this simply as they were the regal and monstrous beasts that could be found all over this Celestial Realm, but others also knew them by another name because of their prime feature.","They were also known as...Behemoths!","Noah could feel his heart pounding as he listened to the carefully given lecture by the Commanding Officer Raizel, the picture of this Celestial Realm only getting bigger and bigger as the image of these beasts called Behemoths filled his mind.","They were called Behemoths simply because of their monstrous size, where just a single one was like an entire moving building!","In the explored areas that Celestials had observed so far, the smallest of these Celestial Beasts had turned out to be 50 meters! This was a shocking size for a normal beast, actually being 25 times Noah’s human stature, where even in his Lesser Cthulhu form he would still be considered smaller.","These were the beasts populating the Celestial Realm, these were the Celestial Beasts known as Behemoths!","\"You will be lucky to come across one that would usually be protecting a certain area which is usually filled with treasures. If you come across 2 or 3 Behemoths congregating, then it means the treasure is especially more potent and rare.\"","The Commanding Officer Raizel said with a solemn tone as his eyes locked in towards Athena and Noah.","\"The defenses of these Behemoths are extremely terrifying, where we have come to learn that they have insane resistance to many laws, and only Supreme Laws like the Law of Fate are extremely effective in passing through their defenses. It takes other attacks twice as much time just to get through their thick skin.\"","The story continued as the descriptions of the Celestial Beasts became more clearer in Noah’s eyes.","The Behemoths had horrendous levels of defenses, and this also stood the same with their attacks! You could actually come across a Behemoth that held huge attainments in the Law of Water and find yourself outmatched as they used spectacular skills you could not easily defend against.","\"The even more ferocious Behemoths are those that are proficient in Supreme Laws. It is these beasts that act independently and are the main cause of us losing an area we already explored and claimed, where we face monstrous casualties every time a Behemoth at such a level comes to these areas.\"","The face of the Commanding Officer Raizel only became more and more solemn as he talked about the ferociousness of the Celestial Beasts.","Because of the terrible power of these beasts, when the Celestials moved to explore the Celestial Realm, they always moved in teams in order to match these Behemoths that they came across!","This created an atmosphere where numerous teams were created in the Sanctum for the purposes of hunting down Behemoths.","\"These Celestial Beasts are extremely dangerous, but their rewards are also just as stupendous. This is what propels the many teams formed in the Sanctum forward, as aside from the areas filled with treasures that these beasts protected, their own bodies contain unheard of materials that are drenched with the universal laws!\"","Yes! Aside from the abundant rewards you could claim from the area that the Celestial Beast was protecting, their bodies themselves were profound materials that carried with them the laws that the Behemoths were proficient in.","When Noah heard the mention of materials, his heart beat slightly faster as he knew he was already sold on everything about these Behemoths, but they just continued to tell him more and more things that made him want to go out and start exploring right away!","\"Those capable of carrying bodies of Behemoths back, or those with achievements in the Law of Space that can easily transport them are favored as a single Behemoth’s body is a valuable treasure trove that could be enjoyed for days. Its meat alone holds special properties and rejuvenates you with energy, and their Origin Cores are something we have never come across before anywhere else.\"","Thus, it was extremely crucial to form a good hunting team to go and explore the Celestial Realm, as if you attached yourself to a single good team that had a powerful figure, you would be feasting on treasures and delectable meats for years to come!","\"Teams are crucial in the Sanctum, as the power of the Behemoths is simply that great, forcing us to group up if we want to ensure our lives. Too many geniuses have overestimated their abilities as they left to hunt alone, being successful at first as they were able to keep all the treasures they found to themselves. But...\"","The eyes of Commanding Officer Raizel became cold as he said the next words.","\"...eventually they chance upon a Behemoth that they cannot handle alone, and escaping a Behemoth is a rare thing to occur in the Celestial Realm.\"","The message was clear- no matter what type of genius you thought yourself to be, it did not apply in the Celestial Realm!","The Behemoths dwelling within are that terrifying, that even the strongest of the Celestials made sure to always move in groups.","\"You two are those with Noble Fates, so I’m sure multiple teams will be scouting for you to join them as soon as word about your arrival spreads. If you didn’t know, those with Noble Fates actually hold another title in the Sanctum, and that title is...Golden Goose!\"","Boisterous laughter erupted from Commanding Officer Raizel and Grandmaster Vredral as they looked at each other and laughed at this mention, Noah and Athena turning towards each other as sharp lights passed through their eyes.","Their supposed Noble Fates meant that their exploration in this Celestial Realm was bound to be filled with dangers and great opportunities.","The new information about the Celestial Beasts that were known as Behemoths rolled around in Noah’s mind as he wanted to soon try them himself!"]},{"number":370,"title":"Chapter 370: Chapter 369 - Hunting Team?","paragraphs":["In the expansive Sanctum they just arrived in, the Celestials almost always formed teams in order to hunt these terrible Behemoths and continue their exploration of the Celestial Realm.","\"It is routine for Grandmasters at the Domain Expansion Realm to move out together as an Elite Team, these teams being the ones that make the most breakthroughs into new areas or come across wondrous treasures. You two...\"","Commanding Officer Raizel locked his gaze towards Noah and Athena as he continued.","\"...will either have the option of joining a normal team, or the two of you creating a team yourselves!\"","A pondering look appeared on Noah as he turned to see the shining expression of Athena. He knew the War Princess already had her battle sense excited as it could be, her body seeking these dangerous Behemoths they were hearing about even more than him.","He personally enjoyed moving solo, and it went even more spectacularly because of his abilities, but he had to admit that there was still a lot of unknown factors about this Celestial Realm!","This was the realm after all, that even the Celestials themselves had only explored less than 10% of. He would take this dangerous land of opportunity very seriously, and move carefully at first as he gained more and more knowledge of it before he began risking his life by moving solo.","If he had to move with a team though, who better than the War Princess blessed with a Noble Fate, the destructive Celestial that he knew to have a few screws loose, but also had tens of thousands of Fate Lines?","Athena had apparently already made up her mind as she spoke towards the closely watching Grandmaster Vredral.","\"I’ll move with Junior Brother Crixus. All we would need is the information on the layout and the zones we need to be careful of.\"","Grandmaster Vredral nodded carefully as the Commanding Officer Raizel chipped in.","\"That may be a good idea, but you still need to have someone show you around and familiarize yourself with the norms and the dangers of the Celestial Realm. So for your first hunt, I will have you two move with the best team that is currently not made up of Grandmasters, the Exploration Team called Righteous Fire that is under the lead of your Senior Brother Boru!\"","The name of the Senior Brother Boru seemed to carry some weight as the Commanding Officer Raizel had a proud expression, the words he said seeming more like a command and being non-negotiable as he would have the two newcomers become familiar with the Exploration Teams and how they moved first.","Athena and Noah nodded towards this Commanding Officer as the boisterous atmosphere returned.","\"Good, this compound we are in is one of the many spread out over the regions we have gained control of, and you will find that many of the bases you go to will have lodgings no less luxurious than the ones you all had in your Celestial Star. For now, go out and explore the close areas of the Sanctum. I’ll catch up with this old fool and call you all when I get the status of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team.\"","\"Yes, Grandmaster!\"","Noah and Athena stood up while placing their hands to their chest respectfully as they saw Grandmaster Vredral give them the go ahead, the two of them leaving the expansive room and going down the spiral staircase as they came out to see the wondrous sight of the Sanctum once more.","The ancient trees shimmering with essence that were even taller than the building they just came out of, as well as the numerous Prime Warsh.i.p.s they could see coming in and out occasionally made for a unique aesthetic in this paradisiacal Celestial Realm.","Noah walked along the marble roads as he breathed in deeply, immensely enjoying the atmosphere filled with essence as he began to observe the Celestials he could see moving all around.","Many were occupied with their own tasks as they moved quickly, where he could not catch many that were alone, with almost everyone in groups.","What he found interesting was the type of armor and weapons these Celestials carried. Each one could be seen fitted with bulky armor that one could clearly see to be made out of the scales or skin of a beast, with the armors holding a rough exterior that looked impenetrable!","He could also see their weapons were most likely poorly refined bones or teeth of Behemoths as he came to realize ever so slowly just how important these Celestial Beasts were. Athena was looking at this same scene with shining eyes as she spoke out.","\"It seems to be the norm to use the materials from the bodies of these humongous behemoths to create armor and weapons that are more effective in hunting down even more of them.\"","The War Princess had already analyzed what they were seeing as she came up with the exact reason why many of the Celestials they saw were carrying ridiculously large weapons and bulky armor.","Noah nodded as they continued to observe more of the area around them, their eyes landing on a particular group of Celestials that let out a wild aura, causing many of the teams that came across them to move out of the way as they seemed to be heading straight towards their position.","He looked towards Athena who had her eyes squinted as she also focused on this group of beings with powerful auras heading their way as a single one came to the forefront and neared them rapidly.","His body seemed to be of humanoid shape, but he was extremely bulky and large, his stature made even more extreme by the heavy behemoth armor he wore. His height reached 3 meters as he spectacularly had a large jagged Broad Sword that was double his size strapped horizontally to his back. A wide smile covered this being’s face as he came close to Noah and Athena, their bodies feeling an oppressive air of a predator as this being’s body surprisingly pulsed with a unique and explosive fiery aura!","Noah could see visible sparks of flames appearing and disappearing around this large figure’s body, and this was compounded with the numerous Fate Lines he could distinctly sense hidden within. This was the first Celestial that Noah had come across who seemed to actively be proficient in two laws- both Fate and Fire, and the power each of these laws released from his body did not seem to be too far apart from one another!","\"Haha, you must be the fresh meat that Commanding Officer Raizel is sending me message transmissions about. Nice to meet you! The name is Boru, Boru of the Righteous Flame!\"","RUMBLE!","The air seemed to shake with his introduction as the explosive fire elements around him singed the air, the two newly arriving Noah and Athena coming face to face with the leader of one of the most powerful Normal Teams of the Sanctum."]},{"number":371,"title":"Chapter 371: Chapter 370 - A Lesson in Elements","paragraphs":["The air in front of Noah and Athena palpated with power as the figure of Boru was soon accompanied by numerous other beings that pulsed with power no less than his, their gaze that of curiosity as they landed on the two of them.","A fully armored girl who only had her small head protruding from her oversized armor glanced at them doubtfully as she spoke up.","\"Still at the Void Realm, are you sure these two will be ok to join our team?\"","Her words received nods from her team members as they inquisitively looked at Noah and Athena, Boru laughing boisterously thereafter as he spoke out with a loud voice that caught the attention of many of the Celestials moving in the surroundings.","\"It matters not what their levels are right now, because these two are new disciples ordained with Noble Fates!\"","\"What?!\"","\"Noble Fates?\"","Many of the teams moving in the background heard these words as they looked over, their gazes shaking deprecatingly after seeing that the Righteous Fire Exploration Team was already surrounding the two beings.","\"Ah, they got their hands on two Golden Geese.\"","\"Haha, having a Golden Goose isn’t everything. We’ve been perfectly fine without one all these years.\"","\"What are you talking about, we’ve only been meeting Elite Behemoths that we couldn’t even defeat all this time, leaving us with nothing these past few months.\"","\"You...\"","Noah tuned out the numerous discussions erupting around him as he shook the hands of the large Celestial called Boru, getting the pleasantries out of the way as his focus remained on the enormous weapon strapped on his back that was most likely crafted from the remains of a powerful Behemoth.","\"My team and I planned to set out tomorrow after relaxing for a bit today, but as the Commander wants us to show you two the ropes, we will just move out today!\"","After the pleasantries, the voice of Boru continued its boisterousness as Noah and Athena nodded, following along this Righteous Fire Exploration Team as they began to point out the various structures and what they signified.","\"Living quarters will be over there...dining area will be...\"","A tour of the Sanctum was given as Noah and Athena followed this team as they went towards the North of the Sanctum, the layout of this grand place itself being explained by Boru as they passed the phenomenal looking structures surrounded by shimmering trees with sizes no less than the buildings themselves.","\"Once you guys accomplish hunting your first behemoth, you can bring the material over there...\"","Boru pointed to a grand building designed with a sleek black outlook that had the outline of an anvil and a hammer displayed outside of it.","\"...at Grandmaster Simeon’s Shop as he will craft you the strongest weapons that are most proficient in taking down Behemoths. This broadsword of mine was a commission I was able to make after my 14th year here, and it’s been with me ever since.\"","Boru caressed the enormous blade twice his size as he lifted it off his back effortlessly, going on to teach Noah and Athena more about the Behemoths as they began leaving the Sanctum!","\"You will come to find that the Behemoths are very proficient in particular laws, where finding one with deep achievements in the Law of Fire where we are going in the North is almost certain.\"","\"But, in other locations, you can find those proficient in the Law of Water, Earth, and even Supreme Laws if you explore further out.\"","Noah listened closely as the environment around them gradually changed, their figures leaving behind the expansive Sanctum gradually as less and less structures became apparent around out.","They continued walking out as useful knowledge about the Behemoths was released.","\"Their proficiency in laws is terrifying, but it is also their weakness that can be exploited to take them down more smoothly.\"","Boru waved his hands as the Exploration Team continued to move out, the enormous blade that released spurts of fire disappearing as another one slightly smaller than it appeared in his hands. This one released vibrant water elements on its blade edge that caused it to take a shining blue color that calmed the atmosphere as Boru continued.","\"When we hunt in the North where we know we will come across Behemoths proficient in the Law of Fire, we bring weapons of the water element that we were able to procure from the bodies of Behemoths from the south. It becomes much easier to take down the Behemoths proficient in the Law of Fire when you have weapons made from the bodies of Behemoths drenched in the Law of Water. We exploit this weakness to manage to take down these crazy powerful beasts!\"","Weapons drenched in the Law of Water could be used to effectively bypass the horrendous armor of Fiery Behemoths! This was a lesson that the newcomers came to learn about the Behemoths in the Celestial Realm- that using their strongest feature of proficiency in laws as their weakness!","This also applied to the armor that Boru wore. It released bursts of fiery light as it came from the body of a Behemoth found in the Northern area that was proficient in the Law of Fire, this type of armor granting increased resistance to its horrendous fire element attacks.","To put it simply, carry a weapon of the opposing element to deal more damage, and wearing the armor of the same element to resist its attacks!","\"Of course, using these types of weapons and drenching them with our abilities of the Law of Fate that deals Soul Damage just goes on to further enhance our strength, allowing us to gain the foothold we have gained so far in this Celestial Realm.\"","Boru had a wide smile as he carried the long jagged blade filled with water elements, Noah paying close attention to his words as the Exploration Team went out of the expansive Sanctum and into the mystical path laid out in front of them. His mind was on the Blood Stained Infernal Oath Set that he had produced a numerous amount of in the Spiritual Land, recalling how this Item Set gained from the bodies of Infernals had many resistances to the Fire Element! He hid a wide smile from appearing on his face as he thought of the possibilities of Items and possible Item Sets appearing from the bodies of Behemoths.","The further they went away from the Sanctum, the less buildings they came across as the archaic and humongous trees became more common. The flowing wisps of colorful blue and green essence shimmering from the fantastical trees brought about an atmosphere filled with fantasy and adventure, making Noah’s heart thirst for adventure as he explored this mystical environment!"]},{"number":372,"title":"Chapter 372: Chapter 371 - Worthy of the Title- Behemoth!","paragraphs":["It felt like a scene out of a fantasy book as Noah passed his hands over the colorful essence that was so thick that it had actually materialized into the atmosphere. The area that the Righteous Fire Exploration Team was walking across was filled with silence as the humongous trees all around them carried the air of mystique and danger.","\"Haha yes, the environment of the Celestial Realm is so special that it will take you a few days to get used to it. After a while, all of these pretty colors will seem like the norm as you get to experience even more fantastical things.\"","Boru’s voice pushed out the eerie silence of the now quiet environment of a forest as they walked further and further from the Sanctum.","\"We’re gradually leaving the perimeters of the Sanctum, and the areas further from here you will only find Watch Towers that monitor the surrounding regions for any activity.\"","Another one of Boru’s teammates chimed in as they continued to move forward, their steps gradually becoming faster as they picked up the pace while moving through the thick foliage that increased around them.","The atmosphere of a fantastical jungle only became more and more prominent as they went further in, Noah and Athena continuing to listen to the information of the layout they should be paying attention to and what areas they were passing through.","After a few minutes, Noah felt a significant change in the level of essence in the air, noticing it becoming immensely thicker as the Boru advancing in the front brought his hands up and brought the party to a halt.","He explained slowly as he closed his eyes, a wide smile appearing on his face as his body pulsed with power.","\"Whenever you feel that change in the atmospheric essence...know that a Behemoth is near. In this region in the North that we are in, you can occasionally come across a wandering Behemoth that nears the Sanctum to this extent. These Behemoths are usually the easiest ones to take care of as they have no sense of danger!\"","Boru’s boisterous voice rang out as he grasped the over sized jagged broad sword that palpated with the water element, giving a signal to his teammates as they advanced steadily.","\"You two, observe our movements and coordination first before choosing to join in. Watch how we handle the attacks of these Behemoths and the weakest points in their tough bodies that we attack.\"","Noah nodded as he turned towards Athena who had been relatively silent, her gaze continuously kept on the phenomenal sight around her as the moment they heard that a Behemoth was nearby, Noah saw the restlessness that always overcame her body as she thirsted for battle.","As they came here, Boru had mentioned that aside from the weakness of opposing elements that the Celestial Beasts held, the other weaknesses had to be learned for each specific type of beast depending on their size and build. One had to learn where their wrappings are, and this only occurred with time!","The two of them proceeded with caution as they followed behind the Righteous Fire Exploration Team, watching as the five members of this party had their weapons ready and drawn out.","Aside from the oversized jagged sword that Boru carried, two were hoisting large bows, another carried a menacing flail, and the last one had a shimmering staff.","The one unique thing about all of their weapons was that they all had the water element strongly exuding from them!","This was because the Behemoth they would come across in the Northern region from the Sanctum were those that were proficient in the Law of Fire. Noah began to feel this first hand as he felt the temperature around him gradually begin to increase, to the point that he knew any normal being would have begun to have their skin singed at the heat.","As they continued forward, the heat only became stronger as he felt that even lower ranked awakened could be burnt into crisp, but the wondrous thing was that the foliage and enormous trees around them peacefully continued their fantastical swaying as this temperature did not seem to bother them one bit!","Noah kept his senses spread out as they finally neared the point that released this much terrifying heat, his eyes noticing it first as they landed on a large mountain.","Or it seemed like a mountain, but it was actually moving!","THUMP!","Noah’s mouth flew wide open as his senses went on to wrap around this humongous mountainous figure, each of its features becoming extremely clear in his eyes as he observed a thing that was more than double the size of his Lesser Cthulhu form nonchalantly move in front of them.","THUMP!","The closer they neared, the more they could feel the shaking of the earth caused by its simple movements.","He could only describe the thing in front of his eyes to resemble an oversized dinosaur that was pumped with too much meat and bones!","It was walking on four legs, a ferocious looking head languidly moving around as a spiked tail that was covered with pulsating red crystal stalagmites that shone dangerously weaved behind it.","THUMP!","The l.u.s.trous red crystals went on to travel from its tail and all the way across its back as it gained a spiked appearance, its entire body releasing horrid waves of heat that seemed capable of melting anything they came in contact with!","Looking at the enormous size of this Behemoth as well as its fiery appearance, Noah had to agree that its title was well deserved.","This was a Celestial Beast that a single person would in no way be able to take down. This...was a Behemoth!","THUMP!","As Noah observed the immense heat being released from this powerful being, he saw with a shaking head how even the simple foliage and trees around this mountainous beast were still swaying peacefully, the environment of this Celestial Realm being something too unique. He could see some trees pushed aside or fallen to the side, making a clear pathway of where this mountainous Behemoth had come from, but that was the only damage he could find.","The moment the Righteous Fire Exploration Team neared the position of this Fire Behemoth, its large eyes shifted as its head turned towards them at an unnaturally high speed, bursts of flames beginning to erupt from its body as a world shaking roar rang out!","\"ROAAAAAR!!!\"","The roar was that of arrogant reality, of a being so powerful that the aura of a few ants getting near it shifted its mood as it warned them not to even come close!","RUMBLE!","It felt as if the air itself was shaking as waves of flames erupted from this fearsome creature, the wild laughter of Boru being heard at the same time as his body lit up with tens of thousands of Fate Lines, his power at the Soul Realm exploding out fully as the jagged sword he wielded let out a dazzling blue light! He swung this blue glowing blade forward as the roiling flames coming towards them were cut in half, preventing them from reaching the team members in the back as the first battle with a Behemoth unfolded for Noah and Athena!"]},{"number":373,"title":"Chapter 373: Chapter 372 - A Battle With a Fire Behemoth!","paragraphs":["Waves of power erupted out as Boru’s Soul Forging Realm was revealed gloriously, the heavy armor made from materials of a Fire Element Behemoth shining an arrogant red color as they went on to push back the raging flames being propelled forward by the mountainous beast in front of them!","The long BroadSword letting out palpating waves of the water element went on to further disperse the powerful attack coming towards them as the members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team spread around the Fire Behemoth, each one knowing their positions as their grasped weapons let out colorful attacks.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","The moment the wide area attack of the Behemoth ended, attacks layered with the strength of thrumming Fate Lines from 5 Soul Forging Realm Celestials began to land on the large beast.","\"Heave HO!\"","BOOM!","Boru took the center point as he kept the attention of the maddened beast, swinging his large blade downwards as it released a spectacular blade light of gold and blue, the unique energy provided by his Fate Lines passing through the weapon he held as this blade light went on to leave a scratch on the thick skin of the Behemoth.","That was right, a scratch!","That was all that the numerous attacks did to this terrible creature!","Noah and Athena were observing the ensuing battle from the back to get a grasp of how the team normally handled these types of creatures, their own bodies aching to join the battle themselves as the splendors of colorful skills bloomed in the area.","\"Zeke, left flank! Reiner, get behind it! Sylphy...\"","Boru was giving numerous commands as multiple Empyrean Guards began to appear around the raging Behemoth, these Empyrean Guards soon turning into streaks of light that went on to wrap around the bodies of the members of the exploration team.","OOOM!","The immense aura of fate spread out as the five figures of the exploration team became golden armored and winged beings, tens of thousands of Fate Lines on each of their bodies pulsating as they rained down even more attacks with vigor.","ROOOAAAR!","The Behemoth roared out as it felt dents beginning to appear on its armor, the numerous spiked crystals attached all over its huge back and tail shining a murderous red light as they erupted from its body and flew to the skies, very quickly raining down in the form of dangerous spiked flaming lances that attacked the entire perimeter around it!","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Boru and his teammates weaved in and out of the area as they evaded the flaming lances that exploded on impact, their armored bodies taking the brunt of the explosive forces as one of the teammates had to even pull back after cracks began to appear on her armor.","\"Sylphy, pull back! Everyone else, get [Judgment] ready!\"","Boru shouted out as he oversaw the entire area closely, his Soul Rank strength bubbling with power as he dual wielded a golden hammer in one hand and the long jagged water element BroadSword in the other.","\"Hooo...\"","A hot breath released from him as Noah shockingly counted more than 80,000 Fate Lines thrum within his body, his body coiling like a spring as it propelled itself towards the head of the Behemoth in a straight line!","Boru’s body began spinning in the air as wave after wave of golden blue blade lights began to erupt from him and smash onto the large head of the Behemoth, the monstrous beast itself going on to reply by releasing a horrid breath of fire that disintegrated the very air itself towards him.","SHAA! SHAA! SHAA!","The numerous golden blue blades of light met this attack as Boru continued spinning, his team mates moving to the sides as they prepared a skill Noah was very much familiar with, [Judgment]!","\"Ready!\"","\"Ready!..\"","The four of them called out as Boru used the force of his weapons to push himself out of the way of the destructive fire breath, the Behemoth choosing to pursue him with more attacks angrily before it came to a stop, its senses telling it that danger was coming.","RUMBLE!","Essence converged around the Behemoth as an enormous barrier of colorful flames appeared around it, but would the attacks of 5 Soul Forging Realm Celestials be that easy to block?","[Judgment]!","[Judgment]!","...","Four calls resounded first as Boru’s teammates released their abundant mana to release this powerful skill, numerous golden spears appearing in the skies as they aimed straight down towards the enormous Behemoth.","BOOM!","The wide and colorful shield of flames it had erected was pierced through after the first and second round of spears rained down, the third and fourth casts going on to pierce through its thick hide as a squeal of pain was finally released from this monstrous beast.","ROAAR!","A roar of pain erupted out as the beast felt enormous damage in its soul from the numerous attacks layered with abundant Law of Fate, but its pain was not done as the one who had been peskily running around it had the time to collect himself and prepare an even more powerful attack with his abundant lines of fate and something else that Noah could not yet figure out.","[Judgment], [Smite of Liberation].","OOONG","The air trembled as Noah used his senses to observe the being called Boru call upon every drop of energy in his body, his senses observing this energy pass through his tens of thousands of fate lines as it was released in a unique manner to initiate the cast of two abilities from [Fate’s Guardian].","BOOM!","The numerous sharp golden spears arrived first, piercing the wide body of the mountainous Behemoth that had actually begun to bleed bubbling red blood and going on to skewer its body even deeper!","The golden spears were followed by the sky clearing up as a large incorporeal golden Blade of Liberation that was more than three times the size of the blades Noah normally cast descended down.","This single blade was half the size of the more than 50 meter Fire Behemoth as it shot down at high speeds, the Behemoth sensing this danger as a destructive fire storm raged around it, but the damage it had received to its Soul affected it too much!","SPLUCH!","The abilities of [Fate’s Guardian] could be vastly different depending on who was using them, the enormous Blade of Liberation being cast by the Soul Forging Boru being phenomenally powerful as it went on to pierce the hard hide of the mountainous Behemoth and sink deep into its body.","ROAAAR!","\"Haha!\"","A defiant roar rang out from a deadly beast inflicted with immense Soul Damage, while a spent Celestial hoisting a large BroadSword laughed as he knew the battle was as good as over."]},{"number":374,"title":"Chapter 374: Chapter 373 - A Shocking Feat Done Effortlessly","paragraphs":["Gushes of blood erupted from the mountainous Behemoth, but it was not the physical damage that made it roar out a dying bellow, it was the horrendous damage to its soul that it received after these attacks pierced its hide!","The attacks were even further exacerbated as they carried with them a hint of powerful water elements that were destructive to its heavily flame based essence. The Behemoth tried to move its beaten down body as it felt weary, but the Celestials ganging up on it would not give it such a chance as Boru that was breathing heavily called out to his four team members along with Noah and Athena.","\"Finish it! And you two, let’s see some of your strength that makes you those with Noble Fates!\"","His four team members were already moving the moment Boru’s attack finished, Noah and Athena dashing into the scene of the battle quickly thereafter as Athena was quickly wrapped up in a golden armor as she valiantly went into close combat with the dying Behemoth, Noah himself looking to the skies as he cast [Smite of Liberation], the rumbling of descending blades being felt their after as five Blades of Liberation that were nowhere near as large as the single one that Boru had sent down came to smash into the Behemoth.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Their attacks landed on the wounded and dying beast, continuing on relentlessly as they knew they could not give it a second to recover its strength or gather its energy for attacks. The life force of Behemoths was enormous, where they would start healing in a matter of seconds if given the time as you found yourself in a long drawn out battle that you would eventually pay with your life!","\"ROAAAR!\"","Dying roars rang out from the enormous beast as the Celestials ganged up on it relentlessly, the battle only ending after another few minutes as the members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team all slumped towards the ground breathing heavily.","Their bodies were drained of energies as their faces were those of extreme achievement as they looked at the mountainous body of the Behemoth that had finally stopped moving, only its muscles spasming as fountains of blood continued to leak out from it, waves of burning elemental energies slowly beginning to build up around it.","\"Gulp, Gulp, Gulp!\"","Noah looked towards Boru’s position to observe this sizable Celestial actually near a position close to the Behemoth where spurts of blood were leaking out, his mouth wide open as he swallowed what rained down with huge gulps, his face that of extreme satisfaction!","His teammates looked at this site while they breathed raggedly, shaking their heads with a smiling expression of slight disgust as they were used to this behavior.","\"Ahh, that’s the spot. Another lesson for you rookies, the bodies of Behemoths being valuable treasures was not a joke, where even its blood is filled with immense life force that will quickly rejuvenate your lost energies. You wanna give it a go?\"","The dangerously smiling Boru invited them as Athena quietly shook her head, Noah himself training his level of control as he knew better than anyone else the quality of blood leaking into the earth!","His [Blood Gourmet] was telling him that the liters of blood gushing down would have a heavenly taste that even a voluptuous Soul Rank Vampyre could not even come close to comparison, but he would control himself at this moment as he did not want any unnecessary slips.","Boru wiped his mouth as he came towards him and Athena, his team mates recouping their strength as they began to surround the Behemoth.","\"So, first hunt. You observed and then joined in later. You got the feeling of it?\"","The Celestial thrummed with power that was gradually retuning to his body and Noah and Athena nodded, their gazes on the party members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team that had begun to cut apart the body of the Behemoth.","\"We work as a team, and so we have to divide the treasures the same way too. It is merit based of course, with the one contributing the most to bringing down these huge beasties taking the larger portion of it.","BOOM!","His words were masked as a Blade of Liberation descended down to precisely cut apart the Behemoth at a certain section, his party members using their [Smite of Liberation]s at this time to divide up the mountainous body of the beast as they each began to divide numerous parts and place them into their storage rings or bags.","Boru watched calmly as the largest portion of the Beast was left to him, along with a huge glistening core that released enormous waves of fire elemental essence in the surroundings!","The eyes of the boisterous Celestial shone as they came onto this huge Origin Core, waving his hands as it disappeared, along with the chest and head of the Behemoth as only a few pieces were left behind for him and Athena.","\"Here you go rookies, for those last attacks after you observed comfortably at a far distance, haha!\"","Boru used his expansive strength to throw the wide tail of the Behemoth that was still larger than Noah’s entire body towards him, two of the limbs of the beast containing horrendously sharp claws going towards Athena.","He waved his hands as the enormous tail filled with numerous shimmering crystal spikes entered his [Expansive Space], his heartbeat increasing every so slightly as he got his hands on the body of a Behemoth from the Celestial Realm, even if it was a small part of it.","\"Let’s move out from here. We’ve caused a big commotion, and don’t want to be in the same location in case we attract anything.\"","Boru voiced out as the party began to move from the bloodied site of destruction, the serene environment of the Celestial Realm gradually going back to normal as the shimmering trees and foliage continued to stand strong.","Noah followed the Righteous Fire Exploration Party half heartedly as he was doing something incredibly unique that he knew no one else could currently do!","He was excited to get his hands on the enormous spiked tail of the Behemoth, putting it in his [Expansive Space] as the Ancient Blood Clone that was millions and millions of miles away in another Realm entirely teleported into the [Blacksmith’s Forge] from the Time Space of the Spiritual Land.","This Ancient Blood Clone was an extension of himself, so he could just as easily access the [Expansive Space] that he placed the enormous tail of the Behemoth in!","A wide smile appeared on the devilishly handsome clone’s face as he waved his hands, the same body part of a Flame Behemoth appearing in the [Blacksmith’s Forge] as it almost took up the entire space! Noah laughed as he performed this feat so effortlessly, his thoughts quickly throwing a command to the Hearth of the Blacksmith’s Forge as he wondered, what would come out from the body of a Behemoth drenched in the Law of Fire?"]},{"number":375,"title":"Chapter 375: Chapter 374 - Materials, A Soul Rank Item!","paragraphs":["As Noah was moving in the Celestial Realm, his Ancient Blood Clone had begun the tedious work of raising the proficiency of skills in the Time Space while also taking the time to craft new sets of Blood Stained Infernal Oath.","The Item Set had a wide array of uses as it effectively created Berserkers that only became stronger as their vitality fell, finding great uses in the hands of the Beasts of the Spiritual Land and the Harbingers.","So far, he had created more than ten complete Blood Stained Infernal Oath Sets that he went to distribute to his people, but none of these crafting sessions had made him as excited as he was now!","Because currently, the burning blue flames in the Hearth of the Blacksmith’s Forge flew out to wrap around the enormous tail of the Fire Behemoth that held numerous spiked crystals on it. The blue flames acted like a snake as they wrapped around this tail in its entirety, Noah watching with rapt attention as he began to oversee the process where the massive tail filled with life force was cut apart as small pieces flew towards the Hearth and disappeared in the flames.","The process was quick and smooth, but something different occurred as the Ancient Blood Clone went on to observe the blue flames taking the thick hide, meat, and bones of the Fire Behemoth, but the numerous crystal stalagmites that were all over the tail were left floating in the air as a new panel filled with shining blue text appeared on Noah’s eyes.","[You have obtained x34 Soul Rank Fire Crystals, a normal material capable of enhancing flame-based Items with greater efficiency than Cores.]","Noah’s eyes widened as he observed the finished process of the entire tail being cut apart and the muscles and bones disappearing in the Hearth, the only thing left behind being the shining crystal spikes that were all over the tail of the Behemoth, their identity actually being materials that could be used with the [Refine] feature of the Blacksmith’s Forge!","He thought back to the huge chunks of the Behemoth that Boru and his teammates had gotten and the numerous stalagmite crystals that were still spread out all over the back of the humongous beast as his main body in the Celestial Realm hungered for the body of a Behemoth all to himself. He would take it one step a time though, and observe exactly what results it would bring out first.","The clone continued to observe the burning flames in the Hearth as the essence of the Spiritual Land was quickly and without reservation sucked towards the Blacksmith’s Forge, the Item coming out from the forge this time ultimately being something of great value. The ingredients were the enormous tail of a Behemoth that was standing stably at the Soul Rank, so Noah looked forward to the sort of weapon that would be one level higher than the Blood Stained Infernals Oath Set Items that he had been creating recently.","The process continued on for another few minutes and before long, an eruption of essence and light occurred yet again in the Blacksmith’s Forge as a regal aura spread out, the temperature in the surroundings beginning to rise rapidly a red shining weapon rotated in front of the Ancient Blood Clone’s eyes!","It was a weapon that passed Noah in size, being slightly larger than himself as it slowly came to life before his eyes. This was a type of weapon that Noah had seen before, but had never actually used in his lifetime. It was a weapon with a single handle in the middle, but it had sharp blades sticking out from each of its ends as it looked like a double edged sword-spear. If he knew his weapons correctly, this should be something that goes under the name of a Glaive!","His thoughts were affirmed as the rotating item slowly released waves of heat in the air, calming down as its description appeared in front of his eyes beautifully.","<strong>SOUL [Glaive of Simmering Ember] :: From the rage filled embers of a Behemoth, a glaive simmering with deadly flames comes to life. +100 Fire Elemental Power, +100% Physical Damage, +100% Elemental Penetration, +50% Attack Speed. Additional Ability: Descending Conflagration. (Part of the Incandescent Flameborn Set)</strong>","<strong>{Incandescent Flameborn Set} :: An Item Set that only an experienced hunter of Behemoths can adorn. 2 Set Item Bonus- An Ember Phoenix accompanies your side as they attack your enemies with fiery attacks. Ember Phoenixes are spiritual beings that can be summoned again as soon as they perish. 4 Set Item Bonus- When dealing damage with the Fire Element, enemies will take 500% extra damage over 5 seconds as the Burning Effect is applied on their bodies. The damage dealt by the user will also be increased by 50% and the damage taken is reduced by 3% for every Flameborn Item they have equipped. 6 Set Item Bonus- A Blazing Ring of Fire passively and constantly erupts with you at the center, applying the Soul Immolation Effect to your enemies. Enemies under the Soul Immolation Effect take 1000% more damage from abilities of the Fire Element.</strong>","A beautiful set of words that were extremely pleasing to the eyes appeared in front of the Ancient Blood Clone as he sucked in a breath. The weapon itself was crazy enough, but he had just finished reading the possible Item Set that could be created from the materials of a Fire Behemoth as his jaw nearly dropped to the ground!","The set bonus for 2 items seemed interesting, the bonus for 4 items looked crazy, but the bonus for having 6 items from the Incandescent Flameborn Set was simply insane! Noah looked over the description of the achieved ability that dealt something called Soul Immolation, as well as the huge 1000% boost that was attached to this ability. The numbers were too crazy for one to wrap their minds on the first time, and could only be viewed and tested fully on the battle field!","He went over the description of this fantastical weapon another three times before he reached out and grabbed onto it.","RUMBLE!","He felt the ever so increasing temperature of his surroundings gradually calm down as he grasped the weapon in his hands, its size a few inches bigger than his as he swiftly began to move it around. He felt an unnatural heaviness coming from the weapon as every time he moved it, thin streaks of flames began to bubble forth dangerously!","This was the first weapon that he had crafted that had an ability also attached to it, his eyes going over the [Descending Conflagration] as he wondered exactly what it would be. The attack speed boosts, physical damage boosts, and the Elemental Penetration were also amazing qualities by themselves, but he also came to the new introduction of something called Elemental Power!","He observed the [Glaive of Simmering Ember] as the flames that were asking to erupt within it continued to dance wildly, his thoughts moving rapidly as he went on to test the normal materials that had appeared from the tail of the Behemoth. The Glaive flew out of his hands as it went back into the Hearth, his mind sending a command to use the [Refine] feature for the first time.","RUMBLE!","15 of the crystal stalagmites that were considered Soul Rank Fire Crystals flew into the Hearth along with the Glaive of Simmering Ember, essence converging yet again as this session was much shorter than the last one, being less than a minute before the Item was thrown out of the Hearth once more. Noah glanced at the description yet again as he noticed some changes.","<strong>SOUL [Glaive of Simmering Ember]+1 :: From the rage filled embers of a Behemoth, a glaive simmering with deadly flames came to life. +110 Fire Elemental Power, +110% Physical Damage, +110% Elemental Penetration, +55% Attack Speed. Additional Ability: Descending Conflagration. (Part of the Incandescent Flameborn Set)</strong>","A +1 had appeared on the powerful weapon, as well as its boosts being increased by a small amount!","But...this was only a single successful refinement that had pushed the power of this weapon by more than 10%. Noah’s thoughts were running wild as he thought of all the possibilities of refining this type of weapon numerous times, as well as the other Items that were part of this Incandescent Flame Born Set that this [Glaive of Simmering Ember] was a part of. Although his thoughts were brought to a stop as he remembered he currently did not have any more pieces of a powerful Soul Rank Behemoth, and he only had 19 more Soul Rank Fire Crystals remaining on him!","This reminder brought his hungry thoughts back to the Celestial Realm, where the Righteous Fire Exploration Team was moving back towards the Sanctum to recuperate their spent essence. Noah walked along with them in the fantastical forest atmosphere of the Celestial Realm nonchalantly, fitting in perfectly as his clone had finished creating an Item from the materials of a Behemoth that was more refined than any weapons that the members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team were wielding!"]},{"number":376,"title":"Chapter 376: Chapter 375 - Bustling Atmosphere","paragraphs":["As Noah continued moving in the Celestial Realm, motions continued to flow in the Light Expanse of the Novus Galaxy as the major powers in the Prime Worlds were finishing their preparations to set off towards a certain location after agreeing to the conditions of the Celestials.","First, only beings of the Void Realm and above were allowed entrance to this paradisiacal Realm that the Celestials released information of, as anyone of lower strength would simply not be able to survive even a day in this Realm.","The second condition was the most important one, and it stated that for every being entering the Celestial Realm, whatever treasures they found in this dangerous realm would have to be shared with the Celestials, and this applied to half of everything they found!","Last and not least, everyone that entered would be kept track of, the Celestials needing to know exactly who was coming in and out of the Celestial Realm!","The powers from the numerous Prime Worlds agreed to these conditions without a second thought, their sights already set on the fantastical treasures of this Celestial Realm, no matter what they had to do to get their hands on it.","In the tumultuous Underworld, the forces of the Pureblood Vampyres were prepared as a devilishly handsome Prince Cassius had reappeared, his gaze as aloof as ever as his power thrummed at the peak of Void Realm.","Hos gaze was currently locked on with the beady eyes of a particularly arrogant penguin that was being carried by his Aunt, the Royal Vampyre Elena.","The Emperor Penguin seemed to be looking at the face of the prince up and down with its beady eyes that were filled with a prideful light, ultimately raising its beak up as it disregarded the devilishly handsome Prince and sunk back into the chest of a happy Elena.","This Royal Vampyre had just received a command from her Progenitor that she would be coming into the Celestial Realm with the forces that he sent, this Emperor Penguin being just one of the few beings that she would be traveling with!","Among them were fearsome Vampyric Calamities of the Sea, with the even more powerful beasts that were even more familiar with the particularly cute penguin she was holding tightly onto her. She ran her fingers down the sleek feathers on the raised head as she spoke to her nephew.","\"Get everyone else ready and we shall board the ship. The journey should take quite some time.\"","\"Yes!\"","Prince Cassius affirmed with a determined expression as he thought about Noah, learning of the results of his recent actions as his face hardened.","He had reviewed the recorded events of the massacre in the Magus World, seeing this being he knew to be ok his level not too long ago actually stand against two Soul Forging Realm opponents and actually take them down with ease. This wasn’t to even mention the Devouring Winged Serpent that was at the peak of Soul Forging Realm that he helped to finish the life of.","Prince Cassius felt a sense of shock as a flame began to burn in his heart, committing to strengthening himself to the fullest so he could at least match that being again!","His gaze was that of determination as he went towards the Interstellar Warship, looking forward to what the future would bring.","The Vampyre King watched his son head out as he looked back towards Elena, his gaze that of care as he spoke out slowly.","\"Take care of him while you all are there, Elena. He is my only son.\"","\"Bah stop with that brooding mood. I’ll keep everyone safe and bring you back some treasures. That is if I have the time while overseeing all the missions of the old fogey in the Dark Expanse.\"","Elena replied as she revealed some unknown secrets behind the scenes, secrets of how the Dark Expanse was using this opportunity to put some of their own forces into this Celestial Realm and observe its inner workings carefully. At this stage, the conflicts continued to occur behind the scenes as everyone seemed to be preparing for a coming war that would surely come to pass!","As the Celestials busied themselves with the Celestial Realm and rising the strength of their own weapons, The Infernal Lords were waiting patiently for the inevitable rise of the 9th Infernal Lord. They were a special existence, coming to understand that things would always move how fate intended, no matter what the being flowing in the river of fate tried to do. So they did nothing but simply wait as in the First Realm of Hell, an Abhorred Lich Emperor continued to direct a legion of Undead to continue depleting the rapidly populating Infernals of the expansive Infernal Realm of Hell.","Its body was bubbling with strength as golden flames eerily waved in its bony sockets, a green-gold light going on to shimmer over its body as it realized a change had occurred within itself.","The terrifying Lich did not have to wait long while wondering as soon after, its owner appeared in the skies where it stood atop a Bone Dragon, a smiling expression stretching out from his devilish face as he saw from the stat panel that the Abhorred Lich Emperor had finally reached maximum proficiency, and could be upgraded towards the next rank!","\"Haha!\"","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone let out a laugh as his thoughts moved towards the Abhorred Lich Emperor Skill Tree, getting ready to use the many Void and Void+ skills he had gained from the events in the Magus World to bring up this Skill Tree into the Soul Rank as well.","The required skills were sacrificed as a change began to occur to the Abhorred Lich Emperor in front of him, even bigger changes in store as he looked at the possibilities of advancement of its skill tree.","<strong>[Lich Lord of Abomination] (15/15)</strong>:: Abilities- Summon Poison Totem(5/5), Summon Undead(5/5), Noxious Outburst(5/5), and Dereliction of the Saintly Poison Lord(5/5) <strong>>> [Abhorred Lich Emperor](45/45)</strong> :: Additional Abilities- Undead Legion(5/5), Will of the Undead Emperor(5/5), and Delay Death(5/5). Two Skill Trees for evolution are possible once sufficient points and a base requirement of two equivalent level sacrificial skills are reached: <strong>>> [Arch Lich Ra’Zan]</strong> :: A dreadful calamity steeped in death. Enhances all death aspect abilities, as well as gaining the capability of summoning Supreme Tier Undead. >> <strong>[Pernicious Death Lord]</strong> :: A being with utmost proficiency in the art of poison and death, gaining wide area of attack abilities that decimate its foes.","The Ancient Blood Clone gazed at the blue set of words in front of his eyes as he smiled, his mind going on to select the pathway he wanted right away as a dense black light engulfed the summoned Lich Emperor, the air trembling as it announced the coming of an even more dreadful being!"]},{"number":377,"title":"Chapter 377: Chapter 376 - [ArChapter Lich RaZan]","paragraphs":["The selection of the next advancement made was [Arch Lich Ra’Zan], the pathway that led to even more deathly and terrifying additions being made to the Undead Legion!","RUMBLE!","Essence converged to the already summoned Arch Lich as he underwent a transformation, the Ancient Blood Clone going on to view the new abilities given by the advancement of this skill tree into the Soul Rank.","<strong>SOUL [Lich Lord of Abomination] (15/15)::</strong> Abilities- Summon Poison Totem(5/5), Summon Undead(5/5), Noxious Outburst(5/5), and Dereliction of the Saintly Poison Lord(5/5) <strong>>> [Abhorred Lich Emperor](45/45) ::</strong> Additional Abilities- Undead Legion(5/5), Will of the Undead Emperor(5/5), and Delay Death(5/5) <strong>>> [Arch Lich Ra’Zan] (0/60) :: Additional Abilities- No Man’s Land(0/5), Reward for Servitude(0/5), Field of Torment(0/5), and Abyssal Summoner(0/5).</strong>","The clear and crisp addition of four abilities came with the advent of Arch Lich Ra’Zan, with their names already sounding overly powerful as Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone focused on the individual skills to see exactly what their effects were!","<strong>[No Man’s Land] (0/5) :: The area of 1 mile around the Arch Lich Ra’Zan becomes a domain of death for 10 seconds. The Arch Lich and its minions are healed 3% of their maximum health every time an enemy dies in No Man’s Land. Enemies found in No Man’s land will suffer -25% All Element Resistance and -50% Death and Poison Element Resistance. Death related skills’ mana consumption is reduced to 0 while No Man’s Land is active. Cooldown: 360 minutes. </strong>","<strong>[Reward for Servitude] (0/5) :: The legion of the Arch Lich gains the capability of spreading the damage each of them received throughout the whole legion, bolstering their resilience as the vitality of many is greater than the vitality of a few. The damage that the Undead Legion receives can also be redirected towards the Arch Lich momentarily.</strong>","<strong>[Field of Torment] (0/5) :: Enemies are brought into an isolated space where they shall be tormented until their souls break down. The origins and memories of tormented enemies will be given to the Undead Legion as they are strengthened even further.</strong>","<strong>[Abyssal Summoner] (0/5) :: The terrible Undead from the Abyss can be called upon, their sheer size dominating the battlefield as only the strongest of Arch Liches can control them, Currently Available Abyssal Undead: Abyssal Death Knight, Abyssal Ghoul. Abyssal Summon Limit-1</strong>","The set of skills shone with a blue l.u.s.ter as the clone’s own eyes shone, his gaze landing on the newly improved Arch Lich Ra’Zan who was rising up from the cacophony of essence.","His features had fully erased the green color as it became a dominating black figure with golden flames blazing in its eye sockets, its size now nearing 3 meters as the skull staff it held became even more menacing!","Numerous black runic lines ran across its skeletal body that was half covered with a cloak drenched in darkness, the Bone Dragon it stood on beginning to perceptibly change below it as an aura of darkness spread out to cover it, along with the tens of thousands of the Undead that filled the surroundings.","OOOOOH!","Resounding cries of death erupted out as the Undead Legion underwent a transformation and further increased in strength, Noah wanting to observe the exact changes of the new skills as he began to pump skill points into them freely!","<strong> [Arch Lich Ra’Zan] (60/60) :: Additional Abilities- No Man’s Land(5/5), Reward for Servitude(5/5), Field of Torment(5/5), and Abyssal Summoner(5/5).</strong>","The effectiveness of [Field of Torment] and [Reward for Servitude] were increased, but the ones that showed their increased effectiveness most clearly were [No Man’s Land] and [Abyssal Summoner] after they were filled with maximum Skill Points!","<strong>[No Man’s Land] (5/5) :: The area of 6 miles around the Arch Lich Ra’Zan becomes a domain of death for 60 seconds. The Arch Lich and its minions are healed 21% of their maximum health every time an enemy dies in No Man’s Land. Enemies found in No Man’s land will suffer -50% All Element Resistance and -100% Death and Poison Element Resistance. Death related skills’ mana consumption is reduced to 0 while No Man’s Land is active. Cooldown: 60 minutes. </strong>","<strong>[Abyssal Summoner] (5/5) :: The terrible Undead from the Abyss can be called upon, their sheer size dominating the battlefield as only the strongest of Arch Liches can control them, Currently Available Abyssal Undead: Abyssal Death Knight, Abyssal Ghoul, Abyssal Revenant, Abyssal Jiangshi. Abyssal Summon Limit- 6</strong>","For the [No Man’s Land] ability, the affected area had increased from 1 mile to 6, as well as increased debuffs for all the enemies that were contained in this range of 6 miles, with the limit of how many the Arch Lich could summon becoming 6, while the cooldown came down from 360 minutes to only 60 minutes!","For the [Abyssal Summoner], additional possible summons called the Abyssal Revenant and Abyssal Jiangshi were added. Noah very much looked forward to seeing what exactly these Abyssal creatures were as he gave a command to the Arch Lich, the deathly being nodding as it waved its skull staff forward and cast, [Abyssal Summoner]!","RUMBLE!","A storm of essence erupted out with the Arch Lich at the center as a huge runic circle filled with darkness appeared in the skies of the First Realm of Hell.","The runic circle was more than 50 meters wide as it pulsed with power, a dark light shining from it as the forms of expertly designed Abyssal Undead erupted out and crashed towards the blazing earth!","BOOM!","Their arrival caused a huge impact that even crushed a few weaker Undead that were in the surroundings, their sizes being so massive as the two Abyssal Undead towered over 40 meters.","One was an Abyssal Revenant, a being that had a humanoid mummified form, and on its back was a huge coffin that spanned the length of its entire body!","The other was the Abyssal Jiangshi, an enormous being that held two dark columns bubbling with darkness in its arms, its entire body looking very similar to a four legged beast as it crouched down like an ape, the two dark columns of darkness it carried within its arms causing the earth they touched to decay.","OOOOH!","They screamed out as they announced their arrival, their screams traveling back to the far away Spiritual Land and spreading out tens of miles in theFirst Infernal Realm as even the wrathful Infernals received a tremor throughout their bodies!","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone only smiled as he looked at these powerful beings called Abyssal Undead, knowing his collection of Skill Points was about to get much faster, his heart already set on getting the percentage of the Infernal Lord title towards 100% soon!"]},{"number":378,"title":"Chapter 378: Chapter 377 - The Time Nears!","paragraphs":["In the Celestial Realm, the Righteous Fire Exploration Team had returned to the Sanctum as they went towards Grandmaster Simeon’s Blacksmith Shop.","\"Old Man Simeon, are you in here? We got some new material you can work on!\"","Boru’s boisterous voice erupted towards the large smithy in front of them as an even thicker voice returned out.","\"If it’s the materials of some Normal Behemoth, don’t even bother.\"","\"Ehh...\"","Boru shook his head willfully as he heard these words thrown out a moment after he called out, motioning for the team to continue towards the dining quarters.","\"Sometimes Grandmaster Simeon can be busy and turn you down unless you bring him an Elite Behemoth’s materials that are drenched in Supreme Laws. For now, let’s celebrate by gorging ourselves with food!\"","The members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team cheered as they followed along, Noah and Athena close behind them as the valiantAthena looked at Noah who seemed to be in thought.","\"You have that same light as when you proposed the alternate path for the mission in the Magus World. What could my little Junior Brother Crixus be thinking?\"","The Senior Sister that had spent a significant amount of time with Noah over the past month noticed the sharp light that was passing through his eyes, sending him a telepathic message as they went towards a spectacular looking building that had a heavenly smell of food and was bustling with the movements of numerous Celestials.","Noah glanced at the War Princess as he replied.","\"This expansive Celestial Realm that is largely unexplored...I want to see exactly what its secrets are!\"","His thoughts were simple, so he said them in a straightforward manner as Athena’s eyes shone at his answer, feeling a similar feeling deep in her heart. She looked towards the boisterous exploration team they just had their first hunt with as she sent back another telepathic message with a smile.","\"Haha, don’t worry. After learning all we can from this top ranked Exploration Team and grow our knowledge and power, it won’t be too late to explore the unknown regions.\"","The words of Athena only affirmed Noah’s thoughts about how he should move forward from here on out, knowing it would be very hard if he wanted to move out alone, as the Grandmaster heavily favored his life!","He thought of all the possible ways he could achieve his goal of exploring this Celestial Realm freely as many possibilities floated in his mind, one of them even being simply waiting a few days until the powerful figures of the many Prime Worlds began entering for him to enter as well, or to simply teleport his clone to also move right away in the Celestial Realm!","These ideas floated in his mind as he decided against teleporting the clone for now, not fully understanding the extent to which the Celestials were watching the explored regions surrounding the Sanctum, and for the simple fact that nobody other than Celestials were currently in the Celestial Realm. If anybody came across a single being exploring the dangerous Celestial Realm, he would raise a lot of dangerous flags with the Celestials at this point in time. The idea of waiting for more foreign powers to enter the Celestial Realm was most ideal, as things would become even more chaotic then, and if he chose to bring his clone into the Celestial Realm as well, he could do it with out any reservations.","This would mean momentarily losing the bonus of constantly using the Time Space of the Spiritual Land to raise the proficiencies of the skill trees, but he could still divide his time to do this if the clone moved alone in this mystical realm. The other cause was the [Treasure Hunter] feature that was attached to the Spiritual Land, which he knew would be immensely helpful in this realm filled with treasures. So bringing his clone into this realm with the Spiritual Land was an inevitable action, all that mattered was when exactly he would do it.","So for now, he would learn all about the explored and unexplored regions, and prepare for when he could actually start to move in earnest in a few days. He wanted to explore this expansive realm for himself to see exactly what awaited him, and to understand just why it was that Celestials had only ever explored 10% of this entire Realm!","He now knew that to the North of the Sanctum lied the Fire Behemoths, and to the South were the Behemoths knowledgeable in the Laws of Water and Ice. He still did not gather the knowledge of all the surrounding regions, and where exactly he would have to go to come across Behemoths that were proficient in Supreme Laws, or what treasures they could be guarding.","But after seeing the types of Items he could create from the bodies of Behemoths...his heart shook as he recalled the boosts of the Incandescent Flameborn Set that he only held a single item of currently.","The Item Set was so powerful that he knew if he hunted Behemoths of the opposing element, his task would be that much more smoother from the huge boosts given by equipping all 6 Items in the Set!","So he would continue amassing his knowledge of this establishment of the Celestials in the Celestial Realm, the Sanctum, and then get a good grasp on all the surrounding explored regions as he waited for the masses of beings from the numerous Prime World to gather.","He had been extremely productive the past few days, this being attributed mostly to his clone as he had quickly managed to upgrade another skill tree to the Soul Rank, and [Lesser Cthulhu] was not too far away from getting its own upgrade as the Ancient Blood Clone continued to work hard in the Time Space of the Spiritual Land.","A world shaking aura could be felt in the wide space most of the time as the clone adopted the fearsome form of the Lesser Cthulhu and used its numerous abilities, its Skill Proficiency continuing to be raised more and more as numerous days passed in the Time Space of the Spiritual Realm. Noah looked forward to the next form of this skill tree greatly, as there were too many mysteries associated with this particular ability.","He continued moving with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team as his thoughts were occupied with many ideas, occasionally asking more questions to learn about the Celestial Realm as time progressed.","Like this, the days continued to pass as the river of fate moved forward and in a few days, tens of thousands of Interstellar Sh.i.p.s were nearing the same position near a wide Golden Door that Noah had passed through not too long ago, their eyes shining with hunger as they also sought for their own opportunities!"]},{"number":379,"title":"Chapter 379: Chapter 378 - The Denizens of the Light Expanse Enter","paragraphs":["Throughout the Sanctum, a bustle of activities were taking place as the Celestials moved to ensure everything went their way with the entrance of the numerous beings from powerful Prime Worlds into the Celestial Realm. The expansive colonized area of the Celestial Realm that was hundreds of miles long had communications running throughout the different parts as they prepared for the massive increase in the number of beings.","The central area of the Sanctum that was cl.u.s.tered with most buildings was the busiest, while the empty areas of mystical forests that only had watchtowers every few tens of miles monitoring the explored regions had the least amount of activity. It was decided that the coming beings would be residing in these empty but explored regions, regions similar to the ones that Noah and Athena had entered into with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team where they had encountered a Fire Behemoth!","These regions weren’t entirely safe, but those entering would be given this information and told to prepare as they forged their own path in the Celestial Realm.","Talismans that could be given to all those who entered so they could be kept track of were produced en masse as hundreds of thousands were ready, the Celestials looking forward to the future where their resource collection would multiply by an unknown factor as they received even more treasures through the intrusion of these beings, while also influencing them greatly for the coming future.","In a particular nondescript vessel, the forces of the Pureblood Vampyres of the Underworld were cl.u.s.tered together neatly as they continued towards the Golden Door. There were hundreds of Prime Warsh.i.p.s in the surroundings, causing every single being to be very well behaved as they knew very well the power of these fearsome weapons","The Pureblood Vampyres watched the procession of beings getting out of their vessels as they were read the rules and accepted the tracking talisman, their turns soon nearing as the Royal Vampyre Elena led her forces forward.","Among them were the forces of Beasts from Noah’s Spiritual Land and the Calamities of the Sea that had used the numerous cores that Noah brought back to upgrade their rank to the Void Realm, their gazes shining a dangerous light as they looked at the beings that so easily destroyed their world.","Their hearts were stifled, but they knew they could not do anything at this moment as they continued to improve their strength until they achieved a level of power that would allow them to move however they wished.","The arrogant Emperor Penguin floated in the void of space as his body pulsed with a unique force, his spatial attribute going very well with the unique qualities of space as he stood at the forefront of the forces right next to Elena.","Their turn came as they floated towards the front of the procession where multiple Red Robed Celestials were located, golden lights shining upon them as they were read the agreement for entering the Celestial Realm and each one was given a tracking talisman. This would effectively act as their identity for when they wanted to enter or leave the Celestial Realm in the future!","Something of important note was the reminder from the Celestials that even though whatever they obtained in the Celestial Realm would be reduced by half as they gave the other half to the Celestials, whatever treasures they fought for and obtained would ultimately be theirs. They would not be bullied, and it was first come first serve when it came to battling the creatures in the Celestial Realm, or its vast mystical treasures.","Like all the previous denizens of the Light Expanse, the Pureblood Vampyres agreed as they were granted access to move forward, their origins coming in contact with the Golden Door as their figures disappeared, instantly reappearing in a bustling area at the center of the Sanctum that now held even more people!","Different to when Noah first entered, a huge change had occurred in the past few days as the Celestials anticipated the many uses of the increase in beings, going to institute a few things, with one of them being shops!","There were numerous stalls spread out all over the Sanctum that offered a variety of products unique to the Celestial Realm, some being oversized weapons and armor made from the bodies of behemoths, others being medicinal herbs or unique treasures that Celestials ran into themselves as they explored.","Currently, many of these shops were spread out as each one held a singular similarity, and that was the incredulous prices that were attached to the things offered for sale!","As they were unique products never to be found anywhere else, they were traded only with the highest quality cores or other treasures as a form of payment, with the least acceptable cores or refined cores(Spirit Stones) being those at the Soul Realm, and the prices ranged in the tens of cores.","This was just a preliminary test that the Celestials were conducting, their future goal being to create an economy as this new force entered the Celestial Realm, using the many things they obtain within to circulate as they grew more and more attached to the Realm and everything in it.","This also went in their favor as to them, they were simply lending out weapons that would help these beings to take down Behemoths that they would eventually be taking 50% of whenever the denizens of the Light Expanse defeated them, and this also applied to any treasures they were lucky enough to find!","It was a win win situation that promoted the strength of the newly arriving beings while only furthering the goals of the Celestials more.","The forces of the Pureblood Vampyres looked around their surroundings in wonder as they sensed the engulfing and overflowing essence in the surroundings, the Emperor Penguin being particularly happy as he could sense the Spiritual Land Master not too far away from where they were!","’Master, we can finally fight in the same location as you!’","The arrogant penguin felt a tight knot in its chest loosen as it achieved the goal of helping its Master, finally gaining enough strength to be able to stand in the same region as him. Its beak raised to the skies as it vowed to enact the legend of the most fearsome Spiritual Beast that ever lived and leave a mark in this Celestial Realm for its Master!","Many hopes and dreams were flowing through the minds of the newly arriving beings from powerful Prime Worlds in the Light Expanse as the largely unexplored fantastical Celestial Realm received a large influx of forces, on the first day gaining tens of thousands of beings at the Void Realm, and hundreds at the Soul Forging Rank as the tides of change swiftly moved forward.","The influx of these new forces only meant one thing- that this largely unexplored realm was about to become even more lively, numerous beings with their own fates entering as mysteries would more quickly be unveiled. Although, the result of this project on a large scale could only be seen by those actually moving the pieces in the dark."]},{"number":380,"title":"Chapter 380: Chapter 379 - The Order of Blood is Formed, Arrival!","paragraphs":["A few days passed as the liveliness of the Sanctum only increased, the influx of people increasing by the day as many familiarize themselves with the knowledge of the Celestial Realm.","To gain this knowledge, they had to pay the price of multiple Soul Rank Cores or simply begin venturing into the mystical forest of the Celestial Realm themselves as they braved the dangers and tested their luck on fantastical treasures.","Some groups heavily believed in themselves as they moved out, many beings coming to face the power of the Behemoths for the first time in the past few days as many casualties occurred for the newly formed exploration teams, this event acting as a reminder to those coming in as they watched dejected faces walking through the expansive Sanctum carrying dead bodies of their comrades.","Some were from powerful Prime Worlds and made Exploration Teams filled with Soul Rank individuals and hundreds of Void Rank beings, using this overpowering force to take down Behemoths as they began to enjoy the treasures of the Celestial Realm!","The moment these victories began to appear, the newly arrived beings from numerous Prime Worlds saw the importance of creating powerful Exploration Teams to hunt down these powerful but wondrous Behemoths whose bodies were filled with treasures, sparking the competitive beginning of the creation of numerous teams as some forces were powerful enough to form their own complete teams capable of hunting down Normal Behemoths, while other forces from different Prime Worlds joined together in order to achieve the same goal.","On the third day as even more and more beings continued to pour into the Celestial Realm and begin exploring it, the careful observing force of Pureblood Vampyres finally decided they gathered enough information, which was simply what Noah passed towards the Emperor Penguin and Royal Vampyre Elena as they became one of the most prepared groups of the incoming forces.","They finally felt their confidence rise on the third day as they finally stopped watching how the events would continue to move forward, choosing to set out to explore themselves as Elena received very specific directions from Noah in order for this team to keep their lives and not face a complete massacre.","One of those things was the simple rule that their force would not move past the unexplored regions that might hold powerful Elite Behemoths or even worse for now, spending this time to get accustomed to the fighting power of Normal Behemoths as they strengthened themselves and obtained phenomenal treasures.","The Royal Vampyre listened to the words of the Vampyre Progenitor to the tee as on this day in the Sanctum of the Celestial Realm, the Exploration Team under the name of The Order of Blood was formed!","This exploration team consisted of powerful Vampyric Beasts like the Emperor Penguin and numerous Pureblood Vampyres that were led by the curvaceous Royal Blood Vampyre Elena, a force that would actually fall on the weaker side as it did not have that many Soul Forging Beings.","But they would make up for what they lacked in strength with their numbers, and also with something that was unique only to them, the blazing red Item Sets they wore that were the Bloodstained Infernal Oath Set Items!","Noah had used the Absolute Skills <<Herald of Fate>> to observe the Items created from Infernals numerous times as he confirmed that their origins were not able to be ascertained as the enemies of Celestials at all.","But these items would play a special role in the Celestial Realm, as they were items strong in the Law of Fire, being especially effective in hunting down Icy Behemoths in the South region or withstanding the Fire Behemoths in the North with the armors that provided defense against such a beast.","The concept that having the armor of the same element helped in withstanding the damage of the Behemoth while holding a weapon of the opposing element helped you deal more damage to the Behemoth would soon become understood very clearly by the arriving beings as they flocked to create weapons from the bodies of the Behemoths they hunted, wanting to equip themselves with the right set of armors and weapons that would dictate what they hunted in the future.","The combination of armor drenched in the Law of Fire along with a weapon drenched in the Law of Water was needed to hunt Fire Behemoths with most efficiency. While the combination of armor drenched in the Law of Water and a weapon filled with the Law of Fire were utmost if one wanted to pierce through the defenses of an Ice Behemoth. This concept applied to all the other elements, as they had not yet stepped into the realm of worrying about Elite Behemoths that could be proficient in Supreme Laws.","The Law of Light and the Law of Darkness opposed each other, as well as the Law of Fate and the Law of Chaos standing on opposite sides of the spectrum, but not a single one of the new beings were worried about these types of laws at this moment.","The newly formed Order of Blood with Elena leading was equipped with the Infernal Sets as they set off carefully towards the explored perimeters near the Sanctum, wishing to find a weak wandering Behemoth to have their first battle as they move to strengthen themselves.","Meanwhile, Noah and Athena were in the company of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team as they continued to go out and hunt the Northern Region with Fire Behemoths every day as they learned more and more about the Celestial Realm, Noah’s mood being particularly good today as while he walked with Boru and his group back to the Sanctum, in another location of the Celestial Realm, someone had intruded.","The intrusion was not through the Golden Door that led one into the Celestial Realm, but through the use of a particular Teleportation Skill that allowed one to appear at any place in their memories.","This time, a devilishly handsome Ancient Blood Clone had appeared in an empty region of the Celestial Realm, a confident expression on his face as he had a miraculous Spiritual Land anchored to his body.","A single blood clone carrying a Spiritual Land that had a unique feature entered the Celestial Realm, the effect of this event being something only Noah could imagine as he got ready to move into this expansive realm in earnest as he used the cover of the newly arriving beings to move freely.","This wide realm and the numerous mysterious treasures within it...he wanted them all to himself as the Ancient Blood Clone raised his hand up, holding the miniaturized Spiritual Land as he began by activating a single feature- [Treasure Hunter]!"]},{"number":381,"title":"Chapter 381: Chapter 380 - Covert Exploration","paragraphs":["In the expansive Celestial Realm, a single Ancient Blood Clone was moving further and further away from the Sanctum as he passed through numerous areas that were already explored by the Celestials, the path he was taking actually taking him towards the unexplored regions as time passed.","The usage of the [Treasure Hunter] feature of the Frozen Plateau Spiritual Land was a unique one, with the clone observing a golden light shoot forth from the center of the miniaturized Spiritual Land as it trembled with vigorous essence, this golden light forming into the shape of a literal golden arrow that pointed even further north from the position that he was standing on.","Noah shook his head with a smile as he looked at the small golden arrow that was barely a meter long, wondering exactly what thing could be considered a treasure that this arrow had locked onto, and what he would have to do to obtain it!","Before he began moving towards the direction it pointed towards, he used the [Unique Origin] ability gifted from the Vampyre Progenitor as he chose to look for this first treasure covertly, not knowing what powerful creatures he could possibly run into as he went further and further away from the Sanctum.","He used [Unique Origin] as his body rapidly changed, becoming a pool of blood that slowly dwindled in size until it became less than a few inches, his humanoid shape becoming clearer as the size continued to reduce until he became a single inch! As he used the ability, he made it so that not a single aura of power leaked from him, the presence he gave off being even less stimulating than the plants that gave off abundant essence around him.","In the surroundings of the fantastical environment of the Celestial Realm where everything was filled with overflowing essence, a being that could barely be seen by the n.a.k.e.d eye that did not have even an aura of essence would be nearly impossible to find unless someone powerful was specifically looking for them appeared!","The miniaturized Ancient Blood Clone looked up towards the now even grander forest around him, even the small swaying grasses seeming multiple times larger than his own figure as the earth below him that was abundant in essence expanded even further. The ancient trees that were tens of meters tall looked even more massive, the cover of all of these magical surroundings making him feel extremely safe.","The size of the miniaturized Spiritual Land became even smaller than him, less than one tenth of an inch as it was anchored to his left hand, the golden arrow coming from it reflecting in size as the clone smiled, its body still bubbling with enormous power as it shot forth in the cover of numerous grasses where the arrow indicated!","He was moving in an extremely covert manner as while he moved beneath the numerous plants and foliage, not a single disturbance occurred in the fantastical surroundings of his location. His goal was to find out exactly where [Treasure Hunter] would lead him, and that was it. What would happen after that would be determined by what exactly he came to find.","His main body had been moving with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team the past few days, their hunts gradually giving him more and more information as he knew what terrible Behemoths could be found in the nearby areas that he was advised to keep away from.","The explored areas near the Sanctum were filled with Normal Behemoths, their strength varying in ranks but almost all of them being stably at the Soul Forging Realm. Because of their unique enormous bodies and proficiencies in laws, tens of normal Soul Rank individuals were required to take them down, or the most powerful Exploration Teams from the Celestials like the Righteous Fire hunting team.","Going even further out would put you at risk of coming around the Domain of an Elite Behemoth, which would almost certainly guarantee death for any Normal Team!","The Celestials warned Normal Teams to be extremely careful of entering a domain of such Celestial Beasts because as the name implies, these Elite Beasts would commonly have power at the Domain Expansion Realm!","That was a shocking realm that the Celestial Grandmasters held, their power being immensely powerful as they formed what was called Elite Exploration teams to hunt down such Behemoths.","Some of these Behemoths could have a rank at the Soul Forging Realm, but if they were proficient in a Supreme Law, it automatically placed them at the Elite Behemoth level. Some could be half a step into the Domain Expansion realm, this small advancement added to their already terrifying bodies allowing them to also be ranked as Elite Behemoths. Of course, the Behemoths that had already stepped into the Domain Expansion Realm were the most powerful at the Elite Rank, needing a team of Grandmasters to fully take them down.","What Noah currently dreaded the most was coming face to face with an Elite Behemoth, as he knew it would mean a very arduous and nearly impossible mission for his clone, but the further out he continued to follow the golden arrow, the more somber he became as he also grew more excited!","His miniaturized figure continued running speedily beneath the cover of its surroundings, coming to a stop after an hour as he felt the overflowing aura of a Behemoth filled with the Fire Element.","He stopped his quick movements as he climbed the grasses that were huge proportionate to his size, peeking from beneath the earth as he did not use any of his skills that allowed him to spread out his aura to check his surroundings. As long as he didn’t use any mana in this place where even plants overflowed with immense mana, even the extremely perceptive Behemoths would not be able to locate him.","The Fire Behemoth he came across adopted similar features to the ones he had been coming across as he moved with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team, this one looking similar to an oversized Iguana that was slowly strolling through the mystical swaying trees.","Noah observed this powerful beast as he finally came across a Behemoth while moving alone, the presence of it being at the Normal Level being apparent as Noah was confident in being able to take it down with time.","He glanced at the calm surroundings and the Fire Behemoth that continued to stroll undisturbed as he smiled as returned back under the shade of the grasses, continuing towards where the golden arrow pointed as he marked the location of this Behemoth.","He had used the abilities of {Herald of Fate} to determine the best pathway for him to take that would cause the least chaos for his mission, and it told him to continue on his path towards where the golden arrow pointed to!","So for now, he only marked the location of this Behemoth as he continued forward, fully trusting the abilities of {Herald of Fate} as they lead him to upgrade [Blood Lord] skill tree that made possible for the Ancient Blood Clone to come to life, as well as the reminder for the profound uses of the Spiritual Land that he was currently using right now.","A single Fire Behemoth was not hard to find in the close proximity of the Sanctum, and he could come to find one whenever he wished to start a long and arduous battle with it alone. But his goal currently was the location where the golden arrow that the unique feature of the Spiritual Land, [Treasure Hunter], was pointing to. After he ascertained exactly what was considered a treasure in the eyes of this ability and got his hands on it, he would hunt all the Behemoths he could!"]},{"number":382,"title":"Chapter 382: Chapter 381 - Hidden Beneath a Mountain!","paragraphs":["The miniaturized Ancient Blood Clone continued to go further and further away from the sanctum as he came across a few monstrous auras of Fire Behemoths, marking all of their locations as he continued forward and mapped out the fantastical areas of the Celestial Realm himself.","He had come across and taken down a few Fire Behemoths with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team over the past few days, each time getting his hands on a piece of the large beasts’ bodies as he went on to create another 4 Pieces of the Incandescent Flameborn Set, the other four pieces being the b.r.e.a.s.tplate, leggings, boots, and armguards. All he had left to craft was the crown and he would have all 6 pieces of the powerful set.","The boosts of these items were not a joke either, Noah looking at their description as the clone continued speedily moving towards an unknown location.","<strong>[B.r.e.a.s.tplate of Simmering Ember] :: An item created from the wrathful body of a Behemoth. +150% Enhanced Defense, +50% Fire Element Resistance, +50% Increased All Element Resistance, and Grants the ability of Extreme Heat Resistance.</strong>","<strong>[Leggings of Simmering Ember] :: An item created from the wrathful body of a Behemoth. +100% Enhanced Defense, +50% Fire Element Resistance, +50% Increased All Element Resistance.</strong>","<strong>[Boots of Simmering Ember] :: An item created from the wrathful body of a Behemoth. +50% Movement Speed, +50% Enhanced Defense, +25% Fire Element Resistance, +25% Increased All Element Resistance. Unaffected by the burning grounds they stand on. </strong>","<strong>[Armguards of the Simmering Ember] :: An item created from the wrathful body of a Behemoth. +25% Enhanced Attack and Cast Speed, +25% Enhanced Defense, +25% Fire Element Resistance, +25% Increased All Element Resistance.</strong>","The items had huge boosts when it came to withstanding the attacks of flame Behemoths, making them top tier pieces of armor to wear for anyone traversing the Northern region that was filled with Flame Behemoths.","The Glaive that was of the fire element would actually deal less damage to these same behemoths as they were extremely proficient in the Law of Fire, with Noah needed to find a weapon or the water element similar to the ones that Boru and his team carried to gain extra battle power against Flame Behemoths.","He put this in the back of his mind as he focused on carefully following the golden arrow forward, noticing that the arrow was now blinking!","This made him excited as it indicated he was actually nearing the supposed location!","He continued traveling below the waving grasses as he observed the ground he was running on gradually becoming elevated as he continued forward, this actually causing a change to the arrow as instead of pointing straight, it began to edge further downwards as he continued following the ascending ground.","He brought himself to a stop as he climbed the grasses around him, picking his tiny head to observe the surroundings more as he confirmed he was now beginning to go up an enormous volcanic mountain that had bubbling molten earth at the top. This mountain covered his entire sight as he could barely discern its peak or where it ended as it encompassed everything around him.","The surroundings were much hotter than the explored regions near the Sanctum as a dangerous feeling was permeating all throughout this mountain.","The Ancient Blood Clone’s face hardened as he realized that the golden arrow had begun pointing downwards the moment he began ascending the mountain, which meant that whatever treasure it pointed to was located at the bottom of this enormous volcanic mountain!","He took a deep breath as he changed his tactics, his body glancing at the earth below him as his figure disappeared beneath it. His speed became unbearably slower as he used the tiniest amount of power to allow his small body to drill through the extremely hard earth, following the blinking golden arrow as it continued leading him to an unknown location, and this particular location was in the middle of an enormous volcanic mountain in the Celestial Realm. More than half an hour passed as he continued to drill further and further down, the only thing around him being gradually reddening earth.","SHAAA!","The figure of the clone came to a stop after some time as it broke through the layers of earth that were getting hotter and hotter, actually finding himself breaking through an enormous underground Cavern that had a powerful red tint from the overflowing lava and molten earth that could be seen from all around!","He had pierced through the layers of this enormous mountain and arrived at this expansive underground Cavern that was actually tens of miles wide, seeming like an entirely new world to the miniaturized Noah.","What was shocking about this lava filled cavern he had found himself in though, was the single mountainous Behemoth that was lazily floating atop the sea of lava!","The eyes of the Ancient Blood Clone widened as they landed on this regal but monstrous beast as he shook his head exasperatingly.","’Haaa...thats a f.u.c.k.i.n.g Elite Behemoth isn’t it?’","Noah stared into the expansive cavern where molten lava flowed from all around while a single monstrous beast floated atop this flowing molten earth peacefully.","The aura coming off its body was that of an oppressive beast that could devour everything, but Noah’s mood slightly became better after he noticed that the overpowering feeling wasn’t exactly the same as Grandmaster Vredral who at the Domain Expansion Realm.","Yet...this being had a hint of that aura, making Noah believe that this was a Behemoth that was half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm, and this still classified it as an Elite Behemoth!","The clone released a tense breath as it observed not too far from the immense Behemoth, there was an exquisitely raised pedestal that was filled with ancient runic lines, and at the top of this pedestal there lay a brilliantly shining red crystal that caused his heart to tighten just from looking. The golden arrow from the [Treasure Hunter] of the Spiritual Lana was blinking rapidly at this moment, seemingly trembling with excitement as it had reached the goal it was pointing to as it began to slowly fade away. The eyes of the Ancient Blood Clone glowed a sharp light as he finally came upon a treasure in the Celestial Realm!","This apparent treasure was actually protected by a beast that would normally be taken down by an Elite Team of Celestial Grandmasters, even if it fell on the weakest side that could possibly be hunted by the strongest Normal Exploration Teams like Boru’s that now had the addition of Noah’s main body and Athena.","The main issue remained the same though! Whatever this fantastical treasure that the Spiritual Land’s [Treasure Hunter] had led him to was, to get his hands on it, he had to get past this powerful Fire Behemoth that was half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm!"]},{"number":383,"title":"Chapter 383: Chapter 382 - A Dragon Guarding a Treasure","paragraphs":["Noah found himself in an extremely tense environment as he stared at the lazily floating Elite Behemoth that had half of its body sunken in the blazing lava.","The mountainous figure had its eyes closed as Noah could only see half of its body, which actually spanned over 30 meters as it magnificently rolled around the Cavern. His attention was pulled towards the large red crystal of the ancient runic pedestal that seemed to be calling out to him, his eyes becoming hot the more they remained on this shimmering treasure.","He breathed out slowly as he brought himself to calm down and think of the numerous ways to proceed, pulling out the Dagger of Time stored in the [Expansive Space] as well as equipping his miniaturized body with the items from the {Incandescent Flameborn Set} to provide even more protection in this fiery hell!","Numerous calculations passed through his mind as he didn’t activate any skills yet, knowing the moment he used his mana this extremely dangerous Behemoth lazily floating in lava would notice him.","A few minutes passed as he observed its movements in this tense atmosphere, coming to map out its large body gradually as it continued to swim in the lava. The Elite Behemoth actually adopted the features of something that Noah had come across a few times in his life, and that was a Dragon!","The enormous head that continued to dip in and out of the lava peacefully had a rough draconic outline as enormous wings were tucked into its sides, with Noah not even being able to see their end as they sunk in the molten earth.","A dangerously glistening tail that held numerous crystal stalagmites that shone with a deep red hue could also be seen occasionally rise and fall from the flowing lava!","Numerous ideas came and went in Noah’s mind as he tried to map out multiple possibilities, planning for every possible path as he only came out with two. One was miraculously taking this unknown treasure right under the nose of its powerful protector, getting away safely just as the powerful beast was reacting to his movements. This was the best possible course of action, as Noah was not fully confident in being able to take down an Elite Tier Behemoth at this stage, even with his fantastical cheats!","This also brought the consideration that he didn’t consider too much of a limitation because of his nearly infinite mana, and that was the 60% limitation of power given to this clone. This also bought numerous new questions about this limitation that he had to slowly understand.","The other possible pathway for him to take this treasure was if the first plan of snatch and run inevitably failed, where he would then have to leave it to fate and go all out, testing exactly how powerful this Elite Behemoth that was half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm would be. This was the second pathway, and he already sent telepathic commands to a special someone if this path was to be followed, knowing he would need all the help he can get.","His face became stern as he pulled back from the wide Cavern and followed the path that he came in, going more than a few miles as he took out the miniaturized Spiritual Land and used [Anchor] to expertly hide it among the grains of earth in the mountain. This was the last preparation, where just in case something horrendous happened, only the clone would be affected as his main body would suffer a significant blow from the loss of a portion of his Origin.","He made his way back towards the wide Cavern thereafter as the same scene greeted him, getting himself ready as he was going to go for the first possible pathway first- taking the treasure right under the nose of this monstrous Draconic Fire Behemoth!","To do this, he looked at the description of a particular ability from the Seven Deadly Sins that he had not used too often, one that came from the Sin of Greed!","[Emperor of Greed] The user can steal the ownership of any item they see or sense.","The skill stated that he could steal the ownership of any item he could see or sense, being extremely useful, but also raising many questions on what it applied to. This treasure in front of him, could it be considered an owned item that he could use this skill to take? Could this ability be stopped in any way if the perception of this Draconic Fire Behemoth was as monstrous as his intel from the Celestials told him?","There were many unknowns in this first plan, which was why Noah was still fairly unconfident with it, and was simply giving it a shot! He breathed out as his eyes honed in on the faraway glowing crystal, getting ready another phase of this first plan that involved physically teleporting his body as he risked the life of the clone to the close proximity of this enormous Behemoth just incase [Emperor of Greed] did not work.","But before this, there was the ability from the Sin of Greed, and there was also...the Dagger of Time! The abilities that the Dagger of Time had were few, but they were extremely powerful as he always kept the Sheath filled with Time Essence from the Time Space, always ready for use if drastic situations like these demanded it.","When he saw the Draconic Fire Behemoth was at the position furthest away from the ancient runic pedestal holding the treasure, Noah’s face hardened as his eyes locked in on the profoundly glimmering crystal and cast multiple abilities, starting off with the ability from the Dagger of Time that actually stopped time, [Stop]!","SHAA!","Stillness spread through a wide region of the Cavern, Noah spreading out his aura and senses finally as his eyes locked on to the glimmering crystal above the ancient runic pedestal and also cast, [Emperor of Greed]!","..."]},{"number":384,"title":"Chapter 384: Chapter 383 - Authority!","paragraphs":["An unbelievably powerful entity was swimming peacefully in its natural habitat filled with blazing, flowing, lava, enjoying the nice swim as it continued to build up the Law of Fire throughout every molecule of its body.","The environment of extreme heat in its surroundings only made it more powerful and efficient in its comprehension of the Law of Fire, its body attuned to the lava flowing around it and the immense heat all over the cavern as it continued its cultivation.","At this moment though, around a certain region of the wide cavernous space that covered the entirety of its body and the region where a special item stood peacefully...time had actually come to a stop!","RUMBLE!","The shaking of essence could barely be discernible as in this frozen area of time, the enormous eyes of the Draconic Fire Behemoth actually snapped wide open, its overpowering senses observing the changes around it as it felt chains of time restricting its oversized body!","’HMPH!’","The eyes of the Draconic Fire Behemoth actually opened wide in this stopped area of time, its body that was frozen in place staying still as its humongous eyes locked towards a particular location where it could feel the movements of an enormous amount of mana.","Its powerful Origin that was drenched in the Law of Fire and enhanced even further in this environment and its inborn ability actually allowed it to observe the movement of essence that was spreading out from a certain being in a far away location!","This unique essence had already covered the expansive space it was in as it actually made possible for time to come to a halt, but the Draconic Fire Behemoth sensed the movement of even more vigorous essence shooting towards a particular Ancient Pedestal that held a special treasure which made its high achievements in the Law of Fire possible.","One must know that within the time period that time had been stopped, not even an instant had passed as in this stopped time, the Elite Behemoth came to attention and observed all of these things instantaneously, its terrifying power going forth another level as it even sensed the spectacular movement of mana of a cast skill that was heading towards the treasure atop the archaic pedestal!","The opened eyes of the Draconic Fire Behemoth locked on the small being that was releasing this mana, realizing its purpose instantly as its red eyes sparked with flames in this stopped time, the vigorous and fantastical essence within its body bubbling forth as it uttered three words within its heart.","{{Flame Lord’s Authority}}.","RUMBLEEEE!!!","From the very origin of the Draconic Fire Behemoth, a unique power roared forth and erupted from it, going on to cover the entire area where the essence of a certain intruding being was stopping time, as well as the essence that was snaking towards the special item atop the ancient pedestal!","CRACK!","A ludicrous scene played itself thereafter as in the grey world of stopped time, sparks of fire erupted as they went on to actually shatter this frozen space, the energy from this stupendous ability that the Draconic Fire Behemoth had cast going on to wrap around the energy going towards the ancient pedestal even faster as this energy was dispersed, whatever ability being directed towards the special treasure being cancelled right away!","Shocking!","Majestic!","Powerful!","Time flowed freely again as the air vibrated with power, the enormous body of the Behemoth beginning to rise as its gaze filled with an aura of regality and strength locked towards a particular intruder. The ability that the Draconic Fire Behemoth had cast was still in the surroundings, wrapping up everything this fearsome dragon could see, and that included the intruder.","As a being extremely proficient in one of the Universal Laws, as a powerful Dragon born in the Celestial Realm...this was its Authority!","Its gaze continued to lock towards the individual that had tried to get his filthy hands on something that had been with it since it was born, watching this being arrogantly as its power only continued to climb higher. Its mystical senses that could discern even the movement of essence and cancel already cast skills wrapped around this being as a surprised look appeared on its fearsome face, a voice of immense power ringing out in the wide lava filled cavern.","\"You were actually able to withstand my Authority, little worm?\"","Its voice reverberated across the space as vibration spread across the lava below him, his enormous body moving directly in front of the ancient pedestal as it obscured its gaze completely and stared towards the trembling being.","The creature that had intruded became more clear in his eyes, the outline of a small being barely an inch long zooming and expanding in his eyesight. The intruder wore a unique set of armor that let out a fiery aura that seemed to be protecting him, his body and limbs being completely wrapped around this set of armor as they were protected fully from his expanded Authority that had even burnt away mana!","The only thing that was showing injuries on the intruder’s body was the devilishly handsome face that did not have this armor wrapping around it, burn marks that were rapidly appearing and disappearing apparent on the face as the energy surrounding him burnt his face, but he was healing the injuries just as fast.","\"Curiouser and curiouser.\"","The rumbling voice of the Draconic Fire Behemoth rang out again as it saw the being in front of its sight, the body of this being rapidly enlarging as he became around two meters in size.","In his right hand, a fearsome Glaive appeared as it rotated around his body and dispersed the fearsome strength {{Flame Lord’s Authority}} slightly, reducing the constant damage it dealt to the one part of his body that wasn’t covered by the unique armor as his face began healing completely.","The boots this being wore shone a brilliant red l.u.s.ter as they stood on the flowing lava with ease, the extreme heat seemingly giving this intruder only a little trouble as his gaze also locked on the enormous Draconic Fire Behemoth that overshadowed his sight.","Both had red eyes shining resplendently, one more beastial than the other as a man and dragon locked gazes!"]},{"number":385,"title":"Chapter 385: Chapter 384 - Spamming Skills","paragraphs":["Noah’s gaze looked with the monstrous Behemoth in front of him as he thought about this Celestial Beast’s ludicrous level of power.","The overpowering essence it let out still confirmed with him that it was a beast half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm, but its power, even while putting its the crazy strength Behemoths usually showed, was still crazy!","The reason for this was because of this concept that the Draconic Fire Behemoth had mentioned...the concept called Authority!","Noah’s heart trembled as he thought back to the frozen time that he never thought could possibly be broken. This went out of the bounds of his knowledge as he had cast the ability of the Dagger of Time and moved speedily, casting [Emperor of Greed] thereafter. But this was when the ridiculous power of this Draconic Behemoth put itself on display!","The Ancient Blood Clone in this frozen time was actually able to hear the calm release of three words that reverberated throughout the wide underground cavern.","{{Flame Lord’s Authority}}.","The words were calm and light, but the effect they caused was horrendous as they directly went on to shatter the essence that created stopped time, and it even went further to destabilize and cancel [Emperor of Greed] that was heading towards the Ancient Pedestal!","This was an entirely new concept to Noah, but he had just seen the type of strength that a truly high level being could portray, the strength that somehow allowed them to shatter formed skills and disrupt the casting of abilities.","After the monstrous Draconic Fire Behemoth uttered these three words, it stood in front of the treasure as its gaze locked onto him, its message being loud and clear- you will not be able to run.","The utterance of {{Flame Lord’s Authority}} had spread out some kind of a blazing flame domain that caused huge damage for anyone in it, the clone being able to survive it fairly well because of the numerous compounded Enhanced Flame Element Resistance that came with the items of the Incandescent Flameborn Set.","Only his head that did not have a helmet was undergoing the process of burning and healing constantly until he took out the Glaive of Simmering Ember and reduced the damage caused even further, bringing him to this point in time where the brilliantly shining red eyes of the Draconic Fire Behemoth. A smile of immense arrogance seemed to spread on the lips of the fearsome beast as it spoke out again.","\"I can see that you have not yet gained an Authority, so you being able to withstand mine is quite a feat.\"","The Behemoth glanced at Noah closely as it continued.","\"Is it the items you are wearing? Or some innate ability? Hmm...\"","The Draconic Fire Behemoth did not seem to have an ounce of worry about Noah, continuing on nonchalantly as it wanted to sate its curiosity, and that was it.","\"Well, no matter. For the crime of intruding into my layer, for the crime of setting your eyes on something that is not yours...how would you like to die, little worm?\"","RUMBLE!","Strong words resounded throughout the underground Cavern as Noah felt the fantastical {{Flame Lord’s Authority}} recede, the Draconic Fire Behemoth letting out words that already condemned him to death as the only option!","He sighed again as his heart shook with slight excitement, knowing he would have to go with the second plan where he would actually have to match this monstrous being, and actually come out on top.","As his armored body covered in the {Incandescent Flameborn Set} floated atop the boiling lava smoothly, his strong heart actually began feeling a sense of thrill as he stared at this enormous Celestial Beast!","It was a dangerous situation where nobody knew what the results would be, but Noah was actually finding himself getting strong feelings of excitement whenever he was in situations like these. It was something terrifying and out of his wildest dreams that someone like him could be standing face to face with a Celestial Beast, an Elite Behemoth half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm, and he could actually stand against it with some level of confidence.","This was the adventure he longed to have! This was the strength he wanted to achieve! To be able to look at something this powerful and still believe there was a way for him to trump over it!","A bright smile covered the devilishly handsome face of the Ancient Blood Clone as he replied to the fiery Behemoth while casting numerous skills.","\"I will not be dying here today...little dragon.\"","His words held a tinge of excitement over this unavoidable battle as above the molten and simmering earth around him, the aura of death appeared in the skies, the figure of [Arch Lich Ra’Zan] beginning to shoot down towards the lava as its body shone, an enormous Bone Dragon appearing below it as it flapped its wings and allowed the powerful Lich to remain in the air.","In the Celestial Realm, flying was restricted until one broke through to the Domain Expansion Realm, but winged beings could still fly nonetheless!","[Arch Lich Ra’Zan] looked at the monstrous opponent its Master had as golden flames blazed from its sockets and the skull staff it held, the essence of death spreading out in the surroundings as huge runic circles appeared in the skies.","These runic circles signified the casting of [Abyssal Summoner], the ability that called forth enormous Abyssal Undead to fight for the Arch Lich.","This wasn’t all though, as Noah uttered multiple skills without reservation while his gaze continued to lock with the Draconic Fire Behemoth.","[Empyrean Guards]. [Empyrean Armament]. [Blood World]. [Dawn of the Blood Lord]. [Ancient Blood Scion]. [Summon the Ancients]...[Lesser Cthulhu].","RUMBLE!","The atmosphere quaked as an enormous amount of mana was used wantonly, the numerous number of wide area buff, strengthening, and transformation abilities forming with a gorgeous array of colors in the expansive Cavern below a volcanic mountain in the Celestial Realm!","Yet at this moment in time, a single Dragon remained calm as its voice reverberated out.","\"What did you just call me?\"","The nonchalant tone of the large Draconic Fire Behemoth had changed as it ignored the fantastical essence and splendor of skills and transformations that Noah was undergoing as it asked a simple question.","Noah’s resplendent but still transforming figure that still seemed smaller than the 70 meter Dragon held a devilish smile as he taunted out a reply the numerous skills he cast coming to life around him gloriously!","\"A little dragon. You know, those small little lizards you can find scurrying in crevic-\"","BOOOOOOOOM!!!","The very air itself shattered as a wrathful Dragon’s Roar resounded, the start of a monstrous battle going underway!"]},{"number":386,"title":"Chapter 386: Chapter 385 - A Lich! Ancients! Cthulhu!","paragraphs":["In the expansive underground space bubbling with extreme heat, a storm of essence was ravaging all around as numerous skills were manifesting in a grand fashion!","The most ill.u.s.trious one was a dark bubble of blood that continued to expand around the wide underground cavern for miles, covering almost every inch of it as the function of hiding whatever was happening in this cave hidden from prying eyes.","[Dawn of the Blood Lord] was the next most eye-catching one, a foreboding miniature moon appearing at the highest point of the cavern as it began releasing a dominating red light that gave numerous buffs to the caster while giving debuffs to the opponent!","But the two skills that caused the most pressure were the transformation abilities that allowed the clone to take on the form of something monstrous. The first transformation was something obtained from the upgrade of [Blood Lord] and opening the path to the [Kin of the Ancients] skill tree, it was [Ancient Blood Scion].","<strong>[Ancient Blood Scion] (5/5):: Take on the form of the scion of blood and rain down destruction on those that oppose you. This form allows you to heal 30% of all damage dealt and received, increase Physical and Elemental Damage by 100%, as well as enhance all the abilities of [Blood Lord] by 30%.</strong>","A transformation that allowed for the passive healing from 30% of the damage he received, as well as the damage he dealt! This wasn’t to even mention the boosts to all the other abilities of the [Blood Lord].","The form caused the clone to rise to the level of a giant, regal red vampyric wings erupting from his back as a gorgeous set of silver hair overflowed, his face taking the features of a humanoid bat as he rose above 10 meters.","Yet...above that and going overboard, [Lesser Cthulhu] was cast as another transformation ensued, the baleful destructive power of Aether covering the clone’s body as the size continued to increase, another set of wings erupting out as tentacles and feelers accompanied numerous grotesque eyes, the look of a terrifying creature with four wings, multiple pairs of eyes with differing colors, as well as overflowing shimmering silver hair came to life.","Yet again, this wasn’t enough! On top of this, numerous [Empyrean Guards] became streaks of light as they went on to change into a regal golden robe that attached itself to the grotesque figure, an enormous sword and shield appearing on its huge hands as palpated with the power of the Law of Fate! In front of the eyes of the DRaconic Fire Behemoth, a grotesque creature made from multiple transformations layered with a ridiculous number of skills made its appearance.","But once more, this didn’t seem like enough so another skill was cast, this time a summoning ability that called forth beings that Noah did not fully understand yet!","<strong>[Summon the Ancients] :: Your call travels through space and time as you call forth the Ancients that are bound by blood. Limit: 3 Ancients</strong>","RUMBLE!","A unique runic sigil spread out in the surroundings as the maddened dragon felt an air of ancientness permeate the surrounding space, a grey light shining through as it covered the appearance of unique beings that very few had the chance to see in the Light Expanse.","SHAA!","Three beings appeared around the still transforming clone, the only thing that one could use to describe them being one word- enormous!","Their sizes overshadowed the transformed Noah, and actually neared the huge size of the Draconic Fire Behemoth! Their bodies looked grey and stoic, adopting a humanoid form as they were garbed in old grey robes. From their back, a shining pair of dark wings folded beautifully as they granted these beings a unique outline Noah had not come across before.","The Ancients were actually humanoid in shape, and they held powering wings behind them! Their eyes were fully white as they eerily turned towards Noah the moment they were summoned, these white eyes scanning the figure of the clone up and down as they actually paid it no heed, their gazes actually turning in a completely unexpected direction of the cavernous underground space, peering through the cast [Blood World] and the layers of earth as they were directed towards the direction of the Sanctum.","Noah’s real body that was moving with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team became shocked as his gaze turned, and he felt the eyes of the three Ancients standing beside his clone below the volcanic mountain were staring straight at him!","[--------]","They scanned Noah’s real body up and down with gazes that traveled far, Noah hearing some form of static voices in his mind as he could make nothing of it. After a few seconds, their gazes left his real body and began turning their blank faces away from the direction of the Sanctum as Athena looked at the surprised Noah.","\"Everything okay, Junior Brother?\"","\"Ah, yes. I spaced out there for a second. Let’s catch up with the others.\"","Noah’s real body continued his movements with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team as his heart shook, the beings called Ancients still being something he did not fully understand!","In the underground space, the enraged Dragon finally adopted a careful expression at the appearance of these three unique beings that were letting out an air of desolation, their eerie blank faces and white eyes now turning to look towards it.","As the Draconic Fire Behemoth finally took the enemy in front of it like a possible threat, the Arch Lich Ra’Zan finished casting his necromantic spells as he summoned two Abyssal Death Knights, two Abyssal Jiangshi, and two Abyssal Revenants.","An energy of death spread in the surroundings as shockingly, an entire army had appeared around the Ancient Blood Clone in less than a minute, the levels of power of each of the beings summoned standing powerfully at the Soul Forging Realm, with some of them even letting out unique desolate auras that made one do a double take!","The enraged Draconic Fire Behemoth looked at all of this as its gaze ignored every single one of the newly summoned beings and locked on Noah again.","\"Ugly little worm. You come to my abode, try to steal from me, then you insult me, and now after summoning these creatures...you still think you are leaving from here alive?\"","The voice of the enraged dragon rang out as Noah looked towards its apathetically, only his rapidly beating heart showing the excitement he felt as he pointed the golden sword he held forward, initiating the start of a wild battle as the forces he summoned began to move forward!","ROAAAAAR!!!","The roar of the dragon was the only response as storms of flames began to permeate through the air, the monstrous Behemoth finally moving to attack!"]},{"number":387,"title":"Chapter 387: Chapter 386 - Grandiosity","paragraphs":["A world shaking battle was taking place below a nondescript volcanic mountain that nobody was privy to!","A world of blood had expanded all around to hide anything that was happening within, while in the underground space of this mountain where the fight was taking place, a red moon hung at the highest point!","At this moment, the Draconic Fire Behemoth roared out as the very air trembled, its eyes shining as flames coagulated in front of it.","[Immolation Pillars].","RUMBLE!","A barely discernible whisper was heard. But this whisper was the command of something terrible as tens of blazing fiery pillars of flames appeared without reservation around the Dragon, each one heading towards the clone and the summoned forces.","SHAA! SHAA!","They streaked towards them menacingly as Noah put the golden shield on his left hand out, withstanding the fiery attacks as they exploded in a shower of sparks and flames. The summoned Abyssal Undead that felt no pain were struck head on, numerous parts of their bodies being set aflame as they still continued forward valiantly, the Abyssal Revenant shining the dark coffin it was carrying towards the Dragon as it opened to release a viscous cloud of poison and death! The Abyssal Jiangshi carried the deathly pillars in their hands as they weaved their large bodies forward and threw the pillars like spears, chains being seen attached to these pillars that they could pull back whenever they wished!","The eerie Ancients that were summoned were the most spectacular, their white eyes shining as the pillars of flames snaking towards them simply dissipated as they neared.","Thereafter, their gazes locked on the enormous beast as their dark wings flapped, their figures disappearing into particles of light as they appeared near the Behemoth, clenching their fists as grey air wrapped around them and let out a strike towards the Dragon!","DING!","The sound of metal deformity rang out as shockingly, only a few dents appeared on the body of the Draconic Fire Behemoth. The even more shocking thing though, was that the indented portions of the Dragon’s skin actually began to decay as an eerie energy began to spread from their point of contact.","ROAR!","A wave of power released from the Draconic Fire Behemoth as it actually felt pain, using its high achievements in the Law of Fire to wrap around the weird energy trying to enter his body as his wrathful head glanced at the many beings ganging up on him.","\"Do you think you are the only one that can summon things to aid you, ugly worm?\"","A voice filled with wrath resounded as the body of the Draconic Fire Behemoth pulsed with power, another set of words being heard all around as the fire energy around them went berserk!","[Dragon Summoning]. [Rejuvenating Flames]. [Elemental Soul Reinforcement]...[Domain of Fire].","WAA! WAA! WAA!","The very space trembled as it squeezed in upon itself, the Draconic Fire Behemoth using its expansive mana to cast many skills!","All around it, the incorporeal forms of deadly dragons around half his size began to appear en masse, their reddened eyes locking on the many summoned beings around Noah as they began moving right away.","On the body of the Draconic Fire Behemoth, golden flames appeared as they healed the decaying strikes caused by the three Ancients, an even more mystical set of flames appearing deep inside its origin as they protected its Soul. This was because the Behemoth had seen a tinge of the Law of Fate around the enemy in front of it, and prepared to counteract it as well as protect itself.","The last thing cast by the Draconic Fire Behemoth was a domain...and this was a domain that only those in the Domain Expansion Realm, or those half a step into it like this Behemoth, could actually utilize!","OOOONG","An air of majesty spread out as the domain of the Draconic Fire Behemoth went on to expand just as wide as the Blood World, covering everything within it as it heavily bolstered the strength of the Behemoth and the numerous dragons it summoned, while Noah and his forces felt a heavy weight placed on their shoulders as if the very air around them had become viscuous and hard to move in!","ROAR!","A resounding roar was released yet again as fiery attacks flew, the many summoned dragons finding their targets as the Abyssal Undead began fights of their own, the Arch Lich Ra’Zan waving its golden staff as more and more Bone Dragons, Undead Phoenixes, and Specters came to life.","The mystical Ancients floated in the air as they sensed the heavy pressure of the domain, their blank white eyes shining as they pointed towards Noah and his forces.","[-----]","A blank set of sounds appeared in Noah’s mind once more as he noticed a change on his body, the three Ancients initiating a skill that caused for a shimmering grey shield to appear on his body and the bodies of the numerous summons, the oppression they felt from the [Domain of Fire] gradually lessening as they actually began to feel their strength be bolstered!","The moment this finished, the three Ancients went back to duking out terrible attacks towards the Draconic Fire Behemoth and its summoned dragons, these mystical and yet eerie beings actually being the ones that were dealing the most damage in this battle so far.","Noah looked at these hard to understand beings called Ancients as he thirsted for more knowledge about them, the shimmering grey shield wrapping around his body causing him to feel weightless as he smiled and flapped his pairs of wings forward.","He felt the [Domain of Fire] that the Draconic Fire Behemoth had cast just now, finding the extreme difference between it and the first ability that the Dragon had used to actually break apart his time stop and even stop the activation of [Emperor of Greed]. The ability the Dragon had used, which he called a type of [Authority], was much stronger and was one of the bigger causes for worry as this battle continued!","Yet from all his observations as he spammed numerous skills and began cornering this powerful beast, this Authority was not used again, making him believe there were certain restrictions to such a fearsome power that could even go as far as canceling enemy skills. He would confirm his thoughts later after this battle finished though, for now, he had to focus.","He placed the Glaive of Simmering Ember behind him as he carried the golden blade and shield from the abilities of [Fate’s Guardian], his sword tip pointing towards the many incorporeal dragons summoned in the surrounding as he called out vibrantly.","[Portals of Terror]. [Sever]!","RUMBLE!","ZING!","Numerous dangerously colored portals began to appear on the sides of the Draconic Fire Behemoth as they trembled to release destructive energies, the cast [Sever] going on to bisect the incorporeal dragons as a few were cut in half!","\"Haha, come on!\"","Noah couldn’t help but call out as the thrilling battle continued!"]},{"number":388,"title":"Chapter 388: Chapter 387 - A Budding Economy","paragraphs":["As a spectacular battle took place in the underground cavern of a volcanic mountain, elsewhere in the Celestial Realm, wild adventures of numerous Exploration Teams continued!","Tens of thousands of Void Ranked beings continued to pour into the Celestial Realm, with a few hundred at the Soul Realm making their entrance as well as more and more hunting teams to take down Behemoths and explore the wonders of the Celestial Realm were formed.","The Celestials were the biggest winners as always and as planned, watching as many beings perished while others learned from their mistakes, and ultimately create a smooth process where they received the resources of numerous materials from the bodies of Behemoths, and even further increased their exploration of the Celestial Realm. The benefits were slowly opening up as a bright future showed itself in front of their eyes.","The more powerful forces of some Prime Worlds guessed the intentions of the Celestials, but the rewards were simply too enticing so they went along with it!","This was because they found out the immense uses of the bodies of Behemoths that were drenched in universal laws, finding that the consumption of these beasts would rapidly propel their own comprehension and increase their power, not to mention that swallowing their Origin Cores where most of the universal laws were condensed gave one years worth of comprehension in that Law!","This made for a very competitive atmosphere as many beings formed powerful teams to gain access to even more resources. On this particular day, the newly formed Order of Blood was conducting its first hunt, the Royal Vampyre Elena at the lead as they faced a powerful Ice Behemoth.","This particular Behemoth had huge tusks that made it seem like an oversized Mammoth, its large amount of fur acting like a thick coat in the freezing and snowy region of the Celestial Realm. Numerous spears of ice continued to form and shoot out from its body every second as it faced its enemies!","The curvaceous body of the Royal Vampyre twisted as her hands flew forward, initiating a sea of blood that formed into powerful lances that smashed towards the Behemoth and kept its attention. This powerful Royal Vampyre was actually acting as the tank while the Emperor Penguin and others adorned with weapons pulsating with the fire element released their attacks towards the Behemoth.","ROAR!","The Behemoth roared out as Elena sent a telepathic message to the others.","\"Ready?!\"","Focused looks appeared on the other Vampyres in the surroundings, the Emperor Penguin stretching its flippers as it replied and nodded, the Calamities of the Sea and other Harbingers that were not staying and training in the Time Space of the Spiritual Land ascertaining as they carried out a plan they discussed beforehand.","The body of the Emperor Penguin teleported as it disappeared and reappeared far into the skies, feeling the strong gravitational pressure begin to pull its body downwards already as it did not have the capabilities to fly in this Celestial Realm like many others. Its goal was something else though, as its beady eyes locked in on the Ice Behemoth still letting out wild attacks towards its teammates, a shimmering silver light appearing over it’s body as it cast a particular skill it unlocked from its skill tree!","[Spatial Displacement]!","RUMBLE!","A shining silver light flashed in the skies as the body of the Emperor Penguin disappeared, the even more shocking thing being the mountainous body of the Ice Behemoth disappearing as well, their positions actually switching as the huge Celestial Beast found its body high in the skies and dropping towards the ground at an extremely fast rate!","\"Attack!\"","Elena’s valiant scream rang out as the group below released colorful bouts of mana with their own skills towards the mountainous beat falling from the skies, the job of the Emperor Penguin not done as it waved its flipped once more, the silver light it released going on to cover the bodies of the Calamities of the Sea and the Imperial Phoenix as their bodies appeared even higher in the skies above the Ice Behemoth, their attacks also ready as they released them in a splendor of colors.","Attacks from above, attacks from below, and all while disorientingly falling from the skies!","ROAAR!","The Ice Behemoth let out another roar as the many attacks pierced its thick hide, its mountainous body acting against it as it smashed towards the ground at a horrible speed.","BOOM! CRUNCH!","The breaking of bones could be heard as the many skills lowered its defenses and pierced its skin, the fall damage going on to disorient it even more as the beings from the Order of Blood released even more attacks, not giving the beast even a chance to retaliate as they successfully went on to hunt their first Behemoth!","Scenes like these continued to spread out over the Celestial Realm, whereas in another location, the Righteous Fire Exploration Team was finishing hunting yet another Fire Behemoth, Athena’s potent Blades of Liberation striking down from the skies and ending the life of the mountainous beast.","\"Haha, I never knew your abilities were this unique, being able to read the flow of battle like it is nothing!\"","Boru’s boisterous voice rang out as he looked towards Athena in admiration. The past few fights, Athena’s unique ability shone as she actually began to conduct the pace of the battles, directing the teammates on how to move and expecting where the enemy would strike even before it did!","This led to a shift in the paradigm where Boru was not the only major contributor in the team, Athena coming in close as their fights became easier and easier.","\"With you two, maybe hunting an Elite Behemoth would be a possibility.\"","Boru’s eyes shone as he said this, looking forward into the future as he gained the spectacular ability from Athena that allowed for his team to move even faster, and the addition of Crixus that released a unique attack from [Fate’s Guardian] that even they weren’t aware could be utilized to that extent, causing enormous Soul Damage to the Behemoths and taking them down even faster.","\"Bah, an Elite Behemoth? Don’t even joke. Maybe once one of us breaks into the Domain Expansion Realm...\"","One of Boru’s teammates replied while divvying up the body of the dead Behemoth, Noah smiling as he waved his hands and accepted a material that would create the last piece of the Incandescent Flameborn Set while enjoying the words of the Celestial around him.","Little did they know, his clone was trying to take down an Elite Behemoth right now!"]},{"number":389,"title":"Chapter 389: Chapter 388 - Ancients Lead the Way, An Elite Behemoths Fall","paragraphs":["Five Hours.","This was the amount of time that had passed in the underground space of the blazing volcanic mountain as a ferocious battle was underway!","The Draconic Fire Behemoth still had an air of regality, but its body held numerous deep gashes and decaying muscles that were caused from the eerie energy being released from the three summoned Ancients.","Numerous incorporeal summoned dragons roamed the surroundings as they supported the Behemoth, but the Arch Lich Ra’Zan summoned even more undead to combat them, every time that an Abyssal Jiangshi or Revenant Fell, another one taking its place soon after.","Truth be told, the power of this Draconic Fire Behemoth was simply too powerful at this stage, its body not being able to be pierced easily by many attacks. Even with Noah overlaying the abilities that relied on the law of fate, he could only deal a small amount of damage that was healed by the monstrous life force of the Dragon soon after!","So the pathway that led to victory for him was to simply...protect himself while wearing down the energy of this monstrous beast!","The body of the Ancient Blood Clone continued to stay far in the distance, the transformed combination of [Lesser Cthulhu] and [Ancient Blood Scion] releasing powerful attacks as [Portals of Terror] and horrible strikes of Aether erupted here and there.","Even while staying at a far distance, the clone received enormous amounts of damage from the Draconic Fire Behemoth, to the extent that his wings were burnt off numerous times and lances of fire dismembered his limbs, but they all healed rapidly under the abilities of [Ancient Blood Scion] that allowed for him to heal from 30% of the damage he dealt and received, as well as the passive life steal he had from the abilities of the Vampyre Progenitor Bloodline! He simply became an undying c.o.c.kroach as he ridiculously withstood all of the powerful attacks and continued forward.","On the front lines was the Arch Lich that directed the undead, acting as cannon fodders as they continued to wear down the strength of the Draconic Fire Behemoth.","But the ones leading the charge and actually piercing through the thick scales of the Dragon and dealing the most damage so far were the Ancients!","These mystical beings flapped their dark wings and they teleported across the field of battle, their bodies acting like their own weapons as they released sharp lights whenever they struck the Dragon, leaving behind a powerful energy that caused the inflicted portions to actually decay!","If it wasn’t for the fantastical life force of the Draconic Fire Behemoth, as well as the [Rejuvenating Flames] that wrapped around his body and continued to heal him passively, the mountainous body would have long succ.u.mbed to the injuries.","So the battle of attrition continued, but this was the biggest mistake that the Behemoth could have made, because the enemy it faced was the worst to fight a battle of attrition with!","As the fight continued, Noah’s main body got a hold of yet another large portion of the body of a Behemoth, these materials directly being placed in the [Expansive Space] as a thoughtful expression covered his eyes.","He glanced at the pace of the battle as he gave a few commands to the summoned creatures, his body shrinking in size rapidly as he teleported away from the cavernous area and caused the Draconic Fire Behemoth to become even more vigilant as it guarded its surroundings while parrying off the many attacks still coming towards it.","But Noah’s teleportation target was the Spiritual Land as he appeared in the Blacksmith’s Forge, showing the most possible disrespect in a battle as he left midway to forge the last piece of the Incandescent Flameborn Set!","The enormous body part of the Behemoth defeated by the Righteous Fire Exploration Team was cut into pieces and swiftly absorbed by the Hearth, a few minutes passing before a resplendent fiery helm shot out of the shimmering Hearth.","<strong>[Crown of the Simmering Ember] :: An item created from the wrathful body of a Behemoth. +50% Enhanced Damage of All Fire Attribute Skills, +25% Fire Element Resistance, +25% Increased All Element Resistance.</strong>","The last piece of the Incandescent Flame Set appeared before him, the clone equipping it right away as it went on to wrap around the head of the grotesque transformation he still had.","A wide smile was now covered beneath the helmet as the excitement from getting to try the huge boosts given from the Incandescent Flameborn Set filled his heart! Even though the enemy this time was of the Fire Element and they held tremendously powerful defense against attacks from that element, the boosts given by wearing the complete set were simply too monstrous!","<strong>{Incandescent Flameborn Set} :: An Item Set that only an experienced hunter of Behemoths can adorn. 2 Set Item Bonus- An Ember Phoenix accompanies your side as they attack your enemies with fiery attacks. Ember Phoenixes are spiritual beings that can be summoned again as soon as they perish. 4 Set Item Bonus- When dealing damage with the Fire Element, enemies will take 500% extra damage over 5 seconds as the Burning Effect is applied on their bodies. The damage dealt by the user will also be increased by 50% and the damage taken is reduced by 3% for every Flameborn Item they have equipped. 6 Set Item Bonus- A Blazing Ring of Fire passively and constantly erupts with you at the center, applying the Soul Immolation Effect to your enemies. Enemies under the Soul Immolation Effect take 1000% more damage from abilities of the Fire Element.</strong>","He glanced at the description of the completed set boost as he reappeared right above the fiery Draconic Behemoth that always had its guard up for him, its wide jaws shooting up as they attempted to swallow the controller of these horrible summons right away!","Yet the only thing that met the wide open jaws of this dragon was the eruption of a blazing ring of fire!","SHAA! SHAA! SHAA!","Like the sound of waves crashing into the shore, a molten ring of flames erupted from the clone’s body once, and again, and again!","This ridiculous ability smashed into the Dragon right in the face as it looked incredulously towards this being that was actually using attacks in the law it was proficient in, and these attacks were actually causing it a great deal of pain!","\"What the fu-\"","SHAA! SHAA!","A blazing ring of fire continued to be released as soon enough, the strong soul of the dragon actually began feeling a burning sensation, an unbelievable reality opening itself up in the underground cave as the Behemoth that had been worn down for 5 hours finally had its defenses pierced through the moment the Soul Immolation effect was applied to it.","Even though it was a Fire Behemoth, even though it was extremely proficient in the Law of Fire, its worn defenses actually began taking great damage from the flame attacks released from its enemy!","It was ludicrous, nonsensical, and did not follow the natural course of actions! But because of the 1000% boost in damage achieved from the Soul Immolation effect that could only come by from the completed Incandescent Flameborn Set and its other monstrous boosts, abilities that relied on the flame element actually damaged a being extremely proficient in the law of fire!","\"Monster.\"","The regality of a dragon remained as the Draconic Fire Behemoth felt its strong soul actually burning, something it never thought to be possible occurring as even more attacks smashed into it from the mystical summoned Ancients and Abyssal Undead. Its Authority could not be used any longer, the damage to its soul and body actually increasing as time passed.","Swarmed on all sides, its air of a ruler stood strong as it knew that unbelievably, it would be facing its death today!"]},{"number":390,"title":"Chapter 390: Chapter 389 - Loot from an Elite Behemoth!","paragraphs":["Destructive portals surrounded it on all sides, terrible winged beings nearing its size let out mystical attacks that left a unique energy that caused the decay of the essence protecting its body, and the tireless and fearless Abyssal Undead that continued to be brought to life the moment another one died.","It was an extremely tiring and helpless battle for one to go through, especially so for someone as powerful as a being nearing the full title of an Elite Behemoth, just needing a few more years to advance before fully stepping into the Domain Expansion Realm!","Alas, fate would not have it so as the Draconic Fire Behemoth could feel its origin trembling, knowing it had overused all of its immense mana as its prideful aura of a ruling race shook when looking at the being that apparently beat it in terms of mana capacity.","\"Truly a monster.\"","The Dragon shook its head in exhaustion as a brilliant light began to burn from it, the fearsome being actually choosing to burn its own soul and face death by its own accord!","Noah observed this change as he sent numerous commands to his summoned forces, his own body that continued to release immense heat waves from the effect of completed Incandescent Flameborn Set nearing the burning body of the Draconic Fire Behemoth.","The bright heat the beast released seemed like hot blasts of wind towards the clone protected by the shimmering item set, its body fearlessly coming close to the Draconic Fire Behemoth as yet another ability of the Seven Deadly Sins was cast!","This time, it was coming from the Sin of Gluttony, it was the ability that allowed his to absorb entities and working in conjunction with another skill, it also allowed him to look at the entity’s entire life history and abilities, allowing him to choose two skills in addition to the ones he normally received as loot. The first skill was [Devouring], the latter was [Large Stomach]!","[Devouring]!","WAA!","A dark cloud released from the clone as it went on to cover the enormous head of the blazing Behemoth, the dark cloud expanding rapidly as it went on to cover the entirety of the humungous body as a large amount of essence began to senselessly leak out from the clone and into the ability.","What he was doing now was casting the [Devouring] ability on a live being, and it was an Elite Behemoth at that! It wasn’t a hunt of dead meat that could swiftly be taken, but a being that had their body blazing in flames as it tried to nobly take its own life!","The gluttonous quality of the skills fully wrapped around the body of the drained and heavily injured beast, its unique energies going on to stop the self destruction as the dark cloud that had wrapped around the large Celestial Beast began to reduce in size gradually.","From the more than fifty meters, it became thirty, then ten, five, until finally, the darkness surrounding the Draconic Fire Behemoth disappeared completely, taking along with it a monstrous beast that was already getting dissected and analyzing in the [Large Stomach]! From the position where the huge beast used to be, a brilliant golden light shone as a few skill books, cores, and a shining round item also floated in the skies as the clone waved his hand and quickly placed them in the [Expansive Space].","The enormous body of this beast, its materials, everything that it had...all of it was devoured as Noah favored the knowledge of this particular beast more than anything else at this moment.","As he breathed heavily at the finished battle that had taken hours and too much mental stress, he deactivated [Ancient Blood Scion] and [Lesser Cthulhu], as well as the wide area buffing skills like [Descent of the Blood Lord] as the only thing he left behind was the [Blood World] that kept everything occurring in this underground space a secret.","He turned his eyes towards the three summoned Ancients that had been the major cause of this battle going smoothly, finding that their blank white eyes were turned towards him as they seemed to be scanning him up and down, nodding their heads as a scratch nonunderstable voice was released in his mind again.","[-----]","The forefront Ancient seemed to be speaking as no communication came across, nodding his head towards the clone in affirmation thereafter as these summoned beings actually began to disappear into particles in front of the clone’s eyes, somehow having the power to desummon themselves as they wished!","Noah looked at this as he mentally shook his mind in frustration, one of the messages he was sending towards the summoned Ancients seeming to go through as the mystery surrounding them increased. He put this aside for now as he began looking at the boon from the defeat of a Dragon of immense stature.","Between Noah’s real body and his clone, he was currently giving over half of his mental processes over to the clone as it speedily began going through the memories of the fearsome Draconic Fire Behemoth, as well as the loot that had erupted from it.","Of the Skill Books that came out, two were at the Soul Rank, and one was at the Soul+ Rank, with no such luck in easily gaining a skill of the Domain Rank!","The other was an abundant amount of cores that in addition to the few that Noah already had from the massacre in the Magus World as well as the divided Origins from the Fire Behemoths that the Righteous Fire Exploration Team continued to defeat, he would have more than enough to propel himself from the Void Rank and into the Soul Rank, all the while having more than enough cores for the refinement of items.","As a large number of memories of the Draconic Fire Behemoth continued to be sorted, the clone took out the other loot that had erupted out in an aurora of light when the beast was defeated. This particular one was something unique that Noah had not come across from defeating an opponent before, finding himself quizzically looking over the scintillating red gold ovular item that was nearly as tall as he was.","His confusion was cleared up soon after as a resplendent set of blue words appeared in front of his eyes, the description of the item becoming clear as he gained something new for the first time ever with the defeat of an opponent.","<strong>[Origin Core- Behemoth Zygote] :: An incubating Origin that will eventually give rise to a pet that the user can bind to themselves. Caution is required as the position of pet and master can change if there is a large gap in Origin strength. Incubating time varies depending on location and amount of essence available.</strong>","...!"]},{"number":391,"title":"Chapter 391: Chapter 390 - The First Treasure from the Celestial Realm","paragraphs":["Noah’s clone was staring blankly at the set of words that described something out of his wildest dreams!","<strong>[Origin Core- Behemoth Zygote] :: An incubating Origin that will eventually give rise to a pet that the user can bind to themselves. Caution is required as the position of pet and master can change if there is a large gap in Origin strength. Incubating time varies depending on location and amount of essence available.</strong>","Aside from the numerous Cores and Skill Books, the other thing to come out of the loot from the Draconic Fire Behemoth was an incubating egg that would actually gift him a Behemoth!","This was something unique that Noah was coming across for the first time, sending a message to the Planetary System as a reply was quickly sent back.","[The Celestial Beasts have extremely potent Origin Cores that are fused with their souls, making it capable to extract their origin and reproduce it into this form of being.]","Shocking words were transferred into Noah’s mind as something huge was said so simply, nodding as he looked at the Incubation Time for this huge egg to pop. The time varied by location and the amount of essence, so he would see if it was possible to achieve some results today. His thoughts transferred from the loot as he now placed his attention towards the memories of the devoured behemoth that were slowly made clear, the hundreds of years worth of this monstrous being’s life playing themselves out rapidly in his mind as he sat down on the back of an Abyssal Revenant to absorb all the information.","The life of this Celestial Beast was extremely unique, its first memories beginning while it was still in an egg when it first came to be in this same volcanic mountain! It very rarely left this home it found itself in, but it did move around over the last hundreds of years, which granted Noah a large amount of information on some of the nearby geography.","But the thing that made the Draconic Fire Behemoth stay in this volcanic mountain and continue to guard it all this time...was the resplendent red crystal that was attached atop the mystical ancient pedestal.","The eyes of the clone opened briefly as he looked at this pedestal not too far away from him that he could grab as the victor of the last battle, but he held himself back as he carefully perused through the memories to learn everything he could first.","Shockingly, the treasure in front of Noah’s eyes was actually some type of Inheritance, something that very few beings would manage to come across in the Celestial Realm, but these Inheritances were some of the most valuable treasures!","It was this particular Inheritance that the Draconic Fire Behemoth found himself with since it was born that allowed it to reach the heights it had in the Law of Fire. When the memories came to this point in time, Noah finally got the bits of information that explained the unique {{Flame Lord’s Authority}} that the Dragon had managed to use to cancel out his Time Stop and the already cast [Emperor of Greed]. This ability that was called an authority...actually stemmed from achieving high comprehension in a particular Universal Law!","The Inheritance in this volcanic mountain had been an extremely powerful one from the Law of Fire, the staunch Behemoth choosing to practice it for hundreds of years as it advanced rapidly and got the strength that it had until today. To obtain this {{Authority}}, the Draconic Fire Behemoth had to actually advance and comprehend close to half of the Law of Fire.","This was something crazy to think about, as from the knowledge that Noah had gathered, very few beings in the Light Expanse were proficient enough to actually have comprehended even half of any laws. The only ones he could think of were the Celestials themselves, their power being boosted as they obtained a set of techniques in the Celestial Realm that taught them to be extremely proficient in the Law of Fate, with Noah still being unsure at the level they had reached after hundreds of years. But he did not doubt that there were many in this powerful organization that held some form of {{Authority}}!","Yet, this Inheritance in this volcanic mountain and the stern hard work of the smitten dragon that practiced it for years allowed this Behemoth to actually come close to attaining an {{Authority}} in the Law of Fire, which brought about the spectacular ability it used against Noah!","THUMP!","He could feel his heart beating faster as his gaze locked on to the glistening crystal atop the ancient pedestal, rising up from his position as he slowly pushed the newly flowing memories aside and neared this wondrous piece of treasure himself.","The ancient pedestal let off a mystical air of blistering flames as it was still standing calmly at the corner of the cavern, the crystal on top of it becoming larger and larger in Noah’s eyes as he neared.","His eyes felt a searing pain as he came closer upon it, tears almost falling out as he came within a meter of it, and then an inch of it as he reached out and laid his hands upon it!","RUMBLE!","A brilliant red light shot out as extreme calm returned in the surroundings, Noah opening his eyes as the Planetary System worked to decipher the treasure in front of him, a radiant description appearing in front of Noah’s eyes soon after.","<strong><<Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire. Includes techniques that allow one to inscribe the essence of fire into their bodies, as well as offensive and defensive techniques only those cultivating the Inheritance can use>></strong>","A set of beautiful words flowed in front of Noah’s eyes as his excitement shot off to extreme levels. In his hands, his first treasure from this mystical Celestial Realm was giving off a powerful light as he placed more of his essence into it, keen to know exactly what awaited him from this <<Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire>>!"]},{"number":392,"title":"Chapter 392: Chapter 391 - An Inheritance!","paragraphs":["<strong><Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire> :: Left behind to those fate intended, this inheritance grants the unique cultivation ability {Disciple of Fire}, as well as the Absolute Skill <<Herald of Flames>> that are meant to create the most powerful Incarnation of Flames.</strong>","The knowledge swiftly came into Noah’s mind as he hungrily looked at the abundant information stored in the crystal, the immense value of this treasure just now becoming clear in his mind!","The biggest value that could be gained from this <Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire> was not just its unique cultivation ability and the Absolute Skill, but the fact that this Inheritance was something that could be learned by others!","Similar to the treasure that the Celestials came across that they spread out to their disciples, Noah could bring his people into this area for them to gain this Inheritance themselves, or see if he could learn how to make Inheritance Crystals similar to what the Celestials were doing.","He had used his abundant essence to try and move this ancient pedestal from its spot as he began reading the information on this inheritance, but found that some sort of inviolable law was keeping it in place, where he could not even make it budge an inch! This would not be a problem though, as he would simply have to teleport his people here to have them experience this amazing boon as well.","His gaze went down towards the unique cultivation skill, {Disciple of Fire} first.","<strong>{Disciple of Fire} :: A technique geared towards cultivating the Law of Fire. Grants the user the ability to form a unique Fire Origin Core.</strong>","Only two sentences for the description of the skill, but he found it eerily similar to the {Fate’s Disciple} ability that cultivated the law of fate by inscribing Fate Lines on the body of the practitioner, but this {Disciple of Fire} instead allowed one to form a Fire Origin Core!","Noah put everything else aside as this unique skill that was extremely similar to the one dealing with the law of fate that he received from the Celestials took his central focus.","Far away from his position, the Righteous Fire Exploration Team had already returned after they finished hunting the last Fire Behemoth that also provided Noah with the last piece of the Incandescent Flameborn Set, with his main body going into the regal structures that served as the sleeping quarters of Celestials as he secluded himself.","A mini Blood World bloomed in the scintillating gold room that Noah was in as it covered him entirely, the knowledge about the unique skill {Disciple of Fire} filling his mind as he wanted to see how different it was to {Fate’s Disciple}!","RUMBLE!","It felt like an explosion was occurring inside his body the moment he activated {Disciple of Fire}, something new appearing deep inside him! At the position that could be considered the center of Noah’s body, there was an incorporeal blue colored core that held streaks of gold that was standing stably. This could be considered the center of his Origin, his Origin Core!","Besides this large Origin Core, a small dot that shone with a fiery red light began to come to life, not even being one hundredth the size of his Origin Core.","This could be referred to as the Fire Origin Core!","RUMBLE!","A storm of converging essence rushed into the room that Noah was staying in as the other Celestials in the exquisitely built structure noticed this wild convergence and looked forward while shaking their heads with smiles.","They knew this to be the dwelling of a new Celestial that was also a being with a Noble Fate!","They took this wild convergence of essence as a breakthrough that affected the surroundings of this being, choosing to be respectful and not even send their auras towards the dwelling.","Meanwhile, an enormous amount of essence continued to acc.u.mulate as Noah absorbed both the surrounding essence, as well as the reserves of the planets he was connected to and drove them all according to {Disciple of Fire} into this budding Fire Origin Core.","At the very center of his origin, besides the stably rotating blue core inlaid with a few golden stripes, the formation of an extremely small red core was completed as it was quickly wrapped up in a mantle of flames, a unique energy being released from it and into every single cell on Noah’s body as it began to rotate slowly, absorbing as much essence as it could with no reservation!","The unique energy that the Fire Origin Core released the moment it was fully formed went on to wrap around every cell it came across, having an arduous journey in front of it as there were trillions of cells to cover!","The process was slow, but Noah sent his awareness into his own body as he observed this unique energy being released from the Fire Origin Core begin to slowly strengthen the affected cells, each of them gaining a hint of the universal laws, this one being the Law of Fire!","RUMBLE!","It felt like his body was undergoing euphoria as his cells drank this unique energy being released from the Fire Origin Core with wild enthusiasm, Noah sensing his body gain yet another law, this one going on to boost him in a different way than even the Fate Lines that he continued to condense with {Fate’s Disciple}.","{Disciple of Fire} had nothing like fate lines, but it did create another Origin Core inside him that had begun to slowly rotate as it accepted the input of a large amount of essence and then released a unique energy that was passively going on to strengthen Noah’s body, the crazy effects only being able to be discovered with time.","The aura of fire began to slowly burn within him, his awareness closely monitoring this process as he asked himself- would this be similar to the cultivation of the Law of Fate where he could not condense a large number of Fate Lines continuously, or would this be something different?","Essence was continuing to be absorbed by the small Fire Origin Core that began slowly growing larger as seconds passed, showing no signs of stopping as it went on to release even more of its unique energy to bathe Noah’s body. So he wondered as this mystical scene played out inside of him, was there actually a limit?!"]},{"number":393,"title":"Chapter 393: Chapter 392 - Fire Origin Core, <>","paragraphs":["The small Flame Origin Core continued to spin as it absorbed mana and released a unique energy that continued to release an intense energy drenched in the Law of Fire, this essence continuing to delve throughout Noah’s body as he began to feel a constant feeling of increased strength.","His clone that was simply an extension of his limbs also had this energy wrap around him, the body of the clone actually having a more intense reaction in the underground cavern of the volcanic mountain as it brought Noah to the confirmation that he would be able to progress even faster in the environment filled with extreme temperatures and flames.","He continued to test whether there would be a limit to how much essence he could feed the Flame Origin Core as it continued to strengthen his body using the Law of Fire, his gaze turning to his stat panel as he noticed the addition of another law!","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(41%)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 23,486]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-1]","[Vitality: VOID]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: VOID]","[Law(s) : Water-11%, Space-8%, Fate-.23%, Fire-2%]","In the condest stat panel, Noah observed the addition of a section that listed Origin Cores, with the only one currently being listed being the Fire Origin Core that was placed at Stage 1!","There was no mention of his much larger Origin that shone with a blue l.u.s.ter slowly rotating at his very center, only this new Origin Core being given a stage as it continued to grow ever so larger and begin to drench Noah’s body in the Law of Fire more and more.","Different from the Fate Lines which he could activate and use the strength they provided to bring forth even larger amounts of physical and soul damage, the energy released from the Fire Origin Corewent on to directly enhance the strength of his body as he felt like his attacks would alway be even more explosive, taking with them a destructive power that would burn all those that stood against him.","Essence continued to pour into this Fire Origin Core as Noah continued to test the limits, because if there wasn’t any, then he did not see a problem in raising the Stage of this Fire Origin Core from 1 and all the way to 10, or whatever the maximum stage of such a core was!","But would the universal laws allow for such world shattering possibilities to come to life?","His question was answered soon as he felt his body become drenched in the law of fire more and more, wisps of flames appearing on his skin as they danced around him beautifully.","Beneath the volcanic mountain where his clone was surrounded by immense heat, his body was having an even greater reaction as it fully became wrapped in dark red flames, both the body of the clone and even his main one not feeling any pain as these flames felt very comfortable for them!","POP!","At this point, a metamorphosis seemed to occur with the Fire Origin Core as it instantly doubled in size, its presence even stronger as it changed from Stage 1 to Stage 2!","Noah also saw the Law of Fire slowly rise from 2% until it reached 10%!","In the span of a few minutes, he had ridiculously raised his comprehension of a law from nothing until it reached 10%! He was expectact to continue, but this was when the worries he had were affirmed as similar to when he first gathered Fate Lines, something stopped him from completely breaking the rules and just piercing through the stages!","The large amount of essence from the atmosphere and from the reserves of the many planets he was connected to simply stopped going into the now Stage 2 Fire Origin Core as began rotating peacefully, not even paying attention to the bountiful energy trying to get into it as it now slowly underwent a cycle of releasing the unique energies it was released before, and then slowly absorbing the essence around it at a rate that would be considered a turtle’s pace.","Similar to Fate Lines, he was stopped from rapidly shooting through the ranks of the Law of Fire, his thoughts now focusing on to what extent the effect of this new restriction was, and whether his thoughts of these restrictions being lesser than the supreme Law of Fate would be confirmed.","Noah sighed with a light smile as he finally hit the wall he was testing for, shaking his head as he observed the changes to his body. He felt a fiery and explosive strength in every single part of him, knowing that if he went hunting for Ice Behemoths in the future, he had the perfect skills and body to take them down with a much easier time than other behemoths.","When he thought about the skills that came with the inheritance, his gaze landed on the shining absolute skill called <<Herald of Flames>>, reading its descriptions as he tried to understand exactly what abilities it held.","<<Herald of Flames>> A technique coming from the inheritance of the Disciple of Fire that strives for the aspect of extreme in the Law of Fire. Abilities include Incarnation of Fire, Rejuvenating Flames, Elemental Soul Reinforcement, and Armageddon","[Incarnation of Fire] :: You continuously release flames from your body, dealing Fire Damage to all enemies in the proximity as any Fire Element skills are enhanced. The released flames can be manipulated to form varying shapes depending on the comprehension of the user. The Stage of the Fire Origin Core will determine the enhanced damage. Current Enhancement- +200%","[Rejuvenating Flames] :: Flames of rebirth and healing wrap around your body, granting you increased health and mana regeneration. The Stage of the Fire Origin Core will determine the enhanced regeneration. Current Regeneration- +200%","[Elemental Soul Reinforcement] :: A unique shield of flames rich in the elemental law of fire wraps around the soul of the user, granting increased protection from any sources of Soul Damage. The Stage of the Fire Origin Core will determine the enhanced reinforcement. Current Reinforcement- +200%","[Armageddon] :: The area within five miles of the user becomes a Consecrated Flame Ground that calls forth meteors from the skies, destroying all enemies standing on this Consecrated Flame Ground. The Stage of the Fire Origin Core will determine the damage. Current Damage- +200%","A beautiful set of words appeared in front of eyes, the descriptions of multiple new abilities that fell under a different system than the ones he usually came across opening itself up in front of him. Most terrifying of all was the name of the last ability that fell under <<Herald of Flames>>, and that was the ability coining the name [Armageddon]!"]},{"number":394,"title":"Chapter 394: Chapter 393 - Mysteries and Questions","paragraphs":["Noah continued to read through the percentages granted to the <<Herald of Flames>> absolute abilities as he realized that it was all affected by the Stage of the Fire Origin Core, watching as this shimmering red core slowly rotated at his very center while his body continued to pulse with power.","He thought back to all the recent events as he breathed out, choosing to continue moving forward as he got used to these new skills while also tending to the bountiful treasures he just received.","This brought into focus the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire that he could share with his people, the treasure being an inheritance that had a unique skill which allowed one to condense a Fire Origin Core, and an absolute skill that had crazy abilities contained within.","He smiled at the possibilities of the future as he used [Unique Origin] to conceal the strong hint of the Law of Fire on his body while the clone in the underground cavern of the volcanic mountain stretched its body that was now filled with abundant fiery essence and looked over at the ancient pedestal which held the huge Inheritance Crystal that could not be moved.","The Ancient Blood Clone reclaimed the Spiritual Land from the faraway location and brought it close to the blazing ground that had molten magma not too far away from it, the unique floating landmass standing stable against the extreme heat as he sent a few telepathic messages to his people.","Barbatos, Kazuhiko, and a few others chose to train their skill trees in the Time Space of the Spiritual Land, their hearts set on seeing if this cheat area where time was much faster than the outside world would allow them to catch up to a single person.","Many of the ranks of the Harbingers now neared the Void or were stably on it as Noah was coming across Cores very easily, their ranks almost reaching his as he had yet to choose to break through into the Soul Rank yet.","His considerations for this were currently because of the restrictions of the Infernal Realm of the First Hell, which only allowed the origins of beings up to the Void Rank to remain in it. Those who were not of the Void Realm were pushed out of the First Realm of Hell, and in the case of Infernals, they were transferred into the Second Realm of Hell that was much wider and grander, the location where some genuine Infernal Lords made their home!","Many thoughts crossed Noah’s mind as he wondered whether they would be a change on the restrictions of the First Hell because of the Infernal Lord title that he held, many of the thoughts leaning towards this possibility as his cast ability that he pushed into the Soul Rank, [Arch Lich Ra’Zan], could be cast in the First Realm of Hell and actually remain there.","To him, this could simply mean because it was a skill cast by a being at the Void Rank, it did not violate the laws of the First Realm of Hell even though its power reached the Soul Rank. This was similar to the strength that Athena showed which made it possible for her to take down an Infernal Aberration that had its power touching the next rank and was about to ascend to the Second Realm of Hell.","Many of these possibilities continued to flow in Noah’s mind as he chose to wait before rushing into the Soul Rank for now, the only thing he would be getting being his other attributes hitting that milestone, which was not that big of a deal for him who was now beginning to enjoy the boosts of Universal Laws.","What he wanted to do now was explore the Celestial Realm even more as he used the memories of the new regions that the Draconic Fire Behemoth had explored in his lifetime when he chose to reluctantly leave the volcanic mountain that had the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire, as well as observe the other regions that held numerous different Behemoths!","There were Ice and Water Behemoths he had yet to come across, Earth Behemoths he had only heard about from the Celestials, and even the powerful Fate Behemoths that were nearly impossible to kill, these Behemoths also being the ones that were disrupting the advancement of Celestials the most.","To combat these Elite Behemoths that were proficient in the Law of Fate, Noah’s mind was already on the Behemoths that stood opposite them with the Law of Chaos as his mind continued expanding to multiple places.","The biggest question on his mind was similar Inheritances like the Disciple of Fire and Fate’s Disciple that he now had his hands on. If he went into the regions of other elements, would he be able to get his hands on other Inheritances of those elements? Would they be similar to the Origin Core given by the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire or similar to the Fate Lines made available by Fate’s Disciple?","There were so many questions that made his curious heart tremble in anticipation as he wanted to quickly get the answers to all of them!","Among these many questions, the biggest one that still remained unanswered was about the Celestial Realm itself.","What exactly was this esoteric realm that had Inheritances like Disciple of Fire and Fate’s Disciple? What was the true identity of this realm that was filled with enormous beings that were extremely intunned to the Universal Laws?","This was the biggest mystery on Noah’s mind, and the one he was not even close to answering as he continued to move forward with his own aims!","The Ancient Blood Clone took out the [Origin Core- Behemoth Zygote] from the Expansive Space as he chose to begin with this first, waiting while his people gathered themselves after he sent the telepathic messages pertaining to them partaking in the recent treasure he had found. A curious smile spread out from him as he looked at the shimmering egg in front of him, wondering of the being that would come out of this!"]},{"number":395,"title":"Chapter 395: Chapter 394 - A Land of Fire","paragraphs":["The [Origin Core- Behemoth Zygote] stated that its incubation period would be affected by the region it was in, Noah looked at the bubbling lava around him as this region was extremely suitable for this purpose, but there was another possibility he could think of that was even more perfect!","He teleported into the miniaturized Spiritual Land as he appeared atop a snowy region in the north of the expansive landmass. He gazed at the beautifully falling snow as he glanced at the description of a particular feature of the Spiritual Land.","<strong>[Law Space] :: Fields containing a higher concentration of particular laws can be created, granting increased comprehension speed to all that cultivate within. Currently unlocked spaces: Water, Fire, Earth, Air. Locked spaces: Time, Space, Light, Dark, Fate, Chaos...</strong>","Yes, the place he thought would be the most perfect for the incubation of this spectacular egg was something that he could make in his Spiritual Land, and that was the Law Space!","The clone smoothly landed on the snowy field as he breathed out, using Spiritual Land Management to initiate the feature of Law Space. His thoughts went forward as he selected the element of fire, a holographic square image of where he wanted this space to be appearing in his eyes as he tweaked with it.","He found that he could increase its size and also decrease it, expanding the holographic field as he made it a few tens of miles before he used his mind to overlay it to the vibrant snowy field in front of his eyes.","RUMBLE!","The moment he affirmed with Spiritual Land Management and the blue holographic layout was selected, a tremor passed through the entire Spiritual Land as its abundant essence began to congregate towards this selected region!","The bountiful snow that was spread throughout the nearby fields melted rapidly as the clear earth below it was revealed, a shade of red beginning to spread out from all directions as the calm earth of the surrounding area began to crack and fissure.","Some areas were elevated as others were brought down, the phenomenal creation of the Law Space filled with the Law of Fire occurring in front of Noah’s eyes in real time.","The environment of the Frozen Plateau Spiritual Land that was always cold and frigid began to change in this particular region as heat spread from all around, the formation of small blazing mountains appearing as the area quickly changed from an austere white and into a blazing red atmosphere with palpating heat.","RUMBLE!","Just as it had begun, the process continued to finish rapidly as the changed geography stopped shaking, the concentration of fire elements in the region now beginning to rise as even Noah felt it becoming increasingly hotter. This was the field being created by a feature of the Spiritual Land, this was the Law Space where there was a higher concentration of the Law of Fire!","WAA!","Waves of heat released outwards continuously as the process finished, the surrounding region that was not even designated as the Law Space also seeing its frigid air melting as the effect spread out for quite a distance. The melting of the snow continued until an area of spectacular balance was reached, Noah observing as a region of flames and fire came to an intersection point as neither of the two invaded the other. Calmness returned to the surroundings as his attention locked in on the newly built Law Space.","To put it simply, it was a shimmering Land of Fire that actually had wisps of flames dancing in its atmosphere, the very earth itself blazing hot as spurts of lava could be seen coming from the ground.","The Ancient Blood Clone entered this spectacular region as he felt the Fire Origin Core attached to his main body tremble in joy as he came in contact with the unique fire elemental energy in this space, its slow spinning in his main body becoming slightly faster as it moved with even more vigor.","The clone walked through the Space filled with the Law of Fire, whipping out the [Origin Core- Behemoth Zygote] as the moment it was released into the hot atmosphere, it shone a red l.u.s.ter as the excited fire elements in the surroundings began to be absorbed into this crimson egg.","Noah carried this large egg the same size as him further into the Fire Space as he neared the center where bubbling lava could be seen, laying this egg down at the location he felt the most congregation of the Law of Fire as half of the [Origin Core- Behemoth Zygote] sank into the rapidly changing earth.","OOONG!","The speed of fire elements converging into the egg only increased with this action, the egg actually rising slightly in the air by itself as smoldering flames and lava began to swirl around it, the intensity of fire elements only increasing in this region as the clone pulled back and watched this process occur.","He watched for a few minutes as this process continued without a change, affirming in his mind that he expected the possible awakening of the creature inside this egg to happen in a matter of hours as he left it alone to float in the sea of flames and lava, his body disappearing to the underground layer of the Spiritual Land where multiple portals stably stood.","He would give the enormous egg the time it needed as he moved on to another task he had to take care of, this one involving the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire!","Of the portals present in the underground layer of the Spiritual Land, one shone with a red l.u.s.ter, another was tinged with white, one was swirling in darkness, another was verdant green, and the last one was a beautiful blue.","This particular blue portal was connected to his home world, where he had laid down numerous portals in this world and the others that he was connected to, forming something close to what he observed in the World of Cultivation below where a circle of portals that led to different worlds stood.","From the portal that led to the Demon World, the Tactician Agares who was overseeing this world was the first to arrive as he sunk to his knees while bowing his head down towards Noah.","\"Master.\"","From the Beast World, those in the upper echelons from the remaining three Mythical Beast Kingdoms and the Frozen Kingdom also began to appear from their portal as they all did similar bows of respect towards Noah, Queen Adelaide coming to Noah’s side with a shy smile.","Steel Mikhail soon came from the portal leading to his home world as he nodded towards Noah with his same strict face, the bulky protector’s body gleaming with power as his eyes shone for whatever opportunity laid in store for them today.","From the Ancient Blood World, the exploring Vampyres also appeared from the red portal as the Frost Race of the Icebound World also made their entrance, the underground layer of the Spiritual Land becoming livelier as many beings were granted permission to enter into the Spiritual Land for an opportunity they did not yet fully know of.","Barbatos and Kazuhiko’s auras could also be felt as they came out of the Time Space and joined them, a unique event about to take place as Noah was about to share a spectacular Inheritance that could only be found in the Celestial Realm!","An Inheritance that granted one a unique cultivation ability and an Absolute Skill was about to be freely shared to multiple beings as the erection of Noah’s own powerful force continued, this time their power being boosted at an unimaginable level as they got their hands on something that nobody else could even find!"]},{"number":396,"title":"Chapter 396: Chapter 395 - A Scholar, Chaos and Fate","paragraphs":["In the region immediately south of the Sanctum, frigid winds ravaged the snowy environment as a large Ice Behemoth was rolling in the snow peacefully.","Not too far from this Ice Behemoth, a hidden figure covered head to toe with a dark robe was crouching beneath the sparkling snowy vegetation as he wrote a few lines in his note book.","’Both the Northern and Southern regions have a similar level of elemental particles in the atmosphere, but their levels are still much higher than any other realms.’","The being was carefully doc.u.menting his findings of the Celestial Realm as his vibrant power at the peak of Soul Realm hid its aura from the nearby Behemoth.","This was someone that had managed to enter the Celestial Realm with the aid of the Pureblood Vampyres from the Underworld, a powerful covert operative from the Scholar’s Guild that boasted great power in the Dark Expanse!","’The supposed Celestial Beasts are even more unique, their bodies holding an abnormal amount of universal laws.’","The being continued placing more findings, pushing up his glasses as his eyes remained on the Ice Behemoth rolling in the snow with its enormous body.","’The structures of the Behemoths I have managed to get my hands on shows that their physiology is similar to their species counterparts in other worlds and realms, but their Origins seems to have been influenced greatly by the force behind this Celestial Realm’","Numerous possibilities passed through the mind of the Scholar, comparing his abundant experience and knowledge with the new land that the Celestials had managed to explore for the past thousands of years. With his tenure in the Scholar’s Guild that only the most genius Wizards and Magicians had a chance to take positions in, his experience was wide and vast!","’The biggest possibilities so far is that this Celestial Realm is one of the highest tiered realms to be found in our Novus Galaxy, or the even more unbelievable possibility is that this Realm could be what we have all been searching for...the place where universal laws are abundant and the atmospheric essence is immense, this could just be the C-’","ROAR!","The man from the Scholar’s Guild stopped taking his notes as his gaze went towards the mountainous Ice Behemoth, seeing an Exploration Team from a Prime World nearing the beast and beginning a hunt as the Scholar used his power to veil his body even more, sinking into the earth as he continued observing. What was on his mind was the same thing that many beings were recently trying to figure out, and it was the question of what exactly was this mystical realm that the Celestials had been enjoying for so long?!","---","Near the center of the Sanctum itself, Athena and Noah were meeting with a serious Grandmaster Vredral as they discussed their recent ventures, the Grandmaster approving of their fast progress as he adopted a careful expression and spoke.","\"You’ve gotten used to the pace of Normal Behemoths and learned how to best take them down, and we can move on to the next stage of your training as you tackle even more fierce Behemoths, and these ones will actually be of great aid for you to increase the speed at which you obtain Fate Lines!\"","Grandmaster Vredral spoke with a powerful Voice as Noah and Athena looked forward respectfully, many thoughts passing through Noah’s mind as he looked forward to anything that could enhance the speed he could raise the Supreme Law of Fate.","\"Past the Fire Behemoths in the Northern region, the danger increases as you start getting into the dangerous regions where mainly those at the Soul Forging Realm explore, with the highest tiered teams like the Righteous Fire Exploration Team and Elite Teams coming into play as the enemies you might come across...are those proficient in Supreme Laws!\"","A powerful light shot through the eyes of the Grandmaster as he said this, using his power as he waved his hands and created the illusory image of a dark Behemoth in front of their eyes.","\"The ones that are the most dangerous to us as well as the most profitable...are the terrible Chaos Behemoths that are proficient in the opposing element that we cultivate. This means that our attacks backed with the law of fate are especially harmful to them, but it also means that their attacks filled with the Law of Chaos are especially dangerous to us as well!\"","\"But with danger comes opportunity, where the hunting of Chaos Behemoths has shown to rapidly cause an increase in the number of Fate Lines one can condense, rapidly gaining strength through this dangerous path.\"","The Grandmaster finished his words as the two disciples in front of him had shining eyes, Athena being the first one to speak as her body pulsed with a gold light, her expression that of excitement.","\"We are willing to brave the dangers, Master!\"","Noah’s eyes also showed an enthusiastic expression as he nodded towards the Grandmaster, their next steps to increase their already rapid rise in power being set in stone as they prepare to delve further into the mysterious Celestial Realm, and this time it was to search for Elite Behemoths that were proficient in a Supreme Law!","Preparations went underway as the leader of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team became excited at the news that their team was granted clearance to delve past the Fire Behemoths and into the more dangerous regions further away from the Sanctum, the boisterous Boru bringing Noah and Athena to celebrate the entire night as a feast was carried out.","To them, another milestone was coming up as they would get the chance to brave dangers and increase their strength, but Noah’s mind was filled with other possibilities as he had entirely different thoughts when he thought about the Chaos Behemoths and their proficiency in the Law of Chaos.","His mind continued to wonder what Items and materials would come out of them, what treasures or Inheritances he could find if he delved into this region, and exactly where his power would be as he amassed more Fate Lines while increasing the Stage of the Fire Origin Core slowly growing inside him!","As others looked at one or two possibilities in front of their eyes, Noah was seeing a bright future filled with endless opportunities that were all just waiting for him!"]},{"number":397,"title":"Chapter 397: Chapter 396 - Schemes, Sharing Treasures","paragraphs":["In specific locations around the Sanctum that were now designated as marketplaces, a bustling atmosphere spread out as shouts could be heard from all around.","\"Claw of an Earth Behemoth for sale, will only trade for Soul Cores or materials from a Fire Behemoth!\"","\"An Aurora Fruit for sale! The one and only Aurora Fruit!\"","\"The map layout of the nearby eastern region is available, looking for Ice Behemoth materials to trade!\"","Powerful voices spread out as beings from all over congregated and looked for things they could buy if they did not want to risk their lives fighting terrifying Behemoths, many of the materials being on sale currently only being half of the ones that the sellers brought back from their adventures, with half of it already being pocketed by the Celestials.","In the past few days, the Celestials had begun seeing the effect of their decision as they collected materials at a pace multiple times greater than before, these materials coming from every single being moving in the Celestial Realm only acting as another source of rapidly increasing the strength of their disciples as many Prime Warsh.i.p.s were moving from the Celestial Realm and heading towards the Celestial Stars to distribute these wondrous materials to these planets.","They were achieving their purpose of continuing to influence the lives of many of the powerful figures in the Light Expanse, as well as enjoy the benefits of the Celestial Realm at an even faster rate than before.","But as always, decisions had their own positives and negatives!","Among the many beings entering the Celestial Realm, many of those with expert hiding skills from the Dark Expanse also made their way in! Whether in the initial party of Pureblood Vampyres that came in with Elena, or the arrival of later parties as they began to explore and map out the Celestial Realm as well.","Among these beings, there were those who had skills similar to a certain imposter that allowed them to teleport across realms and planets, their only limitation being the distance they could jump across. More mana was required the longer the distance was, which presented an arduous challenge for those in the Dark Expanse as the location of the Celestial Realm was surrounded in all directions by the eyes of the Celestials, any nearby planets being kept under close watch as they took into account the unique spatial abilities that some beings held!","On this day though, another unique being from the Scholar’s Guild of the Dark Expanse had managed to pass through the eyes of the Celestials and smoothly enter into the Sanctum, sending a telepathic message to another member of the Scholar’s guild that was observing Ice Behemoths in the southern region.","\"Argus, I have arrived. We can now begin!\"","The contents of the message could only be well understood by the one that heard it, a telepathic message being sent back right away.","\"You finally arrive, Malthus. We have much to do. This realm...\"","Numerous messages began to be sent back and forth on this day as two well known beings in the Scholar’s Guild of the Dark Expanse actively began their plans in the Celestial Realm.","One was known as Argus, the Walking Library who was proficient in covert skills and held a large amount of information on many things!","The other was Malthus, the Spatial Magician that excelled in the Law of Space, holding abilities that many beings envied!","\"Yes yes slow down Argus, you’ve been keeping in contact with Elena? I am ready to establish the spatial connection that will allow us to transfer the boons of this realm with ease in the coming future. Which locations have you scouted?\"","\"...start heading South, I’ll send you my location.\"","One expert talked to another in the field of powerful beings moving around the wide Sanctum established by Celestials, moving directly under their nose as the initial stages of the plans of the beings from the Dark Expanse went underway. They knew the strength of their enemies stemmed from this realm, and these same enemies were bold enough to open this realm to others as the conflicts heated up and the way neared!","Before all hell broke loose, they would harvest the boons of this realm themselves as they strove for one goal- finding treasures at the same level as the Celestials that have allowed them to move with extreme strength these past thousands of years!","---","As many beings continued to move across the vast Celestial Realm, a few lucky ones were getting their hands on a powerful Inheritance beneath a volcanic mountain. The forces of numerous worlds connected to Noah were freely getting their hands on a powerful set of techniques that would give them a huge edge over cultivating a universal law, something that many of them had not even done before and would be the first time for them to try!","But they had no need to ponder or try to comprehend the law in an abstruse manner, all they needed was to have enough energy to use {Disciple of Fire} and create the Fire Origin Core, continuing to build up this new origin as they also became able to use the Absolute Skill that came with the inheritance.","The Spiritual Land was stationed very close to the ancient pedestal that held the Inheritance Crystal that could not be moved, Noah guiding those that were too weak with a protective barrier, and those who could handle the baleful lava floating in their surroundings simply went out themselves to accept the Inheritance.","But when this initial process was complete, the many individuals found themselves directed towards a certain location in the Frozen Plateau Spiritual Land that went against the original nature they knew of, observing a wide area that was filled with extreme heat that only got more intense as one went further in!","Those that were more powerful followed Noah’s directions as they went further into the field concentrated with the Law of Fire, being told to initiate {Disciple of Fire} for the first time in this mystical area.","RUMBLE!","The power leveling of numerous beings was underway as at the center of this Law Space, a huge egg was resting rapidly while absorbing the abundant elemental particles of the Law of Fire in the surroundings, immense heat being given off of it as it looked ready to pop at any moment!"]},{"number":398,"title":"Chapter 398: Chapter 397 - A Pet Behemoth!","paragraphs":["Some of the Harbingers of Sin were the first few to enjoy the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire, their bodies already producing a seedling that they needed to nourish before it could become a Fire Origin Core.","Unlike Noah, they did not have unlimited reserves of mana to play with, so they actually had an arduous task just to acc.u.mulate enough mana to establish the Fire Origin Core in the first place!","Noah expected them to take a few days before becoming successful even in this beautiful region that was now filled with the dense elemental particles of the fire element.","His gaze transferred towards the pulsating [Origin Core- Behemoth Zygote] that was showing an even more vibrant reaction after a few hours, his clone teleporting near the very center of the Fire Law Space as he observed the changes with anticipation!","His main body was communicating with Elena as she faithfully released the details of the movements of the Dark Expanse and their covert operations in the Celestial Realm, Noah keeping himself up to date on the occurrences that moved the future forward as he noted the arrival of two powerful unique combatants from the Dark Expanse in the Celestial Realm.","\"My Progenitor, could I be so bold as to request for you to create items for us using the materials of the Behemoths we take down?\"","A smile came on Noah’s mind as he heard this telepathic message from Elena, sending a reply right after.","\"That is something I already planned to do. Also, I’ll need you guys to find a chance to come into the Northern region of the Celestial Realm to personally accept a unique Inheritance I’ve gotten my hands on...\"","His main body continued communicating with his people who did not get the chance to partake in the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire yet, as well as begin the process of preparing to move out with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team as they went against Chaos Behemoths!","His clone remained in the fiery Law Space as he observed the [Origin Core- Behemoth Zygote] to be pulsating, its size having already grown double to his own as it began releasing wondrous waves of scalding fire elements as cracks began to spread all around it, a red light beginning to shine out.","RUMBLE!","A unique regal essence began to permeate outwards as the cracks audibly spread across the egg, this regal essence stating the arrival of a powerful being as the fire elements in the surroundings danced wildly!","ROAR!","The clear and crisp roar of a young dragon rang out as magnificently, an eruption of red light blew apart the cage it was held in as the widespread wings of a small Draconic Fire Behemoth became apparent when the light began dying down.","The highly abundant fire elements rushed towards this Dragon speedily as Noah observed with wonder as the size of this beast expanded until it reached 10 meters, its widespread wings shining brilliantly as its young draconic features came to observe the only being near it.","The moment the gaze of the young dragon landed on Noah, its eyes shone with a subservient light as an extremely defined runic circle erupted from it and bound itself to Noah, traveling through the Ancient Blood Clone and his Origin feeling a small connection that was considered the attachment of a pet as this Dragon formed a bond with him successfully with the aid of the unique means of the Planetary System!","The eyes of the young dragon remained on Noah as it looked at him with a mixture of care and confusion, its innate mental strength and power soon coming to play as numerous bursts of information were released from the connection it felt with this being in front of it, the young dragon coming to an understanding as it moved across the blazing atmosphere filled with fire elements and neared Noah.","Its size now towered at 10 meters, being less than one fifth the size of a normal Behemoth right after its birth.","The young Draconic Fire Behemoth brought its regal head near Noah’s clone as it cutely nudged and rubbed its head towards him, the clone having a wide smile spread across his face as he patted the subservient dragon in front of him!","\"Master.\"","The voice of a young dragon rang out in Noah’s mind as he nodded, looking over the body of this 10 meter beast right after its birth as he calculated its strength.","Currently, it actually held vibrant strength at the Phantasmal Rank, its strength right after being born depicting the regal rank of this being and the huge possibilities it would have for the future.","The thought of the uniqueness of this Draconic Fire Behemoth that he just got his hands on did not pass by Noah, and he perfectly understood that he was most likely the first one to ever hold a Behemoth from this Celestial Realm as a pet!","This was made possible with his Planetary System that took the Origin of the monstrous Fire Behemoth that was half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm and fused it together with the shattered soul, making way for the possibility of this spectacular young dragon in front of his eyes.","In the brief period of time that his clone had entered into the Celestial Realm and began moving by himself, he had managed to find an Inheritance, defeat a Draconic Fire Behemoth that was already half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm, and get his hands on a pet of an unknown caliber as a powerful dragon subserviently nudged his body!","His expectations for the future were bright as he looked towards the Dragon and called out.","\"Come!\"","There was much to do as he took the time to absorb the boons of the recent venture and continue strengthening the people around him, his thoughts especially focusing on the Behemoth he had gotten his hands on as he prepared to raise a terrifying beast for his own uses. Just the thought of this now 10 meter tall Dragon that could someday grow to become the mountainous Draconic Behemoth that he just battled made him look excitedly into the future!"]},{"number":399,"title":"Chapter 399: Chapter 398 - Time is of the Essence!","paragraphs":["Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone temporarily returned to the First Realm of Hell, his figure teleporting to the blazing skies as he stood on top of a curious young Draconic Behemoth.","His gaze stretched across the area around him as it had already filled with droves of Infernals. The essence within his body thrummed as he adorned the Incandescent Flameborn Set with its ridiculous set boosts, getting ready to carry out high speed farming of the Infernals as he set the goal of fully obtaining the title of Infernal Lord soon!","He had only been leaving the Arch Lich Ra’Zan behind to farm the Infernals and increase the Skill Points along with the progression of the percentage on the title of Infernal Lord, but he planned to move personally and claim this title even faster as he wanted to enter the Soul Forging Realm soon.","He wasn’t confident of breaking the laws of the Infernal Realm if he reached the rank that was always pushed out of the First Realm of Hell, so this was his next best choice as his main body began moving with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team to delve deeper into the Celestial Realm looking for Chaos Behemoths.","\"Let’s go!\"","He sent a command to the young Dragon that was ever so slowly growing larger by the minute, the clone providing abundant cores to bring the rank of this Behemoth up as he expected it to reach the Void Realm in no time!","He had with him numerous Saint and Void Rank Cores, with a decent amount of Soul Rank cores put aside to propel his own level forward when the time was right.","As the dragon reveled in another fiery environment that was the Infernal Realm, Noah’s clone began casting numerous skills as the Arch Lich Ra’Zan appeared once more in the First Realm of Hell, its qualification as a skill cast by a being at the Void Realm allowing it to bypass the restrictions of this Infernal Realm as it began summoning a large amount of Undead, the huge runic circles that brought forth Abyssal Undead also appearing in the skies!","RUMBLE!","The mystical Ancients were brought to life once more from the use of the ability in the [Kin of the Ancients] skill tree, the dark winged humanoid creatures grandly appearing in the Infernal Realm as they glanced towards the clone.","Noah’s thoughts seemed to have gone through to them as their gazes turned towards the maddened Infernals below them, seeing how weak these beings they were summoned to kill were as they turned their heads to the side and glanced at Noah again, seemingly posing a bewildering question that was asking- ’Really? Summoning us for such weak creatures?’","Yes! Compared to the power that Noah and his summoned beings held, this campaign that he was about to carry out against these Infernals whos strongest powerhouses were at the Void Realm was going to be really one sided!","It was similar to a high level veteran coming back to a low level area filled with mobs that dropped loot which still had great uses for them!","If just the Arch Lich moving alone with droves of undead over the past month brought the percentage of the Infernal Lord title over 30%, with how he planned to move personally while using his overpowered abilities in this realm, the only question that remained was how many days it would take him to bring the percentage of the title to 100%.","[Arch Demon Lord Transformation]. [Lesser Cthulhu]. [Dawn of the Blood Lord]. [Incarnation of Fire]...","The repetitive casting of numerous skills and stacked transformation and buffing skills were being cast as a terrifying aura bent on hunting down Infernals with extreme efficiency appeared in the First Realm of Hell!","OONG!","The shining Trident of the Sea appeared in Noah’s enlarging hands as he adopted the terrible combination of the transformations of the Lesser Cthulhu and Arch Demon Lord, his other hand carrying the Glaive of Simmering Ember from the Incandescent Flameborn Set as the gorgeous casting of skills erupted from him again, the targeted infernals almost pissing their pants as they felt an aura that was in no way at the acceptable level of this realm come for their lives!","---","Noah’s main body was standing next to a boisterous Boru who was talking about the fearsome power of the Chaos Behemoths they would soon be facing as they waited for the rest of the team members to join them.","\"I was able to battle a single one while following an Elite Exploration Team of Grandmasters. I can tell you now that these beasts will make the superiority you feel while aided by the Law of Fate disappear! They will truly show you what beings proficient in Supreme Laws are like!\"","The power of the Chaos Behemoths continued to be hyped up as Boru continued.","\"The only reason I am confident of our chances this time is because Grandmaster Vredral favors his two disciples that have Noble Fates and will be coming along, haha!\"","Noah smiled at this comment as he knew for this upcoming trip, they would be accompanied by the powerful Domain Expansion Realm Grandmaster as they withstood against the unique strength of Chaos Behemoths. The Grandmaster favored their lives too much to let them explore such a dangerous location where these beings resided with just the Righteous Fire Exploration Team, so he would be acting as the leading figure in this upcoming hunt as Noah got a glimpse of the power of this Grandmaster that had a relatively high position on the 7th Celestial Star.","Noah and Boru didn’t wait too long before the rest of the team began to gather, Athena appearing last with the Grandmaster as eyebrows were raised at her entrance. A proud smile was apparent on Grandmaster Vredral’s face as Athena walked in with an aura that had just broken through from the Void Realm and into the Soul Forging Realm, the strength of the War Princess pulling ahead as her body seemed to be bubbling with power!"]},{"number":400,"title":"Chapter 400: Chapter 399 - Venturing Further North","paragraphs":["\"Congratulations, Senior Sister.\"","Noah replied with a light smile as he looked towards the shocking strength being released in the small body of the girl in front of him. She had already been at the Void Rank when he first met her months ago, her power slowly continuing to build up as she finally exploded upwards and entered the Soul Forging Realm today!","\"Thank you, Junior Brother Crixus. You must not tarry behind.\"","Her eyes were languid and filled with longing for battle as she joined the team, all the other members sending her their congratulatory words as Noah was instead wondering where the power of this War Princes was actually at now.","As he spent more time amassing fate lines, he was growing more and more capable of discerning just how many lines of fate a Celestial held, and his intuition told him that Athena was actually nearing on the magical number of 100,000!","This was a number that made one qualified to be a Celestial Grandmaster, something that very few joined the honor of achieving in their lifetimes. The power of this War Princess when she was at the Void Rank was terrifying, where she was capable of standing against a Soul Forging Realm Devouring Black Serpent in the Magus World and battle against Soul Rank Behemoths in the Celestial Realm. A smile spread across Noah’s lips as he wondered the power this woman could now wield as she entered the Soul Forging Realm herself!","\"Hmm, let’s go!\"","Grandmaster Vredral spoke out jovially as they went towards a particular area where numerous Primal Warsh.i.p.s were located, an expansive space that only Celestials were permitted into as for this exploration trip, they would be using a Prime Warship to traverse the vast distances of the Celestial Realm and into the region where Chaos Behemoths could be found.","From the Sanctum that could be considered an enormous metropolis filled with an ever expanding population of new beings, a particular group of Celestials entered a grand Prime Warship as the energy of a Domain Realm expert wrapped around it and lifted it to the skies.","The nearby forces of numerous Prime World now populating the Sanctum glanced towards the location where this Vessel lifted smoothly and began shooting off to the Northern Region, this not being the first time they’ve observed something like this happening as they looked enviously at the means of the Celestials.","A particular party that was returning from their hunt, the newly formed Order of Blood, stared at this particular ship as a few of them felt a familiar aura from it!","The Emperor Penguin was walking through the mystical streets of the Sanctum valiantly as it raised its beak towards the skies, a sharp light passing through its beady eyes as the Royal Vampyre Elena had an even more fervent look in her gaze while she stared at the direction that Noah had gone to.","\"Onward!\"","She decisively sent a message to her people as she communicated with the forces of the Dark Expanse beginning their own plans in the Celestial Realm, the current goal of the Order of Blood being heading towards the same direction where numerous Fire Behemoths could be found, using this as a source of training as they made their way towards a certain Inheritance beneath a volcanic mountain!","The many pieces on the board continued to move as Noah comfortably stood in the advancing Prime Warship and looked out to the expansive landscape of the Celestial Realm below him.","The enormous shimmering trees and the fantasy-like atmosphere always took his breath away, linking this feeling to a similar one he felt when he observed his Spiritual Land but on a much larger scale. He found his thoughts actually wondering as he arrived at this comparison. Would the Spiritual Land ever be able to reach something as remotely as amazing as this? He shook himself out of his fantasies with this thought as he serenely watched the passing surroundings, not trying to daydream about impossible things at such a time.","They came across quite a few Fire Behemoths that were moving below, their gazes turning up towards them with a sharp light as they only observed the powerful vessel shoot past them.","A few times he observed attacks being thrown their way, the vessel either completely evading them, or a thin barrier of light appearing around the Prime Warship that stopped the incoming attacks.","So far, they had not come across any flying Behemoths that would have caused them trouble, beings like the Draconic Fire Behemoth being unique and rare.","Like this, a few hours passed in the Prime Warship as the Grandmaster steered it competently through the explored areas of the Celestial Realm, a contemplating Noah watching the passing scenery and committing it all to his memory as his clone was moving with vigor in the Infernal Realm.","He could observe the constant shooting up of the Infernal Skill Points at a speed multiple times what the stationed Lich was bringing in the past, with the percentage next to the title of Infernal Lord also continuing to rise every now and then!","After another few hours, the Prime Warship that they were on started to slow down and lower towards the tall ancient trees in the ground, Noah noticing that the atmospheric essence had been getting even thicker as he looked towards the location they were arriving at.","Not too far from them, the slowing vessel was landing next to a large tower like structure, this exquisite architecture being a place where powerful Celestials were stationed far into the Celestial Realm, the junction where one could draw a line from Normal Behemoths and Elite Behemoths based on which direction they took.","Noah had arrived at his first Celestial Watch Tower that was surrounded by numerous Prime Warsh.i.p.s, the auras of powerful Celestials even wilder than the ones he normally sensed in the Sanctum being present as he further pierced into the ranks of Celestials, this time following a team being led by a Grandmaster as they planned to hunt Chaos Behemoths!"]}]);
